window.FWN_NECROPOLIS_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_NECROPOLIS_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2101,"title":"Chapter 2101: Chapter 2056: The Bridge of Life","paragraphs":["Chapter 2056: The Bridge of Life","“Demonic breeding grounds...” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes, finally seeing the truth of the situation on the other side of Quietus.","Innumerable wills of death swirled in that world, devouring the powerhouses suppressed here and possessing their bodies to walk the world in their stead. But they were wills that lacked a soul, so they naturally lacked thoughts of their own. Under the guidance of a frightening power, they became tools of the overseer.","Ancestor and the Spacetime King had indeed lost control over the World Heart, and completely lost control at that. If it wasn’t for Quietus, the overseer would have taken over all of existence, not just the World Heart.","“Who plunged Quietus into Ancestor’s heart and killed him? If it was the overseer, he wouldn’t create this kind of obstacle for himself...” The question popped into Lu Yun’s mind. It would seem that the circumstances surrounding Ancestor’s death were far more than what they appeared.","Supposing that the overseer was Ancestor’s murderer—he would never leave Quietus behind to create further trouble for himself. Even with the Spacetime King on the scene, he was certain to retrieve the sword.","“So who killed Ancestor?” Lu Yun’s heart pounded as he stared at the enormous weapon. He found it incredibly familiar as it’d once been his weapon. Although he’d given it to Tianqi now, he could take it back at any time if he so desired.","It was the sword’s primary body in front of him!","The young man felt that he could easily pull it out and turn it into his own treasure. But once it was removed, Ancestor would come back to life. Yet, the one who came back to life would not be him.","In this place suffused with boundless wills of death, who knew which one would seize Ancestor’s body as a vessel for themselves?","What was also certain was that the existence created from his body would instantly collapse and all of their plans go to waste. Quietus was the crux of everything.","“Lu Yun,” a voice suddenly sounded in the young man’s ear. Lu Yun’s expression changed drastically when he turned back and he threw himself back several thousand kilometers before stopping.","“What are you so afraid of me for?” The speaker was a young man dressed in a purple shirt and blue outer-robes, a jade belt around his waist. Appearing to be the son of a rich family, he beamed at Lu Yun.","Unrest.","The nihil powerhouse that Yun Yi had sacrificed to, the one who coveted Lu Yun’s Tome of Life and Death. The one who held the Imperial Seal as collateral to ensure that Lu Yun would enter the nothing. He wanted to take the Tome of Life and Death from the young man as soon as Lu Yun entered his territory.","Who would’ve thought that he’d come to the World Heart before Lu Yun had a chance to enter nothing? And it wasn’t his replica, but his primary body. A true nihil powerhouse was here in the flesh!","Lu Yun could ignore empyrean and sacred supremes, but he was far from being a match for nihil powerhouses.","“You can visit the World Heart?” Lu Yun took in a deep breath as his eyes darted uncertainly around the area.","“Of course I can.” The smile deepened on Unrest’s face. He reached out a hand and crushed the dark empyrean supreme to death with a single finger.","Lu Yun’s eyes widened. Thankfully, his new recruit could come back to life through the Tome of Life and Death. He’d already written the empyrean supreme’s name in the treasure. An empyrean-level powerhouse could not be treated like the others.","“How about this, I’ll let you go if you pull out the sword.” Unrest flashed to the young man and pointed at the center of his forehead.","Lu Yun’s temples throbbed painfully.","“Ancestor will come back to life if the sword is removed, aren’t you worried that he’ll kill you when that happens?” Lu Yun sneered, but he was very unsettled. Unrest couldn’t possibly not know the consequences of removing Quietus, but he still insisted on Lu Yun doing so. Plainly, Unrest and Yun Yi didn’t share the same goal.","They were just using each other from beginning to end.","“That’s none of your business. I’ll kill you right now if you don’t pull it out and take your book. I can pull out Quietus myself if I have the book in hand.” Unrest’s fingertip slowly sank into Lu Yun’s forehead; a streak of crimson trickled out through the wound.","“Then kill me. I’ll die anyway once Quietus is removed, so you might as well kill me and do the deed yourself.” Lu Yun stretched out his neck with a snort and closed his eyes. Everything he protected was in the chief worlds. That realm would perish as soon as he removed Quietus, a destruction that would be beyond salvaging.","To Lu Yun, it would make no difference then if he was alive or dead.","“I see, then I’ll do it myself.”","Bam!","A muffled collision sounded from his body. He shook and hurtled backward, like something had punched him.","A hint of a smile appeared on Lu Yun’s face.","“With Yun Yi’s unsurpassed intelligence and watertight planning, how would she fail to take into account the unstable factor that is you?” He breathed out more easily, but the wound in his forehead didn’t close. It still oozed blood and took the power of reincarnation to repair.","“Not bad, is this the power of nothing?” Lu Yun relaxed and inwardly rejoiced that he’d never used the power that Unrest gave him. If he had, the man would probably take possession of him through the power and turn him into a puppet.","A jade seal had flown out of Unrest’s robes and pummeled him with blows as a ball of light.","The Imperial Seal.","The treasure that Unrest had seized was now aimed at his throat and attacked him tirelessly.","“Are you still alive, Yun Yi?” Lu Yun asked haltingly as he looked at the bedraggled Unrest. Although he didn’t sense Yun Yi’s life force anywhere, that didn’t mean she was dead.","The Imperial Seal continued attacking Unrest instead of responding to Lu Yun.","BOOM.","It expanded into a bridge and charged into Unrest’s body, growing rapidly and suppressing the nihil powerhouse. The other side of the bridge slowly extended until it reached Lu Yun’s body.","“This is!!” Lu Yun’s eyes went wide. The Disordered Empyrean Supreme’s replica had once deployed a life extension art that helped him see everything about the grand supreme life form. Yun Yi was now using the seal as a bridge of life to connect their bodies so Lu Yun could see the intricacies of a nihil life form!","“I had a chance of life still... but now I am completely dead,” Yun Yi’s slightly mischievous voice rang out. “Live well in my stead. Don’t die.”","The voice faded away."]},{"number":2102,"title":"Chapter 2102: Chapter 2057: Divvying the Spoils","paragraphs":["Chapter 2057: Divvying the Spoils","Yun Yi’s transaction with Unrest had been a gamble with two potential outcomes. The first was that she might have a chance to come back to life and escape from death if Unrest didn’t harbor any ulterior motives.","If he did, she would use the final spark of life preserved in the Imperial Seal to eliminate him. That would also scatter her to the four winds and consign her to death.","The situation in front of them was the second possibility.","Yun Yi was dead.","Her vitality was the strength that propelled the Imperial Seal to deliver a thorough beating to Unrest. Lu Yun never thought that the final traces of power she left behind would be so formidable that a nihil powerhouse wouldn’t be able to fight back!","Indeed, the woman who had the right to participate in the grand game and complete the final plans to revive the primordial world of immortals was no ordinary soul.","Unrest squawked with terror and outrage, trying to break through the void a few times so he could return to nothing. However, the strength of the Imperial Seal was so magnificient that it restored the void whenever it was split open. Unrest had no chance to leave.","Through the bridge of life, all secrets about the nihil cultivation level traveled from Unrest’s body into Lu Yun’s mind. He operated formula dao at the same time to deduce as much as he could about it.","With his current cultivation level and the fully evolved Tome of Life and Death, he could discern everything there was to be known about the nothing.","“So my daughter really is dead...” sounded a grief-stricken voice as the primordial heavenly emperor appeared. The Imperial Seal landed in his hand and he flung out a backhand, suppressing the struggling Unrest to the point that the heavyweight couldn’t move.","Lu Yun raised his head and regarded the newcomer with a slight frown. He’d drawn the primordial heavenly emperor into an akasha ghost, but the man had freed himself from that state and returned to being a true living being.","He’d come back to life and must have done so when Lu Yun was in the Three Thousand. The young man wouldn’t have been unaware of the development otherwise.","“She wouldn’t have died if you’d appeared a second earlier,” Lu Yun said quietly.","“I am no match for Unrest,” sighed the emperor after a long moment. “I wouldn’t be able to suppress him if it wasn’t for Yun Yi keeping him under control. He’d kill me instead.","“I’ll say it, I am less than my daughter. I don’t even know what she was doing or wants to do. I only thought she wanted to revive the primordial world of immortals and conquer this part of existence.”","He laughed mercilessly at himself. “Now I know that she wanted to create a real existence, but what’s the point of knowing now?”","“It’s never too late to know.” Lu Yun didn’t fully believe the strange emperor. It didn’t seem that much of what he said was true. Maybe he’d turn on Lu Yun at any second.","“You’ve killed Wei Lie, haven’t you?” He suddenly thought of the man.","“How would I dare do anything to him? He’s the Dao King’s disciple. I just killed his past and future self to refine this body. His present self is fine and running affairs in the World of Immortals on his master’s behalf.”","Wei Lie was Shenyu, the one that the Hongmeng Tower had titled the Runaway King. Ordinary people would never catch the Dao King’s eye, only someone like the ancestor of dao forms had the right to become the Dao King’s disciple.","But Shenyu was only Shenyu now; everything that’d been Wei Lie was no longer. This was also done with the Dao King’s tacit approval, or the primordial heavenly emperor would have never dared be so bold.","Unrest was beet red as he furiously glared at the emperor and Lu Yun. Both of them were ants in existence yet to reach nihil, but these two ants were making use of the Imperial Seal to devour his power!","Indeed.","Lu Yun was imitating the life form of a nihil being while the primordial heavenly emperor was beginning to absorb Unrest’s power. Once he was finished, the powerhouse would scatter upon the wind and the emperor would be a new nihil powerhouse.","All of it was planned. In Yun Yi’s plots, she would attack Unrest even if he didn’t harbor ulterior motives so that her father and Lu Yun could divvy the spoils.","But his betrayal was also within her calculations. She wouldn’t have purposefully left the Imperial Seal to tempt him otherwise.","While Unrest snarled and howled, there was nothing that he could do. There were plenty of other sealed nihil powerhouses in the World Heart and they were absolutely delighted to see a peer being slowly devoured. Only in schadenfreude could they find some joy in their misery.","“Hoi hoi hoi, little fellows, how about you let me out too?” boomed one of them. “I just wanted to watch the show back in the day, but Spacetime and Ancestor got the better of me, the damned old farts.","“If you let me out, I’ll give you a replica on par with all of Unrest’s power. How about it?”","“Demonfire, your name is well known in the void. We’ll be the first to die if we let you out,” the primordial heavenly emperor snorted before Lu Yun could respond.","The speaker blinked, completely taken off guard that the other knew his name. So they were acquaintances!","“Oh hang on, so it’s Primordial,” Demonfire roared with laughter. “Primordial, your death was a grim and nasty affair. To think you’d come back to life in Ancestor’s patch of existence! Tsk tsk tsk, you sired a good daughter.”","Demonfire shrank back after his response, unwilling to provoke the primordial heavenly emperor.","The emperor didn’t deign to respond.","“So you are a nihil powerhouse?” Lu Yun realized as he watched the emperor furiously absorb Unrest’s power. He didn’t dare take part in that, even with the Tome of Life and Death.","“It’s all in the past. I was once stronger than Unrest and Demonfire just a pipsqueak.” Having paid a visit to earth, the primordial heavenly emperor had picked up some Earth sayings. “However, I am still less than even one of the overseer’s fingers.”","“The overseer is that strong?” Lu Yun’s heart skipped a beat. He could sense that Demonfire was far stronger than Unrest, and he was just a pipsqueak to the primordial heavenly emperor? Yet the emperor couldn’t withstand one of the overseer’s fingers?","“Too strong, he really did use just a finger to kill me.” The emperor shook his head. “I’m afraid there is no one in the universe who can withstand him.”","Lu Yun nodded without a word. He could probably crush the overseer with a finger if he entered the nihil, became one with the Tome of Life and Death, and turned into the one of dao. But what was the point of living as a being with emotions or desires?","Perhaps that version of him would take joy in his existence then, but the Lu Yun of now didn’t want to turn into thought.","Where there was a will, there was a way. Since the overseer was that strong, surely Lu Yun could be the same. He had the Tome of Life and Death, after all.","Purple light flashed through the air in front of them as a figure walked out of the radiance. The primordial heavenly emperor shook to see the other, the bleakness in his eyes growing stronger."]},{"number":2103,"title":"Chapter 2103: Chapter 2058: Mountain of Blades","paragraphs":["Chapter 2058: Mountain of Blades","“Dead, Yun Yi truly is dead,” the primordial heavenly emperor repeated with anguish.","“Mmhmm,” the newcomer nodded. “I would not be free if she was not dead.”","Violetgrave.","Violetgrave had originally appeared as the physical manifestation of the Netherdark Hell. Only later did Lu Yun understand who she was—Ancestor’s divine weapon.","The god of Mount Tai wasn’t capable of independently creating hell dao and building the five hells by himself. There were many hands in the shadows behind his feats.","Violetgrave was one of the most important links for these accomplishments. She’d hid herself as a sword to conceal her identity, successfully pulling the wool over other people’s eyes. No one had suspected that she was Ancestor’s weapon, or they’d never allow her to assimilate into hell dao.","Now they knew, and that she was a treasure that contained the civilizations of life, but it was too late.","Only Yun Yi had known before this. She’d protected Violetgrave with her strength and also limited everything about her so she could successfully meld into hell dao. Now that Yun Yi was dead, Violetgrave could depart from hell and be truly free.","She came to the World Heart the moment she was a free person.","“Congratulations,” Lu Yun smiled at her.","She smiled back at him. “It’s all thanks to you. Otherwise, I would be a public enemy even after gaining my freedom through Yun Yi’s death. I would have to go on the run and hide from everyone.”","“What are your plans now?” Lu Yun asked.","\"I want to visit the nothing. They all say that the nothing is boundless without end, that the Three Thousand is the only existence within it. I don’t believe that. I want to take a look for myself and see what else is out there beyond the nothing.” Yearning filled her eyes. “I’ve left the seed of civilization in the Violetgrave sword. You can take it if you need it.”","Violetgrave retained her old strength—that of Ancestor’s personal weapon. But having been part of the Netherdark Hell for countless eons, she’d long since removed the seed of civilization from herself. That was what everyone wanted from her.","Without that, no one desired to provoke the incredibly strong manifestation of a divine weapon.","“Alright,” Lu Yun nodded.","The sword was Violetgrave’s original form. Relinquishing it meant that she was a true living being and no longer the manifestation of a weapon.","She vanished after her words—the World Heart could not hold her.","The primordial heavenly emperor sighed deeply.","Unrest was dead without hope of salvation. The emperor had absorbed his strength and his nihil cultivation level was fully displayed to Lu Yun. There were no secrets of this cultivation realm that the young man didn’t know.","It was even possible for him to break through to nothing if he wanted, but he’d join their ranks as the lowest on the totem pole. He wouldn’t be able to stay in existence either, he’d at most be able to visit some place like the World Heart.","If he set foot in a place like the Three Thousand, he’d be attacked by the great daos within sanctuary.","The great daos within the Three Thousand remained the same they’d always been and were firmly under the overseer’s control. There were no benefits to becoming a nihil powerhouse now, so Lu Yun ignored the primordial heavenly emperor. He had his own plans in mind.","He also didn’t really approve of the heavenly emperor because the man hadn’t been able to protect his daughter. Yun Yi wouldn’t have died if there’d been any better options or if the heavenly emperor had been willing to do things differently.","Lu Yun flashed to the mountain of blades. A Jin Huo drenched in blood was still climbing it—all of the blades on the mountain were connate divine weapons. Born out of the heavenly dao, a connate weapon’s strength was determined by the strength of the world.","The World Heart was the strongest world in this part of existence, so these blades could easily slice through a peak grand supreme’s body or even kill an empyrean supreme.","The tree god sitting at the peak of the mountain finally opened his eyes. He seemed to be kept here by something and couldn’t move. He could only watch as Jin Huo weathered life and death again and again upon the mountain of blades.","Anyone who wished to save him had to climb the mountain—Jin Huo wouldn’t be able to climb it otherwise with her level of strength. It was a test that someone had set for her, not a condition created by this world.","It naturally wasn’t the tree god who was testing Jin Huo.","Lu Yun sighed softly. Thank goodness he’d come early, or she might really die! She’d already died nine thousand, nine hundred and ninety-eight times. There was only one Resurrection Talisman left on her.","At this rate, she’d be doomed after her next death.","Dying here meant that one wouldn’t even leave behind a hint of soul. One directly turned into the will of death and was subjugated to the overseer on the other side.","Lu Yun waved another nine thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine talismans onto Jin Huo. All things had their limits and the extremity of anything led to backlash. There could at most be nine thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine Resurrection Talismans on a person at any given time. More than that would lead to immediate recoil that would obliterate the holder.","Having reinforced Jin Huo, Lu Yun stood patiently to watch her ordeal continue.","She turned back to look gratefully at him, then set her jaw and continued climbing.","The Disordered Empyrean Supreme appeared by Lu Yun’s side and sighed softly.","“Were you successful?” He looked at her.","“Yes.” A smile spread across his face. “He has reincarnated into the shamanic race and will be their new master.","“What do you plan on doing now?” Hell dao no longer mattered to the Disordered Empyrean Supreme after she accomplished her goal, but Lu Yun also showed no inclinations of taking it back.","“Conquer the chief worlds, I suppose.” The young man gave it some thought. “I want to fold the entire realm into the World of Immortals. I’ve already sent the dark empyrean supreme to take care of the Infinite Deorc.”","The land of darkness only possessed one empyrean supreme. Since he’d sworn fealty to Lu Yun, then the entire realm was the young man’s.","Conquering the chief worlds was only the first step. He wanted to conquer this entire patch of existence. That would accelerate the primordial world of immortals’ recovery and bring it into the nothing as a portion of true existence.","“Alright, I’ll help you,” the Disordered Empyrean Supreme nodded. “Conquering the chief worlds is an easy task for you now. You don’t even need to do it yourself.”","That was true—Lu Yun’s subordinates were strong enough to accomplish the deed.","“Mmhmm,” he nodded. “So I’m going to the Three Thousand to change the great daos there.”"]},{"number":2104,"title":"Chapter 2104: Chapter 2059: The Overseer Shows Himself","paragraphs":["Chapter 2059: The Overseer Shows Himself","Due to the effect of the Tome of Life and Death, Lu Yun’s cultivation level was beginning to recede. It headed in the direction of Pangu’s original cultivation.","In his current condition, he was on par with a sacred supreme. No one was his match in the Three Thousand—unless the overseer was present.","No, the herd of vicious beasts was also stronger than him.","The Three Thousand was an incredibly mysterious place that resulted in the deaths of even nihil powerhouses. If Lu Yun wished to change its great dao, he had to proceed with caution. For the moment, he remained standing in front of the mountain of blades and watched Jin Huo continue to scale it. Her life was in peril at every moment of her trial.","Whoosh!","A black demonic shadow formed in the air and charged Jin Huo in a cloud of demonic energy.","“Watch out!” The Disordered Empy—Sacred Supreme rushed to help Jin Huo.","“Don’t move.” Lu Yun stopped her. “Only she can do the deed. If we take action, the tree god will forever be trapped on the mountain.”","Jin Huo swiftly died, then immediately came back to life. She ignored the demonic shadow and continued clambering over the blades.","The demonic shadow struck again and again, killing Jin Huo again and again. Lu Yun’s stock of Resurrection Talismans was soon depleted. He waved another nine thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine talismans into her.","“ROAR!!” snarled the demonic shadow. It dove from the mountain and flung itself at Lu Yun. Plainly, it possessed intelligence and wasn’t a dead being.","“I wouldn’t be able to do anything to you if you didn’t come down. But look at this, you’re the one presenting yourself to me!” Lu Yun gave a long peal of laughter and pointed at the shadow, activating the Judgment of Life or Death.","Whoosh!","The retribution infested shadow instantly flew apart.","Most of the existences imprisoned here carried overwhelming retribution, making them as weak as paper in Lu Yun’s eyes. It was why very few nihil powerhouses had dared show themselves after Lu Yun arrived. They’d witnessed how his death art worked and understood how the Judgment of Life or Death killed people.","The demonic shadow was the guardian of the mountain of blades. Giving Jin Huo the Resurrection Talismans was cheating. Hence, the shadow had flown into a fury and come for the young man.","It would’ve never descended the mountain otherwise.","Jin Huo breathed out with relief and climbed much faster without the shadow’s interference.","Hummmm.","Emerald light flashed over her as she broke through from peak grand supreme to empyrean supreme. She was already the strongest level of peak grand supreme to begin with since she grasped the order of life. After experiencing death again and again on the mountain of blades, her fortuitous opportunity finally arrived and she naturally broke though.","After ascending to empyrean supreme, she bounded to the top of the mountain in one leap and flung her arms around the seated tree god.","Lu Yun relaxed. Everything he’d come to the World Heart for had been accomplished and he’d also managed to overawe the demons suppressed in this region with the Judgment of Life or Death.","“These demons will become demons of the world of immortals in the future. They will counterbalance those already there.” The tree god jumped down from the mountain with Jin Huo in his arms.","“Greetings to the senior,” Lu Yun bowed. The tree god’s replica in the world inside the Tome of Life and Death had grown into a towering specimen. But when the tree god walked down from the mountain, he instantly severed his connection with that tree and his karmic relationship with Ling Weiyang in the world of immortals.","The tree inside the Tome of Life and Death was now a spirit root that wholly belonged to Lu Yun.","“You really did it!” The tree god smiled at Lu Yun. The section of withered wood that he’d left behind carried the resentment of hundreds of millions from the original Hongmeng. He’d meant for it to help Lu Yun light the fire of order.","Lu Yun had fully succeeded and progressed to the step of rescuing the tree god from the mountain of blades!","The mountain of blades was a collection of sword qi from Quietus. It’d transformed into keen blades that killed untold numbers after being tainted by the demonic qi in the World Heart. Whether it was the tree god or Jin Huo, both were restricted by it.","The orders within the World Heart were too strong. No one could break them once they started operating; Jin Huo could dismantle the seal only if she climbed the mountain herself.","During this time, the tree god’s true spirit borrowed Ancestor’s strength to create his own soul parts and become an independent living being that could be separated from Ling Weiyang.","This set Lu Yun at ease. It looked like the dark empyrean supreme really hadn’t lured him and Jin Huo here to do them harm. He really did just want them to rescue him. Having been reborn, he was headed for the Infinite Deorc. The land of darkness would come under the World of Immortals’ banner before long.","With the Disordered Sacred Supreme and the tree god in residence, that also meant that the chief worlds were fully protected. Given that, Lu Yun opened the Gates of the Abyss and left with his people.","The demons imprisoned in the surroundings sagged with relief when the young man left. The Judgment of Life or Death was horrifying; it was as if it’d been made for entities like them.","......","After taking Jin Huo and the others to the World of Immortals, Lu Yun spent a very long time with Qing Yu and the little fox before returning to the Three Thousand. He arrived at Ancestor’s tomb again, but this time with someone else.","Diexi—Ancestor’s dao partner, Forebear.","She brought her empyrean crystal coffin as it held her past self. She’d been wondering who it was inside, but all was apparent now.","While Ancestor’s corpse had become a patch of existence, her body had stayed as a skeleton. Her remains were complete, which meant that she could become Forebear again if she wanted to.","“Forebear,” Jiang Chen greeted Diexi. His layouts of the secondary worlds in the chief worlds had resulted in three hundred and sixty-five Diexis setting up the formation of the corpse kings. It’d been done for her benefit, so that she could call upon her coffin of empyrean crystal.","This matter was also completed, thanks to Lu Yun’s help.","“Jiang Chen.” Diexi frowned slightly. A cold glint flashed through her eyes when she looked at him, an edge that swiftly vanished.","The reaction wasn’t because Jiang Chen had once schemed against her, but that he was a zombie from the nothing and therefore nothing good. He stood guard here for himself, and they’d once been enemies.","Although Diexi didn’t possess the same past as Forebear, her instincts were the same.","“So everyone’s finally assembled!” rang a resonant voice. A faint shadow walked down through the void.","“Dao King!?” Lu Yun’s jaw dropped when he saw the man.","“Not the Dao King,” Jiang Chen frowned. “It’s the overseer.”","“The overseer... looks the same as the Dao King?!” Lu Yun floundered to make some sense of the situation.","It was one thing to have a doppelganger in the world, but for two preeminent personages like the overseer and the Dao King to look exactly the same? That was unbelievable.","“Overseer? I don’t like that title. I am Jin, Che’s older brother.”","Che was the Dao King’s name."]},{"number":2105,"title":"Chapter 2105: Chapter 2060: Mo Yi’s Identity","paragraphs":["Chapter 2060: Mo Yi’s Identity","“What the? Isn’t he supposed to be staying out of sight?” Wariness flashed through Lu Yun’s face as he looked from the overseer to Jiang Chen.","Jiang Chen’s brows were tightly furrowed and a grave expression hung on his ashen face. Numerous Great Formations of Corpse Refinement gathered around him and endless zombies poured forth, as if they were his personal strength.","Hell’s ability to bury the corpses of the living was a contribution from Jiang Chen. What he wielded himself was infinitely stronger than was present in the Abyssal Hell.","Lu Yun drew in a sharp breath to see hordes of zombies amble around Jiang Chen. The zombie’s strength was many times stronger than Unrest! In fact, any of his zombies could beat Unrest to death!","The overseer stood in the void, bathed in a ball of fire. His long black hair began burning as well, turning the color of flames.","“Keep yourself safe. The overseer is born of the first flame of dao that came to be after the appearance of existence. He controls all fires that exist,” Jiang Chen cautioned with utmost gravity.","Lu Yun nodded mutely, despite not sensing any killing intent from the overseer.","“Give it up,” the overseer sighed in a melancholy fashion.","“Give it up?” Lu Yun knew that the words were meant for him. He shook his head lightly. “Success is within reach, why should I give up?”","“Because someone will die if you succeed,” the overseer replied.","“You?” Lu Yun snorted with laughter. Diexi watched the overseer warily while standing by the young man’s side. Her hand was on the empyrean crystal coffin and she communicated with Forebear’s strength inside.","“I won’t die,” the overseer shook his head. “I won’t die even if this existence collapses. I am the undisputed strongest within and without existence. There is nothing within creation that can kill me.”","He lifted his chin, displaying a slightly wan face. He’d plainly suffered uncountable injuries in the past.","“He’s bluffing,” Diexi grumbled.","He glanced at her. “You are well aware of my condition. Who can possibly harm me if I wasn’t preoccupied with suppressing the growth of the great daos of the Three Thousand? You and Ancestor? You two didn’t even measure up to one of my arms in your prime.”","Diexi fell silent. She didn’t know that. She was Diexi, not Forebear.","Lu Yun frowned slightly and looked at Jiang Chen. The Karmic Tree still wasn’t sensing any killing intent, just an... inexplicable emotion toward the young man.","Meanwhile, Jiang Chen kept a wary eye on the overseer. “One person dying compared to all of the living beings within and without nothing and creation. Which would you say is the right decision?” he sneered. “How else would Che agree to do this?”","“Che... the Dao King?” A sudden thought struck Lu Yun. Mo Yi.","Did this have to do with Mo Yi? Was she the person who would die?","An odd feeling developed in Lu Yun’s heart as he looked at the face that was the exact same as the Dao King’s.","“How do you know for certain that Che has agreed to it?” the overseer responded frostily. Killing intent flared in his eyes when he looked at Jiang Chen. “Do you want her to die?” He suddenly switched to Lu Yun.","“You mean Mo Yi, don’t you?” Lu Yun took a deep breath and slowly voiced the name. “Who is she?”","“Who is she?” chuckled the overseer. “Why do you think creation exists in this part of existence? She created it.” He spread out his arms with a smile. “She hewed the nothing into being and bestowed a trace of life into the empty nihil. She bequeathed it inception and manifested ethos. It is she who fashioned everything of creation.","“What is the nihil? Vacant and desolate, there is nothing there. For everything in existence, it is virulent poison. Anything that dares enter is assimilated. Without her, all of you would be long dead.”","Lu Yun gaped at the overseer with shock, not knowing what to say.","“Then who is Mo Yi? Isn’t she existence within nothing?","“Why, why, yes she is. She is born of the nothing and granted a true spirit from the nothing. Her tracks form the river of time and her gaze marks the true nihil.","“Her voice interweaves in the void and transforms the rules of disorder into organized order.” The overseer’s voice rang with conviction, but he grew paler the more he spoke.","“Then why are you suppressing the world that she’s created?” Lu Yun understood the ins and outs of everything now—it seemed likely that even the Tome of Life and Death was from Mo Yi’s hands.","Although the nothing was eternal, it wasn’t unchanging. It also underwent reincarnation, and from its cycles was born Mo Yi.","“If the great daos of the Three Thousand continue to grow without end, they will seep into the nothing and assimilate it. They will turn the nothing into existence. The mistress is the spirit of nothing. When that happens, she will vanish,” the overseer murmured. “I don’t want her to disappear, so I stop this with everything I have.”","That was why he suppressed the great daos of the Three Thousand and prevented them from developing, forcing them to eternally remain in the state of ethos.","Meanwhile, having lost the memories of her past life, Mo Yi didn’t even know who she was. That was because the great daos of the Three Thousand had invaded the nothing and the three hundred and sixty-five nihil powerhouses supported the realm.","The greater the damage to the nothing, the more severe the injuries to Mo Yi.","She’d left her strength in the nothing to balance the scales between nothing and existence. She created the power of nihil so that beings of existence could exceed their plane and enter the nothing.","But living beings were of existence, after all, so although they could enter the nihil, they needed additional strength to support their actions. Thus, they wished to turn all of nothing into existence.","That was when the overseer made his move and expelled all of the creatures in the Three Thousand who’d reached the nihil cultivation level, using his own body to suppress its great daos.","The rest of the circumstances was a well known story.","“The nothing was always meant to eventually transform into existence,” Jiang Chen responded coolly. “You can suppress the Three Thousand, but you are unable to suppress a third existence.”","A first existence had once appeared—the Tome of Life and Death. It’d been refined into a treasure as it developed and later thrown into the river of time.","The Dao King had been behind that.","On the other hand, Ancestor’s body had manifested a realm that would eventually become a third existence in the nothing.","“Is there no way for an outcome of mutual satisfaction?” Lu Yun frowned.","“All living beings have their own desires and no one is content to always remain in the same place,” the overseer shook his head. “Even you are the same. Would you be willing to stay in a world with a great dao that never advances and always remains stagnant?","“Just for the sake of one person?”"]},{"number":2106,"title":"Chapter 2106: Chapter 2061: The Same Person","paragraphs":["Chapter 2061: The Same Person","Could all the great daos of existence be hobbled for the sake of one person?","That person might be very important to the overseer and Dao King, but what did that have to do with everyone else?","They would never allow that to happen!","Even Ancestor and Forebear had constantly tried to breach the overseer’s control and release the great daos held to a state of ethos. It raised the overseer’s attention instead, and he killed both of them.","It really hadn’t been the overseer who’d stabbed Quietus into the World Heart—it’d been the Dao King.","The Dao King had stayed by Mo Yi’s side all this time, trying to find a solution that could satisfy everyone. But when the situation progressed to this point, the next requisite step was for existence to devour the nihil. The Dao King had failed.","This was why the overseer showed himself at this point in time. He wouldn’t allow anyone to harm Mo Yi, even if it took his own life to ensure that.","“One person versus all of existence, how would you chose?” Jiang Chen looked meaningfully at Lu Yun. He’d already made his choice.","“I don’t know...” Lu Yun thought of how Mo Yi had helped him when he was newly come to the world of immortals. She’d stayed by his weak and ignorant side, excavating tombs and digging up burial mounds with him. When the dao immortal of the Qing Clan threatened him, Mo Yi stepped forward and saved his life.","To him, Mo Yi was a friend.","Lu Yun had been alone since childhood and finally made a few friends after coming to the world of immortals. He treasured every single person who had a place in his heart—whether it was Qing Yu, the little fox, or friends such as Mo Yi, Ling Weiyang, and Deixi.","He didn’t want anyone to get hurt, so a decision like this was pure torture.","“Is there really no way for everyone to be happy?” he murmured.","“Yes,” Jiang Chen responded expressionlessly, his heart chilling upon seeing Lu Yun’s reaction. They seemed to have chosen the wrong person.","One should be decisive and resolute for the sake of all existence. Jiang Chen was already disappointed in the young man for waffling and trying to find a so-called solution to satisfy all sides.","“Slaughter everything that lives and destroy existence so that everything begins again,” he said coldly. “When the nothing starts anew and existence is manifested again, that ensures everyone can live. Are you willing to do so?”","Lu Yun frowned, feeling that something was off about this.","“Lu Yun, I know you’re here to change the great daos of the Three Thousand. Only you have the ability to do so and I cannot prevent you from doing so.” The overseer looked calmly at Lu Yun. “But it doesn’t matter anymore. The growth of the realm’s great daos will not affect the mistress. It is the patch of existence that is the greatest threat.”","Lu Yun inclined his head at the overseer, but didn’t say anything.","Jin had said everything that he needed to say. His body faded away, turning into a zombie that fell through the endless void. It wasn’t really his body, just a zombie he’d borrowed to manifest his presence.","Despite that, neither Lu Yun nor Jiang Chen had seen through it.","Jiang Chen looked at Lu Yun with wariness, but didn’t say anything. He walked silently to Ancestor’s coffin of empyrean crystal and sat down cross-legged. This coffin contained all of their hopes.","“What do you think?” Lu Yun looked at Diexi.","“Even zombies can return to yang through yin and become real living beings.” She thought of her own circumstances. She’d been a half-evolved zombie king and slowly progressed to a real being at Lu Yun’s side. She was no longer subject to the constraints of being a zombie.","“If even zombies have a chance of life beneath the heavenly dao, why doesn’t the mistress have this chance?” Being that she was no longer Forebear, she didn’t understand it. She wasn’t Changxi either, she was just Diexi.","“I see,” Lu Yun nodded. He realized why the overseer had shown himself—not to kill Lu Yun, but to drive a rift between him and those he was traveling with.","By now, everyone was aware that he was the crux to whether or not the primordial world of immortals could ascend to the nothing and became a third patch of existence. If he hesitated, there would be those who went on guard against him and perhaps even took action against him.","If that came to be, then it wouldn’t need the overseer’s hand to ensure the collapse of a perfectly operating plan.","The overseer was also right with what he said. He and the Dao King both wanted to protect Mo Yi, the spirit born of the nothing who was on par with a creator. No wonder everyone concealed her identity from him.","If he’d known everything earlier, he wouldn’t have let things progress to this step.","“The Dao King.” Lu Yun suddenly thought of the man in question. The Dao King had died for Mo Yi thirty-three times in the Land of Reincarnation and she had died for Lu Yun. “Is he the creator of the Tome of Life and Death?”","He stood at the core of Ancestor’s tomb and carefully thought through everything.","“The Dao King truly cares for Mo Yi, so he won’t let Mo Yi just die in front of him. The cycles loop in the Land of Reincarnation, so he knows that she will continuously revive. Many important parts of this plot were completed with his hand. He wouldn’t do so if Mo Yi really would die as a result.","“Does this mean that he’s found a way?” He opened his mental eyes and closely observed the internal world of the Tome of Life and Death.","Order was abundant here and it’d evolved to the level of the Three Thousand after the treasure’s third transformation. If this world entered the nothing, it would immediately transform into a patch of real existence that rivaled the Three Thousand.","But the Dao King seemed to have never heard nor seen the treasure before.","“Don’t worry, there is always a ray of hope. There’s a saying on Earth that we can cross the bridge when we come to it, that a way always presents itself,” Diexi comforted upon seeing Lu Yun’s expression.","“I’m actually thinking of another possibility.” Lu Yun stroked his chin and looked meaningfully at the silent Jiang Chen. “Perhaps some people’s goal isn’t to turn the nothing into existence, but to eliminate the mistress.”","Jiang Chen shook.","“Looks like I’m right,” Lu Yun smiled. “C’mon, let’s go to the Three Thousand.”","He and Diexi vanished in the void. With the Gates of the Abyss, he could go anywhere he wished in the Three Thousand.","Confusion flashed through Jiang Chen’s eyes when he opened them.","“The mistress sacrificed herself for all of creation and forcefully propelled the great daos of the Three Thousand forward. She wanted to transform the nothing into existence, but Che stopped her,” he murmured. “There’s one great benefit to living long enough. There’s probably no one else who knows that the so-called Dao King and overseer are the same person.”"]},{"number":2107,"title":"Chapter 2107: Chapter 2062: Source of Trouble","paragraphs":["Chapter 2062: Source of Trouble","Sacred Radiance Nation was a land in which immortal dao thrived and reigned supreme. Though it hadn’t reached the level of affecting the Three Thousand’s great daos yet, it was of significant scale in the realm.","Oddly enough, the Northern and Western Sacred Palaces were unmoved that such a cultivation faction had appeared between them.","Lu Yun stood in the void over Sacred Radiance Nation and quietly assessed its development.","“Is this the immortal nation that you’ve established in this world?” Diexi put away the empyrean crystal coffin and stood by Lu Yun’s side, looking curiously at the kingdom beneath them.","It hadn’t been long since Sacred Radiance Nation started developing from the humble tribe it’d once been, but the world and great daos of the Three Thousand were so strong that supremes already walked through the land. Credit didn’t go to the Disordered Sacred Supreme—someone was secretly supporting the faction from the shadows.","“Actually... the Dao King and the overseer are the same person,” Lu Yun suddenly murmured. “My presence here and establishing the Sacred Radiance Nation is all by his will. I hadn’t known it at first—I only thought through everything when he came out to meet me.”","The one who stayed by Mo Yi’s side was the Dao King’s primary body. The overseer was his replica. It was the Dao King who’d killed Ancestor by plunging Quietus into his heart. He was also the one who manifested the scene at the World Heart. Everything was under his control the entire time, proceeding in an orderly fashion according to plan.","Lu Yun was reminded of Violetgrave.","She’d once borrowed the power of the Netherdark Hell to split herself into two. Violetgrave was the primary body and Bluegrave her replica. It was the exact situation that they found with the Dao King now.","The current Violetgrave was a result of the Dao King entering the Land of Reincarnation and melding the Netherdark Hell together.","“So have you found a way to satisfy all parties?” Lu Yun suddenly raised his head and looked to the horizon.","The overseer appeared once again and nodded. “I have.”","“So those people’s goal isn’t to transform the nothing into existence, after all. They just want to kill Mo Yi, don’t they?” Lu Yun asked.","“Yes,” the overseer nodded. “The way was always there, but they didn’t care. They just wanted to kill her.”","Mo Yi was a spirit born of the nothing, the first goddess. Her trails became the river of time and her gaze was time.","“They’re also using Ancestor and Forebear as their pawns. Do you think the three hundred and sixty-five major cycle existences are really to balance the great daos of this world?” the overseer asked.","“Are they not?” Lu Yun furrowed his brows and cast a critical glance at the boundless void overhead. Three hundred and sixty-five existences were tightly interlocked around the Three Thousand. With the overseer’s question in mind, he shuddered as he realized a critical detail.","These three hundred and sixty-five were more like enormous parasites, furiously absorbing the nutrients of the Three Thousand!","At this rate, the realm would wither away one day.","“What... the... what is going on here??” Lu Yun gasped.","“Your book is the first patch of existence. It didn’t evolve into a realm like the Three Thousand because of them.” The overseer sighed as he looked overhead. “Those three hundred and sixty-five demon gods are the first demon gods to be born in the nothing. They are older than Ancestor and Forebear. Their strength is unparalleled compared to those who enter the nothing from existence in modern times.","“Everyone you know, Hongjun, Pangu, the Three Pure Ones, Leize, Fuxi, Huaxu, and Wahuang shares the same origins. These three hundred and sixty-five are the real enemy of life.” The overseer enunciated carefully as he looked at Lu Yun. “They can only exist in the nothing and cannot enter existence. Once the nothing transforms into existence, they will die!”","“What about Mo Yi?” Lu Yun paused.","“The mistress... will also die,” the overseer shook her head. “But she has lived nine thousand lives in the Land of Reincarnation and continuously weathered tribulation after tribulation. She has long severed her connection to the seed of nothing.","“She will be fine even if the nothing turns into existence.”","“So everything you’ve done...” Lu Yun trembled. The Land of Reincarnation wasn’t a place of rest and recovery for anyone! Neither was it a land of tempering and trial! It was meant to help Mo Yi sever her connection to the nothing!","No wonder, no wonder a variety of reasons had interrupted him from rebuilding a Land of Reincarnation. That goal of his had eventually fallen by the wayside.","“So everything you do now is to eliminate them?” Lu Yun looked up at the three hundred and sixty-five enormous existences.","“Eliminate them? So much easier said than done,” the overseer shook his head. “It’ll fall to you to kill them.”","“Me?” Lu Yun paused again.","“Yes, you,” the overseer nodded. “The first patch of existence is on you and has become your nascent spirit. You are living, breathing existence.","“The final profundity of the nothing is reincarnation. It itself is also reincarnating endlessly without stop. I have borrowed the strength of the first patch of existence to fashion reincarnation into a great dao. It has become your core dao and the strength you command.”","Lu Yun’s cultivation process had been an endless cycle of reincarnation manifesting and perfecting itself. From the five hells to the order of flame and then the formation of reincarnation... Although the Dao King laid the path, reincarnation would’ve still dissolved back into a profundity of nothing without Lu Yun. It wouldn’t be a great dao of existence.","The Dao King, or rather the overseer, was a lighthouse in the sea. He guided Lu Yun to the other shore, but it was up to the young man whether or not he could actually reach it.","Step by step, Lu Yun had reached his destination.","“How am I a match for them as things stand?” Lu Yun smiled ruefully. He believed the overseer without a shadow of a doubt.","The Tome of Life and Death was the source of everything. It wasn’t out of the question for the Dao King to retrieve it at this stage if he wanted to, but he didn’t. He used a variety of ways and methods to spur on Lu Yun from the moment the young man arrived at the Three Thousand, such as the eye and light of great dao.","It forced Lu Yun to continue improving himself and connect with the great dao here so that the world of the Three Thousand would hide the Tome of Life and Death for him.","The treasure had reached its final form upon its third evolution. If the Dao King had other motives in mind and wanted to use Lu Yun’s hand to reach his goal, it was high past time to pull up his net.","But when he appeared for a second time, he severed his connection to the Tome of Life and Death. The treasure was now wholly Lu Yun’s nascent spirit; no one within the nothing or existence could take it from him.","“True, you are no match for them now, but you are still growing. Once you fully control reincarnation, it will be easy to kill them.","“Also, the denizens of the Three Thousand are right. The inhabitants of the three hundred and sixty-five major cycle worlds are really just parasites. There is no meaning or value to their existence. All of their thoughts and nascent spirits are controlled by the demon gods.”"]},{"number":2108,"title":"Chapter 2108: Chapter 2063: Enemy of All Creation","paragraphs":["Chapter 2063: Enemy of All Creation","Lu Yun couldn’t help but tremble violently. He’d viewed the three hundred and sixty-five nihil powerhouses as heroes, marveling at their sacrifice for the greater good. It now looked like that was the furthest thing from the truth.","Few were those that the young man fully trusted. Other than his dao partners and son, there were only Fuxi, Mo Yi, and the Dao King. He didn’t doubt what the Dao King said—or rather, he had no reason to suspect anything the man said. He even knew that the Dao King wouldn’t blame him were he to turn around and leave right this second, taking his people into the world of the Tome of Life and Death and never getting involved in the affairs of existence again.","The man wouldn’t even bother him if he went down that path.","“Alright, I understand,” Lu Yun nodded. “Will we have peace once the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods are dead?”","“In a sense,” the Dao King sighed. “The nihil reveres the three hundred and sixty-five as their gods, so it won’t be that easy to kill them. Remember how there are mortals who do not cultivate in the Three Thousand?”","“Yes, and aren’t the altars they worship your work?” Lu Yun raised a brow.","“Those are altars to the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods... They steal God’s power to reduce him to a mortal state so they can replace him.” The Dao King lifted his eyes to the sky. “God was the strongest powerhouse within and without the nihil. The three hundred and sixty-five demon gods inherited... no, they used his benevolence to steal his power.","“If all three hundred and sixty-five demonic seeds are gathered together, they will possess God’s power. There is nothing that God cannot do, no world he cannot create. Even I am no match for him.”","“But Mo Yi can defeat God?” Lu Yun’s heart skipped a beat.","“Yes, the mistress can defeat God,” the Dao King nodded. “So the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods wish to eliminate her. Her past and identity are strict taboos within the chief worlds and existences outside of it.”","Lu Yun finally understood the situation.","Everyone in the chief worlds seemed to know about Mo Yi, but they were all hesitant to broach the topic with him. It came across as a concerted effort to keep him in the dark, but the real reason was that they were unable to speak of anything regarding Mo Yi due to certain rules.","There were only two real existences in the universe—the Three Thousand and the patch that the chief worlds was part of. The real name of the chief worlds’ patch was the primordial world of immortals.","All other existences were fake and their inhabitants the corpse bugs of dead bodies.","Ancestor had been proceeding according to his original plan when he manifested his existence. His side wanted to create a new existence to replace the Three Thousand so it could grow and occupy all of nothing.","But in reality, they’d been playing into the hands of the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods. Their plans were what the demon gods wished for them to achieve. It wasn’t until Mo Yi was attacked by their wills when she entered the primordial world of immortals that the Dao King realized their true motive.","Occupying the Three Thousand was never their goal. They wanted to kill Mo Yi for her nihil true spirit, just like how they stole God’s power.","Other than Mo Yi personally taking the field, there was another way to kill the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods—have existence expand to the point of devouring the nothing. However, that would entail Mo Yi’s mutual destruction along with the demon gods.","Thus came the Land of Reincarnation.","The Dao King stood in Mo Yi’s place again and again, enduring her tribulations for her until she finally severed her connection to the nothing. She was a true being of existence now. The primordial world of immortals had reached the point of ascending to the nothing, so the Dao King orchestrated its destruction to facilitate everything beginning anew.","Unfortunately, the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods also realized their intentions and began to stir, entering the primordial world of immortals to take things into their own hands.","They injured Mo Yi to the point where she no longer commanded her former strength. If the demon gods continued to awaken and enter the primordial world of immortals, there was no possible outcome for her other than death. The Dao King couldn’t hold them off and neither could God, Pangu, Hongjun and the others. Not to mention, the demon gods commanded armies of nihil powerhouses under their banner.","Even beings such as Jiang Chen and Unrest had unwittingly become one of theirs. Only those within the world of immortals were left in the Dao King’s camp.","There’d been Yun Yi as well, but she’d sacrificed herself to ensure the completion of their plans. Not even her father was trustworthy in her stead.","“Let’s charge into the nothing before they’re fully awake and kill them all!” A crazy light suddenly danced in Lu Yun’s eyes.","“I tried once, but I failed,” the Dao King chuckled ruefully. “How hard is it to destroy an existence, especially considering they’ve become the Major Cycle Worlds of the Three Thousand? They are intricately tied to the realm. Both prosper when one finds glory, both perish when one falls.","“We can kill them only after they awaken and terminate their connection to the Three Thousand.”","It wasn’t due to the Dao King that the Three Thousand didn’t grow, but the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods continuously devouring its core essence. But by now, no one believed anything the Dao King said.","The overseer was the most evil being within the nothing and existence, the enemy of all creation.","“Can’t we do anything before that?” Lu Yun asked subconsciously as his brow furrowed tight.","“Yes!” the Dao King nodded. “Increase our strength so we can kill the demon gods after they awaken!”","Lu Yun lowered his head and quietly operated formula dao.","“If all three hundred and sixty-five awaken at the same time, they will jointly possess the strength of God. What if they awaken one by one?”","“Awaken one by one?” The Dao King looked blankly at the young man.","“They will immediately possess the strength of God if they wake up together. What if we let them wake up one by one? That breaks their collective power and will make it much easier to eliminate them.”","Formula dao operated continuously as it whirred through various possibilities.","“Hahaha!! Tailong was right, you are very suited to be our strategist!” the Dao King roared with laughter. They’d thought of the idea before, but they weren’t able to determine a way to ensure that the demon gods woke up one by one.","“The altars!” Lu Yun raised his head. “There are three hundred and sixty-five major cycle altars hidden in the Three Thousand. That is their core essence! We can use them to dictate who we want to wake!”","His eyes gleamed. “We need your eyes of great dao to investigate. The altars are hidden among the mortals who do not cultivate!","“We’ll need them to give up their faith if we want to completely destroy the demon gods, or they’ll resurrect through the beliefs of the people.”","That was one of God’s methods."]},{"number":2109,"title":"Chapter 2109: Chapter 2064: Demon God","paragraphs":["Chapter 2064: Demon God","Formula dao operated furiously as Lu Yun bent his mind to deriving the roots of the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods. His calculations told him that the Dao King spoke the truth, the man was holding nothing back.","Even now, the Three Thousand was resisting the three hundred and sixty-five Major Cycle Worlds. There should have been Major Cycle Worlds protecting the realm, yes, but they would never be worlds derived from demon gods.","The Three Thousand was an objective existence and thus couldn’t refuse the demon gods, but it could help Lu Yun contend against them. His formula dao gave full expression to its capabilities under the auspices of heavenly dao and easily determined where the three hundred and sixty-five core essence altars were.","“Three hundred and sixty-five dragon points. Three hundred and sixty-five tombs! The demon gods have placed their altars in ancient tombs around the world!” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes and broke out in a large grin. “That’s perfect! My tomb raiding sect is an illustrious faction in the world of immortals and excavating tombs is our bread and butter.","“I’ll have the sect’s disciples come to the Three Thousand and uproot the three hundred and sixty-five tombs! They’ll drag the altars out of the structures!”","Lu Yun didn’t plan on doing the deed himself. Although the demon gods were still asleep, their will had taken note of him. They would be on guard against whatever action he took. It was better to have his tomb raiding disciples accomplish the task!","He’d long since passed on his tomb raiding skills, so it was more than appropriate for his disciples to tackle the mission. What use were his factions if he had to personally accomplish everything himself?","Of course, it was also due to his own laziness and habit of leaving his work for others. If not for Qing Yu and the little fox, he would likely still be fighting alone and have no forces to his name.","The Dao King smiled as well. Nothing was a problem with Lu Yun on the scene.","The Gates of the Abyss swung open with a boom and established a link to the Dao Academy of Mount Xuanhuang in the world of immortals. Tomb raiding disciples poured out of it, setting foot on this unknown world.","Although Lu Yun had given the combined dao of three hells to the Disordered Sacred Supreme, the gates were the treasure of the Tome of Life and Death and thus remained Lu Yun’s. They could even connect to the nothing now. All existences and worlds were potential destinations so long as the young man himself was present within them.","If he wished, he could easily travel to the Major Cycle Worlds that the demon gods had transformed into. But if he did so, he would be traveling to his own doom.","The three hundred and sixty-five demon gods were awakening and those were their personal worlds. If he dared set foot in one, they would instantly kill him and try to find a way to claim the Tome of Life and Death.","With that, the sect of tomb raiders was shifted into the Three Thousand. Qing Yu and the little fox were among them and they dragged Lu Yun off to places unknown as soon as they saw him.","“Young man, everything in moderation!” The Dao King smiled knowingly as he watched them depart.","Lu Yun returned after an indeterminate period of time, wearing lipstick stains on his face and slightly disheveled robes. He coughed awkwardly when he looked at the Dao King.","The man knew nothing. Naturally. Of course.","“Your disciples sure work fast. They’ve learned your style and have already excavated an altar,” the Dao King smirked Lu Yun.","“What fast? It took them a very long time!” Lu Yun protested hotly, feeling that the man was questioning his stamina.","Qing Yu and the little fox blushed hotly while the Dao King remained smiling.","“The demon gods have responded as well,” he changed the topic with a solemn expression. “We are about to have a difficult fight on our hands.”","“The two of you should cultivate in the world of the Tome of Life and Death.” Lu Yun sent his dao partners into the treasure without another word as he also sensed impending danger.","Although they’d done very well to reach empyrean supreme, that level of cultivation was useless in the Three Thousand. They would become his weaknesses instead.","No sooner was that done then countless zombies surged from all directions, announcing the arrival of their enemy. Jiang Chen walked through the void and approached Lu Yun and the Dao King.","“Lu Yun, we trusted you so and poured forth all of our efforts to nurture you. Yet you decide to wallow in the mud with the overseer! Are you going to destroy all of creation for the sake of one woman?” Jiang Chen was present in his zombie form—a ghastly white figure with four heads and eight arms. Two pairs of wings unfurled from his back—this was the true zombie. As the ancestor of all zombies, he’d been born as a zombie.","Yellowish-orange corpse qi flowed from his orifices and he zombified everything in his wake. Trees turned into zombie trees and even the energy of the world metamorphosed into lifeless corpse energy. His cultivation level of a nihil powerhouse was on full display in the Three Thousand.","Color drained from the Dao King’s face; the overseer was just his replica. His primary self was preventing the three hundred and sixty-five from emptying the realm of vitality.","In fact, this was just a replica of a replica that wasn’t even a sacred supreme. THere was nothing he could do but rely on Lu Yun.","Lu Yun threw out a talisman without another word. It turned into tens of millions of talismans that summoned the energy of the realm. Thunder roared and lightning ripped through the sky. It was a Thunder Summons Talisman, one he derived from the Thunder Palmstrike death art.","When the thunder and lightning appeared, Lu Yun employed another death art—Mastery of the Five Elements.","The five connate elements of earth, water, fire, metal, and wood gathered around his body, combining with the sky of thunder and lightning to form the Five Elements Cleansing Thunder. It was a technique on par with a death art!","Zombies were connate demons at their core. Lu Yun’s Five Elements Cleansing Thunder could perfectly counter them.","Zombies keened and wailed as they turned to dust amid the apocalyptic thunder and lightning. Corpse’s eyes turned red as a Blood Sea surged out from him, protecting him from the heavenly discharge.","“I remember—the person who killed me and refined me into a zombie king was you!” Diexi’s eyes shot wide open. Wherever she looked at turned into mountains of zombies and a bloody ocean, just like Corpse’s Blood Sea.","“What a pity that I was one step away from turning you into my replica. I had to go along with the changes in plan.” Mouthfuls of pungent corpsewater drooled out of his mouth when Corpse leered.","“You’re not Corpse!” the Dao King shouted. “You’re one of the three hundred and sixty-five. You’re Feilu!”","“Hahahaha!!” came an answering peal of laughter. “Of course it is me. How else would that brainless old zombie create the Abyssal Hell and populate the existences within nothing with his descendants?","“What a damn pity that you gave hell dao to someone else. I’d be able to turn on you right now if you hadn’t!” Feilu ground his teeth."]},{"number":2110,"title":"Chapter 2110: Chapter 2065 – Diexi and the Diexi Sword","paragraphs":["Lu Yun started and tensed. He had a myriad of ways to restrain his opponent if it was Corpse that he was facing. But it was demon god Feilu, and one of the strongest in the nothing! He was infinitely stronger than someone like Unrest.","Feilu’s form changed from Corpse’s appearance to that of an unknown being. It looked more like a vicious beast than humanoid, which immediately tipped off Lu Yun that the vicious beasts outside sanctuary were likely descendants of demon god bloodline.","The zombies around Feilu transformed into scarlet beasts that snarled and clawed at the air, surrounding their enemy.","Feilu burned with fury to find that hell dao wasn’t with Lu Yun. All of his plans fell short in this second! If the young man still wielded hell dao, then not only could the demon god perfectly negate all of Lu Yun’s moves, but he could also use hell to refine the Three Thousand and accelerate their speed in devouring the realm.","They would even be able to seize reincarnation with hell dao as a springboard. Reincarnation was their true goal as they would be truly undying once they possessed it. They wouldn’t have to worry about the appearance of existence and nothing being devoured by existence.","Mo Yi was a prime example of severing her connection to nothing through endless rounds of reincarnation.","Lu Yun tightened his fists, an uncharacteristically grave expression appearing on his face.","“It’s just a replica and it has to borrow Corpse’s body. You can still use your usual methods to suppress zombies,” Diexi said quietly. “He’s changed his form because he’s afraid that your methods will restrain him. It was this Feilu who killed me.”","“Mm, I understand.” A purple-golden talisman appeared in Lu Yun’s hand. He was deploying the Cleansing Thunder to its utmost, forcing the zombies to cast off their disguises as vicious beasts and fly apart as ash in the wind.","“You’re bluffing, alright!” Lu Yun leapt into the air and sent lightning dancing through the void in a wild frenzy. The Mastery of the Five Elements fashioned the lightning into a massive net that bore down on Feilu.","“Do you know why she said that to you?” the demon god remarked calmly as he watched the young man. “Because I created her.”","“AHHH!!” Diexi screamed as her empyrean crystal coffin exploded. A translucent skeleton walked out of it and became one with her.","She still looked like Diexi, but there was no human emotion in her eyes anymore. She raised her hand and slammed it down on Lu Yun’s back.","Diexi was a pawn that Feilu had placed long ago!","Completely caught off guard, there was nothing Lu Yun could do but take the blow. He spat out a mouthful of blood.","“Die!” she rasped with blood-red eyes. She chased down a defenseless Lu Yun as he’d never imagined that she’d attack him, so he’d never been on guard against her.","Hummm.","A loud hum burst from her body as a sword flitted out like a butterfly, suppressing her actions.","Read this novel and other amazing translated novels from the original source at the \"\"","“Do you know why she’s called Diexi?” sighed the Dao King. Three hundred-sixty more swords fluttered out of her body with a light wave of his hand. Incandescent radiance enveloped her, calming the berserk Diexi.","“Would l let such an important person be ripped out of my grasp?” he chuckled.","“You!!” Feilu choked. Diexi’s first blow had also broken Lu Yun’s Cleansing Thunder, leaving the demon god completely unharmed.","Despite the unexpected, the demon god remained composed. The two were playing a game of chess. After he set down one piece, the Dao King responded and set down one of his own.","Thousands of beasts in the Three Thousand howled when Feilu waved his hand. They flung themselves against sanctuary’s boundary and rushed Lu Yun and the Dao King. All of them were nihil powerhouses and raised incredible pandemonium throughout sanctuary. People fled for their lives, but the vicious beasts weren’t interested in them.","Lu Yun was their only goal.","“Be careful, the beasts aren’t the only part of his plan, he has more up his sleeve!” the Dao King quickly warned.","“More? Just those beasts alone can tear me to pieces!” Lu Yun forced out through grit teeth.","“They won’t reach you, not with me around,” the Dao King frowned. “But I need to expel Feilu’s will from Forebear’s body, so be careful.”","A second Dao King appeared with a flash of white light, ripping apart countless beasts.","Another Dao King!","This one wore all white and wielded a blade of white. The keen edge of yang metal sparkled over him.","“You...” Lu Yun blinked.","“A replica of my replica, it won’t hold out for long. You need to undo the will holding sway over Diexi,” the white-robed Dao King snapped out. The primary replica in red had vanished. The white robed version of him split into numerous copies of himself to duel Feilu and the vicious beasts.","He’d said that he couldn’t help prior to this because once he brought his full strength to bear, this replica would disintegrate. Only his replica fighting the demon gods would remain—he would never be able to set foot in this world to guide Lu Yun.","“Understood!” Lu Yun rushed to Diexi’s side and observed her closely.","Three hundred and sixty-five Diexi swords fluttered around her like butterflies. Forebear had first turned into Changxi before she became Diexi, and she’d become Diexi because of this sword. These swords were personally forged by the Dao King through three hundred and sixty-five reincarnation loops. They were meant to suppress the will of Feilu inside her.","The Dao King hadn’t created her and didn’t know that Corpse was Feilu. He just hadn’t trusted Corpse.","Instead of immediately taking action, Lu Yun operated formula dao to calculate everything in front of him.","“I see!” he smiled. “It’s just an old zombie in front of us, the real Diexi is transformed from the sword. The three hundred and sixty-five swords are her primary body!","“The Dao King collected the fragments of Forebear’s soul to seal it in the swords. if I break the swords to release her soul, I’ll be able to expel Feilu’s will!”","Diexi’s first thoughts had come from the sword."]},{"number":2111,"title":"Chapter 2111: Chapter 2066 – Start With Feilu","paragraphs":["Whoosh!","White flames ignited in the middle of Lu Yun’s palm—the fire of reincarnation. With the strength of at its peak, the flames it released could split into the six domineering hellfires and any connate fire.","The Diexi swords suppressed Diexi, so Lu Yun would use the fire of reincarnation to refine the swords. Each one that was refined meant a weakening of the will that belonged to Feilu. When enough of them were destroyed, Diexi would be freed from his control.","Forebear’s fragmented soul in the Diexi swords had long grown to unparalleled heights. Once she was reborn, her strength would far eclipse what it was in her former life and she would be capable of defeating a demon god by herself.","This was also part of the Dao King’s plans.","On the other side, the Dao King grappled with Feilu. Rampaging energy of yang metal flourished around his thousands of replicas as he slayed vicious beast after vicious beast. The five sacred palaces rose from their territory at the same time to travel to this locale.","Three hundred and sixty-five eyes of great dao flared with the light of great dao, deploying beams that were thousands of times stronger than when they hunted Lu Yun. Not even nihil level beasts could withstand them.","The Dao King was fully deploying all of the power that he could bring to bear in his current condition. After today, the only trace of him left in the Three Thousand would be the replica that contended again the demon goods in the void.","Even the five sacred palaces might eventually slip out of his grasp, but there was no other choice available when the situation progressed to this point.","Lu Yun was similarly calling upon his full strength. The Tome of Life and Death manifested over his head and blazing flames of reincarnation set his entire body on fire. Diexi swords were continuously refined, releasing fragments of Forebear’s soul.","The soul fragments were as if the swords. Corpse King Diexi howled and snarled, wanting to break free of Diexi’s suppression, but Feilu’s will was being eroded away by Forebear’s soul. The bloody light in Diexi’s eyes began to recede.","ROAR!","A tremendous roar came from beneath the earth and a hand covered in scales poked out of the soil, grabbing at the preoccupied Lu Yun.","A nihil level vicious beast!","It’d dived beneath the ground to bypass the Dao King’s blockade and appear beneath Lu Yun’s feet. The sudden attack caught the young man off guard, leaving him no time to react.","Boom!","Diexi’s eyes shot open and she gently pressed her hand down. An enormous gust of sword qi blasted from her hand and pulverized the beast.","“My thanks, you can leave the rest to me.” Diexi smiled at Lu Yun and gently waved her hand, crushing the remaining one hundred swords that were yet to be refined. One hundred strands of soul drifted into her body.","The reborn Forebear was still called Diexi and went by the sword for her name. She carried the keen light of the Diexi sword and her lethal strength was more pronounced than before.","“Fellow daoist, leave this scene to me.” She threw her head back with laughter. “I will protect the Three Thousand from now on!”","Humm!","A massive sword drifted through the air like a butterfly, sweeping through everything and churning one hundred million vicious beasts into bits of blood and gore.","“I was too merciful before and didn’t hunt you beasts down despite knowing that you were demonic god bloodline. I will not make the same mistake again!” Diexi flew at Feilu.","A quick look at will leave you more fulfilled.","“If I could kill you once, I can kill you twice!” snarled Feilu at seeing his bloodline being slaughtered. He spread his eight arms open, each of them wielded a weapon. These were weapons formed from the excess of energy when existence manifested in the nothing. They were true connate treasures and shared the same root as heaven and earth.","The Three Thousand trembled when the weapons appeared—Feilu’s replica had once used them to kill Forebear!","“I leave this in your heads, fellow daoist.” The Dao King raised a cupped fist salute to Diexi as his replica of pure yang metal dissolved, turning into the sharpest of energy that filtered into her sword.","That doubled the Diexi sword’s strength. Lu Yun had retreated as far away as he could; this wasn’t a battle that someone of his cultivation level could observe. Its ripples alone would obliterate him if he drew near.","Boom!","The entire realm shuddered as the strain from the two clashing was too much. The five sacred palaces had also withdrawn to their territories to reinforce the world.","“The current Three Thousand cannot endure our strength. We fight in the void!” Feilu whistled and jumped upward, vanishing into the air.","Diexi glanced in Lu Yun’s direction before following the demon god.","Feilu didn’t want to destroy the realm at this time as he wanted the Three Thousand’s energy. Diexi was even more unwilling to harm this world.","“So that’s a nihil powerhouse, huh? I’m still too green,” Lu Yun smacked his lips. “I can dominate any heavyweight beneath nihil, but one of those great personages can crush me with a finger. Good thing I didn’t really suffer any losses this time.”","He tilted his head back to look into the nothing. He could tell that Feilu, in the borrowed replica of Corpse, was no match for a Diexi at peak strength. His eight connate weapons wouldn’t change that fact either. The Dao King dismantling his replica into the energy of yang metal had reinforced the Diexi sword to the point of restricting the eight weapons.","He didn’t need to calculate the situation to know that Feilu’s replica was doomed. In fact, the demon god had voluntarily gone back to the nothing likely because he wanted to injure Forebear as much as possible before his replica was destroyed.","Calm returned to the Three Thousand. While Diexi had slaughtered one hundred million vicious beasts with a single stroke, it was just the tip of the iceberg for the vicious beasts.","Sanctuary was still sanctuary and the prohibited zones were still off limits.","Disciples of the tomb raider sect had located all three hundred and sixty-five altars. Lu Yun firmly remained out of the matter, permitting the Dao Academy’s disciples to fully rely on their own abilities.","Naturally, there were many casualties during the process as the Three Thousand was more dangerous than the world of immortals. However, the tomb raiders were as if wild horses freed from their reins after arriving in this realm. Everything was fresh, exciting, and no ancient tomb went unturned.","More importantly was that they loved to share dao and eventually convinced swathes of mortals to cultivate after prolonged persuasion. Immortal dao blossomed in the Three Thousand.","Diexi returned from the nothing after three years. Feilu’s replica was dead, but she was also heavily injured. However, since Lu Yun had fully mastered the Tome of Life and Death, this level of harm didn’t mean anything to her.","She would fully recover after some time in the inner world of the Tome of Life and Death.","“When do we start killing demon gods?” she asked eagerly when she saw Lu Yun.","“We can start with Feilu.” The young man had identified which altar belonged to the demon god. Feilu’s primary body would be affected by the demise of his replica, so he should currently be at his weakest.","“But I need to increase my strength a bit more...” Lu Yun stroked his chin. “Although the Tome of Life and Death has finished evolving, it’s just returned to what it should be. My connection to it ought to continue to improve as well.”"]},{"number":2112,"title":"Chapter 2112: Chapter 2067 – A Page of Gold","paragraphs":["The Tome of Life and Death had reached its final form, but that was what it should’ve been in the first place. Based on Lu Yun’s thoughts, the treasure should continue evolving after it became one with him.","The times continuously progressed, developed, and he was the vanguard of the era. The treasure’s current final form should not be the Tome of Life and Death’s terminal destination. At this moment, it was most similar to the first patch of existence that came to be.","However, the worlds themselves also continued to improve.","Lu Yun sat down cross-legged in the void and silently used formula dao to analyze his treasure. The Three Brushes of Reincarnation abruptly appeared by his side and traced something through the air.","Search \"\" for the original.","The young man remained unaware of that development.","Their brushes flowed with blood-like ink that swiftly dyed the area a bright red. Lu Yun also entered a strange mental state.","......","Lu Yun meditated for three thousand years, not twitching a single muscle during this time. The past Sacred Radiance tribe had grown from a nation into a dynasty.","It was an immortal dynasty that conquered all nations.","Too many mortal tribes to count surrendered to them over the years. Sacred Radiance destroyed the altars of every tribe they conquered and demonstrated impressive immortal dao capabilities, forcing their new subjects to cultivate immortal dao.","Immortal dao began to take root and spread throughout the Three Thousand, thereby affecting its great daos.","However, the stifled great daos of the world weren’t due to the Dao King. That was a result of the demon gods devouring the realm’s strength. Thus, when immortal dao became part of the world’s great daos, it was also absorbed by the demon gods.","When immortal dao grew to the point of replacing the local great daos, that would turn the demon gods into terrifying demons of immortal dao.","Under Lu Yun’s leadership, immortal dao walked at the forefront of all great daos within nihil and existence. It was the most advanced dao of the times and the demon gods represented rotten decrepitude—they were unholy obstacles that prevented time from advancing.","The consequences would be unimaginable if they devoured immortal dao.","But the immortal dao of the Three Thousand was so weak that it was immediately assimilated by the realm’s great daos upon being incorporated. The demon gods couldn’t isolate it for specific attention, but the first of them to awaken—Feilu—understood the dao’s marvelous uses. He immediately waged war to seize control of it.","Although his primary body was still asleep, part of his will had awoken. He used his altar to communicate with the human tribes that’d yet to be conquered and also reached out to the vicious beasts outside of sanctuary. The two sides joined hands to raise the banner of war throughout sanctuary.","None of the five sacred palaces were spared. Since the Dao King could no longer send a replica to reinforce them, the only one they could rely on was Diexi.","And yet, she didn’t dare act rashly in the face of an overwhelming horde of beasts. She could only intimidate and awe them into staying out of sanctuary. If any crossed the boundary, she destroyed its entire bloodline in retaliation.","Being direct blood descendants of the demon gods, each species was incredibly precious. When eighteen went extinct, nearly all of the slumbering demon gods awoke ahead of time.","The vicious beasts weren’t intelligent, but part of Feilu’s will was present in them. Thus, the beasts changed tack and coordinated with the mortal tribes, sending empyrean and sacred level beasts to invade sanctuary.","Diexi would not take action so long as nihil level beasts remained out of the territory. If she destroyed the lesser vicious beasts as well, then Feilu would undoubtedly bring another part of his plans to bear.","Their target was the Sacred Radiance Immortal Dynasty, not the world of cultivators under sacred palace rule. With vicious beasts as mounts, human mortals charged through Sacred Radiance territory, trampling endless numbers of immortals to death.","They were met in turn by advanced weaponry that Dao Academy disciples transported from the world of immortals—weapons of war and fortress ships!","These days, the civilization of immortal dao thrived and prospered immensely. Thanks to formula dao, the World of Immortals was a cornucopia of supplemental dao treasures and immortal weapons. Modern iterations of the weapons of war could almost kill empyrean supremes with a single blast!","This was the realm’s greatest accomplishment over the past three thousand years.","Although formula dao traversed the chief worlds as the medium of supplemental dao, the chief worlds also bent to the knee to the World of Immortals. All resistance was vanquished by the latter’s armies.","The World of Immortals had set its sights on the primordial world of immortals at first and was gradually shifting its focus to that world. Now that Lu Yun knew the truth behind the primordial world of immortals, however, he was in much less of a hurry.","Strengthening himself and fighting the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods was the crucial matter at hand. Forging forward in the face of hardships and waging war was the fastest method.","After the World of Immortals conquered the chief worlds, it used the Infinite Deorc as a springboard to declare war on all other realms.","Contemporary immortals were peerless and unmatched. There was no sign of their historic faltering and cowardice to be found. Whether it was immortal dao itself or the numerous treasures derived from the calculations of formula dao, everything was the strongest of the age.","The Three Thousand was the latest battlefield. Lu Qing came striding through the realms and took command of Sacred Radiance, becoming the only liege lord of the dynasty. He was an empyrean supreme now and the foremost among the World of Immortals.","The Three Pure Ones also arrived. While they hadn’t recovered to their prime, they’d all set foot into the nothing and were hidden within Sacred Radiance, ready to deliver fatal blows should the opportunity present itself.","The three hundred and sixty-five demon gods were heroes of the nothing. They’d voluntarily sacrificed their bodies so that living beings might have other chances of survival. Within the nothing, it was the overseer of the Three Thousand who was the demon.","Powerhouses of the nihil populated the battlefield. They searched for Lu Yun, wanting to enact vengeance on their greatest traitor. Fuxi, Wahuang, Leize, and Huaxu were also ambushed in realms removed. Lu Yun’s betrayal certainly had something to do with them!","Perhaps some on the demon gods’ side knew the truth, but since they’d already thrown their lot in with the demon gods, there was no turning back. Perhaps that “some” included Corpse and Unrest.","......","Lu Yun sat cross-legged in the void as the bloody light around him gradually subsided. The Tome of Life and Death turned into a thin sheet of golden paper that melded into his body.","“A page of gold? The heck is this?” He blinked. “I thought it would evolve into a computer or smartphone, but... a piece of gold?”","Electronic books came to replace paper books nEarth as more people liked to read on their phones. Hence, Lu Yun thought the Tome of Life and Death would follow that line of progression.","“Found you,” an excited voice echoed at his ear while Lu Yun stared off into space. “Die!!”","It was a nihil powerhouse; he punched Lu Yun’s head the moment he appeared."]},{"number":2113,"title":"Chapter 2113: Chapter 2068 – Horse-Face","paragraphs":["“Are you sure you’re the one who’s found me?” Lu Yun easily dodged the fatal blow with aplomb. He turned around to regard the nihil powerhouse with a faint smile.","“What?” The powerhouse’s face shifted with surprise and he hastily backed up, but discovered that the air around him had thickened with viscosity. He was like a beast caught in a swamp and sank in further the more he struggled.","The nihil powerhouse was humanoid, but equipped with a horse’s face and hooves.","“I already have the Yama Kings in my kingdom of hell and Infernum soldiers... but if I want to build a reincarnation system, I’ll need Ox-Head and Horse-Face to guide souls to my kingdom, as well as Black and White Impermanence, and judges,” Lu Yun murmured to himself as he stroked his chin. Although he’d given hell dao to the Disordered Sacred Supreme, he still governed the kingdom of hell. [1]","It was easy for Lu Yun to create a reincarnation system since he wielded its power, but a certain degree of pomp and circumstance was required in all matters. Although the god of Mount Tai had created half-baked hells and reincarnation, the formality of his creations elevated them to greater heights than they were worth.","A quick look at \"\" will leave you more fulfilled.","Lu Yun was too lazy to come up with anything original, so borrowing from established mythology was just as well. More importantly was that he knew what his future path should be after the Tome of Life and Death transformed into a golden page.","He needed to build a reincarnation system, establish a world of reincarnation, and transform the entire nothing into that world!","He had to fill nihil with reincarnation!","That was the ultimate meaning behind this power—that all of creation, including the nothing, should be overseen by order and become a paradise for life.","Lu Yun couldn’t accomplish this goal by himself with his current capabilities. He needed helpers to craft a complete reincarnation system, advancing it from a minor cycle to a major cycle, and finally a cycle that spanned the nothing.","Therefore, the horse-faced man in front of him would be his Horse-Face.","“I give you two choices.” Lu Yun kicked the mighty nihil powerhouse to the ground with one gesture and stepped on the man. “One, turn yourself into dust this very moment and doom yourself for eternity. Two, become my subordinate.","“Choose.”","The horse-faced man gaped. He couldn’t understand what was happening. He was one of the strongest in the nothing, someone on par with Corpse! How could Lu Yun, an ant yet to reach nihil, so easily stomp on him like this??","What was going on?!","When did sacred supremes become so strong??","The nihil powerhouse looked blankly at the young man and forgot to reply, given the depths of his shock.","Smack!","Lu Yun delivered a ringing slap, shocking the heavyweight back to his senses.","“Well? Which do you choose?” he frowned.","“This seat is a nihil powerhouse who has reigned supreme for countless eons. How would this seat ever bow to a mere sacred supreme?? Death would be preferable to disgrace!” the man shouted.","“Oh yeah?” Lu Yun waved his hand and summoned a tiny light that glittered on his fingertips—the Tome of Life and Death.","“...I chose the second!” the horse-faced man declared self-righteously. “Greetings to the master!”","Lu Yun: ......","“If master finds it comfortable to step on this humble one like this, then please continue stepping on this lowly one!”","Lu Yun sent a ray of energy into the man and baptized him with the power of reincarnation. A hint of tameness appeared on the horse face. Lu Yun no longer needed to physically write names into the Tome of Life and Death anymore.","He withdrew his foot and nodded. “I don’t care what your name was before, you’re called Horse-Face now.”","“Horse-Face greets the master! May master reign for tens of thousands of years and conquer the Three Thousand!” Horse-Face cried out.","“...I think you should be called Ass-Kisser instead.” Lu Yun blinked. Was this the self-worth that a nihil powerhouse should be displaying?","“Ass-Kisser greets the master! May master reign for tens of thousands of years and conquer the Three Thousand!” Horse-Face fell to his knees again.","Lu Yun rubbed his forehead and understood the situation a bit more once he gave it some thought. Conditions in the nothing were harrowing and danger constantly present. The most dangerous wasn’t even their environment, but the peers around them. There was nothing in the nihil, absolutely nothing to be found, so if one wanted to survive and grow, one had to seize by force.","Thus, these nihil powerhouses would seek to live on at all costs. What was dignity and self-worth good for in the face of survival? Those were follies to be displayed to the weak or others of the same level.","Pursuing dignity in front of someone stronger was to throw one’s life away. Thus, the horse-faced man wasn’t someone who changed with the wind. He was just someone who wanted to live.","“Forget it, your name is still Horse-Face.” Lu Yun rubbed his temples. “Alright, come with me to the Three Thousand.”","Conflict raged in the realm, not just between vicious beasts and human tribes, but also a few cultivation sects under demon god control.","Sanctuary was no longer sanctuary, but a war zone. The fires of battle engulfed the land, dragging mortals and cultivators alike into combat. No one could stay out of it.","Diexi forestalled nihil level beasts from entering sanctuary, but the nihil powerhouses who’d flocked to the demon gods and thought they were on the side of good surged in.","The five sacred palaces joined the fray, their leaders able to employ the strength of nothing when they utilized their sacred palaces. They could meet the enemy toe-to-toe!","But there were too many to contend with. If it wasn’t for the invaders worried about destroying sanctuary if they used too much force, the sacred palaces and Sacred Radiance would’ve fallen long ago.","The Eastern Sacred Supreme held off four nihil powerhouses by himself. He would long be dead if it wasn’t for his sacred palace. As it were, he was drenched in blood and teetered on the edge of collapse.","His four colleagues were no better off and defeat seemed imminent.","Four longswords descended with a formation diagram in the nick of time and landed around the Eastern Sacred Supreme. Sword qi radiated outward and sectioned the four nihil powerhouses attacking him.","A young man with straight brows lifting upward came singing through the void, flicking of his red robes.","“Hahaha, hahaha!! This is nice, I haven’t killed people like this in a long time!” Daoist Yuyu roared with laughter and swigged from the wine gourd at his waist. Thus fortified, he laid around with his swords.","“Ge Long!” Lu Yun was hopping mad at seeing Daoist Yuyu execute four nihil powerhouses with no forewarning.","“Eh? Oh, Lu Yun! You’ve come out of seclusion?” Daoist Yuyu involuntarily shrank in on himself when he saw the young man. Since he’d once been Ge Long, he bore an inexplicable trace of respect toward Lu Yun.","“Just cripple them, don’t kill them!” Lu Yun chuckled ruefully and dismissed his annoyance. “I need helpers, so I want to take these nihil powerhouses if I can. We can kill them if I can’t recruit them.”","1. Ox-Head and Horse-Face are two guardians of the underworld in Chinese mythology. Black and White Impermanence are two deities in charge of escorting the spirits of the dead to the underworld. As their names suggest, they are respectively dressed in black and white. ?"]},{"number":2114,"title":"Chapter 2114: Chapter 2069 – Counter Attacking the Vicious Beasts","paragraphs":["Daoist Yuyu had executed four nihil powerhouses like he was chopping cabbage. Lu Yun wasn’t dissatisfied that he’d saved the Eastern Sacred Supreme, but the young man did find it a bit of a pity.","While the four didn’t measure up to Horse-Face, they could be Infernum bosses. Nihil level Infernum would be able to keep things in good order in the kingdom of hell. The four of them had rivaled Unrest!","Unrest had sent only a sliver of his replica into the chief worlds, yet that proved sufficient to eliminate everyone who opposed him and resolve every danger. Just a wisp of nothing had made the empyrean supremes draw back fearfully and refrain from setting a toe out of line.","Of course, there were thousands upon thousands of nihil powerhouses on the battlefield. There was no need for Lu Yun to pick a fight with Daoist Yuyu for a few insignificant small fry.","The daoist had plainly recovered his full strength and found his true self again. He was a heavyweight in the nothing and had thoroughly severed his karmic ties to the past Ge Long.","Daoist Yuyu was now the worst possible candidate if Lu Yun wanted nihil cannon fodder who was unafraid of death and willing to get their hands dirty.","The daoist understood Lu Yun’s intentions and struck out proactively. After killing another three, he managed to capture a nihil powerhouse alive.","The being looked a bit strange—like an octopus—but Lu Yun used the power of reincarnation to turn him into a man with a cow’s face. He named his newest recruit Ox-Head. That completed the Grim Reapers of his kingdom of hell. Ox-Head and Horse-Face were in residence. As for Black and White Impermanence... he could fill in their ranks later.","Daoist Yuyu’s sudden arrival changed the battlefront. Of the dozen nihil powerhouses in the area, seven were dead. The remaining fled after one of them was captured alive; they recognized the infamous Daoist Yuyu. If they continued to linger, they would either die or be taken alive.","If it wasn’t for the daoist not wanting to harm innocents, he would have set up his sword formation and annihilated everyone from the start.","“Well, it’s a good thing they ran.” Lu Yun smiled at Daoist Yuyu. “This means that those guys in the nihil will know you’re back. They won’t easily set foot here anymore.”","“I am notorious and of ill-repute throughout the nothing. Aren’t you afraid that I’ll ruin your reputation?” Daoist Yuyu harrumphed.","“I’ve become the biggest traitor to them and the second most evil being there is. What reputation do I have left?” Lu Yun chuckled indifferently.","The beings within the nothing had been brainwashed by the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods to the point of revering the demon gods as their heroes and the overseer as the demon. They hadn’t thought much of Lu Yun’s development at first, nor had they bothered to intervene. But one day, someone said that the second patch of existence—an unfettered realm—was about to enter the nothing to replace the Three Thousand. That abruptly made Lu Yun their savior.","The nothing was vacant and devoid of everything. Even though nihil powerhouses could survive in such an environment, no one liked to live in such circumstances. Thus, they greeted the appearance of a second existence with great anticipation. They were ready to rush in as soon as it appeared and seize the first mover’s advantage.","But Lu Yun abruptly submitted to the overseer of the Three Thousand and the second existence was negated before it could fully form! Wrath and hatred boiled over from the hopeful masses.","Lu Yun had betrayed all life and lowered himself to collude with the demon that would destroy the realms and all life. Lu Yun was a traitor!","He hadn’t just betrayed them, but creation itself! He was the greatest traitor of the nothing and of existence!","Of course, these words came from the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods. As their fans, the nihil powerhouses from the Three Thousand believed them without any doubt. Lu Yun’s foulness exceeded Daoist Yuyu’s!","The daoist shifted slightly to the side upon hearing all this, drawing clear boundaries between himself and the young man.","Lu Yun aimed a kick at him, whereupon the two burst into laughter.","“Dad, something’s gone horribly wrong.” A profusely sweating Lu Qing approached the two.","“What is it?” Lu Yun frowned.","“Eighteen out of the three hundred and sixty-five altars have been destroyed, but the rest have been seized by someone,” Lu Qing admitted with an unpleasant tone.","Attacking and occupying sanctuary wasn’t the vicious beasts’ primary goal. They wanted the altars. The altars could awaken the sleeping demon gods. If all three hundred and sixty-five acted in concert, they would be invincible within the nothing.","But if they appeared one by one, they were at most slightly stronger than Daoist Yuyu. Just the Three Purities could jointly kill a demon god!","“That doesn’t matter,” Daoist Yuyu said. “There were more than three hundred and sixty-five demon gods to begin with—actually one thousand and eighty of them. Mm, maybe there were even more before that.","“We combined forces with the mistress and killed hundreds of them, reducing their numbers to three hundred and sixty-five. So what if they all wake up at the same time? So what if they coordinate their movements? We’ll just kill them all!” Daoist Yuyu threw his head back with laughter.","Ancient nihil powerhouses such as he didn’t come from the Three Thousand. Their origins and background were even more mysterious. Those such as Daoist Yuyu had clashed with the demon gods before the Three Thousand was born. Over time, they reduced one thousand and eighty demon gods to three hundred and sixty-five.","Of course, the surviving demon gods were the strongest of those ever born.","Daoist Yuyu and his comrades paid a hefty price for their achievement—they nearly faded out of existence. If it wasn’t for Ancestor transforming into existence to house their true spirits, everyone from Hongjun, Tailong, Primordial, and Leize’s family would be long gone.","More of them were indeed gone and had left nothing behind.","Without the Land of Reincarnation and Lu Yun dismantling it, the survivors would’ve eventually become the demon gods’ pawns and refocus their attentions to helping the primordial world of immortals rise again.","Thankfully, the Dao King had been the counterbalance. He facilitated the Tome of Life and Death to recognize a new master and helped Hongjun, Daoist Yuyu, and others find themselves again. The daoist being captured by the Tome of Life and Death after the human hell shattered and being baptized into Ge Long was also one of the Dao King’s plans.","The Tome of Life and Death was the key to them finding themselves again.","Although the treasure was the first patch of existence to be born in the nothing, the power of reincarnation within it was the most marvelous power of creation. Even the Dao King didn’t know how to describe the treasure anymore.","It can be hard to make great work when its stolen from .","“But it’s still an inconvenience to lose the altars,” Lu Yun frowned. “Minimize our casualties and try not to meet them head on.”","Sacred Radiance had suffered enormous casualties this time, and while the immortals from the World of Immortals were prepared to meet the enemy, they’d taken their fair share of losses. The immortals were very precious to Lu Yun—the death of one would make his heart ache, not to mention the minimum of hundreds of thousands that’d died.","“I remember Diexi cowed the nihil level beasts with one phrase before—exterminating their bloodlines! Let’s counterattack and exterminate some bloodlines!”"]},{"number":2115,"title":"Chapter 2115: Chapter 2070 – Borrowing Force to Deploy Force","paragraphs":["Hundreds of thousands out of his group of precious babies from the World of Immortals had died! This irked Lu Yun. It irked him greatly.","That called for revenge.","Since the demon gods cared so much about their bloodlines, he’d happily exterminate them. He’d come to understand the purpose of the bloodlines through the calculations of formula dao. Once a demon god died, they could distill their bloodline from their descendants and coalesce a new body, thereby rising from the dead.","Given how they treated him, it would be impolite not to reciprocate, wouldn’t it?","Lu Yun wasn’t the type to turn the other cheek when slapped, but he didn’t plan on using the Three Thousand’s strength against the vicious beasts. Legends of their ferocious might constantly circulated through sanctuary. The local inhabitants of the realm lacked courage on a fundamental basis when it came to facing the vicious beasts.","Even the five sacred palaces would encounter the same mental block if they were told to march against the beasts.","Immortals from the World of Immortals had suffered such heavy casualties primarily because denizens of the There Thousand shrank back at the sight of the vicious beasts. They didn’t dare engage the enemy in battle.","As advanced as the immortals’ dao methods were and as sophisticated their techniques compared to the Three Thousand, they still came off worse for the wear against an overwhelming horde of enemies.","Thus, Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered to notify the sacred palaces this time. To him, cultivators of the sacred palaces were flowers raised in a greenhouse. In fact, they were malnourished flowers that hadn’t fully developed. They weren’t good enough to accomplish anything, but more than enough to spoil things.","It was one thing if their dao methods and combat arts lagging behind the times was the only problem. Given the clear progression of the modern era, they could easily supplement their shortcomings if they cultivated alongside those from the World of Immortals.","But these people rejected immortals from the very core of their being, regarding the latter as heretics and their cultivation as blasphemous doctrine. It was a prejudice that didn’t change even when their greatest sacred supremes gave orders otherwise.","Therefore, Lu Yun ignored them this time. Whether it was handling the mortals under demon god control or counter attacking the vicious beasts, he used only his own strength.","The human tribes of the Three Thousand required attention from the immortals of the Sacred Radiance Dynasty. Permitting the tribes to remain in sanctuary was just allowing latent danger to flourish. They had to be eliminated.","Of course, Lu Yun tried to capture the altar-controlled humans the best he could. It was only when it proved impossible that he killed them.","As for counter attacking vicious beasts... Infernum poured out en masse from the kingdom of hell. They were consumables to Lu Yun now. Their talents and intelligence were poor—they’d all been enemies disposed of by Lu Yun and the ten Yama Kings.","Search for the original.","It wouldn’t be any sort of loss if they were fully wiped out, and any vicious beasts they managed to take along the way would also become Infernum. Now that the Tome of Life and Death was a sheet of golden paper and had assimilated strength from the Three Brushes of Reincarnation, it brimmed with reincarnation. Anything that the Infernum killed also became Infernum!","This was a positive feedback cycle that would easily snowball to great effect. It made Lu Yun completely unafraid of war!","He’d gained quite a few beast Infernum with the previous invasion; they charged out of sanctuary with the ten Yama Kings in the lead. There was no setup or strategy to their deployment, just flat-out careening around.","There needed to be a culling of Infernum in the kingdom of hell since it was only so big. A few more ghostly soldiers would fill it beyond capacity. Quite a few of the vicious beasts ran into a gathering of their own kind and self detonated, trading their lives for ten times or even one hundred times new Infernum.","This put Lu Yun in a slightly morose mood.","“I’ll... send a few Infernum to the Disordered Sacred Supreme when she finishes crafting her nine hells.” He relaxed after finding a solution to the problem.","The ten Yama Kings assembled into formation and sealed off a radius of five billion kilometers around them. This range spanned the gathering point of a demon god’s bloodline—not Feilu, but another one called Duosheng.","This demon god took the form of a bird, so most of the vicious beasts in this area could fly. They were inordinately ferocious, but couldn’t withstand the increasing amount of Infernum that blotted out the earth and sky.","Three tremendous nihil level beasts vaporized when ambushed by Lu Yun, Ox-Head, and Horse-Face. They swiftly became the latest ghostly soldiers.","However, Infernum were different from Ox-Head and Horse-Face. The latter two had their names written in the Tome of Life and Death and possessed freedom and independent personalities. If one became Infernum upon death, that made one the lowliest cannon fodder.","However, Lu Yun killed vicious beasts simply to take revenge on the demon gods. Gaining a few nihil level Infernum was a happy bonus. He didn’t hope to capture more yin soldiers on the same level as Ox-Head and Horse-Face.","Indeed, yin soldiers.","Lu Yun had sorted his subordinates into three different categories under the reincarnation system. The Yama Kings were the highest, followed by yin soldiers who enforced the laws of yin and yang. They walked the mortal realms and guided souls to the afterlife. Yin soldiers such as Ox-Head, Horse-Face, the to-be-determined Black and White Impermanence, judges, and Meng Po would be written into the Tome of Life and Death or captured via the power of reincarnation.","If these soldiers died, they would be reborn from the cycle of reincarnation and regain what they possessed in life.","The lowest of his subordinates were the ghostly soldiers known as Infernum. They fell at Lu Yun’s hand or someone who wielded the power of reincarnation. Recreated from the crudest of reincarnation energy, their potential and cultivation were fixed at their moment of death. Dying meant an eternal death, they would not come back to life.","The Infernum could only remain in the kingdom of hell or at most walk the mortal world with the yin soldiers. If they strayed too far from Lu Yun, the Yama Kings, or yin soldiers, they would fly apart upon the wind.","That was the limitation that reincarnation levied on them. It was one that’d gradually faded away as the Tome of Life and Death evolved, but now that it was a sheet of golden paper, it reappeared with greater force than before.","Lu Yun didn’t dare let Daoist Yuyu join him on this campaign outside sanctuary. Invading the territory of the vicious beasts was an act of borrowing force to deploy force. If the daoist came and laid about with his swords and formation, there would be nothing left for Lu Yun to collect.","......","A radius of five billion kilometers was nothing to the unbounded Three Thousand—a grain of corn in the vast sea. However, this area happened to be where the bloodline of Duosheng gathered.","Other vicious beast bloodlines received word when battle broke out and sent masses of reinforcements. However, the Formation of the Ten Yama Kings had reached unfathomable levels—heights that withstood even nihil powerhouses.","The ten Yama Kings were just sacred supremes, but they could slay nihil powerhouses when they joined hands!","......","“Raugh rah roar!” A nihil level beast with the head of a lion rushed out of the formation and frantically called out to its own kind.","A dozen vicious beasts quickly stepped forward to help, closing around the lion. And then...","Kaboom.","A mushroom cloud rose from the ground as the dozen beasts were blown to pieces before they could approach the formation."]},{"number":2116,"title":"Chapter 2116: Chapter 2071 – The Melody of Self Detonation","paragraphs":["After the first instance of self detonation killed some of the reinforcements, as well as a few nihil level beasts, the remaining beast Infernum decided to drop the act.","They’d raised an enormous fuss when they first entered the area so they would draw the other vicious beasts. Now that self detonation destroyed the first group of reinforcements, the others were no fools and didn’t dare approach those not of their bloodline.","Given the reticence, Lu Yun sent his Infernum in a forward charge.","Borrowing force to deploy force, doing battle to sustain battle.","The beasts killed in self detonation were further turned into Infernum. Since the kingdom of hell was almost full, he decided to leave the new recruits where they were. It would be a nice surprise if they managed to fully eradicate the demon gods’ bloodlines.","Formula dao told him that the demon gods would be able to continuously return to life if their bloodlines weren’t extinguished. If one wished to slay a demon god, one had to end its line. And not just the ones here, but also the vicious beasts sealed at the World Heart.","Of course, if Lu Yun turned an entire bloodline of vicious beasts into his Infernum, then the resurrected demon god would likely come back as Infernum.","That left him with one question that he’d had all along—where did these demon gods come from?","Mo Yi was a spirit born of the nothing, the first life form. Her destiny was connected to the nothing, so what of the demon gods?","Where did they come from? Formula dao couldn’t give him even an inkling of an answer.","Although it looked like they also came from the nothing, that their fate was likewise intricately tied to the nihil, there seemed to be a deeper meaning hidden otherwise. A truth that everyone overlooked or ignored.","Mo Yi was the first spirit born in the nothing, but the nothing was a void that lacked everything. There were no rules or existence, so how had Mo Yi come to be?","She was also just Mo Yi, why did everyone call her the mistress?","How did the Three Thousand and the world that’d been the Tome of Life and Death manifest? Why would existence appear out of nowhere in a place that was devoid of all?","Something that seemed so matter-of-fact that it was common knowledge wasn’t necessarily correct.","Lu Yun didn’t know why he was considering this at this particular moment. Where did the bloodlines of the three hundred and sixty-five, or rather, the one thousand and eighty demon gods and even more in the past, come from?","Things didn’t seem as straightforward as they appeared.","His current cultivation level could be deemed as sacred supreme, but he didn’t wield the strength of the five sacred supremes of the Three Thousand. He was one on par with great god Pangu.","It was a level that exceeded empyrean supreme and rivaled the nothing. In fact, he could kill nihil powerhouses if he so desired. Plainly, he and Pangu were the same kind of person.","Instead of joining the fray at the Three Thousand, Pangu remained in residence at the chief worlds and safeguarding the World of Immortals. He didn’t watch over the primordial world of immortals about to enter the nothing because the World of Immortals was Lu Yun’s home.","Like an unstoppable boulder rolling downhill, the army of vicious beast Infernum grew larger and larger. Led by the ten Yama Kings, Ox-Head, and Horse-Face, they charged into the heart of the forbidden area.","Demon God Duosheng’s bloodline had been exterminated; all of them were now Lu Yun’s ghostly soldiers. They spread out in all directions and killed everyone they saw. Self detonation was a prompt course of action when they found themselves in a losing fight. There was no hesitation whatsoever in their actions.","The vicious beasts they targeted howled and cried for their mothers. They were willing to meet the enemy in battle, but how did one fight an opponent who didn’t care for their own life? No normal being self detonated when it looked like they would lose!","Although the vicious beasts didn’t possess much intelligence, they were still normal beings.","Infernum claimed half of the forbidden zone as their territory ten days after the ghostly army began sweeping through the area. The nihil powerhouses residing in the nothing finally couldn’t sit still any longer.","They knew where the invaders came from and their intent. They’d received requests of help from the three hundred and sixty-five heroes to stop Lu Yun.","And so, curtains drew back on the second world war of the Three Thousand. This time, it took place in the forbidden area rather than sanctuary.","No one exercised restraint in this zone as it was vicious beast homeland. The rules and laws in this locality were infinitely stronger than those in the fragile sanctuary. Even self detonation from a nihil powerhouse would result in only a small ripple.","The vicious beasts hadn’t dared invade sanctuary en masse and treated it as their own forbidden zone both because of the Dao King’s replica, and because it was the most fragile part of the realm. Just like the tail of Prince Rupert's drops, the lightest tap would shatter the Three Thousand. [1]","But other than sanctuary, everywhere else in the realm was indestructible.","And so, a war that was thousands of times more magnificent than the one before started in the forbidden zone.","We are , find us on google.","Thousands of nihil powerhouses strode through the void and rushed vicious beast Infernum. In response, the Yama Kings, Ox-Head, Horse-Face, and Black and White Impermanence withdrew from the battlefield. They utilized the Size Manipulation death art to observe from the shadows.","The Infernum would not be obliterated as long as they remained on the scene. They could leave the rest to their minions.","However, a profoundly heart-shaking melody of self detonation soon rang through the battlefield.","The newly arrived nihil powerhouses didn’t have time to react and assess the situation before they were blindsided by a round of explosions.","At the same time, they weren’t vicious beasts. Not only did they possess nihil level strength, they also wielded stunning treasures. The detonations injured them, some to the point of grave wounds, but very few died.","Only those closest to the self detonations were turned into Infernum. Lu Yun took full advantage of the opportunity and baptized them with the power of reincarnation, turning them into yin soldiers.","“I already have Ox-Head, Horse-Face, and Black and White Impermanence... These guys can’t be the judges or Meng Po. How about I make them Wang Chao, Ma Han, Zhang Long, and Zhao Hu?” he murmured to himself.","“Husband, aren’t those the four loyal constables serving Judge Bao?” Standing by Lu Yun’s side, the little fox looked at him with surprise. [2]","The little fox often visited Earth and had gained a full understanding of some of Earth’s myths and legends. Even though tens of thousands of years had passed on Earth, she could easily investigate the folklore of Lu Yun’s time if she wanted to.","She didn’t mean anything else by it, she just wanted to understand his past more.","“Well... um... I suck at naming, so let’s just call them that!” Lu Yun scratched his head sheepishly.","And so, the four latest Infernum were named Wang Chao, Ma Han, Zhang Long, and Zhao Hu. He couldn’t bear to let precious soldiers such as nihil powerhouses self detonate!","1. Prince Rupert’s drops are toughened glass beads created by dripping molten glass into cold water, which causes it to solidify into a tadpole-shaped droplet with a long, thin tail. ?","2. Bao Zheng was a Chinese politician during the Song Dynasty. During his twenty-five years of civil service, Bao was known for his honesty and uprightness, with actions such as sentencing his own uncle, impeaching an uncle of the emperor’s favorite concubine, and punishing powerful families. Bao Zheng today is honored as the cultural symbol of justice in Chinese society. ?"]},{"number":2117,"title":"Chapter 2117: Chapter 2072 – Beyond Nothing, the Divine Temple of Nothing","paragraphs":["And so, Lu Yun completed his ranks of Ox-Head, Horse-Face, Black and White Impermanence, Wang Chao, Ma Han, Zhang Long, and Zhao Hu. His eight yin soldier captains were fully gathered.","Naturally, the young man was very proud of recruiting eight nihil powerhouses, but he wasn’t fool enough to make it widely known. He used the Tome of Life and Death to alter their ripples of strength, making it seem like they were sacred supremes with the power of nihil powerhouses. Their original appearances were fully obfuscated.","Being Lu Yun’s yin soldier captains, the eight flung themselves forward as the vanguard of his ghostly troops. He named the vicious beast Infernum from this campaign as the Self Detonation Corps. This contingent couldn’t even be bothered fighting others. They just self detonated when they saw vicious beasts!","Whether it was nihil level beasts or ordinary ones, all became Lu Yun’s troops once they were blown up. It was no loss to him even if the enemy survived. The kingdom of hell was over capacity; it was nice to control the numbers via several explosions.","The current situation was something he’d never imagined possible. Who would’ve thought that the Tome of Life and Death would be so terrifying after it transformed into a sheet of gold? If circumstances were any different, Lu Yun would’ve burst from the innumerable wills of Infernum that resided in his kingdom, even if he possessed the same cultivation as he did now.","It was impossible for him to command so many ghostly soldiers.","But with the Tome of Life and Death the way it was now, he accepted all comers. He suspected that the treasure wasn’t displaying even one hundredth of its power!","“I wonder what the death arts I use will turn into...” Lu Yun sank into deep thought as he watched mushroom cloud upon mushroom cloud rise into the air within the forbidden zone. They’d performed according to how they should when he previously used them; he didn’t know what their limits were.","At the end of the day, the Tome of Life and Death wielded the strength of a world. It was the first existence to be born in the nothing. Although it didn’t fully take shape and develop to its full potential, it was a germinated seed brimming with infinite potential.","Lu Yun wasn’t soil for the seed, he’d become the seed. It’d taken root in his soul and was inseparable from him. They were one and the same for all eternity. Both prospered if one found glory and both perished if one suffered.","Its evolution process was the story of his growth. The soil that nurtured it was this endless environment, the numerous realms, and the unbounded nothing.","“That is enough, stop!” A dignified voice rang out from the sky.","Lu Yun pushed Qing Yu and the little fox behind him and looked up. He saw a man clad in bright red armor and wreathed in flames. The man had appeared at some point in time, and while Lu Yun could see him, there was only a ball of flames in his consciousness.","It can be hard to make great work when its stolen from \"\".","It didn’t seem to be a living being, but a ball of fire.","“Who are you supposed to be?” Lu Yun asked irreverently.","The blazing man narrowed his eyes. “As expected of the one who possesses the first of nothing. You show no respect to the fire god envoy from the Divine Temple of Nothing!”","\"Fire God Ew?” Lu Yun asked with surprise. “You mean Zhurong squeezed you out of his ass? Ew.”","“You!” The envoy blinked, then realized what Lu Yun was talking about.","Zhurong was the fire god of the great wilderness. Anything resulting from the buttocks was well, disgusting.","“I’d wanted to tactfully persuade you to resolve your differences, but instead, you can die!” The self-styled fire god envoy from the temple of nothing gestured sharply at Lu Yun.","The young man abruptly felt like he was enveloped by a blazing furnace. He recognized this kind of combat art—the ultimate peak of equipment dao, the forge of earth and sky!","It was a level of accomplishment that was rooted in fact. Similar to how the Enneawyrm Coffinbearers layout was derived from the actual coffin, so was the forge of earth and sky!","The forge of earth and sky was an unparalleled treasure as opposed to a combat art. The fire god envoy didn’t have the right to use the item, so all he could do was to derive a combat art using the treasure as a blueprint.","All the same, the combat art was incredibly stunning.","Lu Yun was dragged into an abyss of fire energy before he had a chance to resist. Boundless fire energy surged from all sides and rushed into his body, setting him aflame.","Not only did the forge summon nihil flames, but it also ignited Lu Yun’s own inner fire, heart flame, soul flame, nascent spirit fire, and any fires contained within his body.","“Don’t worry, you two, I kill only Lu Yun and will not harm incidents,” the envoy smiled merrily at Qing Yu and the little fox. “But as the sinner’s dao partners, you must be punished as well. I will bring you back to the temple after Lu Yun dies so you can receive your judgment.”","The two ladies looked on expressionlessly and didn’t say anything.","“This person’s cultivation goes beyond nothing, it’s a completely different level! What should we do?” the little fox transmitted anxiously, but didn’t show it on her face.","“It’s alright, our husband found out through formula dao a long time ago that a development like this would happen. He’d been ready for it, so what is happening now must be within his expectations.”","Lu Yun, Qing Yu, and the little fox had long become dao partners. The two ladies copied Earth custom and called Lu Yun their husband.","Qing Yu was barely keeping herself under control as well. She was simply blindly confident in Lu Yun and willing to believe that he’d already accounted for current happenings.","“Formula dao?” the envoy threw his head back with laughter. “Formula dao can indeed analyze the nothing, but I am a divine envoy beyond nothing! He can make calculations for the nihil, but he cannot touch what is beyond!”","Qing Yu and the little fox looked at each other with shock. The enemy could hear their mental conversation!","The fire god envoy remained where he’d appeared, unmoving as he watched Lu Yun struggle in the flames. The young man was such an unknown factor that while the envoy was completely confident in his skills, he wanted to wait until Lu Yun was burned to death before leaving.","Qing Yu and the little fox’s hands were clammy with sweat.","......","“The forge of heaven and earth? Does he want to burn me to death?” Lu Yun considered as he sat cross-legged in the flames. “But it’s meant to forge weapons... Ah, yes, he wants the Tome of Life and Death. He wants to refine me into the Tome of Life and Death!”","The book had become one with Lu Yun a long time ago, so killing the young man would destroy it. Only when they refined Lu Yun could they obtain the Tome of Life and Death!","“So how do I escape from this?” Lu Yun sat in the middle of the forge of earth and sky, one arm around his chest and his other hand propping up his chin. His mind spun furiously through all possibilities, as did formula dao analyze all potential resolutions.","But... he came to no conclusion.","The gap between the two was too big.","The Divine Temple of Nothing was hailed as greater than the nothing, whereas Lu Yun was just a sacred supreme. They’d plainly come prepared in order to capture him and seize the Tome of Life and Death. Although he was only caught in a combat art derived from the forge, it was compelled by the power of nothing and as such, wasn’t a power that Lu Yun could withstand.","He’d anticipated that this would happen, but never imagined that something like the Divine Temple of Nothing would exist in the nihil. The fire god envoy seemed to be an errand boy, but he was also a powerhouse who’d exceeded nihil?","Why had no one ever told him about any of this?","What kind of random nonsense existed beyond nothing?","Where did the nothing come from and what was the origin of the worlds?"]},{"number":2118,"title":"Chapter 2118: Chapter 2073 – Help","paragraphs":["These seemed to be questions that he’d never asked before. Many truths had been placed in front of him a long time ago, his thoughts never traveled in that direction.","People said that Mo Yi was the first being born in the nothing, that she lived and died with the nothing. So then... where did the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods, and the ones who’d already died, come from?","Out of thin air?","Mo Yi couldn’t have appeared out of thin air either. It was likely that all of this had to do with that so-called Divine Temple of Nothing. As for the circumstances that he was caught in, he couldn’t break through the combat art or dismantle it. There was no answer!","Lu Yun brainstormed for a long while and finally shook his head with resignation. Although the Tome of Life and Death could temporarily withstand the forge of heaven and earth, he himself would be refined given enough time. They would turn into a new treasure without a master.","“Well, this is embarrassing. It’s downright mortifying. I really don’t want to voice that word.” Lu Yun looked wordlessly up at the heavens, taking a moment to compose himself before yelling out, “Help!!”","......","Outside of the forge of life and death, the fire god envoy dug into his ears.","“What is he yelling?” he asked incredulously.","“Our husband... seems to be calling for help,” the little fox said weakly.","“That he is,” Qing Yu responded seriously.","“Haha... HAHAHA!!” the envoy laughed uproariously, derision and scorn in his gleeful laughter. “I’d like to see which idiot who wants to die will come save him! Any who dares intervene in the affairs of the divine temple will find no succor within nihil and existence!”","The envoy brimmed with confidence. He was a representative from the divine temple!","Thunk!","A fist appeared in the void and slammed into his eyeball.","The fire god envoy froze, then flew backward.","“Well well well, aren’t you something, Temple of Nothing.” A lackadaisical young man huffed on his fist and yawned widely.","“Big brother?” Qing Yu goggled at the young man.","“Oh, good morning, baby sister!” Qing Buyi roared with laughter and greeted Qing Yu and the little fox.","The little fox rubbed her eyes, unable to believe the sight in front of her. Someone had come to save Lu Yun as soon as he cried for help?","Qing Buyi?","A spacetime traveler?","“So you’ve been here all along and was just waiting for husband to ask for help?” The little fox understood.","“It’s so pleasing to the ear to hear Lu Yun beg for help,” Qing Buyi cackled. He turned around to consider the man he’d punched. “Yo, and I wondered who it was speaking so cockily. So it’s the venerable fire god envoy! How long has it been since you’ve brushed your teeth?”","“Spacetime traveler, how dare you intervene in the divine temple’s matters?” One of the man’s eyes was swollen shut and his expression the blackest of night.","“Divine Temple of Nothing? You dare call yourselves divine?” Qing Buyi’s tone and expression darkened as well. “Bunch of traitors!”","“Traitors?” the envoy snorted. “The victor is king and God is of the past. Only the Present God is present within the temple now!”","“Present God?” Qing Buyi snickered and bared his teeth. “Then I’ll start with you and beat all you traitors back into the past!”","He rolled up his sleeves and slammed his fists at the fire god envoy.","“Just you? You’re only a mere spacetime traveler! You dare strut around in front of a divine envoy just because you’ve inherited part of the Spacetime God’s power?” The envoy was wholly unimpressed.","A strict hierarchy was in effect at the divine temple. Envoys were the great god’s representatives. The master of the fire god envoys was the master of the fire god temple—the Fire God. Meanwhile, messengers were ranked beneath envoys.","However, the Spacetime God and his envoys were long gone. The so-called spacetime travelers had inherited part of his powers and could journey through space and time. But what did that count for? The Spacetime God was dead.","The fire god envoy had been caught off guard by the ambush, but that didn’t mean he was weaker than Qing Buyi.","BOOM.","A mushroom cloud rose from the ground as Qing Buyi and the fire god envoy clashed against each other.","“Oi, you two can fight if you want, just don’t hurt my precious baby cousins,” came another voice—Chen Xiao.","Chen Xiao and Qing Buyi were peas in a pod. One was never far from the other.","He showed himself to protect Qing Yu and the little fox, calmly taking out a hammer from his robes. He tapped the combat art from the forge of heaven and earth with a casual air.","“Slowly, slowly! Don’t hurt Lu Yun with the reverberations!” Qing Buyi hollered as he fought.","“Don’t worry, it’s just a combat art.” Chen Xiao waved at Qing Buyi, indicating for him to finish the envoy as fast as possible.","The envoy squawked with outrage, but Qing Buyi was oddly much stronger than he anticipated.","“C-cousin, how did you guys get so strong? Isn’t the envoy a powerhouse beyond the nothing?” Qing Yu’s eyes widened and she stammered her confusion.","“We took some time off and followed the river of time to a certain era, cultivating there for a bit,” Chen Xiao responded easily.","Who the hell knew how long they’d cultivated for?","The Temple of Spacetime had been so strong and destroyed first because what they utilized was too uncanny and unbelievable. Although they couldn’t alter the future or present, they could jump to any point in time to cultivate. No one knew how strong they could be.","When one reached the level of nothing, time alone was insufficient to raise one’s level. Opportunity, treasures, and comprehension were all critical factors.","But somehow, those in the Temple of Spacetime could find undiscovered treasures in the river of time, determine their location, and return to present day to excavate them.","And thus, the Temple of Spacetime was no more. Mo Yi had given its last heritage to the four spacetime travelers—Chen Xiao, Qing Buyi, Lu Feng, and Moran Dongning. They were the final hope of the temple, so they would take advantage of the opportunity for all their worth.","No one had any idea how much they’d made off with. And with Mo Yi and the Dao King’s aid, it was the easiest thing for them to increase their strength.","......","Cracks splintered across the combat art from the forge of heaven and earth and it looked ready to shatter.","BOOM.","Bright red flames arced through the void as a massive forge landed from the sky, right on top of where the combat art had been.","It continued to refine Lu Yun. This was the real Forge of Heaven and Earth!","Read this novel and other amazing translated novels from the original source at the \"\""]},{"number":2119,"title":"Chapter 2119: Chapter 2074 – Heaven and Earth, Chaos, Hongmeng, Nothing Divine Temple","paragraphs":["The real Forge of Heaven and Earth had arrived. Chen Xiao jumped with surprise and quickly led Qing Yu and the little fox out of its immediate vicinity. Blazing flames set fifty million kilometers of the air ablaze and burned countless vicious beasts to a crisp.","“Hahahahaha!!” The fire god envoy’s other eye suffered a blow from Qing Buyi’s fist, but he threw his head back with delighted laughter. “The almighty Fire God knows you are here and has sent the real Forge of Heaven and Earth. As strong as you are, you will not shift it!”","“With the sky as the sheath.”","The fire god envoy: ?","“The earth as the hilt.”","The fire god envoy: ???","“Sword of Chaos—rise!”","Bam!","The fire god envoy went flying.","Boom!","An enormous sword that cut through heaven and earth slowly pulled out of the void, then minimized to land in the hand of a young man clad in white robes.","The Sword of Chaos.","Dongfang Hao.","The Sword of Chaos that belonged to the ancient court of divines from the world of immortals was in the Three Thousand! Liege lord of the Exalted Major and emperor of all divines, Dongfang Hao, demonstrated power beyond nothing.","“What’s going on?!” Qing Yu and the little fox looked at each other. They naturally recognized the young man.","In times gone by, Lu Yun was hailed as one of the Five Youth Sovereigns of the world of immortals, alongside Dongfang Hao, Mo Qitian, Zi Chen, and Wu Tulong. They were shining beacons of excellence that countless cultivators and immortals looked up to.","Dongfang Hao faked his death when they adventured through the ruins of the Firmament Prison, withdrawing from the public eye. During his cloistering, he became the true master of the divine race in the world of immortals and received the heritage of the Sword of Chaos from the ancient divine court.","When Lu Yun appointed the celestial kings of the world of immortals, Dongfang Hao became the liege of Exalted Major and the divine emperor of the divine race.","Who would’ve thought that he would abruptly appear in the Three Thousand with the Sword of Chaos?","“This realm is much bigger than what we think,” Chen Xiao sighed. “The nothing, Hongmeng, chaos, worlds... each layer overlays the previous. No one knows where the limits are and what can be found outside the nothing or inside the worlds.","“But one thing can be certain, and that is the nothing, Hongmeng, chaos, and worlds are not separated by a hierarchy. They are on the same level.”","The tree god had demonstrated that when he manifested the fourth realm.","“There is a Divine Temple of Nothing in the nothing that reigns over it, just as there is a Divine Temple of the Hongmeng that oversees the Hongmeng. The same holds true for the chaos and worlds.","“The Sword of Chaos belonged to the Chaos God who oversaw the Divine Temple of Chaos. However, the Divine Temple of Nothing destroyed it and the Sword of Chaos was broken into pieces.","“The mistress brought the sword’s fragments into our world of immortals and gave them to Yun Yi. Yun Yi then used the collective strength of the divine race to manifest the sword in the world again,” Chen Xiao sighed. “For this, the ancient divine court was destroyed.","“Dongfang Hao is the next iteration of Chaos God and exercises authority over the Divine Temple of Chaos. It is a pity that only the Sword of Chaos is left of it. The divine temple has long disappeared with no trace of it to be found.","“However, it is sufficient that the Sword of Chaos has appeared again.”","“Yun Yi...” Qing Yu sighed when she heard the name. Yun Yi had completed a lot of important tasks by herself. “Is she really dead?”","“Dead without leaving behind the slightest crumb. She had a chance of staying alive, but that is no more,” Chen Xiao shook his head.","......","“The real Forge of Heaven and Earth?” Dongfang Hao gripped the Sword of Chaos and stood in front of the forge, howling, “I wouldn’t make a move if your forge wasn’t here. But since it is... I’ll start with the Fire God before moving on to destroy the Divine Temple of Nothing!”","He flared with a daring air and the sword in his hand burst with countless rays of light. Raising the weapon high, he brought it down on the Forge of Heaven and Earth.","Scrambling to get back to the scene, the envoy gaped with shock. He’d never fathomed that someone would be so impudent as to attack the vaunted forge!","The Forge of Heaven and Earth?","Others might not know what it was, but the foremost envoy of the Divine Temple of Fire was very familiar with it! The Forge of Heaven and Earth was the primary body of the Fire God!","Bam!","The Three Thousand trembled when Dongfang Hao’s sword crashed into the forge. Chen Xiao, Qin Yining, and the yet-to-appear Lu Feng and Moran Dongning showed themselves at this point as well. They crossed through the endless void and stood at the four corners of the Three Thousand to protect this grand realm.","Flames erupted over the forge and a furious human face manifested among them. It was the face of a woman with a red complexion and scarlet hair. She glared furiously at Dongfang Hao as his stroke had harmed the forge.","“Heir of the Chaos God?!” she bawled. “So the kid and his Tome of Life and Death was just bait? you set up a plan for hundreds of millions of years simply to lure me out of the Divine Temple of Nothing??”","Rumble!","The Forge of Heaven and Earth spun around as the Fire God’s primary body walked out. The treasure disappeared, transformed into the god’s body.","“Lure you out of the Divine Temple of Nothing?” Dongfang Hao snorted noisily. “Who do you think you are? You think entirely too much of yourself. Hah, are you worth so much time and effort on our behalf?","“You are just a minor consideration unimportant to the greater picture. We kill you as an afterthought!” Dongfang Hao continued to strike as he spoke, dispersing the body that the Fire God had just coalesced.","The Forge of Heaven and Earth reappeared. Still sitting within it, the corners of Lu Yun’s mouth twitched. Repeated operation of formula dao told him that Dongfang Hao spoke the truth!","His side hadn’t planned to create a third existence at first or destroy the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods. They hadn’t even wanted to protect Mo Yi—they just wanted to destroy the Divine Temple of Nothing.","Luring out this Fire God was also part of their plans.","We are , find us on google.","Yun Yi.","The name that Lu Yun arrived at was Yun Yi!","She was dead, but her schemes were in play even now. Her identity was nowhere as simple as it seemed. She was possibly the reincarnation of one of the great gods of the Divine Temple of the Worlds, Chaos, or Hongmeng.","But none of that was important anymore since she was fully dead.","“How dare you think of killing me?!” shrieked the Fire God. Instead of reappearing, she operated the forge at full strength and rushed Dongfang Hao.","“I am capable of killing you alone!” Dongfang Hao flared with killing intent and slashed forward with the Sword of Chaos again, creating numerous cracks in the paramount divine treasure."]},{"number":2120,"title":"Chapter 2120: Chapter 2075 – Collapse of Faith","paragraphs":["“Do you mind going a bit slower? I’m still in her stomach.” Lu Yun’s glum voice traveled from the Forge of Heaven and Earth. He finally understood certain things—crafting a third existence and hunting down the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods had always just been smoke and mirrors!","The group’s goal had always been very clear—lure out the primary body of the forge of heaven of earth and kill the Fire God!","He’d been kept in the dark from beginning to end. Each time Lu Yun thought that he’d seen the final truth and understood their ultimate goal, some fucking thing would appear to turn everything on its head.","This time, for instance, their plan to exterminate the bloodlines of the demon gods had drawn out a fire god envoy from the Divine Temple of Nothing, and then the Fire God herself. He hadn’t known anything about a divine temple or Fire God before this. Although many hints had been dropped beforehand, who the hell knew what they meant if the bosses didn’t speak plainly?","God’s existence, for one, was still a mystery.","Lu Yun spent his time pondering over new information while they fought outside and finally reached a conclusion that the Divine Temples of Nothing, Hongmeng, Chaos, and the Worlds were God’s creations. Mo Yi’s existence likely had something to do with them as well.","But despite coming to these answers, Lu Yun regarded them with skepticism. Only when he stood higher could he see further. He stood high enough and possessed sufficient strength to gradually gain insight into these so-called truths only after the Tome of Life and Death evolved.","He’d thought that he could easily trounce nihil powerhouses after the book finished transforming, but now there were heavyweights beyond nihil??","A great hustle and bustle sounded outside as the Fire God wasn’t an easy target. Although Dongfang Hao had damaged the Forge of Heaven and Earth with the Sword of Chaos, that inflicted only a small wound on the Fire God.","The Forge of Heaven and Earth was likely related to the Divine Temple of the Worlds.","Lu Yun looked speechlessly up at the sky and found himself meeting the eyes of a stunning beauty. She looked to be sixteen years old with a red face and locks of blazing red. The beauty regarded him resentfully.","“Fire God, I presume?” Lu Yun merrily stuck his hands behind his head and flashed a lazy smile at her.","“Yes,” she nodded.","“How about you tell me what else is there above the Divine Temple of the Worlds, Chaos, Hongmeng, and Nothing?” Lu Yun yawned. “My patience is running out with the truth revealed in bits and pieces like this.”","“Are you afraid of dying before you find out the full truth of this world?” The Fire God was still resentful, but her voice was thick with derision.","“You can say that,” Lu Yun nodded. “Is there anyone who death doesn’t come for in the end? Who is truly forever? So-called unending life and immortality is just living a bit longer than others. It’s the same for you, your seniors, and those more powerful than you who died before you were born.”","The Fire God opened and closed her mouth, identifying no proper reaction to his words but a resigned nod. It was true. There was no such thing as forever. Everyone eventually died.","“I want to live longer and even forever if I can swing it. There’s still so much about everything I don’t know. My biggest stroke of luck is being born into an era that enables me to learn so much,” Lu Yun chuckled. “The most unfortunate thing is that there is still so much that I don’t know.","“How about we make a deal?” he suddenly pivoted.","“What kind of deal?” the Fire God blinked.","“Tell me some stuff I don’t know and I promise you’ll make it back to your divine temple alive.” Lu Yun held up one finger. “There’s only upside for you.”","“What gives you the right to transact with me? Those outside will not honor it.” The Fire God arrived by Lu Yun’s side with a gentle shift of her body. Lithe and graceful, she radiated a burning fragrance and was too beautiful to be a living being.","Of course, her primary body was the Forge of Heaven and Earth—an unparalleled treasure. She wasn’t a living being.","“You can’t do anything to me, but those bastards outside schemed for countless eons to get you out here. You will die today.” Lu Yun was unafraid of the god in front of him.","“You also know that they’ve plotted for a very long time, so why would they let me go on account of your say so?” the Fire God pointed out.","“Because I’m Lu Yun.” The young man pointed at his nose. “You are unable to refine me or touch the Tome of Life and Death. They let you swallow me because they aren’t afraid of you eating me.”","“Very well, then,” the Fire God nodded. The Forge of Heaven and Earth possessed impressive stunning defensive capabilities. Although she was suppressed by the Sword of Chaos, she wasn’t in any danger for the near future.","She sat down in front of Lu Yun. “What would you like to know? Don’t ask about the truth of this world or the origins of creation. I don’t know those at my cultivation level either.”","“Who is God?” Lu Yun cut straight to the chase.","“‘God...” the Fire God sighed. “God is the creator. He created the nothing, Hongmeng, chaos, worlds, and their corresponding temples.”","Lu Yun stroked his chin. “Mo Yi... Ah, who is the mistress?”","“She...” The Fire God’s eyebrow twitched. “I don’t know.”","“Everyone knows, so why don’t you?” Lu Yun frowned.","“Everyone tells you that she is the first spirit to be born of the nothing. Do you believe them?” the Fire God smiled widely.","“Fair enough,” Lu Yun nodded. He wondered who’d come up and circulated that bullshit. The bosses outside were full of strength and shit. The most hilarious of all was that they believed their own crap!","“Mo Yi did indeed first appear in the nothing and is connected to it. Nothing that happened after that was kept from you. The replica that Che left in the Three Thousand was indeed to prevent the realm from absorbing the entire nothing and thus taking Mo Yi’s life.”","Lu Yun remained silent.","Find the original at .","“But... God calls her master.” The Fire God’s expression shifted oddly. “This is the major reason why the Divine Temple of Nothing betrayed God.","“I’m sure you’ve already realized that I am not a god of the Divine Temple of Nothing. I come from the Divine Temple of the Worlds. Our faith collapsed when God called her master and so we betrayed him and the temple.”","The modern day Divine Temple of Nothing wasn’t what it’d used to be. It was staffed by traitors of the four divine temples.","Lu Yun paused, dazed. No... he hadn’t realized any of that."]},{"number":2121,"title":"Chapter 2121: Chapter 2076 – Living In Lies","paragraphs":["“What else do you want to know?” The Fire God smiled superciliously. She didn’t really think that Lu Yun could let her go alive. Enlightening the young man was a pointless exercise. It was just to satisfy his insignificant curiosity.","Was any of this knowledge important?","Everyone of the three destroyed divine temples and the Divine Temple of Nothing knew it. As for the truth of this realm... who the hell knew?","Living beings peered into time the way ants observed the sky. If the patch that the ants saw was blue, then they thought the sky was blue. In the same vein, when living beings noted that the sky was nothing, they thought that the truth of the world was born out of nothing.","Was it important?","No, staying alive was the most important.","Lu Yun sank into quiet contemplation. So the origin of everything... was God and Mo Yi. Where did God come from? How about Mo Yi?","None of this is important...","All that spacetime travelers needed to do was to eliminate the traitors in the Divine Temple of Nothing. Perhaps this was just the latest iteration of truth he was seeing, and no one knew what the hell would happen next.","“What’s outside the nothing?” Lu Yun asked out of curiosity.","Being a powerhouse beyond nihil, the Fire God should be able to see outside of it. When ants observed the sky, some of the stronger ones could see further.","The Fire God thought for a bit, then reached out with a slender hand and drew a circle in the air. She separated it with an intangible line, then dotted each side of the circle.","“A yin and yang diagram... a diagram of the universe?” Lu Yun arched an eyebrow.","“Yes,” the Fire God nodded. “God drew this diagram when he taught us and said that this was what the world was.”","One side was nothing and the other was existence. There was a dot of existence in the nothing and a pinprick of nothing in existence.","Lu Yun furrowed his brows. He’d received a similar hint when he journeyed through the fourth realm. The world was presented as a massive yin and yang diagram, but back then, he’d thought that it was the delineation between the known and unknown lands.","As later affairs bore out, it was just the medium that which bore the weight of the Major Cycle Worlds and the Land of Reincarnation.","Here he was, hearing a similar explanation again.","“You know,” the Fire God murmured as a distant look appeared in her eyes. “I used to think that I knew the truth of this world, the reality of this part of existence...","“But I hopelessly discovered in the end that we just live in some people’s lies. I know whatever they want us to know, and I will never know what they don’t want us to know.","“I don't even know if the nothing we reside in is...” She reached out and tapped the side of nothing in the diagram, then tapped the dot of nothing in the side of existence. “I don’t know where we are.”","When you're just trying to make great content at .","Lu Yun couldn’t repress a shudder. Which part of the diagram was the boundless nothing that he had yet to set foot in? If they were the tiny speck of nothing that was located among existence, that would be terrifying.","“We betrayed God because we felt that the second possibility is more likely,” the Fire God continued. “That our nothing is the insignificant dot of nothing in an unbounded existence. We also think that God, and his master Mo Yi, comes from the unending portion of reality.”","Existence was reality.","“It’s very possible,” Lu Yun inclined his head.","“There are countless more terrifying powerhouses beyond the nothing. They can destroy our nothing with a casual backhand, just like I can squeeze the Three Thousand out of existence if I wished to.”","The Three Thousand was the only patch of real existence within the nothing, apart from the ones derived from the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods and Ancestor’s body.","Lu Yun swung his head around, feeling his brain hum from the new knowledge.","“Since you wish to explore the truth of this world, perhaps you’ll see it when you have the right to enter that part of real existence. But perhaps you’ll just see more lies.” The Fire God closed her eyes, her face devoid of color.","Dongfang Hao had gone mad in the outside world and furiously hacked at the Forge of Heaven and Earth with the Sword of Chaos. Ugly cracks spiderwebbed through the forge’s surface. The Fire God had split out a portion of herself to fight Dongfang Hao as she conversed with Lu Yun.","The divine and the Sword of Chaos in his hand were especially prepared for the Fire God, so although she let loose with everything she had, she was hard pressed to withstand her opponent.","Even the dao fires that’d been refining Lu Yun were beginning to recede.","She’d closed her eyes to await death. If they were in the outside world, she would easily swat the Three Thousand out of existence. However, the four spacetime travelers were safeguarding the four corners of the world and utilizing the power of existence to seal away her strength.","She was divested of more than ninety-nine percent of her strength.","“Stop.” Lu Yun suddenly stood up and called out, “I promised her to let her go.”","Dongfang Hao frowned, then halted with a nod. “Since you say to let her go, then she may go.”","The Fire God blinked.","“Aren’t you afraid that I’ll refine you at our next meeting?” she asked subconsciously, unable to believe that this was happening to her.","“I am, but I don’t go back on my word,” Lu Yun smiled. “And what you shared may not be real either. Don’t forget what you just said,” he paused, then enunciated clearly, “All of us live among lies.”","The Fire God’s brows snapped together as she nodded. The Forge of Heaven and Earth vanished with a tremble.","“You let her go just because she said that to you?” Dongfang Hao grumbled with irritation. “I could’ve said that to you too.”","“Intelligence from the enemy is sometimes more trustworthy,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Bah.” Dangfang Hao sheathed his sword and it melded into the world. The Sword of Chaos was the weapon of the Divine Temple of Chaos, but it also contained the power of the Hongmeng and worlds. Thus, it combined the power of the worlds, chaos, and Hongmeng. It was far more powerful than before, which was why the Fire God from beyond the nothing was no match for it.","“I employed formula dao just now and determined that the Fire God is an entry point to dismantling the divine temple. A living Fire God is more useful than a dead one.”","“Well said!” Qing Buyi darted out with a grin. “C’mere, let me tell you our true plans and goals.”","“Not interested.” Lu Yun curled his lip and walked over to Qing Yu and the little fox, leaving with his beloveds. “You guys can clean up your hot mess. Don’t think of using me as bait again.”"]},{"number":2122,"title":"Chapter 2122: Chapter 2077 – Jumping Out Of Nothing","paragraphs":["Hot mess? Of course there was a hot mess.","The entire Three Thousand was a hot mess.","With the demon bloodlines nearly completely exterminated, the demon gods were infinitely close to fully awakening. These bloodlines were the basis of them remaining undying. How would they be able to sleep with peace of mind when the bloodlines were almost extinct?","Each of the demon gods was a premier nihil powerhouse. If all three hundred and sixty-five acted in concert, they would strike with force beyond the nothing.","They would eclipse even the Fire God.","Dongfang Hao could end her not because he’d reached beyond nothing, but because his Sword of Chaos happened to counter the Forge of Heaven and Earth. If the three hundred and sixty-five truly awoke, then neither he nor the four spacetime travelers would be able to hold them off.","Lu Yun’s original plan was to slowly boil them alive by erasing one bloodline at a time. Conducting their movements this way wouldn’t alarm the demon gods.","However, more than one hundred bloodlines had been spontaneously terminated when the Fire God and Dongfang Hao clashed against each other. That’d jarred the demon gods to nearly full wakefulness.","Lu Yun’s departure had been to go on the run.","“We have indeed overlooked this matter... The demon gods are becoming a thorny issue,” Qing Buyi remarked with a long face. “If they return to full consciousness, that will accelerate their consumption of the Three Thousand’s core essence. Che will not be able to hold them off.”","This novel is available on .","Each of the four divine temples was staffed with twenty-seven thousand demon god guards, making for a total of one hundred and eight thousand guards. But after the enormous rebellion, the demon gods recovered their demonic nature and defected to the Divine Temple of Nothing.","Although only three hundred and sixty-five demon gods were left after the uprising, they were the strongest of their kind. All the same, their cultivation levels had declined from beyond nothing to nihil powerhouses after repeated injuries throughout the eras.","However, their instincts remained keen and sharp in their natures.","Come together and strike as one!","It was the strongest technique that God had created, and when all one hundred and eight thousand guards deployed the formation in conjunction, they were able to shake a divine temple.","Even though there were only three hundred and sixty-five left now, their combined force was still sufficient to obliterate a spacetime traveler.","“Let’s kill them first. One dead is one more down,” Chen Xiao took a deep breath. “We’ll be able to forestall their joint forces if we kill one more.”","“Not necessarily,” Moran Dongning stuck out her bottom lip. “I traveled to the past once and observed God inventing the Formation of Combined Force...”","“There has only ever been one God in the past, present, and future. You only saw an image of what he left behind.” Lu Feng dismantled what she was about to say.","“Oh bug off, an image is still an image of God inventing the Formation of Combined Force,” Moran Dongning grumbled. “Three hundred sixty-five formations lead to one hundred and eight, and then seventy-two, thirty-six, eighteen, seven, three...”","“Unless we execute them down to the last, they’ll be able to deploy the formation with only two of them. Strength beyond nothing!” Qing Buyi stared wordlessly at the sky. “How about we make a run for it and leave the Three Thousand to them? There’s nothing much to this world anyhow.”","“The Three Thousand points to the primordial world of immortals. If we give them this realm, then the primordial world of immortals won’t be able to ascend into the nothing.” Chen Xiao frowned.","“Do you four have any actual ideas?” Dongfang Hao interrupted irritably. “The sword in my hand is hungry!”","“How about we follow Lu Yun’s earlier plan and kill them one by one?” Qing Buyi asked hesitantly.","“They’re all awake and will know whatever we do. How do we kill them?” Chen Xiao flicked an annoyed glance at Qing Buyi and harrumphed, “And if my guess is right, Lu Yun calculated this outcome a long time ago and knows how to resolve it. He’s just mad that we didn’t tell him a lot of things, so he left.”","Lu Yun had let the Fire God go after asking her a few questions—although she was an important angle of attack to destroy the Divine Temple of Nothing, that was just one angle. Killing her would immensely diminish the capabilities of the divine temple, making it far more useful than keeping her alive.","Yet Lu Yun had let her go, which was an indication that he was angry that they’d kept things from him. He’d been living in lies—lies from the head honchos running everything, but also lies from those he viewed as his good friends.","You don’t say anything that I don’t ask you about, don’t you? Then very well, why should I tell you how to resolve this problem if you haven’t asked me?","It wasn’t him being petulant or miserly, but that they’d truly gone overboard this time. They should’ve given him time to prepare if they wanted to use him as bait. However, they used him to lure out a terrifying existence that he didn’t even know existed, and they’d done so without saying a single word before.","“Dongning, you go...” Lu Feng said hesitantly. “You’re the only one who didn’t know what we wanted to do, so you go apologize to him and ask how we should handle this...”","Moran Dongning heaved a long sigh and said pitifully, “I... actually knew since a very long time ago about what you guys wanted to do.”","Well, now no one knew what to do.","“Bunch of wimps dithering around like sissies. I’ll go,” Dongfang Hao snapped. “I know Lu Yun, he won’t just give up on this place. The chief worlds and primordial world of immortals will follow suit if anything happens to the Three Thousand!","“He had another nickname in the world of immortals—the Dao Saint! He keeps himself busy saving the world, so the Dao Saint won’t idly sit by if the world is about to go under!”","The four spacetime travelers looked at each other.","“I thought so at first, but Lu Yun has never cared about the world. He’s only ever cared about his people...” Lu Feng sighed. “He doesn’t care about the world perishing and creation dying so long as what he cares about survives. But as people, we need to live among the worlds...”","“Get to the point,” Chen Xiao frowned.","“Lu Yun has a world in his brain, right now! His Tome of Life and Death has manifested a nearly perfect existence! So what if the Three Thousand are destroyed? So what if the primordial world of immortals is destroyed? He just needs to move everyone to his brain!” Lu Feng snorted.","“What say you, Dao King?” Lu Feng called into the sky.","The Dao King’s replica appeared again. While his overseer replica was gone, he’d created another one. This one could only hold down the fort in the Three Thousand and prevent the demon gods from fully devouring its core essence. There was nothing else it could do against them.","“How about we tell Lu Yun what our true goal is?” the Dao King sighed. “Tell him that we want to use the Three Thousand as a springboard and the primordial world of immortals as a second springboard so we can jump out of nothing...”"]},{"number":2123,"title":"Chapter 2123: Chapter 2078 – Curiosity Killed the Cat","paragraphs":["“What’s the point of telling him that?” Chen Xiao shook his head. “Although his book can evolve into a profound existence, it’s still a long ways off from reaching the barrier of nothing. Telling him now will only throw his mental state into disarray and may lead him down the wrong path!","“Based on my understanding of Lu Yun, he’ll use formula dao after he learns of these things,” Chen Xiao frowned. “The barrier of nothing is the greatest taboo in this part of nothing. Formula dao isn’t strong enough to handle it yet. It will be annihilated if it touches the taboo and be completely terminated!","“Formula dao is our only hope of escaping from the nothing,” he concluded morosely.","Escape from the nothing. If they didn’t, all of them were fated to turn into nothing, just like the fourth realm of the original Land of Reincarnation. Nihil World Sovereigns cultivated and cultivated until one day they went poof! and turned into nothing.","That was the true nothing; the process was simply infinitely extended for them now. Meanwhile, nihil powerhouses basked in self-satisfaction, thinking that they were on the proper path and true Nihil World Sovereigns.","It was just reaching the same goal via different means. Even beings beyond nihil would eventually be assimilated by the nothing. The Fire God knew that death was inevitable as everything in the nothing, including existence and everything else, was destined to become nothing.","As for why they’d betrayed God...","God had told them that being assimilated by the nothing was their only end. But when their creator called another person “master”, more than just their faith collapsed. They discovered with greatest shock that Mo Yi was very likely a being from the real existence that could be found outside the nothing.","And so was God!","In their understanding, both Mo Yi and God possessed the ability to exceed nothing. They hid the method for their own purposes, and so the people betrayed God.","Their faith collapsing?","That was just an excuse. The Fire God had spoken a mix of truths and falsehood to Lu Yun. Her hints had been very clear—we all live in lies.","Whether it was the Divine Temple of Nothing, Ancestor, Hongjun, Pangu, and the others—their ultimate goal was to escape from the nothing. What set Ancestor, Hongjun, and the others apart was that they placed their bets on Mo Yi and the God. They looked to the duo to bring the rest of them out, whereas the Divine Temple of Nothing wished to destroy Mo Yi and God so they could extract the method from their souls.","The source of everything lay with the master and servant duo. Mo Yi was even more the crux of the issue. The Dao King followed her lead and was possibly also from the existence outside of nothing, but he kept such a low profile that everyone forgot about him.","He was so nondescript that he was easily overlooked.","Formula dao originated from the Dao King and the Tome of Life and Death was the first patch of existence to be born in the nothing. That it’d become the book was a result of the Dao King’s machinations, and formula dao came from the Tome of Life and Death.","Whether it was Mo Yi, the Dao King, or even God, all of them had lost their original selves. They’d forgotten their pasts and the seed of formula dao that the Dao King had left in the Tome of Life and Death was their only saving grace.","If Mo Yi, the Dao King, or even God wished to reclaim themselves, they needed to jump out of this part of nothing and return to their world. Formula dao became their only hope.","It’d determined in the past that the Three Thousand would be the first springboard and the primordial world of immortals the second springboard to jump out of nothing. The next steps after that required a stronger formula dao to conduct further calculations.","Prior to the Tome of Life and Death coming into being, the Dao King once tried using formula dao to find the complete answer. When its analysis reached the barrier of nothing, it was shattered to pieces and only a hint of its origin survived. That was incorporated into the book and later drawn forth by Lu Yun, becoming what it was now.","The Divine Temple of Nothing wouldn’t believe any answers they were given. They would only believe what they stripped from Mo Yi and God’s souls.","“Then go and tell him the consequences so he won’t be tempted to use the current version of formula dao to analyze the barrier of nothing.” Dongfang Hao’s solutions were as straightforward as his thoughts.","“A person’s will can never overcome curiosity,” Lu Feng shook his head. “If I was skilled in formula dao and possessed its origin, I would certainly use it to determine how to free myself from the nothing. I wouldn’t be able to wait for it to grow stronger.”","Dongfang Hao blinked, then closed his eyes to pose the same question to himself. Deep down, he found that he would do the same.","“In that case, let’s eliminate the demon god bloodlines,” the Dao King chuckled wryly. “At least that ensures the demon gods won’t be able to continuously revive from their bloodlines after they awaken.”","“That is how things should be.” Dongfang Hao put Lu Yun out of his mind.","Thus, the peak experts of nihil powerhouses within this part of nothing completely erased the bloodlines that the demon gods had left in the Three Thousand. Despite that, their bloodlines still existed—Ancestor had left quite a few of them in the World Heart. But if they dared resurrect through the bloodlines in the World Heart, their lives would not be theirs anymore.","......","Lu Yun didn’t know how long it’d been since he returned to the world of immortals. He sat cross-legged at the peak of Mount Xuanhuang in Dusk Province, looking into the setting sun in the west.","The world of immortals was a prosperous, thriving world that was the strongest of the four realms and the entire chief worlds.","But it was also beginning to decline.","Not because of immortal dao, but because the immortals of the world of immortals were migrating to the primordial world of immortals. It wouldn’t be long for the primordial world of immortals to become the new world of immortals, and for immortal dao to officially take root in the primordial world of immortals.","“What are you thinking about, my husband?” Qing Yu whispered as she rested her head on his shoulder.","“Can a person’s will never overcome curiosity?” He smiled ruefully when he looked at his beloved.","“Huh?” Qing Yu blinked.","“Although those stunning powerhouses blocked off the surroundings when they conversed, they forgot that some things are recorded by the laws of heaven and earth as soon as they are voiced,” Lu Yun sighed. “Maybe they were overconfident, or maybe they did this on purpose...","“I really can’t help myself. I do want to use formula dao to determine how to jump out of the nothing. But if I do so, formula dao will violate a certain restriction and be shattered to pieces.","“But I’m unwilling to give up because subconsciously, I feel that the Tome of Life and Death protects formula dao and can withstand the backlash from the restriction.”","Lu Yun was extremely conflicted.","Cultivators, whether immortals or of other daos, went against heaven’s will. They knew what they did wasn’t the course of nature, but they did it anyway. Lu Yun knew that attempting to calculate the way out of the nothing would result in the collapse of formula dao, but he still couldn’t control his curiosity.","His self control could have kept himself in check, but he seemed to be obsessed with the idea. He could barely restrain himself even with the aid of the Tome of Life and Death.","It can be hard to make great work when its stolen from .","He regretted leaving some plans behind in the Three Thousand. Why had he used the Tome of Life and Death to peek into their conversations?","A cat has nine lives, but curiosity killed the cat.","“Why not strengthen yourself?” Qing Yu thought for a bit. “The best way to restrain curiosity is desire. Yours can be the desire to grow stronger! Once you are stronger, you will have the ability to effect changes.”"]},{"number":2124,"title":"Chapter 2124: Chapter 2079 – Temple Master","paragraphs":["Immortal dao had traversed the chief worlds and become the mainstream great dao of the realm. Its guardians—God and Pangu—had left. Their whereabouts were unknown.","Hongjun remained at Mount Buzhou and looked out over the realms. Lu Yun didn’t take the time to meet him. The young man continued to sit at Mount Xuanhuang and contemplated his future.","Qing Yu was right, he did need to continuously increase his strength. It’d always come from the Tome of Life and Death, and while they were one and the same now, what the treasure bestowed was passive improvement.","It was a vastly different concept to Lu Yun proactively cultivating and seeking out improvement. He’d reached the maximum capabilities of the treasure’s passive progression, so there was nothing further than he could glean from the Tome of Life and Death.","If he sought out improvement, he’d not only be able to pull strength from his own body, but also propel the Tome of Life and Death into evolving further. While he contemplated his next steps, he also considered how to raise his strength.","Cultivate immortal dao?","In his current state, he was stronger than the immortal dao. He’d even taken the mantle of Dao Sovereign from Qing Yu’s shoulders and hauled the great dao forward on his back. The stronger he grew, the stronger the immortal dao was.","He also didn’t dare utilize formula dao at the moment. It was very possible that he would prove unable to suppress the curiosity deep in his heart and turn it to analyzing the reality on the other side of nothing.","Of one thing Lu Yun knew for certain, and that was Chen Xiao, Qing Buyi, and the others knew that he’d left certain contingencies behind. The Dao King had purposefully spoken of the world outside nothing as a clear warning that Lu Yun could not employ formula dao on it.","Given his personality, he would certainly try to calculate affairs outside the nothing after the Fire God revealed them. However, the barrier of nothing was a taboo that separated the nothing and reality. Whoever ran afoul of it would die.","If Mo Yi and the Dao King possessed the method to exceed the nothing and return to reality, they would’ve left long ago. Why bother going to all this effort to nurture formula dao and create existence?","Lu Yun even suspected that the Dao King and Mo Yi had created the Tome of Life and Death in order to be a medium for formula dao. Perhaps it was formula dao that’d chosen him, not the Dao King, Mo Yi, or even the Tome of Life and Death.","......","“Stop thinking about it if you can’t come to an answer.” Fuxi suddenly appeared next to Lu Yun and handed him a wine gourd. “Drink with me.”","“Senior, are you from that reality as well?” Lu Yun chugged some wine.","“No,” Fuxi shook his head. “My home is the Three Thousand. We’re the first batch of people to surpass it and reach the nothing.”","He took a large mouthful as well. “The limit of nothing is nothing. You turn yourself into nonexistence with a poof! and all is no more.”","“What about beyond nihil?” Lu Yun blinked. The Fire God and the fire god envoy were both existence beyond nothing.","“The four divine palaces of the worlds, chaos, Hongmeng, and nothing were created to give shelter to beings who’d reached the end of cultivation, so that they could continue to walk their path,” Fuxi explained. “It is a pity that those of the four temples had already mutinied when the Three Thousand was born.","“Those who didn’t mutiny were beaten to death by those who did.”","“Did the four temple masters die too?” Lu Yun frowned.","“The temple master of the chaos died. Only a trace of the soul of the Sword of Chaos survived. Having received the sword’s heritage, Dongfang Hao is the new temple master.","“Of course,” Fuxi continued. “More than the great daos of the chaos are contained within the sword. The worlds, Hongmeng, and great daos of the nothing are also within.”","Lu Yun nodded without a word. He knew that Fuxi was here to discuss things that were appropriate for him to understand now.","“The temple master of the nothing is still alive. He was the first to betray God. Hongjun is the master of the Hongmeng. He was gravely injured and his status unknown...” Fuxi sighed.","“And the temple master of the worlds? Who is he?” Pangu’s name flashed through Lu Yun’s mind.","Pangu had created the heavens and earth, hewn the chaos, and manifested the worlds. He used more than the power of creation, but the power of heaven and earth.","In Lu Yun’s mind, Pangu must be the temple master of the worlds.","“The great god Pangu is a spirit of nothing born from the nothing. All life forms in the nothing are based off of him. He is a so-called dao form.” Fuxi knew what was on Lu Yun’s mind. “Pangu is the ancestor of humanity, not the temple master of the worlds.”","Pangu wasn’t a being born from existence, but a divine spirit born from the intersection of the nothing and existence after existence came to be. Based on what Lu Yun knew before, that was Mo Yi’s identity as well.","But Mo Yi had already connected herself to the nothing and replaced Pangu’s position, so Pangu wasn’t constrained by the nothing. At the same time, the existence within nothing would continue to expand until it eventually occupied all of nothing. This was due to the fact that reality was present beyond the nihil.","But when the Three Thousand occupied all of the nothing, that meant annihilation of all life. Nothing could withstand the destructive force of the Three Thousand colliding with the barrier of nothing, even the existence that’d expanded to the extreme of possibility.","Find the original at readnovelfull.me.","At that time, the patch of reality—the Three Thousand—would also return to the nothing.","Mo Yi had connected herself to the nothing and linked their survival together because she wanted to somehow resolve the dilemma. However, she wasn’t strong enough to prevent the final outcome by herself.","Hence, the demon god guards of the four divine temples connected themselves to the nothing as well and transformed into existences similar to connate demon gods. Yet, the four divine temples and their gods betrayed God all those years ago, resulting in heavy injuries to Mo Yi. She was forced to cross the river of time to travel to the present so she could recover.","The demon god guards who’d melded into the nothing were slowly cleared out after rounds of battle until only three hundred and sixty-five remained.","“Who is the real temple master of the worlds then?” Lu Yun asked.","“She just died,” Fuxi sighed.","“...Yun Yi,” Lu Yun said.","“Correct.” Fuxi inclined his head. “But she passed on the temple’s legacy.”","“To Chu Xingran?” The name came to mind. Chu Xingran had once been the Curse King and who Lu Yun thought would be his greatest enemy in life.","“Mmhmm,” Fuxi nodded. “Chu Xingran has gone to other realms to temper himself and is attempting to activate the legacy within him. God created the four divine temples so they could pierce through the barrier of nothing.”"]},{"number":2125,"title":"Chapter 2125: Chapter 2080 – Hope or Despair","paragraphs":["Lu Yun suddenly fell silent as he looked at Fuxi.","“What is it?” Having just reached the topic of the four divine temples, Fuxi paused when he noticed that the young man’s expression wasn’t what he imagined it would be.","“Senior... do you think there will be other things waiting for us later on?” Lu Yun stroked his chin. “From Mo Yi, God, or plans to come. We might need to overthrow something when we return to that reality, or seek vengeance on someone.”","“Well...” Fuxi blinked, then looked at Lu Yun like he was gazing upon a fool. “What does that have to do with us?” He smirked.","Lu Yun paused. True, no matter what Mo Yi and God’s final goals were, it was enough that the duo’s present goals matched theirs. This way of thinking was a breath of fresh air.","After all, he himself steadfastly remained on one side because their aims were the same as his, no? That was enough, who cared about what was to come?","Lu Yun’s current target was to escape from the nothing. He wanted to live, he didn’t want to die. Once existence occupied the nothing and collided with the barrier, he would have to die too, even though he possessed the Tome of Life and Death.","The treasure depended on the great dao that existed between nothing and existence. Once existence touched the barrier, everything would be destroyed and relegated to nirvana.","It was similar to the great devastation that Lu Yun had witnessed at the end of time in the Land of Reincarnation. In that moment, all laws and rules ceased to exist. The Land of Reincarnation was a microcosm of the greater nothing and existence around it!","Thus, Lu Yun’s current ambition was to survive.","Even though existence had seen a very stunted development and three hundred and sixty-five demon gods leeched off its strongest patch, the trends of the times could not be denied. The demon gods’ actions were just attacking the symptoms, not the cause.","If the Three Thousand perished, a stronger world would appear, one that no living being could shake. And if the Divine Temple of Nothing repeated the same tricks to absorb the world’s core essence, that would propel the new world to greater heights instead of halting its growth.","The primordial world of immortals was not that new world. Once the new world manifested, the nothing would truly return to the nothing and permit no life to dwell within it.","Nihil powerhouses would have to break through the barrier of nothing and leave for reality in order to survive. True survival could also only be found there.","The world in the Tome of Life and Death? It was doomed as long as it was located within their nothing.","“What are your plans?” Fuxi smiled at Lu Yun when he saw that the young man understood everything.","Fuxi didn’t want to die either and was also planning his attempts for survival, just like the traitors in the Divine Temple of Nothing. They differed in terms of ideals and methods, which was why there was a conflict.","In the end, no matter who was right or wrong, whoever was the opposition had to be sacrificed.","“I want to grow stronger.” Lu Yun looked in Qing Yu’s direction in the world of immortals and the two smiled at each other. He’d been lost and didn’t know what to do, it was Qing Yu who guided him back to the right path.","Continue growing stronger.","It was what he’d been doing all along—strengthening himself. He’d walked so far and grown so strong that he’d forgotten his initial motivation.","“Your current strength places you at the apex of this part of nothing,” Fuxi chuckled ruefully. “You avoided the nihil realm and became a sacred supreme. You’re much stronger than many ancient peak nihil powerhouses.”","“Sacred supreme... is a level that comes from the reality outside of the nothing, isn’t it?” Lu Yun asked.","“Apparently it is,” Fuxi nodded. “That was what Pangu was back in the dao as well.”","Sacred supremes existed within the Three Thousand because it was the only reality within this part of nothing. Only denizens of that realm were able to become sacred supremes.","The other existences apart from the Three Thousand were manifestations of great daos of nihil powerhouses. They were also existence, but not real. Hence, they couldn’t produce sacred supremes.","The primordial world of immortals could as it borrowed the rhythm of the nothing to create a real existence. It would become something on par with the Three Thousand as soon as it could ascend to the nothing.","But thanks to the Dao King, Ancestor, and a few others, it would never be able to occupy the nothing. It was the only mark of a tiny rebellion that they could muster.","If an existence couldn’t occupy nothing, then it would ultimately be assimilated in turn. Another existence would then appear until one finally fulfilled its mission.","“Are sacred supremes mainstream in the outside portion of reality?” Lu Yun’s eyes gleamed.","“That’s my guess as they didn’t tell me anything,” Fuxi smiled. “My grasp of formula dao is less than yours, but I can still analyze a fair bit.","“I don’t actually wish to leave this place,” he suddenly sighed. “This is my home, my roots. Even if I live forever, I would be a drifting flower if I left my homeland.","“But we must leave.” A resolute expression appeared on his face. “Only when we leave and enter the real existence can we find the reason why existence continuously expands in the nothing. Only then can we resolve the problem at its root.”","It can be hard to make great work when its stolen from \"\".","“Agreed,” Lu Yun nodded. “But this is all speculation. Even I don’t know if there is reality to be found outside of the nothing or...” He raised his head. “If it’s the end times and all lies in ruin and devastation.”","Fuxi shook and despair flashed through his eyes. It shrouded the hearts of everyone in the nothing. If what could be found beyond the nihil was what Lu Yun said...","That would be horrifying.","The reality outside of nothing was their hope.","“You must know that whether it is the nothing or existence, all are objective,” Lu Yun continued. “It was never a function of conscious thought. It is whatever shape or form they are. The end times in our eyes are just another form to them. We are but pitiful slugs gasping for survival in an insignificant crack.","“But if we grow strong enough that our wills can impact the objective and command everything, then I will be God.”","He would be the creator of an era with a wave of his hand."]},{"number":2126,"title":"Chapter 2126: Chapter 2081 – Within the Nothing","paragraphs":["Fuxi started, unable to find the words for a proper response. God... the creator of an era with a wave of his hand?","God could indeed create everything in the nothing with a wave of his hand. That was how he’d created the four god emperors and numerous life forms within the nothing.","Was that enough?","Far from enough.","God would eventually die as well.","However, Fuxi understood Lu Yun’s meaning. If one grew strong enough to affect the objective with the subjective, then one could alter the objective rules to change objective worlds that did not permit life into subjective worlds that only existed for life.","Life was an accident in the unending expanses of time and space. The objective worlds were not obligated to provide conditions suitable for life. Whether it was the nothing or existence, it was just a process of bilateral transformation.","The nothing could transform into existence and existence could transform into reality.","Life, however, was an unexpected development from these transformations. To objectivity, it was no different from sand and stone within the cracks of a mountain. Perhaps life might appear, reproduce and prosper during this period, but there would be no more life after this period was over.","What was a cataclysmic disaster for life was of no matter to objectivity.","If life wished to continue on, it had to do so through its own strength. It needed to be strong enough to affect objectivity.","Such were Lu Yun’s thoughts.","“Um...” Fuxi was startled by Lu Yun’s theories. “You’re not wanting to just be God, but rather the creator of all,” he chuckled ruefully. “We’re such tiny specks, but you already have your sights set on the objective world.”","“It’s not really setting my sights on anything,” Lu Yun shook his head. “This is just what I’m thinking with my current level of knowledge and observation. Perhaps I might think otherwise when I stand tall enough and am strong enough. Boundless, infinite, unending, unceasing. What is the truth, and who can see the end?”","A quick look at will leave you more fulfilled.","The young man sighed. “All I can do now is stand at the peak of the world I know so that I may live longer. That is all.”","“Not for the good of all?” Fuxi chuckled. The world of immortals hailed Lu Yun as the Dao Saint, he whose heart and mind encompassed the worlds and fought for all life. He was often compared to the deities of old.","“If everything dies and I am the only one left, or just a few of those by my side are alive... then there is no point to living.” Lu Yun shook his head. “Humans are social creatures. Live alone? I might as well die.","“Friends, enemies, passersby. That is a complete life.” Lu Yun stood up with an explosive sigh, expelling all of his accumulated frustration.","“Have you decided where you want to go to increase your strength?” Fuxi relaxed from his prim and proper posture and propped himself up with his elbows.","“The Divine Temple of Nothing,” Lu Yun nodded. “I have an agreement with the Fire God.”","“Um...” Fuxi blinked. “An agreement with the enemy? When did you come to that? In the Forge of Heaven and Earth? I don’t think so...?”","“So you guys were indeed monitoring me,” Lu Yun curled his lip. “Some things don’t need to be said aloud. A simple gesture and a quick glance is sufficient. Take care of Qing Yu and the little fox for me. I’m off.”","He vanished as he spoke.","“Hold on a minute...” Fuxi smacked his head with a grin. “The brat left a long time ago. That was just a pre-recorded image and I fell right into it!”","Lu Yun had just unwittingly played the role of someone else’s weapon and was nearly refined by the Fire God. If he ran off to the Divine Temple of Nothing, many would think that he was going over to the enemy.","That was why he’d left this recording for Fuxi.","Lu Yun had indeed reached a bottleneck. The Tome of Life and Death had evolved to peak form and he could no longer improve his strength. He couldn’t rely on the treasure anymore and since his body was tied to the book, he was also restricted from physical progression.","The Tome of Life and Death had created shortcuts for the young man, but now it limited him. If he wished to continue advancing, he would have to hew a new path.","Formula dao!","And the Dragonquake Scripture!","It wasn’t until the Tome of Life and Death evolved into a sheet of golden paper that Lu Yun sensed the method’s formidable might. It’d been a very long time since he’d dared use it. Had he employed it when caught in the Forge of Heaven and Earth, none of the ensuing trouble would’ve taken place.","Yet the Dragonquake Scripture was so strong that if he utilized it, he would be caught up in the backlash. He might die if he didn’t handle it well. Thus, augmenting formula dao so that it could deduce the way to control the Dragonquake Scripture was his new path.","Lu Yun even thought that the Dragonquake Scripture might come from the patch of reality outside of the nothing. When he spoke of objectivity and subjectivity with Fuxi, it was with a confidence that stemmed from the method. He didn’t talk about the Dragonquake Scripture with Fuxi because the method had been a gift from the latter in the first place.","Other than Lu Yun, all of the Dragonquake Scriptures that the others had cultivated—including Fuxi, Qing Yu, and the little fox—had dispersed. Not a single trace of them was left behind, so he naturally wouldn’t raise it in front of Fuxi again.","......","The Divine Temple of Nothing sat in the middle of nothing. It was the strongest force within the nothing.","“The nothing gives me the same feeling as when I first set foot into the fourth realm...” Shimmering with a golden haze, Lu Yun looked out over the nothing.","He didn’t immediately set out for the divine temple as that would be throwing himself straight into the enemy’s net. However, formula dao also told him that the way to take it another step forward was to be found within the divine temple.","“The Nihil World Sovereigns of the nothing should be the same as the ones in the fourth realm,” Lu Yun murmured to himself with a frown. “What is meant as exceeding nothing should be the equivalent of sequence cultivators.","“But accessing sequence means accessing objective rules and laws. What are the sequences that they access in the real nothing?” he muttered.","“Right... how do I know if this nothing is the real nothing and not someone else’s creation?” He suddenly broke out in a cold sweat.","“You’re right, how do you know if this nothing is the real nothing?” a voice traveled into his ear. The tall and limber Fire God appeared by Lu Yun’s side with a half smile. “They’ve told you everything, haven’t they? What is meant by deeming us traitors and the so-called jumping out of nothing?”"]},{"number":2127,"title":"Chapter 2127: Chapter 2082 – I’m Threatening You","paragraphs":["“Stop blabbing about this nonsense. My ears are growing calluses from all the crap you guys spew.” Lu Yun stuck his finger into his ear and picked at it. “I don’t even believe my friends, so why would I listen to rot from an enemy?”","The Fire God’s expression turned slightly awkward.","“We have a deal—I saved your life, so you need to help me get stronger,” Lu Yun said matter-of-factly.","“When did we strike that deal?” the Fire God grumbled.","“I don’t care!” Lu Yun grumbled. “I can kill you right now if you don’t agree!”","He leered at her as the golden page of the Tome of Life and Death appeared over his head.","“Fine, fine,” the Fire God acquiesced with resignation. She could’ve used the Forge of Life and Death to fully suppress and refine the young man had he been wholly unprepared. But now that he was aware of her existence and on guard against her, that left her no opportunity whatsoever.","It didn’t make a difference that she was stronger than him on an absolute basis.","Formula dao.","Formula dao was too uncanny.","The stronger Lu Yun was, the greater the method became. Not even nihil powerhouses could avoid its analysis. Formula dao was also the medium for supplemental dao—the forge of heaven and earth was the ultimate peak of equipment dao within the supplemental daos. The young man was naturally very familiar with it.","The Fire God had incorporated her primary body into the ultimate peak of supplemental dao so she could exert control over all life. Unfortunately, it ended up backfiring on her.","When Lu Yun was captured by the forge, he analyzed his circumstances with formula dao. Although he didn’t come to an answer of how to extract himself, he discovered how to counter the Fire God. In his days of sitting cross-legged at Mount Xuanhuang, he further deduced a complete method to kill the Fire God.","Thus, there were many things that he didn’t need to say aloud. A simple glance could convey meaning that ran deeper than words.","The Fire God...","If she hadn’t shown up, Lu Yun would’ve hacked his way into the Divine Temple of Nothing and chopped her up. That wasn’t a joke or an empty threat. Since those of the divine temple had designs on him, he needed to set an example. Who knew what might jump out next if he simply scared off the Fire God?","He’d also gleaned some clues about the Divine Temple of Nothing through the course of his calculations. For some reason, its powerhouses couldn’t leave the temple. The Fire God was one of the few who could, so the Dao King and others spent all of their efforts scheming against her.","Just one Fire God alone didn’t mean much, but her strength had reached the peak of nothing and she reigned over it. She was much stronger than the Dao King and others. Only Dongfang Hao wielding the Sword of Chaos could restrain her—and now, Lu Yun as well.","Killing the Fire God was a move of great strategic importance for the Dao King’s side. It would blast a weakness into the Divine Temple of Nothing.","“How should I strengthen myself?” Lu Yun asked with a smile.","“At your level? Battles of life and death, of course.” The Fire God stroked her pointy chin with a grin. “I judge you to be one of the peak Nihil World Sovereigns within the nothing. You’ve reached Ancestor and Forebear’s level when they were in their prime.”","“That strong?” Lu Yun blinked. He knew he was highly capable, but he should’ve paled far in comparison to the Ancestor and Forebear of old.","While they weren’t the strongest Nihil World Sovereigns of the nothing, they were representative characters and monikers for the strong.","“You weren’t before, but you are after you deduced the combat art to kill me.” The Fire God plopped down in the void and tilted her neck up at Lu Yun. “What, do you lack that much confidence in yourself?”","“Of course I do, prior to fighting that kind of powerhouse.” One’s strength was determined by the caliber of one’s opponents, not one’s words.","“Then come with me to the Divine Temple of Nothing and fight the truly strong in it. You’ll know then.” The Fire God laughed like a fox—but not the little fox. Although the little fox was mischievous and apt to be up to no good, she never utilized her wiles against others.","In contrast, the Fire God seemed to be more like a fox as she giggled, “Enter the divine temple and fight with its strongest powerhouses. You’ll find the way to improve yourself then.”","“I can’t even beat your subordinate, the fire god envoy,” Lu Yun frowned.","The truly strong? Everyone in the divine temple was likely powerhouses beyond nihil, weren’t they? He’d be courting death trying to fight them!","“The envoy is the manifestation of the rules, not a living being,” the Fire God said. “Do you think you can beat the manifestation of the rules? Don’t worry, there are only so many beyond nihil in the temple. Most of them are Nihil World Sovereigns and sufficient for you to practice on.”","Lu Yun fell silent. The manifestation of the rules and being bestowed a true spirit meant the ultimate peak of a certain set of rules in the great dao. Being human, he naturally couldn’t fight those. Some others with similar origins, however, came to mind.","The Talisman, Formation, Pill, and Weapon Kings of the Hongmeng were peak titled kings. They also weren’t living beings, but derivations from the four supplemental daos. Being manifestations of the rules, the Dao King had granted them true spirits to safeguard the Hongmeng.","“Very well,” Lu Yun nodded. “Let’s go to the Divine Temple of Nothing.”","“You really dare come with me?” The Fire God looked incredulously at Lu Yun. “Aren’t you afraid that I’ll take the advantage to kill you?”","“Of course I am, why wouldn’t I be?” Lu Yun answered frankly. “But I guarantee that you’ll die first before you take me out.","“Are you that certain of yourself?” The Fire God wasn’t very pleased by the response. She was one of the strongest in the nothing when it came down to it. Not even the current Dao King or mistress was her match. But this young man talked about her like she was someone he could crush to death at any time?","“I rather wish that you guys would attack me,” he suddenly broke out into laughter. “That way, I won’t feel any guilt when I destroy the Divine Temple of Nothing.”","Theft is never good, try looking at .","The Fire God: ......","Lu Yun explained with resignation when he saw her skepticism, “I thought you knew me well enough given that you’d moved against me and wanted to seize my treasure. It looks like you still know far from enough. Or do you guys think that I’m not worth consideration without the Tome of Life and Death?”","The Fire God shrugged—some in the temple did think that way.","“Have you ever heard of the Dragonquake Scripture?” Lu Yun asked merrily. “There’s a method within it called the Dragonspike Litany that can destroy the entire temple if it’s deployed. Of course, I can’t use it now because I don’t know what consequences will result from me using it, so I try not to if I can help it.","“Anyway, I’m not discussing this with you, but threatening you! Take me to the Divine Temple of Nothing or I’ll kill you and go there myself!” he snarled."]},{"number":2128,"title":"Chapter 2128: Chapter 2083 – The Divine Temple of Nothing","paragraphs":["Lu Yun felt very secure in his capabilities after entering the boundless nothing, especially when he realized that he could claim the Fire God’s life at any time.","The Fire God was equally rueful. She never imagined that her target could turn around and suppress her instead!","It had nothing to do with strength. On the contrary, Lu Yun had sent a hint of an incredibly terrifying thing into her body when he was swallowed by the Forge of Heaven and Earth. While the young man possessed the ability to kill the Fire God, he actually boasted of the capacity to spontaneously eradicate her.","The Dragonspike Litany.","He’d sent a tiny bit of the litany into her body, and this was why she’d come out to meet him. As he was able to fully deploy the litany’s full power, he could destroy the Divine Temple of Nothing at any time.","However, the power wasn’t under his control. If he destroyed the temple, he would also destroy everything else in the nothing. It was an act of mutual destruction that he would not activate unless he had no other choice.","Nonetheless, it remained an enormous threat to the divine temple. In their eyes, everything within the nothing was but ants. Their lives and deaths were meaningless, but if an ant possessed the ability to end the world, then it horrified them all the same.","Thankfully, no one in the divine temple knew of the Dragonspike Litany, apart from the Fire God.","The litany was a tiny contingency plan that Mo Yi and the Dao King had left behind. In fact, Lu Yun had calculated hints that the Dragonquake Scripture could be used for more than destruction. The Dragonspike Litany was used for the obliteration of all, but the Dragonsearch Invocation and Dragonshift Method were closer to creation.","“Ai,” the Fire God sighed helplessly as she looked at the young man. “You can choose us too, you know. Our goal is also to survive within the nothing.”","“It’s different,” Lu Yun shook his head. “You guys only want to survive.”","“Hmm?” The Fire God blinked.","“You destroy the existences born of the nothing time and time again for the sake of your survival. You treat the symptoms, not the cause. There will one day come an existence that you cannot erase. At that time, death will be your only option.” Lu Yun looked at the other with a trace of derision.","“Heh,” the Fire God snorted, contempt on her face. “And that makes the path of the mistress and Che—two foreigners—viable? They lead you in abandoning your homes again and again, permitting your homes to be destroyed and reborn in endless fashion. Are you truly able to go to another world with peace of mind?","“While the nothing will eventually destroy us, it is our home.” She cast a sidelong glance at Lu Yun. “The Divine Temple of Nothing seeks to protect our homeland.”","Find the original at .","“Protect your homeland?” Lu Yun curled his lip. “How? By destroying it over and over again like what you do now? By killing your own family with your bare hands?”","The Fire God fell silent.","“I don’t know how many bouts of destruction the nothing has endured, but this time, everything follows according to our plan. Destruction is not upon us,” she finally offered solemnly after struggling for a response.","“Then how did the first patch of existence become the Tome of Life and Death?” Lu Yun sniffed. “Meanwhile, the second patch of existence is a hellish state of nonliving. Dare you say that you guys aren’t behind this?”","The Fire God had nothing to say.","“Although my cultivation level is less than yours, you should understand that someone of my level will hold steadfast to my goals once I have set them. Unless I was on your side to begin with, my perspective will never change.” There was no right or wrong, superior or inferior to Lu Yun. It was simply a matter of perspective. Different perspectives meant different considerations and outlooks of thought.","“...you are correct,” the Fire God sighed.","“Let’s go to the divine temple. We’ve wasted enough time here,” Lu Yun said.","......","The Divine Temple of Nothing.","Lu Yun was unable to see the divine temple. He wouldn’t find it even if he explored every corner of the unknown. The Dao King, mistress, and God wouldn’t be able to either, to say nothing of the young man.","There was no concept of space or time in the nothing. Any locale could be a dot, or an enormous boundless hole. Everything depended on one’s angle of comprehension.","One could say that there was distance in the nothing. It could be very long, it could be very short. One inch could be crossed in a single footstep, or it might be unreachable for endless eons.","This was the nothing.","While it lacked the concepts of space and time, its denizens possessed them. Just as there was originally no great dao or heaven and earth among existence, all of it came into being once life and subjectivity dwelled among it.","Therefore, the Divine Temple of Nothing could both be in front of Lu Yun and be somewhere that he would never reach in his life.","He could even be in the temple right now.","Lu Yun didn’t know what’d happened. They whoosh’ed somewhere and arrived in front of a palace. It was neither ostentatious nor brimming with magnificent multi-floors and pavilions. It was a palace simply because Lu Yun thought it should be a palace.","It would be a thatched hut if he thought it should be a thatched hut.","Thus was subjectivity.","It was a palace constructed from subjective will and given the name of the Divine Temple of Nothing from countless life forms. And so it was the Divine Temple of Nothing.","It was very apropos of the definition of “nothing”.","“A temple of subjectivity...” Lu Yun stood in front of the divine temple, frowning with deep thought. “So the divine temple isn’t within the nothing, but within the thoughts of the people. If everything within the nothing died, then this temple would naturally cease to exist.”","“You finally understand,” the Fire God smiled.","Lu Yun nodded. This was why the Divine Temple of Nothing was the only one to remain out of the four after the rebellion, and why it’d become the home of the traitors.","Its origins were the reason why.","The traitors wouldn't kill everything in the nothing. Even the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods transforming into existence and manifesting life was for this purpose.","And now, Lu Yun also understood why the altars existed in the Three Thousand and who they sacrificed to.","The Divine Temple of Nothing.","Their powerhouses called themselves gods, making it simple to eliminate the temple. Have life forget about the temple. Without the subjective thoughts of creation, the Divine Temple of Nothing would collapse and cease to exist."]},{"number":2129,"title":"Chapter 2129: Chapter 2084 – The Mistress’ Scheme","paragraphs":["However, creation would never lose its subjective thought. If it did, it would no longer be alive. Thus, it was impossible to destroy the Divine Temple of Nothing.","Since that was impossible, they had to turn to killing everything within the divine temple instead. All that needed to be done was to incite the same rebellion they’d conducted when they betrayed God.","......","When Lu Yun stood inside the divine temple, he found it greatly different from the one he expected. In his imagination, the divine temple should have been a towering, dark hall filled with dignified majesty. Its inhabitants would hold various offices and industriously plot how to survive in the midst of the nothing.","But when he truly arrived at the temple, he found that...","He was wrong.","He seemed to be in a world full of hustle and bustle. Dappled sunlight graced the land, birdsong reached the ear and floral fragrances touched the nose. Cities scattered over the lush land like handfuls of scattered pearls. There could be found mountains, valleys, rivers, plains, deserts, forests, and everything a world should have in such a vast expanse.","A sea lapped at the edge of the land. Beyond that was the unbounded nothing.","The Fire Good stood at the peak of a soaring mountain and looked down at the earth beneath them. Next to her, Lu Yun grew lost in thought.","“It’s very different from the Divine Temple of Nothing you thought it would be, isn’t it?” the Fire God chuckled.","“Yes,” the young man nodded.","“The one you imagined is the one of the past.” A distant look appeared in her eyes. “This is the world formed out of the combined core essences of the four divine temples.”","“I find that the sanctuary of the Three Thousand is quite appropriately used here.” Lu Yun nodded.","“Have you changed your mind?” the Fire God grinned.","“No,” Lu Yun shook his head. “Existence continues to expand into the nothing. Sanctuary will be reduced to dust when existence touches the barrier of nothing. Everything will cease to exist, making sanctuary is only a temporary refuge.”","“So... you will leave your homeland?” The Fire God’s expression remained unchanged.","“The existence that you guys cannot destroy has already been born. You know that,” Lu Yun commented with a smile.","“The new world of immortals,” the Fire God acknowledged unpleasantly. Indeed, the primordial world of immortals that Ancestor had nurtured with his life was one that the Divine Temple of Nothing could not destroy.","It would be the springboard for Mo Yi, God, and the others to jump out of nothing. The temple couldn’t crush it, but Lu Yun could with the Tome of Life and Death. The treasure possessed the requisite strength to dismantle the world.","It was why the divine temple had set up a plot to refine Lu Yun so they could seize the Tome of Life and Death. In turn, God, the Dao King, and Mo Yi played into their plans, using the young man as bait to lure the Fire God out of the Divine Temple of Nothing.","The Fire God was the divine temple’s pillar. If she died, the temple was half gone and would no longer be a threat to the nothing and the primordial world of immortals.","The temple remained an enormous threat so long as she was alive. They might not be able to destroy the primordial world of immortals, but they could still move against it and delay its development. Hope remained as long as the primordial world of immortals did not enter the nothing.","“There will be no hope left for the nothing if they fail. Glory is temporary and will ultimately transform to objectivity,” the Fire God continued to try and reason with Lu Yun.","“That is why I’m here to grow stronger,” the young man smiled. “You guys were on the opposite side of Mo Yi and God before, each of you insisted on keeping true to your ideals. And now, I’ve been thrown into the mix. I’m going to use my way to resolve the problem.”","Oh fucking hell, I’m gonna be called the Virgin Mary at this rate. I just want to live, when did I turn into the Dao Saint? Lu Yun grumbled to himself despite what he was saying.","“Not the mistress,” the Fire God shook her head. “She has forgotten who she is. The Dao King is not among them either. He is just her lapdog.","“So they’re all God’s... Hongjun’s people?” Lu Yun blinked.","“God, Hongjun, Pangu, the heir of the Divine Temple of Chaos, as well as the four spacetime travelers,” the Fire God listed. “They are our enemies.”","“Your enemies, not mine,” Lu Yun corrected.","“You have set foot on a different path than them after entering the Divine Temple of Nothing. You are their enemy too now,” the Fire God smiled beatifically.","Theft is never good, try looking at [ ].","“It doesn’t matter,” Lu Yun shook his head. “Nothing matters as long as we survive.”","These were all old monsters who’d lived for countless eons. They might yearn for life, but they wouldn’t fear death. Lu Yun, however, was young. Compared to them, his age wasn’t even a rounding error. Not only did he yearn for life, he definitely feared death.","He would save creation if his own death wasn’t a prerequisite, but would run as soon as his life was threatened. As long as the green mountains were there, one did not need to worry about firewood. He who fights and runs away, lives to fight another day.","“Alright, I’m going to search out my fortuitous opportunity and get stronger.” Lu Yun’s appearance shifted and he bounded upward, entering the world.","“So he’s finally come.” A young woman appeared next to the Fire God. They looked the same, but the newcomer possessed cerulean blue locks and wore a blue silk dress.","She was the Wave God of the Divine Temple of Waves.","“We are no match for him. That Tome of Life and Death is also not derived from the existence before the Three Thousand,” the Fire God frowned. “We’ve been tricked.”","“Hmm?” The Wave God raised an eyebrow.","“The existence before the Three thousand wasn’t the first patch of existence in the nothing. From dao came one, and one begat two... All of that’s bullshit!” the Fire God cursed, suddenly caught in the throes of great fury. “All of it was the mistress’ scheme!","“She never wanted to kill me! She lured me out there so the kid could enter the Divine Temple of Nothing!!”","She shrieked and seethed, gripped in a blaze of wrath so great that there was nothing she could do but let it run its course.","“You guys don’t really think that I brought Lu Yun here because he threatened me, do you?? I brought him here because of the mistress! She threatened me! She can kill me with a thought if I didn’t bring me here and erase the divine temple from the subjective worlds! We’ve all been tricked, we’re all her pawns!!”","“Didn’t you just tell Lu Yun that she’s forgotten everything...?” Startled, the Wave God goggled at the Fire God.","“She had me say that.” The Fire God sagged as anger drained out of her. “She orchestrated the rebellion against God that we thought was our doing.”","Incredulity shone out of the Wave God’s eyes."]},{"number":2130,"title":"Chapter 2130: Chapter 2085 – Not of One Heart","paragraphs":["Chapter 2085: Not of One Heart","Having reached perfection, Shapeshifting turned Lu Yun into whatever he wanted to be. He hesitated as he gazed out over the paradise that was the Divine Temple of Nothing. Although he said that he would resolve things with his own methods, that he would search out a solution from the patch of real existence, he knew that it was impossible.","Existence was born from nothing and slowly grew until it occupied all of nothing. It would return to nothing when it touched the barrier—this was a cycle of reincarnation.","The six orders of the highest degree. Inception, ethos, burgeon, creation, opposition... and nirvana!","This was the objective rhythm that all things followed. Lu Yun was certain that even the real nothing in the outside followed the same pattern, that it would also perish.","But as a subjective entity, he was loath to accept the situation. It wasn’t impossible for subjectivity to affect and even change objectivity and the rhythm. Surely there were already people attempting the task.","Not only was there formula dao in the Tome of Life and Death, but also reincarnation. The rhythm of objectivity was reincarnation, so someone was already trying to refine it. At this stage, the reincarnation within the Tome of Life and Death was still a subjective construct. It’d yet to reach an objective level.","But it was a seed all the same. If Lu Yun could guide it to germination, he might be able to plant objectivity into the subjective reincarnation and continue to attempt to transform objectivity into subjectivity.","He couldn’t accomplish it with his current level of strength, neither could the mistress or the Dao King. Perhaps this was just the hypothesis of a perfect status. The subjective thoughts of subjective beings were still theoretical pondering.","What Lu Yun needed to do now was not to get caught up in these musings. He had to try, even if it was impossible, to realize a perfect condition. Otherwise, there was nothing he could do but accept being assimilated by the nothing. That, he refused to do so.","So he focused his mental efforts on debating where his opportunity might be and how he could enhance his strength. The conclusions of formula dao could not be wrong, so while there might not be fights to be found here, it was where he could grow stronger.","He just hadn’t identified where exactly this opportunity could be found. Unease was also beginning to creep in, but he couldn’t determine its source. Thus, he decided to quietly observe for a while.","He transformed into a blade of grass and stuck himself in the ground so he could monitor the city in front of him. There were humans, monster spirits, demons, and all sorts of races inside. There was an abundance of fights to be found and, in fact, a decently sized battle taking place right now with its neighbor.","Lu Yun watched from the vantage point of a blade of grass and finally understood the origins of the war after half a year. The Wangshu city lord’s daughter had eloped with the neighboring Lunzai city lord’s son. The two met mountain robbers along the way and both were murdered.","Both city lords were of the ingress realm and the strongest within the area. They quickly deduced the truth from the clues they gleaned. What was mystifying afterwards was that their children’s murderers remained at large, free to kill and rob and live their lives as usual. Instead, the two city lords began fighting each other.","Neither city lord thought their child was at fault. It must’ve been the other who seduced their shining example of a child, resulting in a shameful elopement! They wouldn’t have encountered robbers if they hadn’t eloped and thus wouldn’t have died.","Lu Yun didn’t understand these leaps in logic. Wasn’t the matter at hand to jointly raze the robbers first, then decide who was at fault later?","Neither city was close to being a victor after half a year of battle, but the war intensified to the point of a death feud. It started off as wanting to force the other to apologize, but now the two were as if fire and water.","Lu Yun watched for another half year—they were no closer to a conclusion after a full year of fighting. The robbers, however, seemed to have received word and ran away in the middle of the night, never to be heard from again.","“The inhabitants here...” Lu Yun wanted to frown, but gave up as he felt a blade of grass shouldn’t frown. “Seem awfully similar to the feudal lords of Earth’s ancient Europe. They seem to view honor and glory to be more important than a life.”","He returned to human form with a puff of air and left at a leisurely pace. The two city lords were strong, but not much to Lu Yun. They were the equivalent of two cultivators who’d just accessed sequence.","He didn’t plan on intervening in this. Watching two ants fight was boring enough, but getting involved in their war?","Even more boring.","“I’m very happy that you didn’t interfere.” A golden shadow flashed by just as Lu Yun was about to leave, resolving itself into a golden-haired girl. She looked almost the same as the Fire God, but dense metal energy sparkled over her.","“Tsk tsk tsk.” Lu Yun sized up the young woman. “If my guess is right, you’re the Metal God of the Divine Temple of Metal.”","“That is me,” the Metal God nodded. “My primary body is the ultimate nihil treasure called the Golden Chaos Sovereign.”","“Oh, never heard of it before. What do you want?”","“To help improve your strength.” The Metal God looked intently at Lu Yun.","“We’re enemies, aren’t we? Why do you want to help me?” the young man smirked. He wasn’t the least bit worried as he could activate the Dragonspike Litany with a single thought and completely destroy the divine temple.","It would come back through the collective faith of the people, but those who died wouldn’t.","“Your Dragonquake Scripture is yet to reach perfection, so you’ll at most destroy the Fire God’s temple and leave ours unharmed.” The Metal God was wholly unconcerned as she saw right through Lu Yun. “But don’t worry, the divine temples of the five elements are not of the same heart as the other temples.”","“Oh?” Lu Yun frowned. “Not of one heart?”","“There’s no need for you to know about that,” the Metal God shook her head.","“So then what are you talking about it for?” Lu Yun grumbled.","“Fine.” She pursed her lips. “Helps us regain control over the Divine Temple of Nothing. The world you see is formed from the power of the five elements. The divine temple continuously destroys the existences that are born within the nothing. We of the five elements collect the denizens whose homes have been destroyed and bring them here.","“The world you see is not the entire Divine Temple of Nothing, it’s just our territory.”","“So that means I need to go to the other mountains if I want to increase my strength?” Lu Yun raised his brows.","The Metal God: ......"]},{"number":2131,"title":"Chapter 2131: Chapter 2086 – Tomb From Reality","paragraphs":["Chapter 2086: Tomb From Reality","The Metal God inclined her head with resignation. “The temples of the five elements oversee territory populated by beings from existences past. You will not find any opponents here.”","“Existences past?” Lu Yun frowned.","“Your Tome of Life and Death isn’t the notion of dao begetting one,” the Metal God explained. “After the mighty uprising, countless existences were born in the nothing...”","“Stop!” Lu Yun interrupted as she was about to launch into a detailed recounting of history. He stuck to his goal. “Where do I go if I want to increase my strength?”","“Continue north on this road until you see a big door. You’ll reach the other temples if you walk through it—wait, aren’t you going to consider what I just said?”","“Nope, farewell.” Lu Yun raised cupped fists and vanished in the direction that the Metal God pointed at.","She stood dazedly on the spot, abandoned by the young man she’d come to meet.","“He refused, didn’t he?” The Wave and Fire God arrived by her side.","“He didn’t even bother hearing me out,” the Metal God responded helplessly. No one had ever shown her that kind of attitude before.","“I should’ve explained everything to him before I came back to the temple.” The Fire God was equally resigned. As the only god who could leave her temple, she was so constrained by other thoughts and interests that she had to conceal the deepest thoughts that brewed in her heart.","The consequences wouldn’t bear thinking if she died and the existence within nothing kept expanding. Could the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods destroy existence?","For present day life forms, everything ended with the destruction of the world. Although the world would return to being and existence would bloom again, what did that have to do with them?","They would all be dead.","There was another possibility that after existence collided with the barrier of nothing and all life was destroyed, the newly born existence would not contain life.","For objectivity, life was an accident.","“No matter,” the Wave God shook her head. “Since the mistress has her own plans, we can always give them a try.”","“Her plans are to return to that part of reality. Whether or not we survive has nothing to do with her.” Resignation was writ large over the Fire God’s face. The major reason why the gods of the five elements had agreed to mutiny, rebel against God, and gravely injure the mistress was because they wanted to keep the duo in the endless nothing.","Only then would the duo try to stop the great devastation from taking place.","The mistress had subsequently lost her memories—or maybe not—but the Dao King and God’s plans had always centered on how to escape the nothing. They wanted to borrow the existence born of nothing and the Divine Temple of Nothing to jump out of the realm.","The plan relied on three critical steps—the indestructible patch of existence, the divine temple, and formula dao to determine the proper way. Lu Yun was the key now.","“Let’s take it one step at a time. I really can’t just accept our deaths like this.” The Metal God still possessed a bleak outlook for the future.","The process of existence expanding to the point of colliding with the barrier of nothing was an exceedingly long procedure for ordinary beings. It was sometimes so long that it felt eternal for them.","But for those beyond nihil, those who stood at the peak of nothing, it was over in the blink of an eye. There was no rhythm of time in the nothing, but there was the measurement of time. Sufficient time had passed since the temple’s rebellion that they could’ve collided with the barrier more than a hundred times now.","Hundreds, if not more, existences had been born in the nothing while the powerhouses of the divine temple continued to live on.","They hadn’t lived long enough yet and didn’t want to die. Meanwhile, differences in opinion splintered the internal workings of the Divine Temple of Nothing.","Most of the temples other than the five elements had proceeded down another extreme. They wanted to hunt down the foreigners that were the mistress, Dao King, and God.","They wanted to kill the trio and seize their memories, sifting through them to identify how to destroy existence or even ensure that further existences were not born. Only then would the final devastation cease to continue.","The temples of the five elements opposed this extremism. They could endlessly destroy the existences that appeared in the nothing, but they did not wish to kill the foreigners that’d found their way here.","Keeping the trio here and preventing them returning home was enough. The trio would naturally seek to prevent devastation from occurring.","The splintering wasn’t too serious yet, but the differences were there and it was only a matter of time before civil discord rocked the Divine Temple of Nothing. That was why the Fire God and others had set up their plans to seize the Tome of Life and Death.","Only now did they realize that they’d unwittingly fallen into the mistress’ plans. Perhaps she’d lost her memories, perhaps not.","Regardless,Sshe was doing this on purpose.","......","Lu Yun opened the door when he saw it and walked through it. The same kind of world entered his eyes, but there were no weak life forms here.","It was the void that greeted him. Towering and majestic temples hovered in the air, radiating the orders, laws, and great daos of the nothing to all of the distances within the nothing.","He saw the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods. If it wasn’t for the Divine Temple of Nothing, they wouldn’t be able to transform themselves into existences. Ancestor was the only exception.","“I was just about to go look for you, but here you are!” came a delighted voice as soon as the young man set foot over the threshold.","Lu Yun took a look at himself—he was still disguised by Shapeshifting. Although he was human, he wasn’t Lu Yun. He was just a random being, yet someone had recognized him as soon as he walked through.","He prepared to fight.","“Nonono, don’t be so violent. We seek peace!” the voice rang again. Thousands of rays of light gathered in front of Lu Yun and assembled into a charming young man.","Although he was in human form, Lu Yun was certain that this fellow wasn’t human.","“Allow me to introduce myself, I am the Light Deity.” The young man smiled gently.","“Not the Light God?” Lu Yun blinked.","“The gods are the masters of the Divine Temple of Nothing, I am yet to reach those heights,” the deity smiled. “According to the hierarchy of the divine temple, I am one bit higher than the envoys.”","“So we’re gonna fight?” A sharp light glinted in Lu Yun’s eyes and he struck a battle pose.","“No, no fighting! Those of the Temple of Light advocate peace!” the deity reiterated. “We have more important things to do!”","“You, not we,” Lu Yun corrected.","“Very well...” the deity nodded. “I’d like to ask you for a favor. Once it’s done, I can arrange an opponent for you if you wish to fight.”","“What kind of help?” Lu Yun asked warily as he sent formula dao into motion. He couldn’t deduce anything as the Divine Temple of Nothing was too sophisticated. Formula dao sometimes worked on it and sometimes didn’t.","“Tomb raiding!” came the unexpected answer. “A tomb has fallen through the barrier from reality!”","Tomb raiding...","Lu Yun wanted to retort, but nodded. It would indeed be tomb raiding. Tombs were homes of the dead. As a living being, they would be tomb raiding no matter why they entered a tomb and in what capacity.","“It might hold the way to end the great devastation!” Excitement tinged the Light Deity’s voice."]},{"number":2132,"title":"Chapter 2132: Chapter 2087 – Living and Selfishness","paragraphs":["Chapter 2087: Living and Selfishness","Lu Yun: ......","He looked quizzically at the guy who called himself the Light Deity.","Tomb raiding?","This world was turning out to be more unreal than any movie script. Tomb raiding was his bread and butter. He loved it and was naturally happy to help. However, he could see through any tomb with a quick glance these days given his current cultivation level—even that of a nihil powerhouse. There were no challenges whatsoever, so it’d been a very long time since he explored one.","Having reached perfection, the Spectral Eye could pierce through any tomb and identify the background of the tomb owner.","Tomb raiding...","What a term that was so far removed from him! His sect was extremely active in the World of Immortals and the various realms. While Lu Yun didn’t personally raid tombs anymore, his sect’s legacy had been perpetuated and thrived.","Who would’ve thought that someone in the Divine Temple of Nothing would tell him that there was a tomb from reality waiting to be explored?","Excitement crept up in Lu Yun’s heart and though he wanted to decline, the words refused to come out of his mouth.","“Formula dao tells me that the way to improve my strength lies within the divine temple, but it might not be the temple itself,” he murmured. “Can it be the tomb?”","“Yes! It’s got to be that tomb!” The Light Deity’s eyes shone so bright that it was as if they were two light bulbs. “That tomb is our chance to survive and you want to grow stronger, so come explore it with us!” He capered with delight.","Lu Yun rubbed his forehead, beginning to think that this guy was a little weird. In fact, the entire Divine Temple of Nothing was weird. Was this the true mastermind behind the scenes and the enemy they’d been opposing all along?”","It seemed a little... ludicrous.","Putting aside the Fire God and others, this Light Deity fellow seemed completely nuts. He spoke garbled nonsense and an unusual fervor gleamed out of his eyes. But there was no question that he was a powerhouse, the kind that could crush Lu Yun to death with a finger.","He wouldn’t even have time to deploy the Dragonspike Litany before the Light Deity killed him. And yet, Lu Yun felt a complete absence of danger, particularly from the man’s emotions. There was only a plea for help.","“Calm down first and tell me more about the tomb.” Lu Yun sat down cross-legged, opening himself up to something that he hadn’t said to the temples of the five elements. He hadn’t been willing to help them against the other gods of the Divine Temple of Nothing because he was here to grow stronger, not to get involved in random nonsense.","Repeated calculations told him that there was indeed some value in the Light Deity’s words. There was a tomb here, one from the reality outside the nothing. It was the fortuitous opportunity he searched for that would help him grow stronger.","“The Fire God brought me here, so why didn’t she tell me about this tomb?” he asked the Light Deity.","“Because she doesn’t know about it.” The man calmed down and sat down next to Lu Yun, quite concerned that the young man wouldn’t help him. “The Fire God and her fire envoys are the only ones who can leave the Divine Temple of Nothing.","“If she learns about it, then God, Che, and their people will know about it. They’ll interfere with the tomb.”","“Is that bad?” Lu Yun found it odd. Since the Light God Temple was convinced the tomb held the way to end the great destruction, why was it bad for everyone to explore it together?","“Bad,” the Light Deity shook his head. “We are traitors to God and Che. The only possible treatment of traitors is death.","“When the four divine temples of the Worlds, Chaos, Hongmeng, and Nothing were first built, God used merciless tactics to suppress all life. He killed countless powerhouses before he became the true god.","“We’ll be the first to die if he recovers,” the Light Deity said solemnly. “We do this because we want to live, not out of a sense of responsibility for creation. It would be meaningless to us if the great destruction was terminated, but we are dead.”","His words were very selfish, yet quite rational. They’d fended off the great destruction for countless eons not for the good of all, but because they themselves didn’t want to die. In contrast, while those of the five elements also wished to live, they took pains to save those who dwelled among the existences that’d been destroyed.","Theirs was a more ordinary selfishness, but who wasn’t selfish when it came to personal survival?","God, the Dao King, and mistress just wanted to leave this place. What did the local inhabitants have to do with them?","God was still gravely injured and the protector of immortal dao; he was very far off from returning to peak condition. Despite that, the Divine Temple of Nothing couldn’t kill him. At least, the Fire God didn’t wish to kill him.","Although the other gods couldn’t leave the divine temple, they could use a variety of methods to affect the existence within the nothing—such as the three hundred and sixty-five demon god guards.","The endless guards had been whittled down to three hundred and sixty-five, but the gods could also utilize a variety of curses and replicas. They couldn’t kill God or threaten the Dao King and the mistress, but they could create unlimited trouble and obstacles.","You guys won’t have an easy life either if we’re unhappy!","But Lu Yun was an exception. Although he was in the same camp as the mistress and God, he’d set foot on his own path and didn’t belong to either faction. Of this, the Divine Temple of Nothing saw clearly, so the Light Deity came as soon as they sensed Lu Yun’s arrival.","“Uh huh,” Lu Yun nodded. “So you still want to kill God?”","“Everything else can be discussed so long as we terminate the great destruction.” The Light Deity first nodded, then shook his head.","Their rebellion had been successful, but it resulted in God confining them to the divine temple for all of eternity. They would regain freedom only when they killed God or when God left the nothing.","When the great destruction was no longer a possibility, the mistress and Dao King would leave with God. There would be no need to kill God then. However, the divine temple’s current plan was to kill all three foreigners, so further changes might come into play.","“Then let’s talk about that tomb?” Lu Yun remained rational and prudent, despite inwardly stirring with impatience. “Since it’s fallen into the nothing, is there no path to reality inside it?”","“There is,” the other answered frankly. “But it’s a dead path. Someone set foot on it once and turned to dust after taking three steps, returning to the nothing.”","“Are you certain that there is a way to end the great destruction within the tomb?” Lu Yun asked with bafflement.","“No... but there’s always hope!” Enthusiasm sparkled out of the Light Deity’s eyes again."]},{"number":2133,"title":"Chapter 2133: Chapter 2088 – Dead Spirits Within the Tomb","paragraphs":["Chapter 2088: Dead Spirits Within the Tomb","The Divine Temple of Nothing sent the Light Deity to explain everything to Lu Yun when the young man arrived. The connotations behind their actions were clear—Lu Yun had no way out of this. He had to go to the tomb, come hell or high water. He had no chance to communicate with the outside world.","Another point was also clear to Lu Yun—once they excavated whatever was buried inside, he would die whether or not there was a method to end the great destruction.","The Divine Temple of Nothing would not permit him to live.","But neither was he afraid of them.","The ancient tomb was right there and he was incredibly curious, even filled with yearning. If he didn’t go, the divine temple would move against him right now.","“You’re right,” Lu Yun nodded. “It’s always better to have hope. Let’s go now and see what the tomb from reality is like.”","“Really??” The Light Deity looked at him with agitation.","Lu Yun frowned slightly. He could sense the other’s emotions—they looked like excitement, but they were actually as calm as still water. There was even a hint of killing intent within them.","The young man nodded instead of tearing down the facade, operating formula dao at the same time to analyze the tomb.","“Oh?” Lu Yun started. He found something particularly interesting. “The barrier of nothing... the ancient tomb’s pierced through the barrier and is embedded within it?”","His eyes lit up. Formula dao had always skirted around the barrier of nothing as it was the source of the great destruction, the annihilator of all that would return everything to nothing. Formula dao was no exception as it would be instantly rendered to nonexistence if it touched the barrier.","But the ancient tomb had pierced through it!","While Lu Yun would continue to avoid the barrier, he could utilize the opening to deduce reality on the other side!","However, he could only determine that the barrier had been pierced though. The other side remained out of reach for the moment as formula dao wasn’t strong enough and the tomb was too overwhelming. He needed to enhance formula dao before entering the tomb. That way, he could analyze the other side of reality when he reached its end.","As for passing through the opening and entering reality...","The thought didn’t cross Lu Yun’s mind.","He didn’t know what lay on the other side of reality and if it was even suitable for life. Why had the mistress, Dao King, and God appeared on this side?","The only thing about them that he was certain of was that they’d lost their memories of reality. Going home was just an instinctive urge. He needed to know more about reality on the other side before he made any decisions.","This was too important.","...Perhaps... The guys of the Divine Temple of Nothing were right. Maybe what they should do is to find a solution to the great destruction instead of running off to another unknown, foreign world.","“I can’t make any promises, let’s take a look first,” Lu Yun nodded.","“Let’s go!” The Light Deity seemed the perfect picture of frantic excitement as he rushed forward, but Lu Yun remained on guard, ready to use the Dragonspike Litany at any time. He wasn’t able to destroy the divine temple—as the Fire God had happily explained earlier—but nailing a mere Light Deity to death was very doable.","He was the only sign of life that Lu Yun saw in the rest of the Divine Temple of Nothing’s territory. There was nothing else, and no traces of life in a world that seemed otherwise vibrant and lush. Lu Yun arrived at no further answers when he employed formula dao.","The ancient tomb from reality was within the divine temple. Harrowing spatial fractures extended from it as spatial storms roared around the structure. If any of the storms made it to the Three Thousand, the realm would be obliterated.","A bleeding tombstone lay in the center of the fissures. Drops of bright red blood flowed into the cracks and were swallowed without a trace. Numerous characters were carved on the tombstone in a special font, but Lu Yun didn’t recognize any of them.","They were two worlds without any interaction, two wholly different civilizations. Even the Tome of Life and Death couldn’t provide any clues to what the words might say.","“Is that the ancient tomb?”","There was only a tombstone—the tomb proper was embedded in the void. Perhaps the barrier of nothing could be found on the other side of the void...","There was no concept of time in the void, so they might be on the outskirts of the Three Thousand, or they might be on the fringes of the barrier of nothing. The Divine Temple of Nothing could be anywhere.","“Prepare a few things for me.” Lu Yun suddenly turned to the Light Deity next to him.","“What do you want?” The other blinked.","“Your life,” Lu Yun said calmly.","“Huh?”","BOOM.","A pillar of black light descended from the sky and smashed into the Light Deity. He howled as the faint golden light around him dissipated, revealing an inky-black form.","“The Dragonquake Scripture!” he roared.","“Everyone in the nothing knows that I possess this method. You’re the only one who doesn’t.” Lu Yun cocked his head and looked at the other with a half smile. “I’m guessing you haven’t had the chance to make most of your moves yet and that most of the divine temple’s powerhouses are still alive, aren’t they? The only one dead is the unlucky Light God.”","The Light Deity was fake. Even though he didn’t reveal any flaws in his act, Lu Yun’s Karmic Tree could read emotions. The fraud had disguised himself very well, but he hadn’t been able to fool the Karmic Tree.","He’d also underestimated formula dao.","Lu Yun might’ve fallen for it if he hadn’t seen the ancient tomb. But with it close at hand and formula dao in constant operation, it immediately determined what this so-called Light Deity was.","An evil spirit from the ancient tomb!","In other words, he was from the reality beyond the barrier, but he was a dead spirit! Just like... the hordes of dead and yin spirits in the nothing. They were the same species and more terrifying than ordinary ghostly entities.","Was this the source of dead spirits in the nothing?","No, it was just a dead spirit from the ancient tomb, the same as the ones that Lu Yun had seen in the chief worlds. They weren’t related as this one’s only goal was the Divine Temple of Nothing.","Lu Yun’s arrival was outside of its expectations. It’d rushed here and told Lu Yun about the tomb, wanting to borrow it to kill the young man. It didn’t know about Lu Yun, yet none of this was a coincidence. Lu Yun’s presence at the Divine Temple of Nothing was fully part of someone’s plans.","Maybe the Dao King, or maybe the mistress.","Craaaack.","The pillar formed from the Dragonspike Litany brimmed with terrifying power and pierced through the dead spirit. Black flames sparked from it as it began to crack apart.","“Hahahaha!!” it snarled with laughter. “You pathetic ants will never escape from this cage...”","“I don’t need to,” Lu Yun responded calmly. “I just need to refine you.”","Whoosh!","The fire of reincarnation appeared in his hand and slowly set the dead spirit ablaze."]},{"number":2134,"title":"Chapter 2134: Chapter 2089: Lu Yun’s Tomb","paragraphs":["Chapter 2089: Lu Yun’s Tomb","“What does refining me have to do with you escaping from this place? If refining me would make that possible, I would refine myself before you have the chance to!” Overpowering anguish clung tightly to the dead spirit. It was a very foreign, yet very real feeling.","He’d yet to experience pain again after becoming a dead spirit, so while he howled with agony, it was tinged with a few hints of greed and satisfaction.","Pain!","His long lost senses of pain were returned to him. Although this was torment, it was a torment that he enjoyed.","He enjoyed the pain.","Lu Yun sighed as he watched the diminishing spirit. The guy really didn’t know anything, he was just a dead spirit.","A dead spirit sufficient to destroy the entire Divine Temple of Nothing.","The fire of reincarnation was the bane of all dead things. As opposed to saying they were slowly burned alive or refined, they were more sent through reincarnation to become another type of existence. For example, dregs of the nothing.","Even god-level ghostly entities were vaporized by the fire of reincarnation and turned to dust.","It was also a mark of Lu Yun’s current level of strength. If he was strong enough, he would be able to reincarnate the spirit into something different entirely, maybe even something he wanted to create. He’d be able to trace its past life and reverse death.","The process was similar to the Resurrection death art, but even more heaven defying. The death art could only be applied to those dead within the last seven days, but the fire of resurrection could revive even a pile of bone shards.","It’d been the same circumstances when Lu Yun recruited his Envoys of Samsara. The envoys were limited in number, but the fire of reincarnation could be endlessly used once it was perfected and Lu Yun’s strength reached the appropriate heights.","Such were the answers he came to when he refined the dead spirit and made calculations through formula dao.","“All things can be reincarnated.” Lu Yun’s comprehension grew deeper as he watched the dead spirit gradually turn into dregs, then shift from dregs to nothing.","“Then...” His heart spasmed painfully. “If I grow strong enough in the future, can I use the fire of reincarnation to reverse death? No, wait, can I use it to reverse the subjective and objective, turning the objective world into a subjective world?","“My subjective world? I could command all with a single thought, dismissing death and reincarnation, making it so that all things move according to my will?” Lu Yun’s breathing hitched and sped up.","The fire of reincarnation... the power of reincarnation!","It did indeed possess that ability, but he wasn’t strong enough yet to fully deploy reincarnation’s true strength. The ultimate peak of reincarnation was to reincarnate objectivity and subjectivity!","His heart pounded, but the revelations disappeared after reincarnation completely erased the dead spirit. It was as if his comprehension had been a dream. He remembered faint hints of it after waking up, but lost the feeling he’d grasped in his dream.","He fully remembered what he’d dreamed about, but completely forgot how he’d arrived at the conclusion and the spark of inspiration he’d followed to deduce his conclusions.","“The fire of reincarnation isn’t a fire without roots. The dead spirits are its fuel,” he took a deep breath. “Formula dao has to do with the fire of reincarnation as well. The more the latter blooms, the stronger formula dao is.","“If I want to deduce information that is more deeply buried, I need to find stronger dead spirits and use them to fuel the fire of reincarnation. The fire is an outward expression of reincarnation!”","Everything turned into flames when it burned. Thus, burning flames represented the process of reincarnation. Flames were the outward expression of the power of reincarnation.","Out of the five elements, fire was the most special. The other four all gave rise to fire. Even fire’s counter—water—could result in water fire or ice fire.","“The path I walk next is to incorporate all fires within creation and meld them into the fire of reincarnation...” Lu Yun spread out his hands and watched a colorless fire blossom in his hand.","“No, the fire of this nothing is insufficient to support the fire of reincarnation,” he murmured. “The fire of reincarnation is already the strongest beneath the heavens. It won’t evolve no matter how many other flames it absorbs. It will at most turn into a ladder that enables me to slowly sip at the fire of reincarnation.","“I won’t grow strong enough in this process, so I will ultimately end up being reincarnated by the flame. I must get stronger.” He could see the way to enhancing the fire of reincarnation, but he still didn’t know how he himself could grow stronger.","“Perhaps... I should set another dead spirit on fire and see if I can deduce a way to strengthen myself.” He looked at the ancient tomb in front of him. If there were more dead spirits inside, he could utilize formula dao after setting the alight and gain a few more clues.","Lu Yun had thought that all he needed to do was keep fighting to grow stronger, but it now looked like he’d been too naive.","Battles could improve strength, but would do nothing for his cultivation level. He was a sacred supreme, an incredibly strong sacred supreme.","What came after that? And after that? How was he supposed to reach it?","Lu Yun had no idea. The path of sacred supremes was unexplored frontier in the nothing. The cultivation system it contained was to follow the path of nothing and become a Nihil World Sovereign, then ultimately...","Poof’ing into nothing.","Just like the path of old in the fourth realm.","But in the fourth realm, someone had hewn a new path of accessing sequence to avoid becoming nothing. When this nothing was the apex of their world, what stronger sequence was here to access?","Any stronger dao was obscured by the barrier of nothing. If they could break it and guide the great dao of that reality into the nothing... that would strengthen the denizens to the point where they would be able to break the barrier of nothing.","It was a quandary. The indestructible barrier of nothing stood in front of them.","“Forget it, let’s take a look inside first and see if I can find other dead spirits.” Lu Yun didn’t come to any new answers after consulting formula dao. He deployed Boundless Step and entered the tomb, causing some changes to appear on the tombstone after he left.","The characters changed from an indecipherable language to that of the common language of the nothing. Blood seeped from the tombstone into the ground.","Lu Yun’s Tomb."]},{"number":2135,"title":"Chapter 2135: Chapter 2090: Seventeen Hundred and Eighty-Eight","paragraphs":["Chapter 2090: Seventeen Hundred and Eighty-Eight","“How many Lu Yuns is this?” an empty voice echoed in the desolate world.","“Fifty-six,” answered an equally empty voice devoid of emotion.","“But this is the strongest Lu Yun yet, he’s much stronger than the fifty-five that came before him.” A hint of hope slowly grew in the first voice.","“You said the same thing when the fifty-fifth one came. He died a grisly death in the tomb all the same and was buried in it.”","Lu Yun’s Tomb.","The tomb that buried Lu Yun.","“There is no space or time in the nothing. Perhaps the first fifty-five were all the same one,” sounded a third voice.","Time was a measurement. If the power of time existed, then experts could utilize it to accelerate or reverse time. But if there was no power of time and only measurement, then nothing would exist.","The same person could set out from the same place in time, but arrive at the tomb at different times. There was no power of time here, just the measurement of time. Thus, the Lu Yuns that arrived at different moments could only come one by one.","The next one would not come if the previous one didn’t die. They were all the same Lu Yun from the same starting point. They simply arrived at different times when they traveled to a place without time.","“But why were there differences in strength in the Lu Yuns that came?”","“I don’t know. If he dies, there will be a fifty-seventh Lu Yun to come who is even stronger.”","“Ai, we’re all dead people. What do we care about this for?”","“Let’s keep waiting. Our chance to come back to life will arrive only after Lu Yun fills in the tomb.”","......","“Why do I feel like I’ve come here before?” Lu Yun didn’t dive into exploring the tomb after entering. He stood in place and thought quietly to himself. “Have I been here before?”","He looked around blankly and operated formula dao, coming up empty handed after a round of calculations. Formula dao could analyze certain aspects of the tomb when he was outside it, but it was as if he wandered around in a maze after entering.","“Wait, what am I analyzing the tomb for?” He laughed at himself and deployed formula dao again, this time on himself. If he felt that he’d come here before, then the problem lay with him and not the tomb.","“So indeed I have been by... seventeen hundred and eighty-seven times.” Lu Yun slowly wound his deductions to a halt after a long time, his expression grave and solemn. “This is the seventeen hundred and eighty-eighth time. I died in the tomb on all of my previous trips.","“Rather than the temporal difference of the nothing, it has to do with the power of reincarnation. Reincarnation traverses the nothing and reality. In my current form, I am nearly immortal. I wonder what will happen this time.” Lu Yun had come and died in the tomb again and again, but the power of reincarnation had seeped deep into his bones. As long as there was a temporal difference and the power of reincarnation, he would not truly die.","He would resurrect again and again from the origin point and come here again and again, experiencing the same things as before until he entered the tomb. The Fire and Wave Gods from earlier hadn’t detected anything amiss. Such was the marvelous effect of reincarnation.","After the Tome of Life and Death transformed into a golden page, it became the apex of the nothing. When Lu Yun was immersed in the power of reincarnation, he was undying. The current him was like the previous Land of Reincarnation. If he died, he would repeat the loop, cycling through his previous affairs.","The core medium of reincarnation—the Tome of Life and Death—was within Lu Yun’s body. He only needed to utilize formula dao to review everything that had taken place before. He just needed to use it on himself.","Dying more than seventeen hundred times was an indication of how dangerous the tomb was. The dead temple masters of the Divine Temple of Nothing had long since grown numb to the young man’s repeated deaths and arrivals.","They were dead and influenced by the tomb’s power, which was why they could witness his repeated actions. Those alive were affected by Lu Yun’s power of reincarnation and journeyed the cycle with him.","The Light Deity that he’d killed came back to life because of his death and met him again and again.","“The previous seventeen hundred and eighty-seven deaths were because I ran into zones of danger, so I just need to evade them. What a pity that the Tome of Life and Death is strong enough, but I am too weak to deploy its entire strength...”","An eruption of power from the Tome of Life and Death would fill Lu Yun’s body beyond capacity. He would cycle through reincarnation once more after his body exploded. At the same time, he wouldn’t have discovered he was undying if he hadn’t died a few times.","He had to continue his explorations.","Lu Yun knew that the dangers of the tomb couldn’t be plumbed with just a thousand deaths. He avoided the places he’d identified before and headed in a new direction.","“Enough already, damn you!” A massive voice boomed from the depths of the tomb. “Dying again and again and coming again and again! I’m sick of it even if you aren’t! Tell me what you want, I’ll give it to you!!”","“Um... you’re the one who killed me all those times before, aren’t you?” Lu Yun paused and looked warily at the pitch black tomb.","The voice fell silent.","“Forget it, I’ll explore some more myself. No wonder I couldn’t find the way to break the layouts before, there’s an incredibly strong tomb owner here,” Lu Yun chuckled and started forward again. He wouldn’t die—he’d at most return to the starting point and come in again.","“Out with it, what do you want?” The infuriated voice came again when he stepped forward.","“The way to end the great destruction,” he said.","“It doesn’t exist. It is an objective rhythm that cannot be changed unless you are strong enough to affect the objective with the subjective, making the objective your subjective. Otherwise, the barrier of nothing will destroy everything within the nothing again and again.”","“Mmhmm.” Lu Yun nodded and walked forward.","“Are you listening to me??” The tomb owner’s voice grew exasperated.","“I am,” Lu Yun responded as he walked forward. Having died more than seventeen hundred times, Lu Yun had summarized his experiences—there was no solution to this tomb.","The only way to break it was to fill it in with lives—his lives—and explore it. Every death resulted in a lesson, a mistake that he would not repeat.","“I can send you to the real existence. It may contain the answer you want,” the tomb owner said.","“No need, I can find my way there myself.” Lu Yun curled his lip, not believing a single word that the tomb owner said. He’d already seen the words “Lu Yun’s Tomb” on the tombstone."]},{"number":2136,"title":"Chapter 2136: Chapter 2091: Explosion, Explosion Again","paragraphs":["Chapter 2091: Explosion, Explosion Again","The tombstone hadn’t said “Lu Yun’s Tomb” at first. Only after his fifty-sixth entry did the characters appear on the tombstone.","Plainly, the tomb owner was behind it.","Whatever level or kind of existence the dead might be, their greatest desire was to live again. Death was anguish and the only way to escape anguish was resurrection. Even a saint who’d sacrificed themselves for the sake of others would want to live again after dying. Their desire would burn so fiercely that they would be willing to destroy anything if they could come back to life.","The same went for the owner of the tomb. Upon realizing that Lu Yun was undying with the power of reincarnation, it wanted the power for itself so it could resurrect.","However, the Tome of Life and Death was Lu Yun’s and the power of reincarnation was one with the young man. It wouldn’t be so easy to seize it. Thus, the tomb owner changed tactics to burying Lu Yun. As for how it’d then seize the power of reincarnation, Lu Yun didn’t know.","But there was one fact that always held true, and that the words of ghosts could not be trusted. Not a single word or even punctuation mark could be believed. It was impossible that the other wanted to send Lu Yun to reality on the other side.","“What a pity that I never remember anything that happened. I’m brought back to the starting point after I die and need to start anew.” Lu Yun looked around, vexed.","If he could remember everything that took place before, he would make certain plans before entering the tomb and be able to take appropriate action. Death here signified the end and starting over from the beginning. He forgot everything on his current attempt—such was the law of reincarnation.","Starting over didn’t mean retracing his steps from the moment of birth, but from the moment that he set foot on this path of death. Only when Lu Yun returned to the same place that he’d died nearly two thousand times could he discover some clues and regain his memories of everything that’d taken place before.","The tomb owner was so unfathomably strong that Lu Yun’s power of reincarnation couldn’t affect him. It was as if the two were two different planes—the Land of Reincarnation and the chief worlds outside. The power of reincarnation circulated again and again inside the Land of Reincarnation without affecting the chief worlds.","“How about I don’t die this time?” Lu Yun swung his head around, but realized that he wouldn’t find the path to resolving everything even if he didn’t die.","The Dragonquake Scripture...","He’d deployed it seventy-eight times in the tome and died to a mysterious power each time he did so. It could resolve the conundrum of the tomb, but Lu Yun caught only the backlash because he wasn’t strong enough.","Or rather, the tomb owner killed Lu Yun the split second that danger descended.","There was no room for him to strike back in this locale. He could only continuously probe the premises and try to identify where the tomb owner’s strength didn’t reach. That would be the flaw in the tomb.","Nothing was perfect amongst creation; all things held their own weaknesses. The same applied to the tomb and the tomb owner, who seemed to be irritated that Lu Yun didn’t respond. There was desire in its heart and Lu Yun’s repeated deaths tied it up in knots.","Such were the effects of reincarnation.","Reincarnation could destroy dead things and bring them back to life; it had an exceedingly powerful effect on the dead. Lu Yun’s continual usage of reincarnation to come back to life was also diminishing the tomb owner in the process. However, it was such a minute effect that neither Lu Yun nor the tomb owner realized it.","All the same, it subconsciously shifted the tomb owner’s mentality. Granted, the dead had no mentality. They exploded with a touch.","......","“You’ll make it through yourself? A pathetic ant like you?” the tomb owner snorted. It didn’t give up tempting Lu Yun.","“Mmhmm.” The young man inclined his head and ignored it, taking another step forward.","KABOOM!","His body bloomed like a firework.","He’d been blown up.","......","“Have you considered things further?”","“Nope.”","KABOOM!","Another explosion.","......","“You won’t get to take another step forward if you don’t agree.”","“Then I’ll just stand still here.”","KABOOM!","Explosion.","......","“How about I send you to reality?”","“Nah.”","KABOOM!","Explosion.","......","Another explosion.","......","Explosion.","......","Explosion.","......","“Kid, why are you so stubborn?!” The tomb owner was on the verge of mental collapse after endless repeats and explosions. Meanwhile, the temple masters who’d become one with the tomb were completely numb to things.","They were different from the Fire God and the other gods because the latter group was as if residents of the Land of Reincarnation. Thus, they would continuously loop with Lu Yun. The dead temple masters, however, were as if inhabitants of the chief worlds. They silently watched the Land of Reincarnation repeat itself.","“Huh?” Lu Yun looked at the tomb owner blankly. He’d just set foot into the tomb and had yet to analyze himself and receive information from the past. Therefore, he didn’t know what the stranger was talking about.","“Forget it.”","Explosion!","......","“Haven’t you had enough yet?” Lu Yun was growing irritated as well and spoke before the tomb owner could. He hadn’t taken a single step in all of these instances, much less search for the way out of the tomb.","“You’ll have to continuously repeat yourself here if you don’t agree to being sent to reality on the other side.” Smugness tinged the tomb owner’s voice.","“I know what you want to do, you just want to steal my power of reincarnation so you can come back to life.” Lu Yun looked wordlessly up at the sky. “You’ve lured me to the depths of the tomb but still can’t claim the power. You’re playing with fire.”","He opened his right hand and displayed the jumping flame of reincarnation.","“I’ve transmuted the power into fire. If you bury me here, the best possible outcome for you is to be set ablaze by the fire of reincarnation and turn into nothing. The other possible outcome is a fate worse than death and endlessly cycling between life and death.”","After experiencing so many deaths—at least eight thousand, if not ten thousand—Lu Yun had a decent grasp of what the tomb owner wanted. It wanted to bury Lu Yun here so the young man would become one with the tomb. The tomb owner would have procured a substitute and a stand-in for itself. After stealing the power of reincarnation, it would be able to slip away as Lu Yun’s replacement.","It would live in Lu Yun’s stead.","Every time Lu Yun deduced what’d happened to him before, he would also follow his previous line of thinking and analyze what the tomb owner wished to accomplish.","There was great terror between life and death and also great nourishment. A tiny change occurred each time Lu Yun died. He’d harvested that greatest nourishment when he first arrived in the world of immortals—his heart and mind underwent a metamorphosis that enabled his rapid rise and eventual establishment of his own territory in the world of immortals.","If it was the Lu Yun of Earth...","He’d just be a tomb raider for hire.","After repeated deaths and enlightenment, his mind was clear. His strength didn’t change, but formula dao took a qualitative leap forward. He’d deduced the tomb owner’s plans and its ending.","Lu Yun’s own wasn’t any better off—it would be a scheme that ended in grave casualties to both sides."]},{"number":2137,"title":"Chapter 2137: Chapter 2092: Unwilling To Be Lonely","paragraphs":["Chapter 2092: Unwilling To Be Lonely","The strengthening of formula dao and improvement of Lu Yun’s strength was most likely to be found in these repeated instances of death. He just hadn’t realized it yet, so he’d stopped to discuss terms with the tomb owner.","If he realized it, he would likely change tactics and purposefully enrage the tomb owner so he could ensure the repeated deaths. With the tomb owner growing irritated, Lu Yun was equally annoyed himself.","Does this chump think dying and coming back to life again and again is fun?","“Is that so?” Unmoved, the tomb owner manifested a human face in the air—a woman’s face. Long hair trailed past sparkling eyes and she was pretty on the whole, but the dense air of death shone between her brows. She was plainly dead.","“Then die a few more times.” She didn’t believe the young man.","KABOOM!","Lu Yun exploded again.","......","Rumble!","On his eighteen thousandth death, a ball of white flames rushed out of Lu Yun’s body and set him on fire. The tomb owner’s approaching power was dispersed by the power of reincarnation.","“Thank you.”","Lu Yun looked up to see a male face, one with a greatly relieved expression on his face. The young man had only realized his strength was climbing when he neared his eighteen thousandth death. After that, he began actively provoking the tomb owner.","What he didn’t understand now was why the woman’s face had turned into a man’s face. Was the tomb owner a man or a woman?","None of it mattered.","The power of reincarnation pierced through Lu Yun’s body and replaced the immortal force circulating inside him. The fire of reincarnation ignited a page of gold, turning him translucent. Even the Dragonquake Scripture stirred to life.","“You’re curious, aren’t you, why I’ve turned from a woman into a man?” the tomb owner chuckled. “Because I am you right now.”","A figure landed from the air—a limber, handsome young man who looked the same as Lu Yun!","“Did you think you were the only one plotting away?” the tomb owner chortled. “A tomb is a world of the dead. Even if you possess the power of reincarnation, this tomb becomes your tomb if you die here too many times.","“While you tried to provoke me and bade me take you through life and death to enhance your strength, I was borrowing your deaths at the same time. I used the power of death they created to escape from this tomb!","“You will be the new tomb owner in my stead and be buried here. I am finally free to reincarnate!! Hahahaha!!” The tomb owner threw its head back with unbridled laughter. Although it was dead, it was no fool. As an unparalleled powerhouse, it had its own plans.","So what if Lu Yun grew stronger? He would be buried here in the end. The characters of “Lu Yun’s Tomb” on the tombstone were the foreshadowing.","The tomb owner craved life. He wouldn’t hesitate to leap at even a chance of becoming a mortal with less than a hundred years of life. His core essence was powerful and he wouldn’t lose himself when he reincarnated. He would retain his memories and swiftly restart cultivation. It would only be a matter of time before he reached his previous heights.","“Uh huh.” Lu Yun nodded slowly and smirked at the tomb owner. “Your plan was very successful, but there’s one last step left to it, isn’t there?”","“Yes,” the tomb owner nodded. It looked very similar to Lu Yun, but there were a few minute differences. The final step left was to kill Lu Yun with its own hands and bury the young man here!","Anyone else—even the temple masters—would’ve already been buried by the rules of the tomb. But Lu Yun wielded reincarnation and had become one with it. He was reincarnation and reincarnation was Lu Yun, so the tomb owner needed to personally take action and utilize the rules of the tomb to buy the young man.","“I will now personally bury you here and leave, regaining my long awaited freedom and life!” The tomb owner couldn’t control the joy on his face.","“Mmhmm,” Lu Yun nodded. “Can I ask you a question before that? Will I find the way to end the great destruction if I defeat you?”","Black light sparkled from the tomb owner’s eyes and it stared at Lu Yun for a long moment before sighing. “Why are you so stubborn? Or is it as the others say, that you really are a saint?","“Reincarnation is the rule of all living things. Death and destruction, unceasing, unabating. That is the rule—just as this nothing undergoes a reincarnation of new life to destruction. As the manifestation of reincarnation, will you go against who you are?”","After repeated deaths and rebirths, the tomb owner already knew everything there was to know about Lu Yun’s life.","“I am no saint,” the young man shook his head. “I don’t know why people call me that either. My friends, family, and dao partners all live here. If the nothing perishes and we alone survive, what is the point in that?","“We would only face unending loneliness.","“I don’t want to be lonely and I don’t want my dao partners, friends, and family to be lonely travelers. Therefore, I will protect everything here so that no one is lonely,” Lu Yun concluded. “You just need to tell me if I will find the solution or not.”","He’d discovered a problem early on. The great destruction of the nothing was not part of the rhythm of reincarnation. It was all due to the abruptly appearing barrier of nothing—an accidental destruction.","It wasn’t part of reincarnation as reincarnation followed the six orders of the highest degree—inception, ethos, burgeon, creation, opposition, and nirvana. The barrier of nothing forcefully interposed itself during the process of burgeon and incited nirvana in a violent fashion. Life was yet to progress to creation when it was forced into nirvana.","This was a violation of reincarnation.","“No,” the tomb owner shook its head. “You will not find the way to end the great destruction even if you defeat me. That is possible only if you travel to the reality on the other side... But the situation there may be worse than here.”","A strange smile crossed the tomb owner’s face.","“Alright then... I’ll have to figure out how to get there and take a look,” Lu Yun sighed.","“You’ll never have the chance to.”","Boom!","Dense death qi unfurled from the tomb owner’s body and formed a massive spear that stabbed at Lu Yun.","“Heavenfall?? Who are you?!” Lu Yun gasped when he saw the weapon. Heavenfall was God’s weapon!","The tomb owner stabbed the spear forward instead of answering, piercing through Lu Yun’s body with formidable death qi. The young man shook and transformed into white flames, vacating the premises.","He glowered at the tomb owner.","“Don’t worry, I’m not God.” The tomb owner grinned, victory within its grasp."]},{"number":2138,"title":"Chapter 2138: Chapter 2093: Worldcarver","paragraphs":["Chapter 2093: Worldcarver","He wasn’t God, but he possessed God’s Heavenfall??","God once sent the spear to Lu Yun so that the young man could extract himself from peril. He would never mistake another weapon for Heavenfall. It was the genuine article, something that Lu Yun would recognize even if it was reduced to a pile of dust.","What was it doing in the tomb owner’s hand?","Lu Yun operated formula dao to analyze the karmic repercussions within, but the tomb owner didn’t give him a chance to come to any conclusions.","BOOM.","Heavenfall exploded with energy and an enormous “execute” character appeared in the sky.","Execute, execution... to execute all life!","It targeted every drop of Lu Yun’s vitality—even the power of reincarnation could not operate. His death was guaranteed if the character connected. He would not be able to come back to life this time.","The character could pierce through reincarnation. In fact, the entire tomb targeted him and was waiting to bury him. After countless reincarnations and deaths, there were thousands of tendrils of connections between the tomb and Lu Yun. He was half of a tomb owner.","If he died here, he would be the new tomb owner. Forever suppressed, forever trapped.","Just like the previous tomb owner.","It would remain that way until another person with the power of reincarnation entered the tomb and repeated the process that Lu Yun had undergone.","He couldn’t move.","Although his strength was on par with a temple master, he still couldn’t move. Such was the power of burial found within a tomb. While it suppressed the tomb owner at this moment, the tomb owner was able to break through its strength when wielding Heavenfall.","It almost seemed... that Heavenfall had been created for this moment. It was meant to pierce through the layout of burial and kill Lu Yun.","God had built the Divine Temple of Nothing and its worshippers had betrayed him. The mistress was heavily injured and the Dao King not much better off.","God...","Was God truly injured? Was the truth really what he saw?","Every step had been a lie. Whenever a new riddle was solved and every time he thought he saw the final answer, there always turned out to be an even bigger issue or trap behind it.","One that Lu Yun never saw coming.","This time, he thought that the tomb in the Divine Temple of Nothing was the final matter to be resolved in the nothing. And now? How naive and foolish he’d been.","The biggest trap was God!","Lu Yun’s eyes were wide open as the fire of reincarnation spewed from them, forming two pillars of flame that met the “execute” character.","Poof!","The character dispersed, but blood flowed out of Lu Yun’s mouth and nose. His fingers twitched, followed by his body relaxing. He was free of the ancient tomb’s influence.","“You are indeed not God. If God had attacked me, I’d already be dead.” A sword appeared in Lu Yun’s hand when he gently clenched his fist.","Quietus.","The weapon that was named in conjunction with Worldcarver and Heavenfall was in his hands. Heavenfall belonged to God, Worldcarver belonged to Pangu, and Quietus... belonged to Lu Yun.","Although he’d given it to his disciple, this kind of treasure was eternally Lu Yun’s once it acknowledged a master.","“You...” Slight changes occurred in the face that was so similar to Lu Yun’s. The tomb owner wasn’t startled by Quietus—he’d seen it through Lu Yun’s lives and knew that it existed.","Quietus could hold its own against Heavenfall. No, it vastly outstripped the current Heavenfall.","Heavenfall was God’s and the tomb owner was only borrowing it. Although it could deploy all of the spear’s might, it was just a weapon to the tomb owner.","Lu Yun, however, was different. Quietus was his and, in fact, part of his life. That had been fated the moment he picked up the sword. It was a fact that would not change no matter who he gave the sword to.","What the tomb owner feared was why Lu Yun could deploy the sword’s true strength.","Although it was Lu Yun’s, his cultivation level and life form should not have been enough to fully activate the sword. It should not have been able to erupt with full force and manifest the “Quiet” part of its name.","Quietus wasn’t a sharp weapon, but it banished Heavenfall’s strength when they collided.","Quiet!","The end to all, an end to life, and an end to all paths!","“Why?” A stunned tomb owner stared at Lu Yun. “You’re just a rootless being born in this part of nothing, you can’t possibly leverage the power of the four genesis weapons...”","A Heavenfall at full strength was still not the tomb owner’s personal weapon, so it couldn’t fully release the spear’s strength. Even with the “execute” character hovering in the air, it was still unable to be one with the tomb owner and utilize its full might.","Worldcarver, Heavenfall, Quietus, and Creatio.","These were the four genesis weapons from the other side of the void. The legends of yore spoke of these four weapons crafting reality. Worldcarver and Creatio had developed the world while Heavenfall and Quietus destroyed the nothing outside of existence, making it a tangible thing.","This part of the nothing was a cage, a fake world. That made its denizens fake beings. Although the genesis weapons were theirs, they were unable to bring the weapons’ true meaning into play.","But Lu Yun had done it. He walked up to the tomb owner with the sword in his hand. Heavenfall trembled and left the tomb owner’s hand, breaking through the air.","Lu Yun ignored it. He simply looked at the tomb owner and murmured, “So... God... is the bad guy, isn’t he?”","“It’s just a matter of perspective.” The tomb owner nodded. There was no right or wrong, it was just a matter of being on Lu Yun’s opposing side.","Truthfully speaking, the young man didn’t have a side. Everything he was was a result of God’s handiwork, but never did Lu Yun imagine that God would raise him to be on the opposing side. Everything that he’d ever encountered flashed through Lu Yun’s brain. Akasha ghosts, the divine court, the Sword of Chaos...","While they seemed to be the work of the mistress and Dao King, it’d all been due to God—including the Divine Temple of Nothing. God had established the divine temples, so what was this talk of rebellion?","Its powerhouses may not have truly betrayed God. Perhaps they thought they did, but it’d all been under God’s control.","As for why...","God once called the mistress his master. God was just a servant. That was probably why.","Of course, there were many things that Lu Yun was yet to see, such as the reason for the great destruction of this nothing that violated the precepts of reincarnation.","Lu Yun was still thinking when the tomb owner began to fade away.","“Why?” the tomb owner still asked. “You are a rootless being in the cage that is this fake nothing. Why can you use a genesis weapon??”","Lu Yun stretched out a hand; the power of time twined around his fingers.","“The method of nothing...” The tomb owner smiled and gently closed his eyes, dispersing into nothing. “So they’re here too... There are more than just us in this cage of falsehood, they’ve come as well.","“Perhaps I am just a pawn...”"]},{"number":2139,"title":"Chapter 2139: Chapter 2094: It’s You","paragraphs":["Chapter 2094: It’s You","“They”...","Lu Yun sank into deep thought. The overlord of Ice had passed on the method of nothing to him and his true identity was Ancestor.","The method of nothing...","Lu Yun first used it to access the sequence of time and thus thought that that was all there was to the method. But the moment he took up Quietus again, he realized how wrong he’d been. The method of nothing could facilitate him to obtain the sword’s true power.","The method of nothing...","What was it?","Lu Yun still had no idea, but he understood that without the method, he would’ve irrevocably lost to the tomb owner and be buried in the tomb, forever trapped without hope of release.","Reincarnation would be eternally laid to rest with him.","His hands wrapped around Quietus, Lu Yun exhaled softly. Thank goodness for the method of nothing! The tomb owner hadn’t caught a hint of it even when peeking into Lu Yun’s life through reincarnation.","“This is my oversight. To think that you’ve mastered the method of nothing!” A new voice sounded in the void as Heavenfall returned to the scene. A faint shadow stood toward the front, the spear in its hand.","God.","He was here.","Or rather, he was always here and had never left.","“Why?” Lu Yun frowned at the sudden newcomer.","“Does understanding still elude you?” God’s features were obscured, preventing Lu Yun from seeing him clearly. Formula dao returned nothing but a blank haze.","“You wish to bury reincarnation, not me,” Lu Yun murmured. “I am but a tool you chose to be the bearer of reincarnation.”","“Would you believe me if I said that burying reincarnation in the tomb would end the ceaseless devastation and permit things to operate normally again?” God smiled. “Would you be willing to be buried here to stop the repeating great destruction of this nothing?”","Lu Yun looked silently at God instead of replying.","“Aren’t you doing this to go home? Why have you schemed incessantly for the sake of this part of nothing?” he asked.","“So there is something you’ve probably understood for a very long period of time,” God chuckled. “Existence is objective and we—or rather, all of life—are but accidents within existence. The vastness of objectivity was never for life. Life merely ekes out a survival in a trivial crack. This cycle of objectivity saw the birth of life and a suitable environment to house it. But what about next time?","“Therefore, I’m afraid you’ll have to suffer for the sake of the greater good. Your sacrifice will ensure that life possesses sufficient breathing space to survive in this part of nothing.” God looked silently at Lu Yun.","The young man looked back at him; he couldn’t see God’s form. Be willingly buried here? He would probably agree if he really was the Virgin Mary.","But Lu Yun was just Lu Yun. Everything he did was for his own sake or those around him. He just didn’t want to be lonely.","Be buried here for the sake of all life?","His enemies were innumerable. Wouldn’t his wives, child, disciples, and friends be slaughtered down to the last if he was buried here?","Thus, he would never do something so ludicrous.","God had also guessed the young man’s answer, so his aura continuously built as he waited. Heavenfall glowed with a bronze hue that surrounded Lu Yun.","The young man wasn’t strong enough. While he’d reached godhood, this level of strength was defined by God. That meant it was below God’s.","Far below.","God originally wanted to borrow the tomb owner’s hand to bury Lu Yun, but the young man had learnt the method of nothing at some point in time and wielded Quietus. He killed the tomb owner instead!","Therefore, God had to do the deed himself.","The mistress and Dao King were still alive and both stronger than God. God ran the risk of exposing all of his schemes and plots if he killed Lu Yun. Either of the two would take action against him.","“Your goal was never to end the great destruction,” Lu Yun sighed. “You just want to reach the pinnacle and influence objectivity with subjectivity, becoming the master of existence and the sovereign of objectivity and subjectivity.","“Your primary body has always been here. If I am buried here, you’ll be able to take control of reincarnation and use it to reach the peak that you wish. You didn’t dare expose yourself and take action before this because you were concerned that the mistress and Dao King would move against you.”","The young man saw God’s goal thanks to formula dao.","“Is there any difference with what you say?” God chuckled. “I will oversee all if I become that pinnacle of existence and objectivity will divert according to my will, becoming a paradise for life.”","“Don’t you think the mistress and Dao King will kill you for that?” Lu Yun looked at the other.","“I am the guardian of immortal dao and it protects me. They will not detect where my true self is before you die,” God smiled. “But they will notice that you are suppressed here, so we can only race against each other and see if I reach those heights first, or if they are first to arrive after your death.”","If the tomb owner successfully buried Lu Yun, the mistress and Dao King would be swift to arrive. But they wouldn’t know that God was also here, which would’ve left him more time to refine reincarnation.","But if God took action himself... all would be laid bare. The two would come at the fastest speed possible, not to save Lu Yun, but to kill God.","Therefore, God would not take action himself if he had any other choice available to him.","The two exchanged a myriad of blows as they conversed. Qi and killing intent intertwined around each other amid a clash of great daos. Blazing fires of reincarnation smashed into God’s primary body while divine power surged, bringing the “execute” character down on Lu Yun’s head.","Quietus was no match for Heavenfall, so the “quiet” character hovered around the young man, protecting his body. Reincarnation was his best weapon—its fire was sufficient to harm God.","All the same, he retreated at a steady pace. God was too strong. They were on two different levels; it was only a matter of time before he was defeated and suppressed.","Regardless, Lu Yun continued to resist. He would not admit defeat like this, even when he knew that defeat was inevitable.","The method of nothing operated at full force, turning the void around him into a black hole. The entire nothing was his foundation as the method of nothing was the only true method within it. It shared the same origins as the reality on the other side of the barrier.","Or rather, it could be said that it shared the same origins as the true nothing on the other side of the barrier.","Deluged by the method of nothing, Quietus sparkled with brilliant radiance. The entire sword turned into the “quiet” character, but still couldn’t contend against Heavenfall.","God walked up to Lu Yun at a measured pace, giving the young man a clear look at him.","“It’s... you...” Lu Yun’s expression shifted unpleasantly when he saw the man."]},{"number":2140,"title":"Chapter 2140: Chapter 2095: Life, Death, and Civilization","paragraphs":["Chapter 2095: Life, Death, and Civilization","“So it’s you!” Lu Yun evaded a fatal blow, rapidly backing up and glaring at God with clenched teeth.","The layer of ambiguity over God’s face gathered anew, obscuring his form. God smiled without a response. Heavenfall stabbed forward again, enveloping Lu Yun with the “execute” character.","Lu Yun retreated further.","“Why don’t you use the Sword of Chaos? I’d already be dead if you used the sword,” Lu Yun sneered.","“Divine dao has come under immortal dao’s banner and the Sword of Chaos is the weapon of divine dao. The mistress will sense it if it goes on the move.”","The Sword of Chaos was the ultimate weapon of the Divine Temple of Chaos. God had refined it one more time to integrate it into divine dao, whereupon divine dao slowly assimilated into immortal dao.","Thus, the current Sword of Chaos could bring less power to bear compared to Heavenfall. However, the sword was an instrument of slaughter that could execute even the Fire God. It would easily end Lu Yun if it acted in concert with the spear.","God... Dongfang Hao.","Dongfang Hao was God.","The Sword of Chaos had selected him because he was God.","He could use the akasha ghosts’ layout of absolute death to ensure his own escape because he was God.","He’d become the ruler of Exalted Major and oversaw all divines in the world of immortals because he was God.","All of this was because he was God.","He’d been by Lu Yun’s side all this time, silently watching, silently observing. His watchful eye had extended to the mistress, Dao King, Pangu, Hongjun, Fuxi, Wahuang...","That was why it was so logical for him to be here. Rather than wait in the tomb all this time, he’d come with the Fire God.","His Sword of Chaos failing to execute the Fire God was part of his plans. He knew that Lu Yun needed to follow the Fire God to reach the Divine Temple of Nothing, so he’d placed his sword intent on the Fire God.","He waited here to witness Lu Yun’s burial.","Although some unplanned flukes had occurred along the way—he hadn’t seen Ancestor pass the method of nothing to the young man, for instance—it didn’t matter in the grand scheme of things.","Lu Yun’s emotions were in turmoil after seeing that Dongfang Hao was God. Already in an inferior position to begin with, he lost even more ground. The Tome of Life and Death manifested over his head and radiated beams of golden splendor, barely managing to keep Lu Yun safe.","However, its bearer could no longer withstand the attacks. The Tome of Life and Death was his last line of defense and Lu Yun would be buried here once its defenses broke.","“The Tome of Life and Death... is more than just the bearer of reincarnation.” A distant voice traveled into Lu Yun’s ears. It was a female voice. An extraordinarily familiar female voice.","Violetgrave.","“You...” Lu Yun gaped.","Violetgrave had been freed after the six hells became one to form the sole origin hell. She was a true living being and spent her days journeying the realms. Lu Yun didn’t have the heart to ask her to shoulder any more burdens, so he never expected her to appear at a time like this.","“The Tome of Life and Death is powerful not because it is reincarnation’s bearer,” she repeated. “Reincarnation chose it to be the bearer because it is that strong. The Tome of Life and Death... is life.”","Violetgrave’s voice flowed into Lu Yun’s ears like the waters of a spring.","“Books are the steps of civilization, they facilitate civilization’s steady ascension to the peak. Only where there is life is there civilization. Life was an accident of objective existence. Objectivity has never shifted on account of life’s will.","“Life, however, established civilization. Civilization is the key to affecting objectivity.","“God thought he set up his plans with none the wiser, but the mistress and Dao King are no fools. The Tome of Life and Death is their contingency plan.”","“So this means that I never broke free of their scheme from beginning to end?” Lu Yun asked in an emotionless voice as he finally understood the true meaning of the Tome of Life and Death.","The book was the media of civilization, not reincarnation. The words of “Life and Death” in its name didn’t refer to reincarnation as reincarnation was greater than life and death.","Life and death referred only to life. And death.","For creation, life and death were of the highest importance. Yearning for life and fear of death was the true meaning of life. The Tome of Life and Death was the book of all. It carried the true meaning of life and recorded the civilization of life.","Lu Yun suddenly recalled Violetgrave’s past—she’d been the Netherdark Hell. The Netherdark Hell buried civilization. None of those civilizations ever disappeared—they were preserved in the Tome of Life and Death.","She approached Lu Yun and the Violetgrave sword permitted Lu Yun to wield it not because of reincarnation contained within the Tome of Life and Death, but because the book itself was the book of civilization.","Lu Yun slowly lifted his head. Etched deep into his bones, reincarnation exploded out as a ball of white flames that slowly gathered in the center of his forehead.","Reincarnation was still within him, but there was now a clear divide between human and great dao. Reincarnation was still Lu Yun, but Lu Yun was no longer reincarnation.","The mistress and Dao King had long ascertained what God’s plans entailed, but they’d never thought of taking action. They wouldn’t do so even if God used the Sword of Chaos to truly bury Lu Yun here.","If God buried Lu Yun here and obtained reincarnation, becoming the pinnacle that’d never appeared before and affecting objectivity with the subjective wills of life... That was one kind of happy ending.","The great destruction would be fully terminated and everything would become God’s ideal paradise.","They would not stop this from taking place. It was the first kind of ending.","The second was this exact moment, the moment in which Lu Yun saw the Tome of Life and Death for what it was. It was the moment when he saw himself clearly and obtained the true meaning of life.","Life, death, and civilization.","......","“What is going on?!” God gasped. The layer that obscured his features was swept away and revealed Dongfang Hao’s face. His appearance shifted, then shifted again into God’s original form—a domineeringly handsome man in purple robes.","The light of civilization revolved around Lu Yun as reincarnation intersected with civilization.","Civilization represented the will of life. Reincarnation represented objective existence. Once civilization affected reincarnation, Lu Yun would become that ultimate pinnacle and affect objectivity with subjectivity.","Civilization and reincarnation reached a perfect balance in his body, both non-interfering and not affecting each other.","Lu Yun did not become that pinnacle.","Boom!","He thrust out his palm and forced God back, then slashed outward with a sword stroke. It was the first technique of his sword dao—Vast Dragon Seaturner.","Endless rays of sword light collected into a massive dragon that churned toward God. Lu Yun’s strength had risen explosively, but he was unable to crush his opponent. The two were evenly matched.","Calm returned to God’s expression and the corners of his mouth turned upward. He reverted back to Dongfang Hao’s appearance and closed his hand around the Sword of Chaos.","“I lost to you by a single move in Dusk Province all those years back. Let us continue that battle today!” Dongfang Hao blazed with high spirits and threw himself at Lu Yun, just as he had at the battle of the Five Youth Sovereigns in the world of immortals.","Sadly, Wu Tulong, Mo Qitian, and Zichen would never catch up to them anymore.","“Alright!” Lu Yun roared with laughter.","The ancient tomb turned into a battlefield."]},{"number":2141,"title":"Chapter 2141: Chapter 2096: “Mmhmm.”","paragraphs":["Chapter 2096: “Mmhmm.”","Vast Dragon Seaturner.","Peng of Kun.","Starstream Stroke.","These were the moves that Lu Yun invented when he first established sword dao in the world of immortals. They were the foundations of his sword dao.","He was caught on the back foot at first because he was no match for God. God’s sword dao was marvelous and unbelievable; it fully suppressed Lu Yun and destroyed the young man’s sword dao.","But gradually, Lu Yun entered a profound state in which he slowly comprehended the strength within his body. The power of reincarnation, the power of civilization. The power of reincarnation retreated back into the Tome of Life and Death, leaving room for the fire of civilization to sweep through his body.","Fire.","The physical manifestation of reincarnation was fire, as was the origin of civilization. When living beings lit the first bloom of fire, it proclaimed the birth of civilization.","And so, Lu Yun lit a flower of flame now. He illuminated civilization.","Quietus transformed into blazing flames and the aura of civilization spread through the premises, sans the sword’s aura. To living beings, sword dao, immortal dao, great dao, rules, laws, and everything... All had to do with civilization.","Only when there was civilization was there everything else. Civilization was the divine weapon of life.","Barbaric life could become masters of themselves, rule over creation, and defy objectivity only after they grasped civilization. At this moment, the sword in Lu Yun’s hand was the Sword of Civilization.","From Vast Dragon Seaturner to Dragonrise, every stroke was sufficient to establish an undying civilization.","God backed up rapidly, his face settling into a hideous grimace. He’d lost to Lu Yun in Dusk Province and he was still losing to the young man in a tomb that’d never seen the light of day!","God was stronger than Lu Yun. He wasn’t lesser in terms of cultivation level or strength, but mentality.","The Tome of Life and Death carried the weight of civilization and everything that God had ever experienced—everything that he was was also civilization. It was encompassed by Lu Yun’s Sword of Civilization.","One stroke could sever God’s civilization and return him to the state of drinking blood and tearing at raw flesh. He would devolve from civilization to barbarism and be crushed by endless objectivity. He would succumb to its rhythm, to drift along with the ebbs and flows of nature.","Clink!","The Sword of Chaos shattered with a sharp collision. The Sword of Civilization had broken it.","God slowly backed away with a long exhale and threw away the sword’s hilt. “I have been defeated.”","“Yes, you have been defeated,” Lu Yun nodded. The Sword of Civilization dispersed as motes of light and Quietus reappeared in his hand.","Civilization had coalesced as a formless, intangible sword that could not be traced. It came with a beckon and was dismissed with a wave.","This was a cultivation level infinitely close to the pinnacle.","What was meant by the pinnacle was the highest peak that a subjective being could reach. They could affect the objective with the subjective then. No life or objectivity would be able to withstand it.","Not only was it the pinnacle of a being, it was the pinnacle of objectivity.","There could only be one.","“But I do not yield.” Resolution flashed through God’s eyes. “I broke into the nothing from reality and set up plot within plot so I could reach the pinnacle. I may be defeated, but I have not lost!”","Lu Yun frowned as a foreboding feeling rose from the bottom of his heart.","Hummm.","Tremendous force converged from all sides. A destructive force similar to the force generated by the nothing touching the barrier of nothing suddenly erupted.","The tomb from reality... exploded.","God had been defeated, there was no coming back when faced with the Sword of Civilization. But he had one final ace up his sleeve—detonate the tomb!","“Dragonquake Scripture!!” Lu Yun howled. Dragons surged toward him and collected as the core essence of the Dragonquake Scripture. He furiously propelled the power of civilization and reincarnation within his body, trying to corral the tomb and prevent it from exploding.","But across from him, he saw a cruel smile grace God’s face.","KABOOM!","Heavenfall exploded. God had detonated his genesis weapon!","“YOU!!” Lu Yun never imagined that God would do something like this! The tomb was embedded in the barrier of nothing and connected to the Divine Temple of Nothing. This detonation would destroy the temple as well!","Everything in the temple would be destroyed!","God had gone completely mad. If the tomb and divine temple exploded, he would die too!","He would take Lu Yun with him!","Quietus lit the flame of civilization again and returned to being a Sword of Civilization. He raised it high with both hands and desperately brought it down on the strength that was nearly the great destruction.","Terrifying strength bore down on him from all sides, swallowing his body and destroying the sword. Quietus exploded as well.","A massive mushroom cloud rose in the air as the entire divine temple exploded. Everything returned to nothing.","The Divine Temple of Nothing existed in people’s hearts. The temple couldn’t be destroyed as long as they still held faith. Only the strength of the great destruction could destroy it—the collision with the barrier of nothing.","The divine temple was gone and the ancient tomb that’d stood for countless eons was also gone.","A massive crater ripped through the barrier, but it started closing after that split second. When it closed, it was as if it’d never appeared at all.","......","The Dao King was here. He held a ball of light in his hand that contained the territory of the five elements. The Fire God, Wave God, and all those they’d saved were safe and sound within the ball of light.","“Was it worth it?” he gently asked the last vestiges of God.","“Mmhmm,” God grunted before vanishing. There would never be a God within existence again.","The Dao King raised his head and looked at the barrier of nothing, his eyes devoid of emotion.","......","Grayish-yellow clouds loomed over a devastated city like a heavy pot lid. Weathered wagon wheels groaned under overburdened carriages. They creaked as they trundled over dirt mixed with patches of bloody mud. The wagons made slow progress to the outskirts of town.","Thump!","Thump!","Thump!","Tattered corpses were flung from the wagons into a pit three hundred meters deep that held thousands of bodies. Their handlers were numb-faced and occasionally looked up at the dreary sky. There was no hope to be found there.","This was a broken world, one entirely without vitality. It was a world of despair.","Once the first wagon emptied, several people pushed it back into the devastated city. No one noticed a rag doll of a body appear out of thin air and crash into the pit.","A ghastly white sun rose listlessly from the east and scattered weak illumination over the gloomy land.","Another night had passed. Another hopeless day was here.","It was the start of despair once again."]},{"number":2142,"title":"Chapter 2142: Chapter 2097: Despair","paragraphs":["Chapter 2097: Despair","A ghastly pale sun slowly set in the west. Night had fallen again.","Things that looked like corpses, but were actually ghosts, or even the rotten flesh of many lives, crawled out of every nook and cranny like cockroaches. They skittered toward the devastated city. It should’ve been a magnificent and grandiose structure, but it wavered like a boat caught in a ferocious gale.","Its sole remaining formation lit up, silently defending the city against hordes of creatures. A thousand holes and a hundred boils marked its surface. Countless living beings filled its openings with their own bodies.","It was another night of despair.","......","Morning saw the rise of the ghastly sun, one without any vitality. The tide of monsters that’d ravaged the land for a night receded.","Large wagons laden with broken bodies creaked out of the city and shed their burdens into the pit in front of the city walls. Black oil followed the bodies. Moments later, black smoke billowed into the air. What was an already gray world turned even darker.","Those who died to the monsters had to be burned or they’d mutate and turn into monsters themselves.","Lu Yun sat on a large rock outside the city—he’d crawled up from the pit of the dead. It’d been a very close call; he’d nearly died a few times. Slack jawed, there wasn’t a hint of life to be found in the young man. He was like a human-shaped sculpture. People paid him no heed and walked woodenly past him.","There were too many walking dead like him in this world. He knew nothing about this unknown and mysterious world that he’d arrived in.","He didn’t even know why he was here.","There was nothing in his body apart from a hunk of flesh riddled with injuries. The Tome of Life and Death had disappeared, the power of reincarnation dispersed. There was no sign of the power of civilization to be found.","Lu Yun was now a mortal. No, he was trash that was less than a mortal. If the monsters attacked the city again, he would be mashed into pieces by their pungent mouths.","“Is God dead?” he murmured with a cough.","“God? God died a long time ago,” a melodious voice rang by his ear.","Lu Yun looked up stiltedly and saw a charming figure standing in front of him. She was a young woman dressed in green and a rare expression of life force.","He’d sat dumbly on the rock after making it out of the pit last night. If it wasn’t for the young woman protecting him throughout the night, he would’ve been torn to pieces when the monsters attacked.","However, he didn’t lose heart or faith. Even though he possessed nothing at the moment, he was still a powerhouse forged in the fires of hell, one who’d weathered endless trials and reached the apex of another realm. He would not be demoralized by his circumstances.","As much as he despaired, he was still Lu Yun.","He was just... dazed from the explosion.","God’s self detonation had destroyed the entire Divine Temple of Nothing. It no longer existed in the nothing. Lu Yun’s survival was a miracle and his brain yet rang from it. There was nothing he could do apart from sit on the rock.","His previous murmuring was simply a sign that he’d recovered his abilities to think and speak.","“Oh.” Lu Yun nodded mutely as his mind was still foggy.","“God is the hope of all life. Everyone is waiting for him to resurrect and end this world of despair,” the young woman explained seriously as she looked at Lu Yun. “But God is probably really dead. He has been long lost to time and everyone has forgotten him. Why do you remember him?”","“Don’t you remember him too?” Lu Yun said haltingly.","The young woman shook her head and took a deep look at him before leaving. Yuan Yi was the guardian of Jingzhou City and the sole reason why it still stood. She was one of the few cultivators that remained.","Jingzhou City would stand if she was present. It would fall if she left.","“Where is this place?” Lu Yun suddenly asked.","“Jingzhou City.” Yuan Yi paused.","Lu Yun shook his head. “I mean this world.” He already had an answer in mind, he just wanted to confirm it.","“This world is this world, what else can it be?” Yuan Yi responded with puzzlement.","“The only world?” Lu Yun nodded. “I understand.”","“What do you understand?” Yuan Yi frowned and walked back.","She’d personally watched Lu Yun crawl out of the pit yesterday, which was why she paid extra attention to the young man fortunate enough to survive. As she hadn’t seen him fall from the sky, she thought he was just a luckier survivor.","Although Jingzhou City was the only city to be found in the thousands of kilometers around them, millions called it home and it wasn’t possible for her to remember them all. Not to mention that most people walked around like the living dead, eking out life one day at a time. She wasn’t interested in conversing with dull people like that.","Thus, she was the city’s guardian, but no one took a second glance at her.","“You are a cultivator?” Lu Yun asked slowly. “There is no great dao in this world, what do you cultivate?”","“Great dao?” Yuan Yi breathed out. “What a distant name. There is no great dao, we cultivate ourselves.”","“I see,’ Lu Yun nodded. He tried to get up, but failed and sat back down.","“You are heavily injured, but not by the ghost zombies.” Yuan Yi frowned. This was the first time she talked to someone like this in the one hundred years she kept watch over the city.","“Ghost zombies? Is that what you call the zombies that attacked last night?” Lu Yun nodded. “That’s correct, they didn’t cause these injuries. Would you believe me if I say God left them on me?” He broke out in a brilliant smile.","Yuan Yi stared at Lu Yun. How long had it been since she’d seen someone smile?","I... don’t think I’ve ever seen this expression on anyone’s face, not in the one hundred some years of my life. Why is this young man... smiling? He can’t even stand and looks like he’ll die at any second.","Why is he smiling?","Because God inflicted his injuries?","Yuan Yi shook her head and beckoned, jerking Lu Yun’s collar upwards with a gust of clear wind and walking back to the city. Lu Yun bobbed along in her wake.","“The formation needs to be repaired, it’s about to break.” Lu Yun glanced at the defensive formation when they passed through it.","“The last formation master died in battle ten years ago and we haven’t had one since. Even if we did, we don’t have the origin stones to spare for it.”"]},{"number":2143,"title":"Chapter 2143: Chapter 2098: The World Is Dead","paragraphs":["Chapter 2098: The World Is Dead","“I can repair the formation.” Lu Yun’s heart spasmed with pity when he took in the sights as Yuan Yi dragged him into the city. The city walls were falling to pieces; its inhabitants consumed grass and tree roots for sustenance.","He could collect goodwill as he possessed the Karmic Tree and use goodwill for cultivation. Thus, acts of service and kindness had long become one of his habits. That was likely why people called him a saint.","He just couldn’t help himself when he saw the distressing sights around him.","I have to keep it in... I have to keep it in. I left the Karmic Tree in another world, so I won’t receive any karma if I do good deeds here. Mm, it’s not like I have the effort to spare for others when I can’t be sure if I’ll even be alive to see nightfall. Those ghost zombies could eat me at any time.","But he could repair the worn down formation in poor condition—for himself, if not for others.","Who knew if this formation could survive another night? He would die all the same if the ghost zombies shattered the formation and breached the city’s defenses. Therefore, he started shouting his objections.","His yells broke through the lifeless air, particularly ear-piercing in the wooden atmosphere. Many of those repairing the city walls or foraging for food paused, turning blank stares at the young man being dragged into the city.","There were humans and other races among them, with no such thing as a harmonious or otherwise relationship between them. Dead bodies—if not killed by the ghost zombies—were food.","In their eyes, the guardian would also be food after she died.","If she didn’t die to the ghost zombies.","Eating the living wasn’t permitted—that was one of Yuan Yi’s rules. Whoever dared cannibalize the living would die.","“You can repair the formation?” Yuan Yi stopped and looked back with surprise. “Didn’t you hear me? Jingzhou City is out of origin stones.”","Origin stones were the crystallizations of qi in this world and its cultivation resource. They were similar to the immortal crystals of the world of immortals. But with the death of this world, its origin stones dried up. Every stone was exceptionally precious and well hidden. No one would bear to use one on a formation.","As for Yuan Yi... she had no origin stones. Hers had long become part of the formation’s foundations. The city’s defensive formation teetered on the edge of collapse not only because of the damage inflicted to it, but also because it’d nearly consumed its store of origin stones.","“What do you need origin stones for?” Lu Yun shook his head to clear it. He knew what origin stones the moment they were mentioned, but he was a feng shui master. Feng shui masters didn’t need origin stones to set up a killing formation.","Formations and feng shui were two sides of the same coin. When first arriving at the world of immortals, he’d utilized his knowledge of feng shui to become a formation expert.","Feng shui layouts utilized the power of heaven and earth, the traces of wind passing and water flowing. It didn’t require any supplemental reinforcement from outside forces.","In Lu Yun’s assessment, the underlying feng shui layout had been completely ruined, despite the formation still standing. At the same time, the feng shui layout that the formation corresponded to was a simple layout that gathered qi. It facilitated happiness and prosperity for its denizens. Given that corpses littered the ramshackle streets, the layout was naturally no more.","“You can set up a formation without origin stones?” Yuan Yi solemnly regarded Lu Yun. “Feng... shui?”","“You know it?” Lu Yun smiled. No one had known what feng shui was when he arrived at the world of immortals, but Yuan Yi of reality had immediately guessed it.","“The world is dead.” She looked up at the grayish-yellow sky. “Feng shui borrows the strength of heaven and earth. If the world is dead, then so is the heaven and earth. Feng shui is useless.”","She continued dragging him into the depths of the city.","“If heaven and earth are dead, why are the people still alive?” Lu Yun frowned.","“Alive? Do you think this is living?” Yuan Yi snorted with laughter. “They are wheezing for breath. Death is but a matter of time. It is our deepest instinct that forces us to struggle before it comes for us.","“What do you think those ghost zombies are? Living beings turn into ghosts and corpses when they die. When those die, they further turn into ghost zombies.","“Forget about all this, there’s no point,” Yuan Yi said quietly. “In this world, we struggle for every day we can. I’m going to heal your injuries first, we can discuss everything else later.”","“Why did you save me?” asked a baffled Lu Yun. “Because I was staring off into space next to the pit?”","“You are a cultivator and each cultivator is very precious in this world. I’ll live a bit longer with you around.”","Lu Yun: ......","Yuan Yi lived in a shabby house. There was nothing in it apart from wooden bed slats and some flora. The house swayed with the wind, looking like it would collapse at any second. The herbs she used on Lu Yun were items of extreme yin and evil that would grow only in the pit of corpses.","They were exceedingly useful, however.","“The world is alive, it isn’t dead yet,” Lu Yun said as he watched his wounds close. “A dead world would not nurture these things.”","He regarded a small red flower that glowed with a clear hue. It’d taken root on a charred corpse. Yuan Yi had dug it out of the pit and brought it back with them when the fires couldn’t destroy the flower.","“This grew out of a cultivator’s corpse, not the world,” she explained seriously. “The cultivator’s vitality was yet to be fully consumed when the ghost zombies killed them, so this flower grew from it.","“It is a continuation of their life. If I die to them and my body is burned, I’ll probably give rise to these things too.”","Lu Yun fell silent.","“Give it up, this world is dead.” There was no emotion in Yuan Yi’s voice. “All of our efforts are but the instincts of living beings. A futile effort to live a bit longer. We are all meant to die, so every moment longer we live is good.”","“Instinct?” Lu Yun fell silent again. Was this the reality on the other side of the nothing? Was this Mo Yi, God, and the Dao King’s home?","Was this the world that the Divine Temple of Nothing and all of the gods pinned their hopes on? Was this where the way to end the great destruction could be found?","It seemed more like reality was undergoing its own, true devastation.","“I... still don’t want to accept things just like this.” Lu Yun shook his head again. “Is this really the hope of all life?”","“The hope of all life?” Yuan Yi blinked. “There is no hope here, just despair.”","“Then why have I come here? By pure coincidence?” Lu Yun murmured to himself.","It was no coincidence. God had used a variety of methods to help him comprehend civilization and facilitate a delicate balance between civilization and reincarnation. He then self detonated to blast a hole through the barrier of nothing, sending Lu Yun here.","Was it only to let him see a reality devoid of hope?","Lu Yun was no fool. As his thoughts cleared and he realized where he was, he understood God’s intentions and painstaking efforts.","God wasn’t a traitor. He’d used the most extreme method possible to have Lu Yun comprehend civilization and reincarnation, then forcefully sent him here. The young man hadn’t been willing to come, at least not now. And yet, he couldn’t bring himself to hate God.","Was it worth it?","God seemed to think so."]},{"number":2144,"title":"Chapter 2144: Chapter 2099: The Fire of Civilization","paragraphs":["Chapter 2099: The Fire of Civilization","Reality was one massive enigma to Lu Yun. He had so many questions that awaited answers, but plainly, Yuan Yi couldn’t help him in that regard. She herself spent her days in a foggy haze—surviving to see the next sunrise was her only goal.","Lu Yun spent the next month in this world in such a manner.","Things were fine enough during the day, but endless ghost zombies surged from all directions at night, trying to run the dilapidated city into the ground.","People died every night. If it wasn’t for Yuan Yi’s presence, the city would’ve fallen long ago and all of its inhabitants become food. However, Lu Yun could tell that she couldn’t hold out for much longer. She’d saved Lu Yun because she was taking a gamble on him—she thought he was a powerful cultivator.","That was all.","Lu Yun recovered from his injuries, but he couldn’t sense the great dao. Whether it was formula dao, immortal dao, or reincarnation—all had vanished without a trace. The Tome of Life and Death floated listlessly in his consciousness, like it was dead.","“Civilization...” Lu Yun blinked with surprise when he sensed the vestiges of power within him. All of the great daos that he’d cultivated before, including reincarnation, immortal dao, and formula dao, had fallen silent. It was like they’d never existed.","A tiny bit of civilization flickered like a guttering candle inside his body. Instead of growing stronger as Lu Yun recovered, it slowly diminished. It wouldn’t be long now before it fully went out.","“Civilization has nothing to do with my personal strength. It needs the nourishment of external culture. Countless existences bolstered it in the nothing—there was the Three Thousand and existences derived from the three hundred and sixty-five demon gods that nurtured civilization...” Lu Yun suddenly realized the truth of what he was saying, that everything in the nothing had always been within the mistress, Dao King, and God’s grasp.","The betrayal of the Divine Temple of Nothing and destruction of the other three temples was also within their calculations. It was due to the destruction of the three temples that their seeds of civilization could spread throughout the nothing, turning it into a fake nothing in which life could survive.","The three hundred and sixty-five demon gods, as well as Ancestor’s existence and the Three Thousand, jointly propped up civilization within the nothing. It was what enabled the fires of civilization to blossom within Lu Yun’s body.","They wouldn’t have lit otherwise in Lu Yun’s body if it wasn’t for these preparations, even if he managed to travel to reality.","“Their goal is for me to light the fire of civilization in this world so it can revitalize. Civilization is the true meaning of life, the crystallization of wisdom...”","No wonder only the Netherdark Hell—keeper of dead civilizations—gave birth to Violetgrave. The others remained simply hells.","Lu Yun breathed out slowly when his thoughts traveled here. He didn’t blame God, the mistress, or the Dao King despite not wanting to be here. However, he was still angry and resentful. He’d been forced to do something entirely beyond him and had been compelled to come to this world. God even paid the price of his life!","Lu Yun was completely disconnected from the nothing. To those on that side, he was dead in certain aspects. Of course, they knew that he wasn’t truly dead because his life force remained, the Tome of Life and Death was still present in his body, the ten Yama Kings and ghostly soldiers were still present.","He was just... gone.","If he wanted to go home and see his loved ones, he needed to furiously cultivate and light the fire of civilization in this world. Only after he illuminated this world of despair could he break through the barrier of nothing and return to his place.","Lu Yun didn’t know how long the process would take; he had to ensure he stayed alive first. And what if he returned to find that a great devastation had taken place while he was gone?","The great devastation could not be denied. All that the mistress and Dao King could do was to delay it as much as possible.","“That’s really it...” Lu Yun heaved a long sigh and murmured to himself, “Everything I possessed in the nothing was a result of others paving the road for me. Even my great daos and accomplishments were part of someone else’s damned calculations. I never broke free to walk my own path.","“None of the mistress, Dao King, and deceased God’s plans can be found here. This is it. The rest is up to me.”","The mistress, Dao King, God, Hongjun, the Three Purities, Fuxi, and Ancestor had jointly raised Lu Yun so that he could light the flame of civilization and bring the faintest trace of hope to this despairing world.","But their plans remained in the nothing—it was up to him alone once he was in reality.","He had his goal, but he didn’t know what to do or how to even approach lighting the fire. All he could do at the moment was ensure his survival.","Cultivate!","Become a cultivator!","Perhaps he turned out to be vastly different from Yuan Yi’s expectations. He didn’t become a strong cultivator after he was on the mend. Although his physical body was stronger than all the others, it wasn’t to the point of a cultivator.","Yuan Yi was the only cultivator left in Jingzhou City. The rest had died in battle. She had many disciples that she sought to develop into new cultivators, but she failed with every single one.","Lu Yun was her new target.","There was no great dao in this world as the power of heaven and earth was confined to origin stones and buried deep within the ground. Being unable to cultivate external force, cultivators could only train themselves.","Condense qi and vitality, hone their bodies. When they were strong enough, they could withstand the enemy and possibly everything else. However, this included external nutrients as well. Origin stones were one source, food was another.","It was also the law of the jungle here, but every living being was an additional force against the ghost zombies. They were not allowed to harm each other before a natural death occurred. Otherwise, cultivators would become murderers and eat others for food!","Those who died to the ghost zombies were by and large assimilated. Even if they laid still in death, they struggled up before long and turned into new ghost zombies.","Thus, everyone who died in the night was tossed into the pit of thousands to be burned, even if they were ripped to pieces.","Lu Yun had fallen into the pit when he first arrived. If it wasn’t for Yuan Yi saving him, he would’ve been reduced to ashes a long time ago."]},{"number":2145,"title":"Chapter 2145: Chapter 2100: Fire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2100: Fire","The ghastly sun rose in the east at the dawn of a new day.","Teeming masses of ghost zombies receded like the tides when illuminated by sunlight. They instantly vanished without a trace, their whereabouts unknown.","Drenched in blood, Lu Yun was in poor shape. The black corpse of a ghost zombie dangled from his hand. After his recovery, he joined the ranks of this world’s cultivators. Yuan Yi swept him out of her wooden house, leaving the young man to fend for himself and earn his living by joining the battle against the ghost zombies.","The only ones excused from the war and could shelter in the city’s heart were pregnant women and children. The rest, even if they were elders with a foot in the grave, had to join the fray in the battlefield.","Granted, there were no elders in this world. When one’s physical strength began declining after one’s prime, there was no hope of survival against the ghost zombies.","Neither did the ghost zombies attack every night—there were occasional periods of rest. If not, the city would’ve been leveled a long time ago.","There was just one cultivator left in Jingzhou City—Yuan Yi. Lu Yun could very possibly become the second. The cultivation methods of this world were simple, but very difficult. One had to cultivate oneself and continuously excavate the potential of the human body. Human strength had to be fully released so that it could triumph over nature.","The first step was to condense and temper qi and blood. However, external sustenance was needed for this step—such as a meat diet. But in this world, the only meat that could be eaten were those that’d died a natural death.","Other than that, grass and trees struggling equally hard to live were the only other sources of food. People sometimes even ate dirt.","If they didn’t, they would starve to death and their bones become someone else’s food.","Wagons creaked in and out of the city, ferrying corpses through the city gates. Those who died to the ghost zombies were infused with corpse poison and would become ghost zombies before long. Anyone who ate them would mutate as well.","Lu Yun’s qi and blood had long been tempered to a realm of great perfection. He didn’t need to eat meat or take in any sustenance. A massive strength brewed in his body; it was the last trace of strength remaining from the nothing after he arrived in this world.","When he was still in the nothing, he stood at the pinnacle of the realm. This last bit of strength from those heights was sufficient for Lu Yun to forgo the need for food and become a cultivator. It was also this vestige of power that enabled him to recover in such a short period of time.","“What are you doing with a ghost zombie corpse?” Yuan Yi frowned when she drew near and saw what was in Lu Yun’s hand.","Ordinary people didn’t possess the ability to kill ghost zombies. The only thing they could do was fill the gaps in the formation with their bodies, physically providing a stopgap against the enemy so they couldn’t make it to where the children and pregnant women were.","That was all.","The only ones who could kill ghost zombies were cultivators, and Yuan Yi was the only one. It immensely surprised her that Lu Yun had become a cultivator in such a short period of time after his arrival. At the same time, it also provided some relief.","“Ghost zombies don’t really die. That one may look like it’s dead, but it’ll revitalize after seven days,” Yuan Yi said seriously.","“So is this thing a ghost or a zombie?” Lu Yun blinked. He’d found a black crystal core inside the body. Crushing it would truly kill the ghost zombie. In his eyes, this was neither ghost nor zombie, but a strange new creature.","But based on Yuan Yi’s words, especially coming back to life after seven days... Lu Yun found the entity incredulous. There were stories of the dead’s soul returning after seven days in the nothing, and Lu Yun’s Resurrection death art could resurrect anyone who’d died in the last seven days.","If these ghost zombies could also do the same thing... then it might really have something to do with ghosts or zombies.","“No one knows what they are. They appeared out of nowhere one day and turned the world into ruins.” Yuan Yi shook her head. “There were people before who captured ghost zombies like you or studied their corpses. All of them met horrible ends.","“They were either killed by the suddenly resurrecting ghost zombie or struck with misfortune and turned into one themselves. So my advice to you is to throw away the corpse or burn it.”","Burning a ghost zombie’s corpse was the only way to kill it.","Burn...","Lu Yun mused over the notion. The most direct way of expressing reincarnation was fire. Whatever the fire was, it was the power of reincarnation—including Lu Yun’s flame of civilization. Civilization was part of reincarnation and could even be considered a byproduct of reincarnation.","He only possessed the fire of civilization within him now, there was no reincarnation. The young man suddenly grew excited when he saw the burning flames within the pit outside of the city.","Fire!","Reincarnation!","He’d grasped the meaning of civilization with God’s help and lit its flame, but to Lu Yun, the strongest had always been reincarnation! He even felt that the Tome of Life and Death hadn’t truly vanished, that it was only hidden in a corner of his body. If he could reactivate reincarnation, he would be able to summon it again.","There was a patch of real existence within the book! It was a complete heaven and earth that contained a complete great dao and order!","He would have everything again if he held the Tome of Life and Death. He would rise to the peak of this world and then... go home! The flame of civilization could be lit from the Tome of Life and Death, then spread out to this seemingly dead world.","He was no longer lost, he had his goal and direction.","Fire was reincarnation!","All Lu Yun needed to do was to control fire and use it to access the reincarnation hidden in the Tome of Life and Death. He had a hunch that everything he possessed had not disappeared. It’d merely been concealed by the book.","“You seem to have somehow changed,” asked a baffled Yuan Yi as she looked at the young man.","Although Lu Yun had never given up hope and remained in optimistic spirits, a lost look had flashed through his eyes from time to time. In this moment, Yuan Yi noticed that the lost look was no longer there. His whole aura had shifted.","“I have,” he grinned brilliantly. “I’m going to study what the deal is with this ghost zombie. Oh, I’ve built a stone house close to the city gates. I won’t bring trouble to the city if anything goes wrong.”"]},{"number":2146,"title":"Chapter 2146: Chapter 2101: Strength of One","paragraphs":["Chapter 2101: Strength of One","Jingzhou’s city walls were tall and sturdy, occupying fifty kilometers by themselves. There should’ve been four main gates and eight side gates, now there was only an east gate that still opened. The rest were sealed shut by the formation.","City walls were useless against the ghost zombies. Only the teetering formation riddled with thousands of holes had any effect.","Lu Yun built his house in the empty frame of the city gate—it was missing part of its doors, so no one minded his actions. No one dared have an opinion either way since he was a cultivator now.","When he returned to his stone house, he ignored Yuan Yi’s objections and carved the ghost zombie into sections.","“Ah, forget it,” Yuan Yi sighed when she saw how fanatically devoted Lu Yun was. The city had finally gained another cultivator, but he was soon to be no more. Thank goodness he built his house where it was. If misfortune struck him and he turned into a ghost zombie, she’d be able to kick him out with the fastest speed possible.","Although Lu Yun was a cultivator, he was far weaker than Yuan Yi. Even the ordinary beings of this world were stronger than those of the world he’d come from. The weakest cripple here could kill a Supreme Immortal of Original Order with a single punch.","That was no joke or exaggeration, but the overwhelming difference in their worlds. This world within reality was far more sophisticated than any world in the nothing. Therefore, the constitution of its denizens was stronger than the immortals’.","As for Yuan Yi...","Lu Yun made a quick comparison and determined her strength to be the equivalent of a Nihil World Sovereign. Not the fake Nihil World Sovereigns in the fourth realm, but the real ones who’d exceeded existence and entered the nothing.","He’d witnessed her kill a ghost zombie with one punch; there was none other like her. Weak and strong ghost zombies could be found among the horde. The stronger ones were mightier than Yuan Yi, the weak ones were less than an ordinary being.","What made them terrifying was their numbers and poison. What made them horrifying was that any they killed became them as well.","Ghost zombies lacked intelligence and didn’t know fear or pain. Feeding was their only instinct, which set them apart from the living. As numb as the living of this world was, as devoid of hope as they were, they still felt fear.","They were afraid of death, so they wanted to live. They would struggle in the swamp even though there was no hope.","......","Lu Yun dissected the ghost zombie into one hundred and eight pieces, finding it very similar to a zombie, but not quite a zombie as there was ghostly qi that lurked within. It looked like it was made of the soul and body of the dead in a combination of ghost and corpse. No wonder it was called a ghost zombie.","As night fell, darkness crept over the land.","“Hmm?” Lu Yun frowned, keenly perceiving a hint of unnatural cold next to him. It would seem that something he couldn’t see was there.","“A ghost?” he sneered. “How dare a ghost come near me?”","Humm!","Powerful internal qi exploded from his body. It was neither true force nor immortal force; it was just power from a body of flesh and blood, the most primitive force that living beings could bring to bear.","Since the denizens of this world could neither cultivate external force nor absorb it from the world, they could only temper themselves and coalesce blood and qi.","Lu Yun was no exception, but he had a cultivation method. The Method of Life and Death.","Boom.","Immense blood and qi circulated within Lu Yun’s body according to the method’s instructions, forming a massive circulation cycle. It roiled into a black current that exploded outward with his punch.","Blackish-red qi began to burn like flames.","Fire was the external manifestation of reincarnation. Lu Yun was unable to light and cultivate a fire inside his body, but he could use his own blood and qi to mimic the form of a flame and strength of reincarnation.","Thus, what looked like an ordinary attack actually contained the meaning of reincarnation.","A sharp shriek sounded in the air as a black shadow showed itself, then fled in hasty disorder.","“Is that the misfortune that kills those who study the ghost zombies?” Lu Yun frowned in the direction that the shadow left in. “So there are secrets contained in the ghost zombies that it wants to prevent me from discovering.”","He withdrew his projected qi and blood, resettling them into the appropriate parts of his body and dismissing the manifestation of fire.","“I was wrong.” He suddenly smacked his forehead with annoyance. “I shouldn’t have scared it off, I should’ve captured it! Studying it is way more valuable than a ghost zombie! That was probably a ghost, and one with intelligence!”","A sharp light danced in his eyes. “No worries, it’ll come again. If my guess is correct, there will be a tide of ghost zombies tonight! The city’s formation won’t hold for long, I need to think of a way to repair it.”","Having just arrived in this world, he needed shelter. Otherwise, he wouldn’t survive more than three days in his current condition. If he wanted to cultivate reincarnation and civilization, he needed a faction of his own.","Jingzhou City was his only choice. He didn’t know where else people might gather in this world.","As he expected, hordes of teeming ghost zombies flooded out of unknown locales the second sunlight disappeared. They streamed toward the city’s east gate.","The east gate lacked actual gates, making it an enormous opening in the city’s defenses. That made it their primary target.","At the same time, Lu Yun felt numerous gusts of cold winds float around him. The ghost that he couldn’t see was also here.","A cold smirk playing on his lips, he operated the Method of Life and Death again, using blood and qi to mimic fire and rushing out before the ghost zombies could draw near.","“Does he have a death wish?!” Yuan Yi’s jaw dropped to see the young man run out of the city gate. Even she would die when surrounded by the ghost zombies, not to mention an inexperienced cultivator like Lu Yun!","But Lu Yun had regained his dao. Blood and qi imitated flames and reincarnation. Though they weren’t the genuine article, they bore hints of its true meaning.","Reincarnation was the bane of all ghostly entities.","He punched and kicked at the enemies, beating the hordes back. Those guarding the east gate and ready to fight to their deaths were stunned. A new expression appeared on their faces, the second one they’d ever experienced in their lives—shock.","They’d never seen a cultivator like this, one who could block the hordes outside the city gates by himself."]},{"number":2147,"title":"Chapter 2147: Chapter 2102: Cultivation Method of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2102: Cultivation Method of Heaven and Earth","The city gates were Jinghzou City’s greatest weakness and thus the main target for the ghost zombies; casualties here were the heaviest whenever they attacked. Countless beings used their bodies to blockade the gap and forestall the attacks. Other openings in the formation were inconsequential.","Lu Yun charged out with his fists and beat the horde into retreating!","Correct, retreating. The ghost zombies couldn’t begin to approach the city gates.","“What are you guys standing around for?” Lu Yun roared. “The ghost zombies have turned their attention to other parts of the city. Are you going to just sit back and watch the show??”","His shout brought the crowd back to its senses and people hastily streamed off in other directions to fend off their attackers.","“He’s weaker than me and his blood and qi less developed. Why can he kill a ghost zombie with one blow?” Yuan Yi was also shocked. As she watched Lu Yun cut large swathes through the ghost zombies, a strange feeling rose from the bottom of her heart.","She didn’t know what it was as she’d never felt it before. It felt like... light was about to shine on her.","It was hope, something that the living of this world had never possessed.","Hope!","Lu Yun’s blood and qi blazed, forming roiling currents that obliterated ghost zombies with every punch he deployed. His blood and qi were very weak, but the power of reincarnation that it simulated could perfectly counter dead entities.","By now, he was certain that the ghost zombies were derived from the dead spirits!","The dead spirits that invaded the fourth realm were more terrifying and uncanny than the ghost zombies. They could be suppressed by the power of heaven and earth or burned by the flame of order to supplement order. These ghost zombies, however, required the power of reincarnation to defeat.","Lu Yun was so familiar with this power that he could mimic it by burning his own blood and qi. Otherwise, he would’ve been torn apart by the enemy a long time ago.","All the same, he was at the end of his rope and growing incredibly weak. Setting his jaw, he hung on with gritted teeth.","He wouldn’t survive in this world suffused with despair if he was the only one who was strong. He needed to bring hope to others and give them motivation to live. That would bring hope to the entire world and lift the atmosphere of despair, thereby giving rise to civilization.","All of this was so that he could go home.","WHOOSH.","Blackish-red flames ignited in Lu Yun’s eyes. His blood and qi were fully alight and the Method of Life and Death formed a true system that circulated throughout his body.","Being a cultivation method, the Method of Life and Death required external resources for cultivation. But since there was no power of heaven and earth here, Lu Yun could only refine his own blood and qi. He refined them as he would the energy of heaven and earth and concentrated them on himself.","This was a way of forging himself into heaven and earth. It was far more difficult than all of the cultivation methods in the nothing, but Lu Yun possessed prior experience! He’d once refined a body of heaven and earth when he collected the ten connate spirit roots and organs of the world of immortals into his replica. It later became the cosmos of the world and the tool with which he excised the cancerous Dao Tree from immortal dao.","Refining that replica was the experience that he drew upon now, which was why his refinement of blood and qi went so smoothly. If blood and qi could form a circulatory system in his body, one of reincarnation, then he wouldn’t need any external supplement.","He was cultivating as he mowed down the enemy, making his own body into that of heaven and earth.","Lu Yun suddenly understood that everything he’d experienced before, from the world of immortals to the nothing, had been an endless series of tests. He’d never encountered any real enemies. Everything had been preparation for his visit to reality. All that he’d learned and endured had been for this place.","It looked like he’d come wholly unprepared when, truthfully speaking, he came equipped with immense experience, ample knowledge, and incredible practice. He was well fortified for everything in this world.","“The cultivation method of heaven and earth... with blood and qi as the energy of the world, tempering the self and manifesting the flames of reincarnation...” Lu Yun closed his eyes.","Bam—","The circulatory system within his body exploded with a dull roar and expanded outside of his body, forming an even bigger cycle of motion. It vaporized all of the ghost zombies that it touched.","......","The night passed. In the morning, an inexplicable emotion rose from the battered metropolis when they saw that Lu Yun had defended the entire city by himself.","The ghost zombies had attacked them last night, but not a single person died. Hope bloomed starting from yesterday night.","“Who... who are you!” Yuan Yi asked incredulously when she walked up to Lu Yun.","“I am me,” Lu Yun smiled. “I’ll teach you how to cultivate. I can teach the entire city how to cultivate.”","“You can’t,” Yuan Yi shook her head. “Cultivation requires dense qi and blood. Those who lack it in sufficient quantities will consume it all during cultivation and die...”","“My cultivation method doesn’t require that,” Lu Yun smiled. “Anyone can practice it and become a cultivator.”","He sent the cultivation method into Yuan Yi’s mind with a point of his finger, turning qi and blood into will. She stared incredulously at him. Although she was also a cultivator, she didn’t possess this kind of ability.","“Al... right!” Yuan Yi nodded slowly after she spent a while digesting the cultivation method. “Do you know that I’ve only ever known despair from the moment of my birth? The instinctive desire to live is the only thing that’s kept me going to this day—the desire to live a bit longer in the darkness.","“But now, you’ve shown me hope.” She took a deep breath.","“Just from a cultivation method?” Lu Yun sighed. “It is but candlelight flickering in the storm and not worth mentioning.”","“But you’ve lit a candle in a storm and given everyone hope. Look!” Yuan Yi pointed at the city. The citizens who normally spent the day resting or staring off in a wooden, numb haze slowly gathered around them. For once, some other emotions flickered on their faces. While it wasn’t as strong as what Yuan Yi felt, it was cracks in their bleak miasma all the same.","“I’ll teach all of you how to cultivate,” Lu Yun roared with laughter. “Everyone will be as strong as me after you learn! You’ll all kill a ghost zombie with one punch!”","He punched forward and vaporized the remaining corpses at the city gates.","Lu Yun had to change this world if he wanted to survive. Otherwise, he would be a skiff bobbing on top of the waves, ready to capsize at any second. When in the world of immortals, he utilized the Karmic Tree for cultivation and devoted himself to good deeds in order to collect goodwill. He’d disseminated all of his cultivation methods and battle techniques also in preparation for today.","Those actions prompted by the Karmic Tree fostered habits that eventually earned Lu Yun the title of “Dao Saint”."]},{"number":2148,"title":"Chapter 2148: Chapter 2103: Two-Legged Sheep","paragraphs":["Chapter 2103: Two-Legged Sheep","The city’s residents dispersed after watching Lu Yun’s feat of high spirits. Some went to bed, others returned to staring off into space. They busied themselves with whatever their usual business was.","Only Yuan Yi remained staring raptly at Lu Yun.","“Didn’t they... just see hope?” He scratched his head with bemusement.","“When one scrabbles in the dark for too long, one does not think that the darkness is over when a pinprick of light appears,” Yuan Yi shook her head. “What you’ve accomplished doesn’t even count as a pinprick.”","“Then you...” Lu Yun looked at Yuan Yi with surprise. “Are you not the same as them?”","“Of course not. Although I am also accustomed to the dark and scrabble in it, they struggle for survival in the gloom. Cultivators, however, search through the dark. We look for the light.","“Just a pinprick is enough to give us hope, but ordinary people...” Yuan Yi shook her head and spoke no further.","“Okay, then we start with you!” Lu Yun smiled radiantly. “The cultivation method of heaven and earth will create a circulatory system within your body. It will slowly wean you off the need for external energy and ultimately bring your enormous power of the world.","The cultivation method of heaven and earth was a process that wouldn’t bring results overnight. Its prerequisite was a strong body. It wasn’t practical to cut oneself off from the outside world and form an internal circulation system as soon as one started.","Lu Yun had divided the method into three parts. The first was to coalesce heaven and earth inside one’s body. He’d done so before for the immortals who bypassed the void realm in the world of immortals. In order to ensure that they weren’t rendered obsolete with the times, he’d created the formation of heaven and earth.","Coincidentally, it was the crux of the cultivation method of heaven and earth.","He suddenly felt that everything he’d done in the world of immortals had been prearranged. Or at the very least, someone had organized all of the difficulties he’d run into so that he would need to determine solutions.","And solutions he had, which happened to be the exact answers needed in this world.","“It was a conspiracy that started from the moment they got me to the world of immortals and continues to this damned place!” As disgruntled as Lu Yun was, there was nothing he could do about it.","The Dao King, mistress, and God... Forget it, God was dead. Lu Yun itched to go back right now and beat up the Dao King and mistress. But in his current state, he wouldn’t stand a chance against them.","While Yuan Yi possessed the cultivation method, she was unable to etch a formation of heaven and earth. Lu Yun had to do it for her. This world possessed a heaven and earth and perhaps it was still alive, but he couldn’t sense it. Thus, all cultivation had to start from one’s own body. Obtaining nutrients from the outside world to slowly complete one’s internal world would form a complete cycle of heaven and earth.","The second step was internal circulation, transforming the formation of heaven and earth into a true world.","The third step was to expand the internal world outward so that it affected the world around them. However, Lu Yun didn’t know when they’d reach that step. Affecting the external world was a function of the pinnacle of subjectivity affecting objectivity.","Each step was incredibly difficult and arduous to undertake. Although Lu Yun had invented them, he wouldn’t necessarily succeed at achieving them. Even he himself barely managed to make it to the second step.","One’s progression wasn’t a reflection of strength, it was just the process of cultivation. Take Yuan Yi, for instance. She’d just started, but she was stronger than Lu Yun. Even if he progressed to the third step and could affect his immediate vicinity, Yuan Yi would still kill him with one blow.","That was the progression of cultivation, not a matter of cultivation system or realm. He had the vague outlines of a concept and needed painstaking exploration to fill in the details.","Lu Yun was exhausted after etching a formation for Yuan Yi. It was an enormous drain on internal energy and he needed external nourishment for the time being. The most direct method of that was through food.","Yuan Yi delivered a large sum of meat to him of those who’d died in the city. There were humans, monster spirits, and other races among them. Lu Yun shook his head and elected to leave the precious pile of decaying meat alone. Weariness dogging his footsteps, he headed out of the city.","“This world is dying, but it’s not dead. The ghost zombies are devouring everything, but they’re not the source of this disaster. They’re also victims!” Lu Yun murmured to himself as he looked up at the hazy sky.","Yuan Yi wanted to head outside of town with him too, but she kept a firm grip on herself and practiced the cultivation method of heaven and earth.","Internal heaven and earth, internal circulation, and external circulation!","The three steps were immensely entrancing.","Lu Yun walked through the decrepit land, seeing gray in every direction he turned.","“Finally... found it.” A smile curved his lips when he saw a blade of green. Though the blade of grass was withering, it was still a sign of hope in this land.","“Green grass means that this land is not yet fully dead. Some life force still exists within it.” Lu Yun sat down next to the shriveling blade of grass and operated the Method of Life and Death. He breathed in and out next to the grass.","At first, he found nothing. But gradually, he sensed a tiny strand of energy from heaven and earth. His body soaked up the minuscule rivulet like it was a giant sponge.","“It’s not dead, but sealed away by something. There’s... someone behind all this!” He’d fully recovered when he next opened his eyes. A tiny flame burned between his brows as his internal heaven and earth had recovered. It circulated in fully self-sufficient operations and formed a complete reincarnation system.","His cultivation took a step forward as he’d absorbed enough energy to strengthen his reincarnation system. It was stabilized to the point of being able to support his internal circulation. He was now solidly stronger than Yuan Yi.","“There are people alive in this wilderness?”","Lu Yun’s brow twitched when he heard a voice filled with delight.","“A sheep with two legs! We’ll have food for a few days after we kill it!”","“A living sheep means there’s a city nearby, one that hasn’t been destroyed yet!”","“Not a city, but a flock of sheep! We’ll have food for years after we kill its cultivators and butcher the sheep inside!”","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Three figures appeared in front of Lu Yun.","“Take us to your city and we’ll consider letting you join us.” Their leader was a creature that stood on two legs. He wasn’t human as he bore three horns on its head and a pair of fleshy black wings on his back. His emerald eyes bore into Lu Yun, ready to eat the human at any moment.","Two others who looked like him flanked him."]},{"number":2149,"title":"Chapter 2149: Chapter 2104: Wang Shu","paragraphs":["Chapter 2104: Wang Shu","The tri-horned creatures were tall, bulky, and radiated a thick scent of blood and pungent flesh. Plainly, they’d ended the lives of countless beings.","Lu Yun would’ve had to run with his tail between his legs if he’d met them earlier, but after he found the tiny blade of wild grass, he’d located the remaining energy of heaven and earth in this world and absorbed it as nourishment.","Even though it was the tiniest trickle, he was now far greater than who he’d been before.","“The civilization of this world has declined. They...” Lu Yun sighed as he looked at the three in front of him. “Their enlightenment is gone and only savagery remains.”","“What did you say?” Three pairs of emerald eyes narrowed at him.","“Big bro, let’s eat him since this kid doesn’t know what’s good for him. We three brothers run through the wilderness like it’s our own, we don’t need a sidekick!” the smallest of them sneered. “Since the kid’s out here, that means the city is close by. We just need to put our backs into looking for it!”","“Alright!” agreed the biggest of the three. He leered and pounced on Lu Yun.","The young man raised his head and silently watched the beast approach, then swung his fist.","Bam!","The beast’s head exploded and his headless corpse swayed a bit before plopping to the ground. The other two stared dumbly at what’d happened, their brains freezing.","Lu Yun smiled faintly at them. He jumped into the air and kicked their heads off their bodies with a precise motion from each foot. When he landed on the ground, he closed his eyes to carefully assess what would happen next.","Nothing did.","“Ai... I thought I’d be able to pick up a few Infernum if I killed some people. Where the hell did the Tome of Life and Death go to? I got nothing for my troubles,” he grumbled with resignation. Other than three corpses, he gained nothing after killing the three creatures.","“Forget it, they’re meat and can supplement blood and qi. Yuan Yi needs these things since she’s started practicing the method of heaven and earth.”","With one final glance at the blade of grass growing more vibrant, Lu Yun dragged the three bodies back to Jingzhou City.","......","“What are you doing at my house?” Lu Yun raised his eyes to see Yuan Yi sitting cross-legged on the roof when he returned to the stone house he’d built by the city gates. A few pieces of dried black meat could be found next to her—reserves from time past.","Yuan Yi blushed when she opened her eyes and didn’t say anything.","“Eh? What’s that?” she commented blankly when she saw the three corpses looming like hills behind Lu Yun. “Did you go out and kill people?!”","Every life was extraordinarily precious in a world ravaged by ghost zombies. Other than those who died to the ghost zombies or died natural deaths, no other kind of killing was allowed.","It was an unspoken, ironclad law that could not be violated.","“They look to be hunters,” Lu Yun shook his head. “They were looking for living beings and cities. I think they wanted to turn the city into their farm, so I took them out when I happened to bump into them.”","Yuan Yi’s expression shifted rapidly; she didn’t doubt Lu Yun’s words. She wouldn’t have been able to hold off the three beasts if they’d come to the city.","“You can have one for your cultivation needs. I’m going to skin and clean up the other two so I can make a pot of soup for the citizens.”","The three beasts were enormous, particularly after they returned to their original forms in death.","“For the citizens?” Yuan Yi blinked. “You should save the meat for times of need, or slowly dole it out as rations...”","Plainly, she wasn’t against eating the beasts.","“My passionate speech and demonstration of slaughter did absolutely nothing in terms of tangible change,” Lu Yun shook his head. “We need to give them some actual benefits if we want to awaken hope.”","He tossed one of the beasts to Yuan Yi and walked into town with the other two.","Jingzhou City did not lack water. Its denizens normally ate a very fine dirt that was just sufficient to prevent starvation. Yuan Yi occasionally took out some dried meat or withered grass to supplement their diet. Thus, Lu Yun instantly drew a great deal of attention when he set up an enormous stone pot in the city center and began cooking a meat stew.","There were roughly one million people in the city, the sum of this area’s general population. While that seemed like a lot of people, it was but a drop of water in the ocean compared to the vastness of its surrounding territory and the endless ghost zombies.","As enormous as the two beasts might be, they could not satisfy one million stomachs. Lu Yun had his own thoughts in that regard.","A delicious fragrance drifted through the air, prompting hard swallows in the crowd. The people stared blankly at the bubbling pot and didn’t know what to make of it. They’d never encountered anything like it before.","A meat stew? Putting fresh meat into a pot to cook it? Weren’t pots used to cook mud and grass? Could meat be cooked like this too?","“Bring out the tools that you usually eat with and come get your share of soup. Each person gets one bowl.” Lu Yun shook his head at the crowd’s reaction. He couldn’t feed them all meat, but there was more than enough soup to go around.","However, the people continued to remain unmoving. Their simple minds couldn’t comprehend why this scene was happening. No one dared move a muscle.","It was a kind of numbness so chronic that they’d lost the ability to think. If hope arrived in front of them on a silver platter one day, all they would know to do would be to stare at it blankly.","Lu Yun looked down and rubbed his forehead.","“I want to eat...” a hesitant voice rang out.","He lifted his eyes to see a little boy roughly eight years old approach hesitantly. Skinny and frail, his eyes were bright and alive—a marked difference to those around him.","“What is your name?” Lu Yun asked.","The little boy shook his head to indicate that he had no name.","“Then from now on, your name is Wang Shu. You will train with me starting today.” Lu Yun waved a large piece of meat out of the pot and directed it to Wang Shu.","“Wang Shu...” the little boy nodded gently. “Alright then, I’m called Wang Shu from now on.” He gulped and grabbed the meat, running away. “I’m going to share this with my dad...”","He didn’t look back at all, but his voice drifted back on the wind. His actions prompted the others to come forward, but Lu Yun didn’t give them any meat. Just soup was enough for them. He wanted to select cultivators; only cultivators had the right to eat meat.","Wang Shu was the first, and his name was another term for the moon on Earth. There was a famous poem on Earth that one would raise their head to gaze upon the bright moon, then look back down to pine for home."]},{"number":2150,"title":"Chapter 2150: Chapter 2105: Vegetative People","paragraphs":["Chapter 2105: Vegetative People","As enormous as the three beasts were, they weren’t enough to satiate the million plus residents of Jingzhou City. At the same time, Lu Yun never intended to end their hunger. He just wanted to arouse their long vanished desire.","Greed and desire were the most primitive emotions of living beings. If one lacked even that, then one was alive only through sheer instinct.","Such was the case in Jingzhou City and for all of the ordinary beings in this world. Perhaps cultivators still possessed greed and desire, but ordinary living beings were like grass and trees. They lived in order to live and gave their bodies up as food when they died. They were no different from unintelligent grass and trees.","All of their desires had receded.","What Lu Yun sought to do was to spark the long lost desire hidden deep in their souls. But ultimately, he failed.","Out of one million, thirty-four thousand, eight hundred and ninety-six people in the city, he chose only Wang Shu. The boy was the only one suited for cultivation; the others were no different from grass on the ground.","The results left him at a loss; he didn’t understand them. The people left after they ate their portion. Some went back to staring off into space while others returned to repairing the city walls.","Grease ringing her mouth, Yuan Yi walked up to Lu Yun and looked eagerly at the pot. “Why don’t you give me the rest since they’re not eating it.”","“Why are things like this?” Lu Yun frowned. He didn’t read any emotions in the people’s eyes, not even wooden ones.","“In this world, only cultivators are people,” Yuan Yi sighed. “Ordinary beings are just trees and grass. Cultivators look after them out of self interest. And of course, it’s always good to find more of our kind among the trees and grass.”","“Two-legged sheep?” Lu Yun’s frown deepened.","Yuan Yi shook her head. “That’s what the hunters call them. We cultivators protect the cities and cannot kill the innocent. We need to constantly keep our desires in check. Once we look at them as sheep and kill whoever we like, that will be when we are not far from death ourselves.","“We’d turn into those hunters even if we didn’t die. A life of aimless wandering in the desolate wilderness is a short one,” Yuan Yi sighed. “Those three would’ve died out there sooner or later if they hadn’t come across you. They would be eaten by ghost zombies, assimilated by them, or starved to death.","“Huh? Wait!” She turned sharply to Lu Yun and regarded him with astonishment. “Those three are incredibly strong and qi runs through their bodies. How were you able to fight three of them by yourself and kill them?”","Although the young man hadn’t gone into detail, Yuan Yi had safeguarded the city for a hundred years. She knew the rules of this world like the back of her hand and what kind of person Lu Yun had killed.","What surprised her was his strength. He’d been weaker than her before, but now he could kill three powerful hunters by himself?","“I’ve grown stronger.” Lu Yun was in an awful mood as he felt that there was no way to tackle the problem.","He knew what Yuan Yi spoke of. It was impossible for one person to survive by themselves in a world like this. He needed to latch tightly onto the thigh that was Jingzhou City and nurture a few more powerhouses to slowly change the world.","But now... he felt that he had the heart, yet lacked the requisite strength. It was a situation he’d never encountered before.","Turn a group of vegetative people into powerful cultivators?","They possessed no emotion or desire, they didn’t even have a reason to live. It would be better if they were actual plants or vegetables. Lu Yun could spark sentience in those and slowly nurture them. But these walking bodies were sentient, intelligent, and held their own opinions.","Their goal in life was to wait for death.","It was a deeply rooted mindset that resulted in a pot of meat locating only one candidate suited for cultivation. That greatly depressed Lu Yun.","“The city lord once wanted to do the same thing you’re doing, but he also failed.” Yuan Yi knew what Lu Yun was thinking when she saw his conflicted expression. “Give it up, there’s no hope.”","That city lord was dead, long dead. Apart from Lu Yun, Yuan Yi was the only cultivator in Jingzhou City.","“And what about you?” Lu Yun looked at Yuan Yi and said slowly, “What do you live for? Do you wait for death like they do?”","Yuan Yi paused, then shook her head. “I live so I can live a bit longer and a bit more comfortably... and so they can live longer.”","If she died, the whole city would die. She lived for both herself and the entire city of... vegetative people.","“Why has your strength increased so rapidly?!” she demanded solemnly. “It doesn’t make any sense. Heaven and earth are dead, so we must slowly hone our blood and qi without help from the outside world. Even your cultivation method requires a slow process of tempering!","“It’s not possible for you to improve so quickly!”","She was incredibly serious as there was only one possible way for Lu Yun to boost his strength by such a great degree in a short period of time. He would have to have slaughtered an entire city and absorbed all of their qi and blood to bolster himself.","But if he did so, his cultivation would deviate and he would kill wherever he went.","Even the most brutal of hunters didn’t commit such acts. They simply treated living beings as two-legged sheep, eating some when they were hungry. They didn’t treat sheep as cultivation resources.","In other worlds, an increase in a cultivator’s strength was their secret to keep. No one had the right to pry into it. But in a world like this, Lu Yun had to answer Yuan Yi. If he couldn’t, only one of them would remain on the scene.","Either one of them left, or they would fight to the death.","“Heaven and earth still live. I found a blade of living grass and located the vestiges of their power. I used it to improve my cultivation,” Lu Yun answered candidly as he knew what was on Yuan Yi’s mind. “I can take you there right now.”","“I can’t leave the city,” she shook her head. “The wilderness is very dangerous. Although there are no ghost zombies during the day, there are other creatures of misfortune. I would not last a day out there.”","Lu Yun blinked. The only trouble he’d run into was the three beasts with horns.","“But if heaven and earth are still alive...” Yuan Yi hesitated and took out a tattered map from her robes. “This is a map of the world in times gone by. It might be useful to you. Go increase your strength during the day and come back to guard the city at night.”"]},{"number":2151,"title":"Chapter 2151: Chapter 2106: External Circulation of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2106: External Circulation of Heaven and Earth","“I thought you were going to throw me out,” Lu Yun said haltingly as he rubbed the back of his neck.","“Throw you out?” Yuan Yi huffed at him. “Did I spend all that time and effort saving you from the pit just to throw you out of the city? Don’t worry, I’ve memorized your method of heaven and earth and will train Wang Shu well.”","“Okay!” Lu Yun nodded. Truth be told, one’s strength wouldn’t increase by much even if one cultivated for a lifetime in the city. Dangers in the wilderness were also an enormous function of luck.","“But before I go, I’m going to repair the city’s formation,” he mentioned again.","“Repair the city’s formation?” Yuan Yi frowned. She would’ve repaired it long ago if that were possible. With no more origin stones, it was a futile effort to repair the formation.","Jingzhou City’s formation teetered on the edge of collapse. Although there were still a few pieces of origin stones within it, no one knew when they would be fully consumed.","The moment the formation collapsed would be the moment the city fell.","“The formation of heaven and earth,” Lu Yun chuckled. “My cultivation method stems from one formation—the formation of heaven and earth. I can modify the city’s formation into that and have it circulate as a self-contained heaven and earth. That will provide endless origin stones and create its own cycle of reincarnation.”","Lu Yun paused when he said the word “reincarnation”. The heart of a circulating heaven and earth was reincarnation. His method of heaven and earth was actually the process of cultivating reincarnation. Instead of cultivating the strength of reincarnation, the method approached it from the angle of manifesting reincarnation through the operation of heaven and earth.","Flames were the external manifestation of reincarnation. Heaven and earth... were the manifestation of reincarnation.","He nodded without a flicker of change in expression.","“It looks like the solution to this part of reality is reincarnation.” Lu Yun nodded slowly. He would have to save this world first if he wanted to dismantle the barrier of nothing and end the great devastation.","He couldn’t do it alone—he really couldn’t. But who could help him?","He’d have to help himself first. Hope was possible only if he stayed alive. He also felt that those at home—the mistress, Dao King, Hongjun, Pangu, Fuxi, and the others couldn’t possibly remain unmoved. Surely they were also thinking of ways to save this world.","It was more than saving all of life, it was also salvation for themselves. Thus, Lu Yun bent his mind to modifying the city’s defensive formation. When Wang Shu returned, Yuan Yi decided to take the completely inexperienced boy as her disciple. She taught him the cultivation method of heaven and earth.","The method was a manner of cultivation, not an actual instruction manual. Thus, Yuan Yi was able to use her previous methods to cultivate heaven and earth. Compared to what Lu Yun possessed, Yuan Yi’s knowledge was more suited to the boy.","In any case, Lu Yun was used to leaving his work to others. He was in charge of selecting candidates, Yuan Yi could be responsible for teaching them.","Modifying a formation was a walk in the park for Lu Yun in his current state. He didn’t even need to break the formation’s original structure. He just needed to repair what was broken and then alter it into a formation of heaven and earth.","Its foundations were originally one hundred and eight origin stones—thirty-three of them were broken. The remaining seventy-five were more or less intact, but the energy within them was mostly exhausted.","Based on Lu Yun’s calculations, the formation could endure for another thousand years if it didn’t encounter other pressure. If the ghost zombies kept attacking it, however, it would only stand for another hundred years.","The city would fall when it broke after a hundred years.","For the moment, the formation’s overall structure was more or less intact. Even though it wavered, it didn’t run the risk of collapsing.","“While the formation can hold for one hundred years, the people in the city might not be able to.”","After a day’s worth of repairs, a mystical purple haze appeared before nightfall. The formation had been modified into one of heaven and earth. Since it was assembled into an internal circulation of heaven and earth, the origin stones of the formation regenerated with the cycling of the formation. All sorts of energy continuously transformed into each other.","Such was a reflection of heaven and earth. Living beings were born of heaven and earth and died of heaven and earth. They obtained nourishment from the world and excreted waste that they did not need. This waste, as well as their bodies, nascent spirits, and souls decomposed into heaven and earth when they died. They returned to being pure energy and filtered back into heaven and earth.","Such was a process of reincarnation.","Lu Yun also finally understood where he’d gotten inspiration for the formation of heaven and earth in the world of immortals. It was from the power of reincarnation in the Tome of Life and Death!","He’d fully organized his thoughts and knew how to proceed from here. Lu Yun’s strength noticeably increased after he set up a formation of heaven and earth.","“Setting up formations can help me get stronger?” He sat on the city walls and mused over his thoughts as ghost zombies appeared with the setting of the sun. “Heaven and earth are still alive. In fact, they connected to the formation when I set it up and built the circulatory system. Did I absorb some more energy from the world when that happened?","“No, no. My increase in power isn’t just in terms of strength, but also in terms of mastery over reincarnation. My understanding of strength has risen to greater heights compared to before?” Lu Yun frowned and gently pushed the air.","KABOOM.","An enormous explosion detonated in the distance and obliterated countless ghost zombies. In the next moment, Lu Yun noted a current of black air surging through the void and into his body. The energy that he’d just expended was replenished.","“The circulation of heaven and earth!” His eyes lit up. “I’ve completed the circulatory system and now it circulates externally!”","External circulation meant that the energy he released could be recalled back into his body at any time. Even the ghost zombies that he killed could turn into his strength and be absorbed into his being.","This would be called demonic dao in the world of immortals, but it was a life-saving measure in this world.","Brightening immeasurably, Lu Yun jumped down from the city walls and flung himself into the hordes of ghost zombies. He’d repaired the formation and blocked the gap in the city gates, so the citizens used to rushing for the city gates loitered where they were, unsure of what to do.","With Lu Yun as the vanguard before, a few ghost zombies still occasionally made it through. That would be when the people clubbed the enemy to death. But now, the ghost zombies were completely halted outside of the formation. None could make it in.","The modified formation was much, much stronger than before.","etvolare's Thoughts","I really don't know how I feel about this whole vegetative humans concept. It means all of us are vegetables too... I dunno, would love to hear your thoughts."]},{"number":2152,"title":"Chapter 2152: Chapter 2107: God’s Tomb","paragraphs":["Chapter 2107: God’s Tomb","Aooooooouuu.","A long howl cut through the depths of the night, resulting in a rapid recession of the ghost zombie tide.","“What’s going on?” His wonderful time of slaughter cut short, Lu Yun paused and looked into the distance. Two dots of black light flashed through his eyes as he scanned everything within five thousand kilometers.","Death art, Spectral Eye!","The death arts began recovering after he reached an external circulation of heaven and earth. Of them, the Spectral Eye was the first to come back.","Ghost zombies teemed within five thousand kilometers, their origins unknown. It seemed like they’d always been there. They shambled around aimlessly when they didn’t sense the presence of living things, but snapped into a berserk rage the moment they did.","As he watched, Lu Yun saw an unlucky wild beast being dug up from the ground and torn to pieces. It was so unlucky that it didn’t even have a chance to turn into a ghost zombie before it was eaten.","The Spectral Eye couldn’t reach further than that, but Lu Yun could clearly sense an incredibly strong existence in that direction. The howl emanated from it and was calling all of the ghost zombies to it in frenzied motion.","“Is it another ghost zombie?” Lu Yun frowned, unable to see the thing but able to hear the sound it emitted.","The ghost zombies attacking Jingzhou City had swiftly disappeared and congregated in the direction five thousand kilometers away. Extreme curiosity danced in his heart.","“I’m going to take a look and see what’s happening.” He turned around to face a blankly staring Yuan Yi on the wall.","“Oh, okay,” she nodded subconsciously. “Be careful.”","Lu Yun was already gone.","“Has he... really repaired the city’s formation?” She slapped herself hard across the face, trying to determine if she was dreaming or not.","“Teacher.” Next to her, Wang Shu also asked in an incredulous voice, “Are the ghost zombies not breaking in tonight?”","“Not just tonight, but all the nights from now on. They will not be ravaging our home ever again.” A smile blossomed on Yuan Yi’s face. The defensive formation had become a formation of heaven and earth with an internal circulatory system of its own. It needed no energy source and could operate eternally so long as its foundations weren’t ruined.","She didn’t know how to view this change in circumstance.","“Let’s do our best in cultivation,” Yuan Yi smiled. “Hope is needed in this land.”","“Okay!” Wang Shu nodded emphatically.","When Yuan Yi looked down at the boy, she thought back to how her teacher had picked her out of the crowd and taught her everything she knew. Her teacher had wanted her to protect this city. She, however, wanted Wang Shu to protect hope.","......","The night was pitch black; the nights of this world seemed to run particularly dim. Lu Yun wouldn’t be able to see the way if not for the Spectral Eye.","“Five thousand meters to the southeast...” He took out the map that Yuan Yi had given him and took his bearings, studying what the map depicted. It was from very long ago, when the world was still alive. Although it’d been so long, its major topographical features were yet to change.","“God’s Tomb?!” His eyes widened when he saw a landmark in the direction he was heading towards.","God’s Tomb!","The only characters for that landmark, there was no further indication as to what they might refer to. However, Lu Yun noticed that he could read the written language of the map.","“It looks like the civilization in the nothing stems from the mistress, Dao King, and God. It’s an extension of the civilization in this world.”","The label of God’s Tomb made him very uncomfortable. Was it really God’s tomb?","“So did God die once before in the past? Is he dead or alive right now? Or is this another God’s tomb?” Although questions swirled in his mind, Lu Yun kept up the pace. He exerted himself with the Boundless Step and soon arrived at God’s Tomb.","The howl continued to ring through the land and ghost zombies were gathered here, piled atop of one another as if they were protecting something. The characters of God’s Tomb were carved into a towering mountain in scarlet font. They dripped with blood, but the blood within the characters had dried up.","“Whatever it is, it’s inside the tomb.” Lu Yun looked at the mountain in front of him. Roughly five thousand meters across, it was a singular mountain rather than a mountain range. If it wasn’t for the characters carved into it, there would be nothing special about it. He could see the layouts around the mountain, but they were dead.","Feng shui layouts were nurtured by heaven and earth. Feng shui and formation were two sides of the same coin. They were the same, yet also not the same.","Formations were an active existence that required someone to set up so they could release their power. Feng shui was a passive existence that heaven and earth took control of once it came into being. There was no need for anyone to activate it. Once it started operating, no one could stop it unless it broke.","One way to stop feng shui layouts from operating was to kill heaven and earth. These layouts around the mountain had stopped because the world was dead. The remaining vestiges of heaven and earth were insufficient to power their operations.","“The layouts outside aren’t operating, but the ones inside the tomb are! They’re still deploying their full force! There’s power of heaven and earth inside the tomb!” Lu Yun lit up. The power of the world wasn’t in the skies, but in the tomb!","Endless ghost zombies crawled over the mountain, cocooning it with protection. The tomb proper could be found beneath the mountain. Apart from the summons that was the howl, there were also waves of faint trembling coming from beneath the mountain.","Something seemed to be ramming the inside of God’s Tomb.","“Let’s go take a look!” Lu Yun itched for action. He’d analyzed the layout in front of him—although it wasn’t operating, the ones inside were. He could use the ones outside to deduce certain facts from the ones inside.","It was a dual layered layout that he’d never seen before, but he could use their way of assembly to determine their use and power.","With the establishment of an external circulation of heaven and earth, so did formula dao come back to him."]},{"number":2153,"title":"Chapter 2153: Chapter 2108: Wanfeng","paragraphs":["Chapter 2108: Wanfeng","After formula dao analyzed God’s Tomb, Lu Yun vanished on the spot with a shift of his body.","Given the external circulation of heaven and earth, he could turn an area eighteen meters around him into his personal domain. It was his heaven and earth, his world.","He controlled everything within this radius.","If his external circulation grew strong enough, he would encompass all of subjectivity and the objective world. He would be the omnipotent presence that could affect objectivity with the subjective.","But Lu Yun was too insignificant for now and he could only influence an area of eighteen meters.","Still, that was a start.","......","He entered the tomb without needing to dig a thief’s tunnel. Although the tomb was covered by mud and rocks, those were the same as air to someone of Lu Yun’s cultivation level. He easily made his way in when he deployed his personal domain.","If there was a place that the external circulation of heaven and earth couldn’t pierce through, then there would be nothing that a thief’s tunnel could do either.","Scarlet light flooded the premises and countless ghost zombies came into view. They were crammed together like cockroaches in an enormous clearing that housed an altar at its center. The altar was the same as one that Lu Yun had seen before—the mother altar!","It was God’s mother altar!","There was a figure standing on top of it, a faint smear of red. It’d thrown its head back to howl at the sky, like it was summoning something. The masses of ghost zombies in the vicinity were gathered by this figure in red.","When Lu Yun took a closer look, he realized that it was a young woman dressed in blood-red robes. Shapely and lithe, he could see her clearly despite their pronounced distance.","His heart quailed.","Wanfeng.","The young woman standing in the center of the altar was Wanfeng! Someone who he least expected to see!","Lu Yun could plainly identify that it was Wanfeng, not just someone who looked very similar to her!","Wanfeng...","She was the first person he’d seen after the Tome of Life and Death brought him to the world of immortals. He’d met her again when he traveled back to the great wilderness. And now, he’d come across her in reality!","Many had come and gone in Lu Yun’s moderate span of years. He’d drifted away from numerous friends he’d once fought side by side with until they completely lost touch. But Wanfeng had never exited his life.","She’d been waiting for him in the past when he traveled through time. She was waiting for him now although he’d left his existence and was the equivalent of dead to those who’d known him.","Not Qing Yu, not the little fox, but Wanfeng.","His body turned numb and a strange feeling rose from the bottom of his heart. His external circulation of heaven and earth exploded outward with unbridled power, sectioning him from this part of the void.","It was like he’d vanished, though he remained where he was. Nothing could see or sense him as he strode through the void and paced toward Wanfeng dressed in a scarlet silk dress.","She was still howling.","The ghost zombies she summoned furiously threw themselves against an eerie rune on the other side of the altar. It curved and twisted, forming a blood-red skull. The vast tomb was flooded with scarlet light because of it. It was plainly a seal, one that kept the real tomb hidden away.","If Lu Yun wished to enter God’s Tomb, he would have to first break the skull shape.","Wanfeng was directing the boundless ghost zombies to break the seal. They converged onto the altar from all directions and rammed their bodies against the rune.","Lu Yun shook with horror. He didn’t know why Wanfeng was here or why she could control the ghost zombies. Right now, her life form was no different from them. She was also a ghost zombie, but one infinitely stronger than ordinary ones.","Her eyes gleamed with scarlet light—possibly an innate characteristic or a reflection of the blood-red skull. The look in her eyes was remote and emotionless as she considered the skull rune.","Lu Yun arrived next to her and could sense the rampaging brutality inside of her that was the same as the ghost zombies.","She was Wanfeng.","He shook violently as grief emanated from his body, an emotion that was swiftly dispersed by the external circulation of heaven and earth. Lu Yun remained cautious and prudent, furiously deploying formula dao on everything within his domain and trying to determine the reason for what he saw.","He also tried to calculate how to turn a ghost zombie back into a living person.","“Is...” Lu Yun took a deep breath. “Is Wanfeng here from the world of immortals, or was there one here all along?”","He had no idea what was going on. Perhaps the Wanfeng in front of him had come to this world for some reason after he left his original world, or perhaps there was one here to begin with and the one in the world of immortals existed because of her.","No matter which situation it was, Lu Yun had never fathomed the scene in front of him right now.","“I... I can’t fight her” was the only answer he came to after his analysis. Not only was he not a match for this Wanfeng, but she could rip through his external circulation and tear his primary body to pieces.","Lu Yun didn’t dare take the bet that Wanfeng would remember him if he revealed himself. She might not.","Regardless, he had to try and save her.","He stood eighteen meters away from her, silently watching the figure in red. She was still howling and staring at the skull. More ghost zombies gathered around them and threw themselves at the rune, their durable bodies cracking like an egg as soon as they touched it.","At the same time, there were so many of them and the ghost zombies contained a strange poison inside their bodies that continuously polluted the seal.","Finally—","Boom.","The scarlet skull shook."]},{"number":2154,"title":"Chapter 2154: Chapter 2109: A Dream","paragraphs":["Chapter 2109: A Dream","Lu Yun was clueless about what had happened and what the Wanfeng in front of him wished to do. He had even less of a clue what might be hidden in God’s Tomb.","The cracking skull-shaped rune, however, gave him a very uncomfortable feeling. Something in Lu Yun’s heart shattered as well when it broke and his thoughts suddenly ran much more smoothly than before.","It felt like an internal obstacle had disappeared and his cultivation showed signs of breaking through. His domain of heaven and earth eighteen meters around him abruptly expanded by several times over.","“What, what is this??” Lu Yun’s eyes went wide.","“Sir, there are one hundred and eight seals in this realm that seal off this world,” Wanfeng suddenly said. “This servant can only help young master with one of them.”","She’d been able to see Lu Yun all along!","However, she was starting to fade away. Lu Yun reached out a hand to grab her, but his hand closed on empty air.","“Wanfeng!!” he yelled.","“Don’t worry, young master, Wanfeng has entered reality through a dream and become a king of ghost zombies. That is how I was able to direct them into breaking one of the seals. My primary body is fine in the world of immortals.” The maid smiled brilliantly when she saw how worried Lu Yun was. “Big sis Mo Yi says that breaking all one hundred and eight seals will revive this world. There will be more people who come and meet the young master in their dreams. They will break the rest of the seals!","“I was the first, the second is that fatty Li Youcai...”","Her giggling drifted away until her entire being scattered on the air, leaving one final sentence lingering in the air. “Come back soon, young master.”","Enormous reassurance flooded Lu Yun’s heart and a steady undercurrent of background anxiety since his arrival in this world dispersed with Wanfeng’s disappearance. His friends and family knew where he was and what he was doing. They were all waiting for his return.","Entering reality through dreams...","With a dream as the realm and a ghost zombie king as replica to break the seal. This was one of the little fox’s abilities!","The little fox had observed everything that took place in the burial mound via her dreams when she was buried beneath Myriad Formation Summit. She’d even seen Lu Yun and the others while she dreamed and was ultimately woken up by the young man.","There was also Ah Zhi apart from the little fox! All of this was likely the result of their combined efforts, led by Mo Yi and the Dao King. But to Lu Yun, there was another pivotal link in the process—reincarnation!","He’d revived the power of reincarnation after creating an external circulation of heaven and earth. Wanfeng arrived soon after that, an indication that this development had something to do with his actions.","Lu Yun’s mood took a measurable turn for the better when his thoughts traveled here.","“But things shouldn’t be this easy!” His brow furrowed again. “If simply breaking one hundred and eight seals is sufficient to resurrect this world, why is everything so complicated?”","He looked at the shattered rune and scattering ghost zombies.","“As strong as the seal is, there are many ways to break it...” Lu Yun’s mind spun rapidly through a variety of scenarios. He could already tell that the truth wasn’t as simple as it appeared on the surface.","There were indeed one hundred and eight seals, but it was another reason that’d killed this part of reality. He even thought that the seals weren’t killing the world, but nurturing it. The world that resurrected from their ashes might be a new one.","One hundred and eight?","He was very sensitive about this number as his formation of heaven and earth had originally been one hundred and eight Formation of Heavenly Spirits and Earthly Demons. Additionally, was Wanfeng really unaffected by her brief jaunt as a ghost zombie king and command of endless ghost zombies?","New worries flourished in Lu Yun’s mind. But no matter what, there was nothing he could do for them now. All he could do was borrow the opportunity created by the rebirth of heaven and earth and furiously enhance his strength.","His circulation of heaven and earth was more than ten times stronger than before and encompassed a radius of one hundred and eighty meters. More than just an expansion of range, it was also an increase in might.","He felt absolutely invincible within his domain. At the very least, nothing he’d met so far in this reality could threaten him. The same might not hold true for what he’d yet to meet, however. There had to be more than a few ghost zombies in this unbounded, vast world filled with a lifeless atmosphere.","Powerhouses had once thronged the land. Among their ranks had been a being who was infinitely close to the subjective overruling the objective. Although Lu Yun didn’t know whether that wondrous existence was alive or dead at present, none of those illustrious figures from times past were able to save this current existence.","That illustrated one problem—that this world, this existence, was far more frightening than what Lu Yun imagined. What’d destroyed this world still lingered within it. It hadn’t concealed itself and was simply standing there quietly, too big for him to see.","An ant at the foot of Mount Tai was unable to see Mount Tai. Lu Yun believed that he was only an ant at the moment and wholly insignificant to the true horrors of this world.","For now, his greatest enemies were the unending hordes of ghost zombies. He could suppress them, but the ghost zombie king that Wanfeng had manifested as could still easily kill him. All he could curtail were the ordinary ghost zombies.","A ghost zombie king...","That was a powerful existence that Lu Yun had yet to see before this.","“I need to continue to focus on cultivation and see if I can dismantle another seal. That will inject more vitality into this world and then... then...” Lu Yun took a deep breath. “It will meld into my external circulation of heaven and earth!”","He’d discovered that after the seal broke, the revived heaven and earth didn’t return to the world. It assimilated directly into his external circulation and strengthened him. It wasn’t the supplement of a resurrected world but a direct infusion into his heaven and earth.","God’s Tomb...","This was likely another one of God’s arrangements.","Lu Yun took a deep breath and looked at the shattered mark. A drop of blood remained of it; the bloody characters outside of the tomb had vanished. All of the blood had gathered to this place and formed that drop of blood.","It was God’s blood.","Lu Yun beckoned with his hand and retrieved the drop of blood. He could clearly sense that it was a drop of dead blood, one without any vitality. Other than the color that indicated it was blood, there were none of the usual characteristics associated with blood."]},{"number":2155,"title":"Chapter 2155: Chapter 2110: Table and Cup","paragraphs":["Chapter 2110: Table and Cup","Lu Yun took stock of his current level of strength. He was strong, very strong. He’d reached a height that he’d never reached before in the nothing. It was an unparalleled peak even higher than when God ensured their mutual destruction.","This level of strength exceeded what could be commanded by a living being. He could affect his surroundings with his thoughts—the operation of rules, confirmation of laws, and establishment of order.","He could now set order how he wished within the one hundred and eighty meters of his domain. He could design worlds, create life, and consign it all to nothing with a single thought.","Such was subjectivity affecting objectivity.","The nihil was denoted by lack of rules and disorder. It was an empty void that contained absolutely nothing. Rules, orders, and everything related—even disorder—were settings that needed to be arranged.","In this moment, a heretofore unfelt sense of enlightenment filled Lu Yun’s mind.","“Perhaps there was no so-called existence in the far off past, just a patch of empty nothing. It was boundless without end, but also tiny in the extreme. Then, for reasons unknown, an incredibly strong being was born in the nothing. He created order, rules, disorder, and this part of reality with a single thought.”","With his body as the center, Lu Yun could also create a patch of reality that spanned three hundred and sixty meters. It would endure forever so long as he remained alive, just like unending reality.","Of course, this was all speculation. Not even formula dao could determine if his theories were correct. At the same time, they completely upended his understanding of the world. Not even the mistress or Dao King could postulate to this level.","All living beings thought all along that rules, orders, and disorder were objective constructs—that even reality itself was an objective existence.","An impalpable rhythm dominated everything, enabling objectivity to reign over all. But when Lu Yun fully comprehended this level of objectivity and subjectivity, he discovered that this rhythm was also subjective.","A subjective existence had arranged for it to exist in an objective world, giving birth to this rhythm and setting it into motion. If not for this subjective existence, then everything within objectivity would be... nothing.","It was easy enough to understand.","Picture a table and a cup. A person’s hand had placed the cup onto the table. Without the person, there would be no cup on the table. There wouldn’t even be a cup or table.","In the same vein, the rhythm and disorder of creation were the same concept. Without the influence of a subjective will, neither of them would exist.","Little beings thought that a power they didn’t understand put the cup on the table, that this power was the pattern of objectivity. Such was the understanding of all living beings, that the laws and rules that dominated creation were objective patterns unaffected by subjectivity.","“I can create reality with the flip of a hand now, one on par with this patch of reality. But still, it’s not the pinnacle I seek.” Lu Yun shook his head with a sigh. “Everything I create is based off of this part of reality. I would drift around rootless if we break away from this reality. There is no possibility of survival in an objective world in which nothing exists.","“Breaking all one hundred and eight seals is still insufficient to ensure escape.”","A tight frown creased his brow. He’d fully considered everything to come thanks to the determination of formula dao. His heaven and earth would absorb energy from the new heaven and earth once all of the seals were broken. It would be perfected, but he still wouldn’t be at the state of subjectivity affecting objectivity.","“What would be the point of me coming here if things were so easy that the mistress and Dao King could fully pave the road for me? They could’ve just accomplished everything in their era,” Lu Yun chuckled. “So what am I thinking about all of this for? What I should be considering is how to survive in this world.”","Entering reality through a dream was hardly an easy task. Although Lu Yun didn’t know the particulars, he could imagine that it took incredibly arduous effort. The barrier of nothing was indestructible and resulted in death if touched.","Even if the connection between the Tome of Life and Death and ten Yama Kings were severed, there was likely still a price to pay after Wanfeng entered this world through a dream.","Let’s take things one step at a time. Lu Yun had to wait since he was unaware of the situation in the nothing. There was no point fretting, especially as he should be focused on how to stay alive.","Although he now possessed more strength than he ever had before, he was also keenly aware of one thing. There were inordinately terrifying existences in this vast world—such as the ghost zombie king that Wanfeng had borrowed earlier.","Live.","He had to live on in this unbounded reality.","Lu Yun exited God’s Tomb with the map that Yuan Yi had given him. The tomb was now an ordinary mountain no different from the other ones around it.","“There is no second God’s Tomb on the map.” The diagram spanned a range of one billion trillion kilometers. It was infinitely greater than the Three Thousand, yet Lu Yun didn’t find a second place marked God’s Tomb.","Compared to the magnitude of reality, what the map recorded was just the tip of the iceberg.","“This world is too big. Even I can’t quickly walk out of the map’s range with my current capabilities.” Lu Yun shot into the air with a wry chuckle and headed for a tiny plant.","He followed the plant’s roots to find a sliver of heaven and earth. This was the only way he could strengthen his external circulation of heaven and earth apart from breaking the seals.","The young man settled into a routine of returning to Jingzhou City before night fell to hold off the ghost zombies, then exploring the world when the sun rose. Lu Yun wanted to find some clues as to the death of the world and the source of the ghost zombies.","He was certain that the ghost zombies used to be denizens of the world, that they’d turned into these horrifying entities due to various reasons.","“Can it be that the wondrous personage who created this reality is dead?” was Lu Yun’s speculation.","Of course, the notion that a subjective person created this reality was still speculation awaiting confirmation. Meanwhile, his strength continued to slowly increase."]},{"number":2156,"title":"Chapter 2156: Chapter 2111: Hunting a Ghost Zombie King","paragraphs":["Chapter 2111: Hunting a Ghost Zombie King","Lu Yun traveled through the land during the day and returned to the city to rest at night, or to fend off ghost zombies.","This world was many times more terrifying at night. There were no ghost zombies during the day, but they blotted out the land at night. Lu Yun still wasn’t able to survive in this world on his own even though his strength had risen to incredible heights.","Thankfully, the ghost zombies attacked once every three to five days, as opposed to every night.","The young man had fully repaired the city’s formation and transformed it into one of heaven and earth. It was fully self sufficient and would endure eternally so long as it didn’t encounter an existence like a zombie king.","With an internal circulation of heaven and earth inside the formation, all of its energy was converted again and again for repeated usage. Not a single drop was wasted. Of course, energy was consumed when the ghost zombies attacked. That sort of energy needed to be replenished.","Lu Yun explored every nook and cranny within five billion kilometers and found numerous fragments of the strength of heaven and earth. He infused them into the formation while keeping any crystals condensed out of the strength for his own usage.","Yuan Yi and Wang Shu’s strength leapt forward. Though they’d yet to reach the stage of an external circulation of heaven and earth, Yuan Yi was more than ten times stronger than her previous peak. Even Wang Shu possessed the ability to keep himself safe against the hordes of ghost zombies.","......","It’d been twelve hundred years since Lu Yun set foot in this world. He investigated more of the surroundings as his strength grew, but found no second place like God’s Tomb or a place with a seal.","He did find thirty-eight ruins of cities and three that still stood. There were more than one million residents in each of the remaining cities. Though helmed by powerful cultivators, they wavered on the edge of collapse and couldn’t hold out for long.","He brought all of their inhabitants to Jingzhou City without another word. Ordinary people didn’t have the ability to resist ghost zombies, but enough people gathered together would give rise to gifted cultivators and hope.","With his current level of strength, it was an easy task to bring a few million people back to Jingzhou City.","After twelve hundred years of development and the addition of three cities’ worth of inhabitants, Jingzhou City boasted of more than ten million residents. The originally tattered city had expanded outward three times.","There were more than one hundred powerful cultivators protecting it. Apart from Yuan Yi, Wang Shu, and the protectors of the cities that later joined Jingzhou City, all of them were born later and practiced Lu Yun’s method of heaven and earth.","After hundreds or almost one thousand years of cultivation, they rivaled Yuan Yi when she first met Lu Yun.","Jingzhou City finally flared with a different kind of vitality in this bleak and desolate land. Lu Yun also transplanted numerous surviving plants into the city over the years, as well as collected crystalline fragments condensed from the power of heaven and earth. Over time, a tiny hint of energy from heaven and earth budded out of the crystals and plants to circulate around the city.","As for the crystalline shards of heaven and earth... they hadn’t originally existed in this world. Some changes had taken place when the world died, giving birth to these fragments. It was through them that Lu Yun was able to do what he could do.","On this day, the curtain of night once more fell over them and Lu Yun remained alone on the city gates, looking out into the distance. Night was pitch black in this real world. Even with his vision capabilities, Lu Yun could only see five hundred thousand kilometers ahead. Everything else outside of that range was too dark to discern.","This night was quiet without any ghost zombies. Frankly speaking, Jingzhou City no longer feared ordinary ghost zombies. Zombies with a hint of instinct left in them also avoided drawing close to the city.","Lu Yun regarded the night gravely. Although the enemy didn’t attack tonight, he could keenly perceive a terrifyingly powerful presence building outside his range of vision. It coldly regarded the city—a zombie king according to formula dao.","The Jingzhou-City-led changes in the area had finally raised a zombie king’s attention. Ghost zombie kings possessed intelligence and were infinite times more terrifying than ordinary ghost zombies.","Regular ghost zombies were derived from mortals or weak cultivators. Ghost zombie kings resulted from the powerhouses of the world after everything changed around them.","Lu Yun had run into four zombie kings over the past twelve hundred years. Apart from fighting the weakest to a draw, he’d had to run for his life after catching a glimpse of the others from a distance.","The one surveilling Jingzhou City was the weakest one; its territory was the closest to the city.","Jingzhou City had come under another zombie king before, but after Wanfeng entered the world in a dream twelve hundred years ago, it flew apart after she possessed it.","Other zombie kings naturally came to claim its territory after the demise of their brethren.","“Ghost zombie king, there’s nothing I can do about you and you can’t beat me either.” Lu Yun stood up and sent his thoughts through the void, depositing them onto the zombie king.","Given that it possessed intelligence, it would understand him. Jingzhou City was Lu Yun’s home base and he’d long set up terrifying formation upon formation for its defenses. If the zombie king came, he would use the formations of heaven and earth to destroy it.","But at the same time, the zombie king could fully wreck the tiny foundations that Lu Yun had set up over the past one thousand and two hundred years. Far from being alone, it was accompanied by one hundred million ghost zombies.","“ROAR!” It snarled at Lu Yun and slunk away into the darkness.","However, that left the young man more solemn than before.","“So it’s finally found me here... The next time it comes will be when it leads one hundred million ghost zombies in razing the city.” Lu Yun took a deep breath and looked forward with resolution. “Oof!”","His eyes lit up as he trembled. The power of heaven and earth within his body exploded, resonating with a surge of power from the skies. His cultivation increased explosively and his domain expanded by ten times. Everything within five thousand kilometers came under his purview.","“Twelve hundred years! The mistress and others have finally broken the second seal!” Lu Yun’s strength surged with the second dismantling of a seal. “In that case, I’ll strike first and hunt down the ghost zombie king!” A cold light glinted out of his eyes."]},{"number":2157,"title":"Chapter 2157: Chapter 2112: Kill","paragraphs":["Chapter 2112: Kill","Mo Yi and the others in the nothing broke the second seal just when a ghost zombie king found Jingzhou City and readied to lead an army of ghost zombies to the city! Lu Yun’s strength spontaneously increased by more than ten times, so he decided to strike first and kill the zombie king.","“I’m going with you.” Yuan Yi appeared the second before Lu Yun left. Dressed in green robes, she appeared the same as she did twelve hundred years ago. The passage of time had left no traces on her face or body.","However, she could hardly be considered in the same light as before. Although she wasn’t as strong as Lu Yun, there was an imperceptible circulation of heaven and earth outside her body now.","Plainly, this was just a new kind of cultivation technique for her. Her true strength came from herself, the extensive strength of the body that she deployed to dazzling heights.","To her, the external circulation of heaven and earth was an enhancement, but not her core strength. Twelve hundred years of cultivation had finally brought her to this point, but her circulation was a bit different from Lu Yun’s.","He frowned at her. “Do you know what I’m about to do?”","The utter gloom of night wrapped around them like a curtain. Nighttime visibility in this world was so low that the Spectral Eye could only scan two hundred and fifty thousand kilometers around him. He couldn’t say what might exist outside of that range.","Perhaps there was a ghost zombie king out there. Or perhaps there was more to be found.","“I don’t know,” a grave Yuan Yi shook her head. “But your strength noticeably increases each time you return. My strength will never improve like yours if I stay in the city.","“Even after twelve hundred years of cultivation, I am still unable to beat who you were when we first met. Thus, I must go out with you this time.”","There were three other powerful guardians holding down the fort, as well as Wang Shu and more than one hundred cultivators. The ghost zombie hordes could no longer threaten Jingzhou City. What she meant by when they first met was the Lu Yun prior to breaking the seal.","He took a deep look at her and nodded. “I’m going to kill a zombie king.”","Yuan Yi shook, then firmly nodded back at him. “I’m going with you. I may not be able to defeat one, but I’m confident in my ability to protect myself.”","Immense confidence shone out of her eyes. She’d learned about ghost zombie kings and how strong they were from those of the other three cities and their guardians.","“Alright,” Lu Yun didn’t turn her down. If the local cultivators wished to grow stronger, they had to experience battle. The city boasted sufficient protection now. Even if they didn’t have powerful guardians, the formation would endure for countless eons and more cultivators would be born during that period.","It was time that the cultivators focused on improving their strength. Being the strongest, it was easiest for Yuan Yi to improve. Her external circulation was just a shadow, but once she fully realized it and combined it with her own strength, she wouldn’t be that far off from Lu Yun before the second seal was broken.","“Let’s go.” Lu Yun rose into the air and activated his domain that spanned ten kilometers. He easily picked up Yuan Yi. “I’ll fight the zombie king, I leave its minions to you.”","He streaked into a ray of light and vanished with the girl. Their departure was so silent that no one knew that the city’s strongest powerhouses had left.","......","Inside a large rift valley.","Teeming masses of ghost zombies wandered to and fro. Other than Jingzhou City, there were no other cities within five billion kilometers of the rift valley. The city had been their only target before, but it was so strong now that they were afraid of it and didn’t dare approach.","The ghost zombie king resided in the depths of the valley. It had its head tilted toward the sky in a continuous howl, summoning ghost zombies to it. The zombie king would start the war on Jinghzou City once it gathered enough minions.","It was shaped like a massive lizard and ran fifty kilometers long. Bright red scales covered its body and four pairs of similarly colored bat wings sprouted from its back. A bloody light gleamed in its eyes and it constantly swept the premises with a watchful gaze.","Staggering killing intent wreathed around it, but it also showed numerous signs of decay. A putrid scent wafted from it as corpsewater trickled out of its brightly colored scales.","The zombie king suddenly looked upward and released two beams of light from its eyes that were almost tangible. The radiance cut through the void.","“So that’s a ghost zombie king!” Yuan Yi’s heart quailed. An icy grip clenched around her heart despite standing next to Lu Yun. She could sense that a singular zombie king would be sufficient to destroy the current Jingzhou City. All defensive measures and formations would be paper in front of it.","If it wasn’t for Lu Yun in residence, the city would’ve long been razed to the ground.","“Aouuu!” the ghost zombie king howled as its wings unfurled. It sped into a thin line of bright red as it pounced on Lu Yun and Yuan Yi.","The ghost zombies next to it shrieked as well. A dozen of the more powerful ones rose into the air alongside their king. While they weren’t zombie kings themselves, they possessed terrifying strength that placed them over regular ghost zombies.","They couldn’t fly since they didn’t have wings, but they were so strong that they could defy gravity like cannonballs.","“You take care of the ghost zombies, I’ll take out the zombie king,” Lu Yun shouted and separated from Yuan Yi to charge the enemy.","The zombie king snarled with fury, a violent light dawning in its eyes. But when it encountered the five kilometer domain around Lu Yun, it rapidly backed up like it’d been grazed by blazing flames.","Five kilometers wasn’t expansive—it was a rather small distance to the zombie king as it was fifty kilometers long. But those five kilometers were a death sentence to it. Half of its fore claws melted off when it touched the domain.","“Die!!” Lu Yun shouted, his speed far greater than the zombie king’s. He caught up as soon as the zombie king retreated. Magnificent power of heaven and earth condensed into an enormous fist and smashed into the zombie king’s head.","Bam!","The ghost zombie king’s head caved in from the blow."]},{"number":2158,"title":"Chapter 2158: Chapter 2113: A Second Ghost Zombie King","paragraphs":["Chapter 2113: A Second Ghost Zombie King","Yuan Yi and the surrounding ghost zombies froze, unsure of how to proceed. The girl panicked while the ghost zombies were overawed. Their most lofty king had its head caved in with a single blow! A feeling called terror rose from their hearts, an aberration in these ghost zombies that barely possessed thoughts of their own.","“Um... you...” Yuan Yi gaped at Lu Yun. She could clearly sense that the ghost zombie king would easily raze Jingzhou City, but the young man had defeated such an awful being with no second thought?","“What are you standing around for?” Lu Yun snapped. “Hurry up and kill the ghost zombies!”","He punched a second time and connected solidly with the ghost zombie king. It howled with outrage through its flattened head.","It yet lived.","When Lu Yun retracted his second punch, its misshapen body burst with black flames and it pounced on the human in a streak of light.","Lu Yun rapidly backed away, but the currents created by the zombie king’s movement were too formidable. When they swept over the young man, they shook the external circulation of heaven and earth around him.","He went flying as the zombie king recovered its form of a giant lizard. It blurred into a blackish-red shadow and threw itself forward at an unbelievable speed.","Lu Yun stabilized his body and thrust his arms outward, condensing two enormous fists that he brought up to meet the zombie king’s latest charge. He wielded no weapons in this world because he couldn’t find any material to craft with.","As heaven and earth were dead, so were all of its veins and mines of resources withered away. Materials such as stones and bricks used to build cities were mortal items; they couldn’t withstand Lu Yun’s strength.","He could only utilize his fists when he fought. They contained his power of heaven and earth, so each blow was the equivalent of a strike from a world. His further contained the power of reincarnation, a power that could transmute the zombie king’s strength into the purest strength of the world.","Lu Yun had finally obtained a better understanding of the ghost zombies after twelve hundred years of observation and study. They’d all been inhabitants of this world in life—and not ordinary inhabitants, but powerful cultivators. Their internal force of heaven and earth had spontaneously shriveled up when the world died, turning them into ghost zombies.","Yuan Yi and the other cultivators were descendants of the mortals from that time. All cultivators had become ghost zombies the second the world died.","His power of heaven and earth nurtured reincarnation, transforming the withered power of heaven and earth into that of a new world’s. This new strength was incorporated into Lu Yun’s circulation of heaven and earth.","However, there was no possible return for the cultivators who’d transformed into ghost zombies. They were just the bodies of cultivators as their internal force was the power of the withered world.","it might be more accurate to call them akasha ghosts.","Akasha ghosts of the world of immortals stemmed from the resentment of great emperors. They dyed the path of immortality with blood. After he arrived in this world, Lu Yun understood that the akasha ghosts and yin spirits ravaging the world of immortals and entire nothing was a result of strength exuding from these ghost zombies.","The mistress and Dao King made their moves from the shadows—creating these monsters, permitting their rampaging, locating someone who could take care of them, then sending that chosen person to this world.","The nothing encountered the great devastation again and again because of this dead world. That invincible barrier of nothing that caused death with a single touch was also due to the dead heaven and earth in this world.","If this world could be revitalized, then all of its orders would return. It would recover its former state of an incomparably ancient and prosperous world.","The nothing would no longer continue to expand until it ignited the great devastation. It would simply expand until the real existence within it melded into the real world here. Reality was also born from the nothing and a summation of the true existences that gathered time and time again in the nothing.","All devastation would be terminated if he solved the problems here.","Contemplation over twelve hundred years had resulted in enlightenment for Lu Yun, but since the mistress and Dao King had made no explanations—God even consumed his life to send Lu Yun here—then this world was not as simple as it appeared.","Resurrect this world? So much easier said than done.","Why had it been destroyed? Why had heaven and earth died? Why had countless cultivators turned into ghost zombies?","That was the crux of the problem.","All Lu Yun could do now was continuously improve his strength. He had the right to consider these questions only when he was strong enough.","Bam!","He kept up a steady battering with his fists and sent the ghost zombie king flying again. Currents of black air flowed out of its body as he did so and became part of Lu Yun’s external circulation of heaven and earth, turning into his own strength.","The zombie king’s power was beginning to decline.","“I see... so I need to injure him with full force if I want to obtain its withered power of heaven and earth and turn it back to its original form,” Lu Yun suddenly realized. He had to gravely wound the zombie king if he wanted its power.","“ROAR!!” the zombie king snarled, its cries tinged with enormous fury and a trace of unease. It wanted to run, but the human didn’t give it a chance to. Every single one of Lu Yun’s punches landed on its weakest points. It was sent flying again and again with no chance of escape.","The zombie king could battle Lu Yun at first, but as the fight dragged on, the zombie king could only barely fend off the blows.","The skies began to lighten to the east.","“ROOOOOAR!” came a wrathful howl from the north. The earth trembled; it seemed an enormous beast of danger was running in their direction.","Lu Yun furrowed his brows and he looked at the zombie king gasping for breath. He raised a hand and collected a Yuan Yi in full battle fervor. The two left without another word.","The zombie king sprawled on the ground, heaving for air and half dead. Another ponderous beast fifty kilometers tall and seventy-five kilometers long raced in on four hooves. The earth shook in the wake of its passage.","It was a second ghost zombie king."]},{"number":2159,"title":"Chapter 2159: Chapter 2114: Two Young Women","paragraphs":["Chapter 2114: Two Young Women","The second ghost zombie king was far stronger than the first. Lu Yun fled back to Jingzhou City with Yuan Yi in tow; he didn’t look back.","The first zombie king would be dead before he made it back to the city, and the second zombie king wouldn’t dare give chase before it gained a deeper understanding of the human’s capabilities.","Lu Yun also knew that if the second ghost zombie king dared come after him, he would take out his second zombie king of the night. His strength was nearly on par with the first zombie king to begin with. It’d increased explosively after the mistress and others undid the second seal, enabling him to defeat the zombie king with one punch.","While the second was stronger than the first, it wasn’t to a noticeable degree. The young man was confident that he’d be able to kill the second zombie king without breaking a sweat.","But the fight had already drawn the attention of another ghost zombie king. If they continued fighting, it might draw increasing numbers of zombie kings or even more terrifying entities.","Lu Yun was still unable to see through the heart of reality after residing here for twelve hundred years. It felt like a constant gray haze wrapped around the world. The strongest he’d met so far was just a few ghost zombie kings. However, there were certainly more frightening things lurking out there.","The zombie kings were simply mutated from past cultivators, and the stronger ones at that. What about the rest?","And what was it that had caused the death of an entire world?","Lu Yun didn’t dare be too blatant in his actions. Killing one ghost zombie king and intimidating another was enough for the day. It was sufficient that the nearby ghost zombies refrained from harassing Jingzhou City.","The rest could wait until he was stronger.","......","Lu Yun and Yuan Yi returned just as quietly as they’d departed. No one in the city knew what’d happened, including the other cultivators.","Not a single ghost zombie disturbed the city for an entire month; the city’s residents began to breathe more easily. But on this day, two rays of light descended from the sky and halted over the city.","They resolved themselves into two young women dressed in long ivory robes. They wore an indescribable expression of arrogance and aloofness on their charming faces.","“Are you the strongest of this land?” One of them looked down, her gaze cutting through the air to land on Lu Yun, who was teaching a group of children.","While most of the children had no cultivation potential, he could still teach them numerous methods to temper their bodies. They could hone their blood and qi and enhance their strength—it was a different approach to cultivation.","Although this land lacked great dao, making it so that many cultivation methods and combat arts were unusable, one could cultivate the body to the point of tearing apart ghost zombie kings with one’s bare hands.","The city’s inhabitants had grown immensely stronger over the past twelve hundred years. Lu Yun came across numerous hunters in the wilderness during this time. He hunted them down in turn and claimed their flesh and blood for the people.","It was one of the major reasons why they’d grown so strong.","The group of children released rays of blood and qi as they cultivated. Though they hadn’t truly set foot into the ranks of cultivation, their strength could still be regarded as peerless. Lu Yun stood in front of them and raised his head to consider the two young women above them. He frowned despite himself.","They were human and held themselves with an innate bearing of frosty superiority.","“Who are you?” he raised an eyebrow.","“You have no right to know who we are,” one of them creased her forehead. “Do you know anything about a ghost zombie king that’s died nearby?”","“As I thought,” Lu Yun nodded. “I killed it.”","“Just you?” the other young woman snorted. “Come with us then, since you killed it.”","“Am I to go with you just because you want me to?” Lu Yun snorted. “Who the hell do you think you are?”","Although they were exceedingly beautiful, the same went for any woman who cultivated. Other than cultivators who didn’t care about their appearance in the slightest, any male or female cultivator would hone their appearance to the best of their abilities.","It was an instinctive action.","“Forget that, just take him. We don’t need to waste more words with him.” The two shifted into motion after looking at each other, releasing immense power from their diminutive frames. It was similar to blood and qi, but its way of existence was far more sophisticated.","This was the strength of this world’s body cultivators, one more than a hundred times stronger than the Yuan Yi of old. She was no match for them even now—they’d beat her straight into the world of the dead.","“Hold!” Lu Yun called out. “I’ll go with you.”","“Lu Yun!” Yuan Yi rushed in from outside the city. She called out to him with shock.","“Don’t worry, I've modified the formations again during this time. Not even ghost zombie kings will break through them,” Lu Yun transmitted to Yuan Yi. “I’m going to go with them and see who they are.”","“...alright then,” Yuan Yi nodded mutely. “Be careful.”","Lu Yun rose into the air and faced the two women. “Let’s go.”","“Look what you made us do, you wretch,” one of them sneered and adjusted her bearings, flying high into the sky.","These two were extremely strong—on par with a zombie king. Lu Yun, however, wasn’t afraid of them. He’d left more so out of consideration for the city. If they’d fought here, the city would be decimated before he knew it.","Judging from their expressions, the women didn’t think much of the city’s inhabitants. The destruction and death of a city didn’t mean much to them. It was why Lu Yun had changed his mind. He nursed certain concerns, they didn’t.","Lu Yun quickly caught up to them when they vanished into the horizon as beams of light. They didn’t care if Lu Yun was behind them or not. Or perhaps they were certain that the young man would be able to catch up to them.","“In the sky?” Lu Yun blinked with astonishment as he watched them set a course straight up. He’d only explored the vast earth over the past twelve hundred years and never, ever entertained the thought that there might be people up in the sky.","“AOUUU!” A terrible roar broke through the air just when Lu Yun was about to catch up to the women. A massive body approached from the distance.","It was a ghost zombie king, one that could fly."]},{"number":2160,"title":"Chapter 2160: Chapter 2115: Execution With Two Punches","paragraphs":["Chapter 2115: Execution With Two Punches","This zombie king was a big black bird with a five hundred kilometer wingspan. It blotted out the sun when its wings were expanded. Ash-like smoke rose from its body, obscuring what its true form looked like.","There seemed to be a tiny black flame burning in the depths of the ashes.","Lu Yun could make out that the zombie king couldn’t land because it didn’t have legs. It could only hover in the sky.","The bird dived the trio the moment it appeared. A pair of crimson eyes opened in the ash and smoke; its maw yawned open as it spat a gout of black flame.","“What’s it doing here??” The two women looked at each other, both reading fear and shock in each other’s eyes. One of them raised a hand and released a tremendous surge of power, shooting out a terrifying gust of wind from her palm that blasted the flying zombie king.","The zombie king’s fire roiled back on itself and it split apart.","“That’s all it took?” Lu Yun blinked. He could tell that this zombie king was at least ten times more fearsome than the one he’d killed, but the woman had smote it to death with one palm strike!","“Go!” Both women shouted at the same time and scrambled for higher air.","Lu Yun started and immediately sensed that something was off. The zombie king seemed to be made of fire and smoke; its body reformed the moment it was shattered. The young man jumped with shock and raised his speed, trailing closely behind the women.","While they remained expressionless, he could clearly sense the terror creeping into their emotions.","Emotions?Lu Yun brightened with joy—not because the two women were afraid, but because he could sense emotions again. This was an ability from the Karmic Tree, one that he’d lost after arriving in this world. Its return signified that the long-vanished Tome of Life and Death was also reappearing in his body.","However, the ability was simply a sign that the treasure existed. He still couldn’t locate where it was.","But Lu Yun was in no hurry, it was only a matter of time before he wielded it again. Since he was far stronger than he’d been in the nothing, his reliance on the Tome of Life and Death was at an all time low. As useful as it would be to have the book, he was also fine without it. There was nothing to fear.","The ghost zombie king bore down on them—it was faster than the three of them!","“You go first.” Both women stopped and placed themselves between Lu Yun and the zombie king. “Keep going up until you see a floating palace. Don’t look back!”","They flanked the enemy and dove down, making Lu Yun jerk with surprise. The two had displayed immense arrogance from beginning to end, as if they disdained him from the bottom of their hearts. But in this crucial moment, they stood in front of him so he would have a chance to escape!","He didn’t know what to make of it. He could sense through ripples of emotion that they were utterly terrified, but completely consigned to going to their deaths.","It was no act, they really were going to go down fighting.","“Well...” Lu Yun paused and murmured to himself, “People called me the Dao Saint in the world of immortals, so I can’t give up this role now that I’m here now, can I?”","He rolled his eyes at himself and turned around, rushing the zombie king. He’d planned on concealing his strength and observing things from the background, but the women’s attitude changed his mind.","“What are you doing here?!” one of them screamed to see him.","They’d already blasted the zombie king apart a dozen times, but it regathered each time and continued attacking them like nothing had happened. In the meantime, they steadily consumed their energy reserves.","“I’m going to kick the zombie king’s ass, of course.” Lu Yun smiled radiantly and punched forward. His fist crashed into the zombie king like it was a magnificent world, interspersed with the overwhelming influence of heaven and earth.","The void trembled and the zombie king shrieked with anguish. It didn’t scatter from the blow, but it did shrink a full size smaller. The bird with a wingspan of five hundred kilometers now possessed a wingspan of two hundred and fifty kilometers.","“You...” The women’s eyes widened and they regarded the scene with disbelief. Their minds hummed, unable to make sense of what they were seeing.","This was a ghost zombie king, a tyrant of the skies and a fire demon with an undying body!","It’d mutated from an incomparably strong divine beast in reality. When armageddon arrived, it burned to death from a ball of flames that fell from the sky. After heaven and earth finished withering away, it was reborn in black flames as a fire demon.","It swallowed countless powerful cultivators after rebirth and the two women were no match for it.","“You’re still alive after one punch?” Lu Yun hooted with laughter. “Then again!”","BAM!","Black flames also exploded from his body, dying him black. The power of heaven and earth blazed around him as a vortex.","He hadn’t used his full strength when he killed the lizard-like zombie king because he hadn’t been certain what this world contained. Brashly using his full force might attract terrifying existences. But after the women’s appearance and seeing their actions, he changed his mind.","A massive organization still existed in this world. He needed to demonstrate sufficient strength to have them value, or at the very least, be wary of him.","One could not conceal one’s strength in a world that lacked hope. That would lead to ostracization and ultimately being left to fend for oneself.","Lu Yun delivered another straightforward punch that crashed into the fire demon in dominating fashion. The fire demon screeched with despair and dispersed in a shower of black flames and ashes.","The young man had taken out the fire demon that’d ravaged the skies and swallowed endless cultivators with two punches!"]},{"number":2161,"title":"Chapter 2161: Chapter 2116: A Floating Tomb in the Sky","paragraphs":["Chapter 2116: A Floating Tomb in the Sky","The two stared, tongue-tied, at Lu Yun. Their thoughts were in disarray.","“How does such a powerhouse exist among the guilty? The fire demon stood at the peak of the zombie kings. But he killed it with two punches?” one of the women asked haltingly.","“Guilty?” Lu Yun frowned and seemed to understand something when he heard her murmuring. “I’m... guilty?”","“You’ll naturally learn of some things once you enter the heavenly palace with us.” The woman heaved a long sigh as her attitude towards Lu Yun shifted. It shifted because of his strength, but there wasn’t a fundamental change as he was still “guilty”.","“Let’s go.” The two women resumed their trajectory up into the sky.","Lu Yun was immensely confused, but refrained from further questions. He followed them up into the firmament, not knowing how far he flew. A dazzling expanse of gold entered his eyes when the ground vanished beneath his feet, replaced by only a hazy fog.","It was a palace hovering in the void, one sparkling with so much golden splendor that it dyed the air gold. It even outshone the sun next to it.","This was the first time that Lu Yun saw a hint of any color other than gray since arriving in this world. His eyes were wide open with incredulity at the magnificent sight.","“A floating tomb in the sky... a palace above the clouds...” He trembled as his lips twitched.","“What did you say?” The two women seemed to have heard him and paused, looking at the young man with confusion.","“Is this... your home?” He took a deep breath as his expression shifted rapidly.","“Is there anything wrong?” One of the women asked. “Darkness envelops the land, heaven and earth have withered away, all life has crumbled. This is the only patch of light in the world. It is our last home.”","Lu Yun nodded without a word.","“What do you mean by a floating tomb in the sky?” The other one of them frowned. “I read from an ancient book that a tomb is where the dead are buried.”","“You wouldn’t believe me if I told you, you’d just think that I’m spouting nonsense.” Lu Yun smiled.","“No, I believe you.” The look in the women’s eyes sharpened. “My name is Qingfeng and my younger sister is Qingniao.”","It’d been Qingfeng who raised the question.","“A floating tomb in the sky and a palace above the clouds that buries all life.” Lu Yun took a deep breath and tried to make his voice as calm as possible. “If there is a master of this world, he is surely dead. Only with his death would this tomb and palace appear to bury the world.","“He must have been a benevolent person, so the tomb and palace appeared upon his death to safeguard the last hope of this world.","“But this tomb only safeguards hope and doesn’t permit it to grow. Your roots are not here, they are on the ground. If you continue to live in a tomb, you will ultimately become its zombies and ghosts, never to undergo reincarnation.","“Do you believe me when I say this?” Lu Yun looked noncommittally at Qingfeng.","“Mm.” Both women nodded at the same time. “We believe you. We are the few who can walk out of the palace. Many more are constrained by the palace and unable to leave no matter what.”","Qingfeng sighed, “We have a feeling that if we continue to stay here, we will be confined by it sooner or later and be unable to leave like the rest.”","“So what is your goal in bringing me here?” Lu Yun asked calmly.","“You are guilty, but you have the power to kill a ghost zombie king. You have the right to come to the heavenly palace and receive its true heritage. You can inherit the hope of this world,” Qingfeng continued after a long pause, “The palace oversees the land and we welcome anyone who has the ability to kill a ghost zombie king. We help them become stronger so they can kill more zombie kings.","“Your strength is more than we expected. You are already able to kill ghost zombie emperors.”","“Mmhmm,” Lu Yun nodded. “What do you mean by guilty?”","“The guilty...” A sharp light passed through Qingniao’s eyes. “The guilty are the descendants of those who turned the world into this state. Everything that lives on the ground possesses the bloodline of the guilty.”","“What?!” Lu Yun’s expression shifted and he exclaimed, “This world is the work of a group of people?!”","Qingfeng and Qingniao looked at Lu Yun before nodding gently.","“Indeed, the death of heaven and earth is manmade. When it comes down to it, those who live on the earth are descendants of demons. It is the ghost zombies who are the true victims.” Qingfeng looked at Lu Yun. “But who can say who is right or wrong? The guilty created the ghost zombies and ghost zombies have destroyed the world.”","Lu Yun finally understood why the two sisters regarded him with that particular attitude of loftiness. It wasn’t really arrogance, but a kind of contempt.","A contempt directed toward guilty sinners.","But just as Qingfeng said, who could be certain of right or wrong, good or evil? Perhaps they were descendants of the guilty, but when they were strong enough and recognized for their strength, they were taken to the heavenly palace and received the heritage of this world.","At the same time, they were also informed of the matters of the guilty.","“And what about you? Are you also descendants of the guilty?” the young man asked them.","Qingfeng and Qingniao fell silent, the answer apparent without needing to voice it aloud.","Lu Yun spoke no further. He raised his head and looked at the floating tomb at arm’s length, twin spots of dark light appearing in his eyes.","The radiant floating tomb drastically changed in his vision. The glittering facade turned sinister and eerie, filled with yin winds and yin presence. They gusted over his body and raised minuscule goosebumps over his skin.","“A yang tomb and a yin tomb...” he said softly. “Entering the yang tomb leads to life, entering the yin tomb leads to death.","“You all live in the yang tomb, but it is a tomb in the end. Living here for too long will drop you into the yin tomb. You are unable to leave the floating tomb once you enter the yin tomb.” Lu Yun stepped forward as a winding path appeared beneath his feet, one that led to the floating tomb— the yin tomb.","“What is going on here??” Qingfeng and Qingniao noticed the change in him. They couldn’t glean any clues, but they could sense the aberration.","“Go back and tell the honored one these happenings. I will go with him to see what the situation is.” Qingfeng grabbed Lu Yun’s wrist and set foot on the invisible path beneath his feet—the Yellow Springs Path."]},{"number":2162,"title":"Chapter 2162: Chapter 2117: Stone Sculpture","paragraphs":["Chapter 2117: Stone Sculpture","Lu Yun turned around to look at Qingfeng and yanked his hand out from hers.","She didn’t mind his reaction as she was focused on the yin wind blowing over them. Cold and eerie, she trembled from the contact.","“What is this?” Qingfeng asked in a trembling voice.","“A tomb,” Lu Yun answered. “A yin tomb floating in the sky. All of you normally reside in the yang tomb, which is why you are alive. But a tomb is a place that lays kings to rest, so inhabiting a tomb for long means that you will eventually be dragged into the yin tomb.”","The young man took a step forward and entered the floating tomb in the sky. Qingfeng was close behind him.","Familiar sights and layouts entered her vision, but they were entirely different from what she was familiar with. What was ordinarily a scene of vibrant growth was a ghostly world of uncanniness.","She didn’t see anyone alive or sense the presence of the living. Only dense yin qi and the air of death wrapped around her body and heart. She was very familiar with them—they manifested every time someone died.","“This...” Qingfeng shook her head, unable to understand what Lu Yun spoke of. She’d seen tombs before—they forested the world in versions both big and small. Some were built before armageddon arrived, others were established later on.","She’d never imagined that the heavenly palace she grew up in would also be a tomb. However, reality in front of her forced her to believe what she saw.","“The tombs of yin and yang are just a layout of burial.” Lu Yun inspected the premises with the Spectral Eye. “How else would the palace exist for so long in the extremity of life and death if this wasn’t a tomb?”","“What is the extremity of life and death?” Qingfeng forcefully swung her head back and forth. “Is this an illusion you’ve created to confuse me?”","She shook her head just as quickly as the possibility occurred to her. It was laughable even to her. Her cultivation had reached its peak, and while she wasn’t as strong as Lu Yun, her mentality had reached the point of returning to origin and seeing through all falsehoods.","It was impossible to fool her eyes.","Qingfeng could clearly sense that everything she saw was real.","Lu Yun swept a glance over her and remained silent. He followed the path in, heading deeper into the magnificent hall that was filled with a lifeless air.","Qingfeng kept to herself when she saw Lu Yun ignore her and silently trailed behind him.","“You don’t come from this world, do you?” she suddenly asked.","“What makes you say that?” Lu Yun asked instead with a frown.","“Most of the guilty refute me or try to explain when I say they’re guilty. Or they just erupt in open hostility. Your calmness is not their usual.","“Additionally,” Qingfeng looked around them. “The dao of burial ceased with the destruction of heaven and earth. There is no one versed in it anymore. You are the only one. Therefore, I dare say that you are not of this world.”","“Mmhmm,” Lu Yun nodded and didn’t refute her words. It didn’t matter whether or not he was an inhabitant of this bleak, desolate world. Anything alive was on the same side.","“Are there a lot of other worlds around us?” He suddenly honed in on a key point. “In my understanding, your world is the peak of boundless nothing, the point of existence within the nihil from which originates all space and time.","“Are there other worlds apart from you?”","Lu Yun’s home, that patch of nothing, was contained within this existence. It was a vassal state of this patch of reality.","“Yes,” Qingfeng responded. “Your words are proof that you stand at the peak of a world and know many things. But your peak is simply a small step to many others.","“What you see is the truth of the world, but you are obstructed by a bigger and more expansive ceiling.","“The world is unending and infinitely big, no one can fully elaborate on the truth of the world’s existence. The unbounded nothing we see, that nihil in which nothing lives, could be a small puddle to the eyes of even bigger personages.”","Lu Yun nodded in full agreement with Qingfeng’s words. No one could say how big the world was and what the meaning of the world and life was. It was like what he’d postulated before with the table and cup. Perhaps one thought it was an incontrovertible rule or law, but it was also very possible that a bigger existence had casually set a cup on a table.","Subjectivity affecting the objective? Lu Yun could do it with his current strength, but who was to say that there wouldn’t be a bigger and more encompassing world beyond this level?","“There’s no point in discussing any of this,” he said seriously. “What we need to do now is to survive.”","Qingfeng started, then nodded with a rueful smile. Primitive humans ate raw flesh and drank blood in order to live. What kind of life was an existence like that? Yet, only when one survived did one have the right to consider other things. They were the primitive humans of these vast ruins, struggling to eke out a living from the devastation.","It was not for them to contemplate what life and the world was like.","“Wait!” Her expression shifted drastically and she fixated on something. She stumbled forward to stop in front of an enormous human sculpture.","“Ma... master...” Her voice shook as she identified the sculpture.","It was black throughout and shaped into a stunning woman. It was so lifelike that it was as if a real person stood there. She was just a stone sculpture at present, one without any hint of vitality.","“Don’t touch it!” Lu Yun snapped and slapped away Qingfeng’s reaching hand. “Stone sculptures in tombs accumulate yin energy and harbor vengeful spirits. Great horror develops when it develops into a stone spirit after meeting a living being.”","An unbidden thought rose in his mind. He’d met a stone sculpture in the first tomb he explored after entering the world of immortals. If it wasn’t for Ge Long at the time, he and Wanfeng would’ve both died to it.","One should not easily touch stone sculptures in tombs, particularly in this terrifying floating tomb.","“Is this your master?” Lu Yun pulled Qingfeng away.","“Yes,” she nodded. “My master entered the depths of the palace three hundred years ago and never came back... This isn’t a sculpture, it’s my master.”"]},{"number":2163,"title":"Chapter 2163: Chapter 2118: City Brick","paragraphs":["Chapter 2118: City Brick","Lu Yun was already in this world three hundred years ago.","“The final destiny of all beings in the heavenly palace is to set foot in its depths and vanish forever.” Qingfeng’s voice was ethereal with a deep hint of yearning sorrow. She reached out and gently caressed the sculpture in front of them.","The Spectral Eye noted that the sculpture swiftly absorbed Qingfeng’s vitality, but another force within the stone sculpture defied it and returned her life force at the same time.","Lu Yun immediately understood that the sculpture was alive—or at the very least, not fully dead.","“I will come here one day as well and turn into one of these sculptures.” Qingfeng turned around to Lu Yun. “I can sense that master is not yet dead. Can you save her?”","Being no fool, she understood where her master and historic generations of the heavenly palace’s powerhouses had gone to. They’d come to this so-called yin tomb and become these stone sculptures.","“They’ve been summoned here by a powerful existence to become... burial goods of the yin tomb. No, wait, they can’t be called burial goods.” Lu Yun frowned with deep thought and closely scanned the yin tomb’s layout of burial before saying, “They’re here to be decorations for the tomb.”","“...decorations??” Qingfeng’s eyes went wide with incredulity; she also felt a dense sense of grief emanate from the stone sculpture in front of her.","Indeed, decorations. The powerhouses who came here didn’t even have the right to be burial goods. They were just decorations.","“Correct, decorations. We won’t be able to save her even if we break the layouts in the tomb. We would have to kill the tomb owner.” Lu Yun nodded before continuing, “We need to ensure that those who live in the world of the dead forever perish.”","In the world of the dead, the dead were the living.","Lu Yun didn’t know where the true world of the dead was. It wasn’t hell or his kingdom of hell. Just as the nothing opposed existence, so did the world of the dead oppose the world of the living.","The yin tomb around them was the tomb owner’s world of the dead, a man-made world of the dead. Every tomb was a world of the dead to its owner. The tomb owner was considered the living of their tiny world.","This was the greatest meaning behind a burial. It enabled those who could not travel to the real world of the dead to find peace in the world of the living.","“Just us two?” Qingfeng hesitated. “Should we ask for help from those back at the heavenly palace?”","“Do you think we can still make it out of here alive?” Lu Yun smiled.","Qingfeng looked around with solemn eyes and didn’t say anything.","“Don’t worry, there’s only an old ghost around here.” Lu Yun’s smile remained fixed on his face as a long unfelt sense of excitement rose from his heart.","His old trade was that of a tomb raider, but there were no secrets left to him in the nothing. He could see through every single tomb with a single glance, so he left their exploration to the juniors of his sect.","Reality, however, was full of challenges for him. He’d wanted to fully showcase his abilities in God’s Tomb, but it turned out to be God’s seal and a place meant to deliver power to him. Now with a new challenge ahead of him, his blood stirred in this tomb floating in the sky.","Lu Yun rolled up his sleeves. “You must listen to me if you want to save your master. You will do whatever I tell you to do and you must not do anything I tell you not to do!","“Also, you must tell me as soon as any strange thoughts appear in your mind.”","Qingfeng retracted her hand from her master’s sculpture and inclined her head.","“Then my master’s sculpture...”","“Leave it there. She’ll return to normal when we take out that old ghost. Remember what I just said and follow my footsteps from now on. Don’t set a single toe out of line.”","Qingfeng blinked, then nodded again.","“The truly frightening thing in this tomb isn’t the old ghost, but the layouts within the tomb.” Lu Yun started walking forward. “Tombs are the world of the dead to a tomb owner, so he can utilize its strength against anyone.","“A tomb raider can defuse this world from its foundations and disperse this world of the dead. Once the owner is bereft of the world’s protection, he must face us with his own strength.","“Although the heaven and earth are dead, this world is a world of the living. The owner is no match for us in a world of the living.” The young man kept up a litany of explanations as he walked forward.","Qingfeng silently committed his words to memory. Although questions swirled in her thoughts, she didn’t ask any of them.","“Aren’t you curious who I am?” Lu Yun could sense Qingfeng’s curiosity, but he was also curious about her reaction himself. Why would anyone believe him at this juncture? At the very least, they’d want to know who he was.","“What is there to be curious about?” Qingfeng responded woodenly. “Heaven and earth are dead.”","Lu Yun blinked, then slowly nodded in agreement. “Right... heaven and earth are dead, so what else is there worth asking?”","Qingfeng, or rather the people of this world, could see no hope. Therefore, there was no point in asking any questions. If she asked Lu Yun about his identity now, it would just be to satisfy her personal curiosity.","But plainly, she wasn’t a curious soul.","The yin tomb was constructed in the same way as the yang tomb—a massive palace. However, all they saw here were stone sculptures, as opposed to living people.","“All of the powerhouses that have ever vanished from the heavenly palace are here.” Qingfeng’s sorrow grew stronger as she scanned the sculptures. “No, no wait, there’s someone else here. These sculptures don’t seem to be...”","Lu Yun interrupted her before she could finish. “What is that?”","He suddenly halted in front of an enormous wall. Several large characters were written on it in fresh blood.","“We are but bricks for a city.”","“What does that mean?” Lu Yun frowned at the bleeding words. “Does the yang tomb... I mean the heavenly palace that you live in... have these words as well?”","“No,” Qingfeng shook her head. “This is the main hall of the heavenly palace, where the heavenly rulers live. There shouldn’t be a wall here.”","“So someone’s modified the yin tomb layout?” Lu Yun’s frown deepened. The yin and yang tombs should be reflections of each other. Whatever there was in the yin tomb should exist in the yang tomb, apart from the powerhouses that’d turned to stone.","“Go back,” came a long sigh. “It is not yet time for you to be here. I will bring you here when the time is right.”"]},{"number":2164,"title":"Chapter 2164: Chapter 2119: The Truth of This World","paragraphs":["Chapter 2119: The Truth of This World","“The time? What is this right time you speak of?” Lu Yun quickly asked when he heard the voice. It should belong to the dead of the tomb. There was no danger in the floating tomb, but it abounded with uncanniness. Perhaps this dead could answer his questions.","“When it is time for your death.”","Lu Yun shrugged and Qingfeng’s eyes widened.","“Then let’s keep going. Since he won’t say anything, we’ll haul him out here so we can ask him some questions.” Lu Yun strode forward, not intending to turn back. Qingfeng quickly followed in his footsteps.","Although the voice didn’t sound again, the scene changed in front of their eyes. Layers of mist obscured the premises and the pavilions, towers, and halls disappeared. They were replaced by layer upon layer of walls and passages.","The surroundings had turned into a massive maze.","“A maze?” Lu Yun’s lips turned upward with a snort. “Child’s play.”","He walked forward without missing a beat. Mazes truly were child’s play to a veteran tomb raider like Lu Yun. No matter how the layouts shifted, there would always be a path that was the correct one. He would easily find it.","Despite the depths and vastness of the maze, nothing could hide from his eyes.","To him, all of this world’s past glories stagnated the moment the world died and heaven and earth dispersed. Since their grandeur was from times past and their prosperous civilization no more, all that remained were old and obsolete things.","Layouts of burial like the one in this tomb could be found everywhere on Earth. Lu Yun would easily find his way out of here even if he’d never gone to the world of immortals and obtained his current cultivation level.","“Will I see the truth of this world once I exit this maze?” The young man couldn’t help but ask. He knew that the owner of the tomb, the one who lived in a world of the dead, was still keeping an eye on him and Qingfeng.","Qingfeng was so nervous that she subconsciously reached out and grabbed Lu Yun’s sleeve.","“The truth of this world is so harsh that no one in existence can endure it.” The dead’s voice sounded with a trace of an inexplicable emotion. “Outsider, I noticed you the moment you arrived in this existence. You still have time to turn back.”","“Since you discovered me the moment I arrived, you should know who sent me here and why,” Lu Yun chuckled. “I thought they sent me here to revive this world and resurrect heaven and earth, helping creation flourish again. But after seeing this floating tomb in the sky... I realize that I was wrong.","“I have to explore things for myself since you refuse to give up what you know. Just try and see if you can stop me.”","Qingfeng’s expression flickered a few times as she listened to them speak, but she simply sighed in the end.","“This world cannot be revived...” she said. “Its doom was set in stone the moment it died.”","“I know, but how will we truly know if we don’t try?” Lu Yun grinned as a third seal shattered while they spoke. His strength advanced by leaps and bounds yet again. Although he was still very far removed from affecting the objective with the subjective, he was unequivocally stronger than ghost zombie kings now.","“Many tried in the past, but they all failed.” Sorrow crept into the tomb owner’s voice. “You have a chance to live if you leave now, and I will come receive you when you die. You will be able to offer something to this world then.","“But if you continue forward and see the truth, you will not be able to turn back.”","“What will I offer when I am dead?” Lu Yun snorted. “You said so yourself that I am an outsider. I’m not that interested in reviving this world. All I want to do is to save my homeland. I can only know if I want to turn back or not when I actually see things for myself.” Lu Yun knew that there were only two paths available to him the moment he arrived in this place. He either succeeded, or he failed.","He could return home if he succeeded and prevent the great devastation from taking place in the nothing. He would die here if he failed, and his home would undergo that cycle once more. His lovers, family, friends, and child would die in the unending nirvana.","Turn back?","He’d long lost the right to turn back.","“And is turning back something good to eat?” he grinned. “There’s a saying in a city of my homeland, something about the grass being delicious if one turns back. I’ll treat you to a helping of turning back if I ever get the chance to.” He directed the last part to Qingfeng.","“Um... okay?” she responded reflexively. Delicious? She didn’t know what delicious was. Was it food that tasted good? Food had never tasted good to her, it was just a way to ensure they didn’t die and fuel to increase their strength.","The records of the world that’d died spoke of eating as a form of pleasure in an age when civilization prospered. Perhaps civilization still existed in Lu Yun’s home. No wonder his thoughts and actions were at such odds with this world. His heart had not yet died, hope still existed within it.","The dead fell silent upon Lu Yun’s response, but the fog within the maze grew denser. They almost couldn’t see their hands anymore when they stretched it forward.","The fog cleared after an unknown period of time and a massive sarcophagus came into view. A young man sat on top of it, looking roughly sixteen years old. He wore robes of gray cloth and his eyes were gray. The air of death wreathed around him.","“Is this the truth you spoke of?” Lu Yun commented with surprise as he looked at who’d been talking to them before. He looked around them and found nothing else in the vicinity. The brick path beneath their feet had vanished—only the sarcophagus and the young man were present.","It was just an ordinary sarcophagus with nothing special about it. In fact, it looked very much like an... enormous brick to Lu Yun.","“Is this the nothing?” he suddenly realized.","The young man’s eyes couldn’t focus on anything. He looked silently in Lu Yun’s direction and inclined his head. “This is the truth of the world. This is the nothing. You cannot go back after coming here, and this is the truth that you want.”","He jumped down from the sarcophagus and pointed at it. “This world is a brick forged for a city.”","Lu Yun’s pupils contracted violently as he saw a black flame burning beneath the sarcophagus—hellfire.","“The two of you walked out of this brick just now.”"]},{"number":2165,"title":"Chapter 2165: Chapter 2120: Qing Yu","paragraphs":["Chapter 2120: Qing Yu","A light glimmered in Lu Yun’s eyes as he stared fixedly at the brick that looked like a sarcophagus. Was this the truth of this world, an existence so vast that it was undefined by boundaries?","He was beginning to doubt the very basis of his life.","“You... What are you doing!” Qingfeng shouted at the young man. She didn’t believe the scene in front of her, even though she’d glimpsed her own world in the brick. She could pick out the heavenly palace and the bleak land of desolation.","Despite that, she still couldn’t believe her eyes or accept the truth.","“What... a tremendous scheme,” Lu Yun took a deep breath. “Killing the heaven and earth of this world first, then refining the world into a sarcophagus, and finally crafting it into a brick?”","“Mm,” the dead young man nodded lightly.","Was this the ultimate truth?","The truth that the mistress, Dao King, and God paid insurmountable costs and tried to obtain at all odds? All for a grand reveal that their world, their home, had been baked into a brick?","Lu Yun took another glance at the fire used to make the brick—hellfire. It was wholly unexpected, yet entirely with reason. As strong as he was, even he felt black despair descend over him. The thing that he’d been searching for all this time was but a joke to many!","“So who are you?” Qingfeng calmed down and asked the dead young man in a shaking voice, “Are you the one who killed our world?”","The young man shook his head.","“I am the God of this world,” he responded. “I was the first to die in their hands and they shaped the world into a brick after I died.”","Lu Yun frowned. “Did you reach the stage of subjectivity affecting objectivity?”","“I was half a step away.” The young man had yet to reach the pinnacle.","“You are the God of this world?” Lu Yun suddenly stepped forward and closely assessed the young man with twin pillars of black flames in his eyes.","Shock and terror floated to the fore of the young man’s wooden face and he subconsciously took a step back.","“I am the second generation God after God perished,” the young man corrected.","“What do you know?” Lu Yun advanced, forcing the young man to steadily back up. As the black flames grew brighter in his eyes, so did the fear in the young man’s face.","“There are countless real existences like us in the unbounded nothing, we are as numerous as the sands. But there aren’t that many of us left now.”","“Have they all become bricks?” Lu Yun asked.","“Yes,” the young man nodded. “Hellfire activated reincarnation to refine them—no existence can withstand the fires of hell. They were forged alive into bricks. All life within existence perishes at the moment of formation and becomes part of the brick.”","He held nothing back as Lu Yun’s presence here meant that he possessed sufficient strength and right to know these things. And for someone of the young man’s level, this knowledge was no secret.","“I lead those who have reached the end of their life into the tomb so that they can transform from death to life when the brick takes shape. They are reborn that way.”","Instead of responding, Lu Yun looked at Qingfeng. The girl had completely calmed down and there were no other emotions to be read from her face.","“Why are you looking at me like that?” She looked subconsciously at Lu Yun.","“You seem very calm.” He raised an eyebrow.","“I was born of despair and never knew what hope was,” she smiled faintly. “The heart is dead, so what is this talk of calm or not?”","Lu Yun had given her a strand of hope, but that strand imploded in the face of such terrifying reality. She’d returned to her usual impassive, emotionless state.","“Are you not curious? Don’t you want to know the truth?”","“No, and no.” Her tone remained even.","“I finally awoke a strand of emotion in her, but reality crushed it,” Lu Yun sighed as he turned back to the young man. “Based on what I know of this world, the nothing and reality oppose each other...”","“That is indeed the case,” the young man responded. “But the only reality was destroyed later on and became specks of reality throughout the nothing.”","“So... is someone shaping all of these specks into bricks so they can rebuild the original reality?” Lu Yun wondered.","“I don’t know,” the young man answered. “This is all I know, I know nothing else.”","Lu Yun frowned and let the matter drop.","“Let’s go back.” he turned and grabbed Qingfeng. She nodded and followed him into the brick that was still being shaped.","The scene changed in front of them and they reappeared in the yin tomb. They were able to travel back into the world of the brick because Lu Yun wielded hellfire.","“What did you think of that?” he transmitted as he looked at Qingfeng.","“That ghostly entity... was very strange.” She frowned slightly and replied hesitantly, “I’d like to think that he does know the truth.”","“So you don’t suspect him of lying?” Lu Yun blinked with astonishment.","Qingfeng didn’t answer.","“Refining this boundless reality into a brick...” Lu Yun murmured to himself. “And one used to build a city... Whoever’s behind this obviously wants to build a city wall... OOF!”","He grunted as his internal force agitated—multiple seals were being forced through. His strength rose so rapidly and to such heights that it could barely be defined anymore.","And then, a figure appeared in front of him. It was a faint shadow at first, one that slowly filled in and became a real person.","“Little Yu!” Lu Yun exclaimed with delight when he took a clear look and hugged her tight.","The newcomer was Qing Yu, and she was wrapped in Lu Yun’s arms before she had a chance to react.","“Lu Yun, it really is you... I thought I’d never see you again... Wawawa...” Tears streamed down her face as she buried her head in his embrace.","Thoughts bubbled to the surface of Lu Yun’s mind, a complicated snarl of them. He’d left without forewarning and was, in fact, dead to those of the nothing.","“What are you doing here?” he asked in a shaking voice as he hugged the soft form tight. This Qing Yu was real, not a replica or a dream, but a real, living person.","Despite his question, he had his answer.","Dead.","Qing Yu had died in the nothing. Only then could she be here in person."]},{"number":2166,"title":"Chapter 2166: Chapter 2121: Don’t Disappoint Yourselves","paragraphs":["Chapter 2121: Don’t Disappoint Yourselves","Qingfeng went on the alert when she saw someone suddenly appear and she demanded, “Who are you and what are you doing here?!”","Qing Yu’s cheek twitched and she lifted her head from Lu Yun’s embrace, composing herself. She raised her eyebrows with a smile when she saw the frosty girl. “Is this your girl in this world?”","“EH?! Uh, uh, n-no...” Lu Yun stammered wildly, but didn’t know how to explain himself.","Qing Yu burst out laughing at his awkward state and smiled at Qingfeng. “I am Lu Yun’s wife. I’ve come to find him.”","The girl, however, remained frowning. This was the heavenly palace and the yin tomb that Lu Yun spoke of. How had the newcomer found her way here?","“Miss Qingfeng, she is my wife.” Lu Yun collected his senses and smiled easily. “She’s crossed time and space to come in search of me.”","Waves of emotions reared in his heart and none of his usual aplomb could be found. There were only two people in existence who could affect his mental state at his current level of strength.","Qing Yu and Tushan Miao.","“Forget about this, let’s get out first.” He took Qing Yu’s hand and headed for the exit.","The tomb owner... the dead young man... was the biggest threat in this tomb. He wouldn’t do anything to Lu Yun now, so there was no threat to the young man in the yin tomb anymore. All the same, what he saw weighed heavily on his heart.","Bricks!","Reality was being refined into a brick! And one used to build a city!","There had indeed once been a reality in the nothing, one that opposed nihil and formed the yin and yang diagram. But for reasons unknown, someone shattered that reality and extended the nothing throughout everything.","The fragments of reality turned into specks that were the worlds they knew. His patch of existence wasn’t the only reality, it was just one of the fragments. There were plenty of these shards in the nothing.","So his direction had been wrong from the very beginning.","Lu Yun was more lost and confused than anything. Why turn reality into bricks? The fragments could absolutely be reassembled into reality again, just how the broken world of immortals had been joined together again into a whole world.","But he couldn’t be bothered to think through this now. His hand held his entire world—Qing Yu. She’d died for him so that she could come here. Even though it cut his heart with the pain of a thousand blades, he would not be ungrateful for her good intentions.","“Husband.” Her voice echoed in Lu Yun’s mind. “When I came, Mo Yi said not to bother with the truth. Do whatever you’d like to do.”","The young man smiled ruefully at his dao partner. “What I want to do most is to go home. But I can’t.”","“Mm.” Qing Yu pursed her lips and suddenly flung herself at Lu Yun, placing her lips on his. The two of them embraced ardently in the tomb and kissed each other with passion.","Qingfeng was dumbfounded, having no idea what’d happened to the two locked in hunger. Things had been fine a second ago, hadn’t they? Why were they kissing all of a sudden?","Although the world was filled with despair, there was still love and affection as the species needed to propagate. It was part of their instinctive nature, so Qingfeng could understand their actions.","She just didn’t understand why they were suddenly engaging in these actions.","The two exchanged their yearning for each other in a long series of kisses before parting with great reluctance. Lu Yun took a moment to recollect his thoughts—he knew how to proceed from here.","He took a deep breath as he looked at Qing Yu and said softly, “I know what to do. The two of us together is immortal dao. We need to let the flower of immortal dao blossom in this bleak world!”","The Dao Sovereign and the master of immortal dao. The great dao had long since taken root in their hearts, even though they weren’t in the world of immortals at the moment and even if they abandoned immortal dao. As long as they joined hands, they could recreate a new immortal dao no matter where they were.","Since heaven and earth were dead in this world, let immortal dao be its heaven and earth!","Hummm.","Two black flames flared in Lu Yun’s eyes—hellfire. An image of the Tome of Life and Death slowly manifested within them and the long dormant power of reincarnation erupted, running through Lu Yun’s body.","White light also blossomed over Qing Yu’s body as a resplendent golden palace seemed to shine over her head.","The heavenly palace!","The palace of immortal dao.","While Lu Yun oversaw the kingdom of hell, Qing Yu beheld the heavenly palace. It manifested in this world given Lu Yun’s new resolution.","Rumble—","The floating tomb and palace over the clouds trembled. Countless beings cried out in shock as their palace shone with rays of splendor, resonating with the heavenly palace over Qing Yu’s head.","With that, Lu Yun discovered that the yin tomb layout had been destroyed. The yin and yang tombs had become one and the layout of burial was swiftly dismantled in the next second.","Lu Yun, Qing Yu, and Qingfeng arrived at the real palace over the clouds—a glittering, magnificent palace that was filled with a lifeless air. Hundreds of powerful beings stared at them; time froze in the next second and they were petrified on the spot.","A young man in white slowly walked out of the void.","“The Dao King!” Lu Yun nearly went off in another daze when he took a clear look at the newcomer. It was the real Dao King, he was here too!","“Long time no see.” The Dao King smiled at Lu Yun and Qing Yu beneath him. “This is also our last meeting.”","“What do you mean?” Lu Yun blinked, then watched as the Dao King spread out his arms and slowly faded away into motes of white light. “What are you doing?!” He knew what the Dao King intended to do and roared with protest. “What will Mo Yi do if you die?!”","“She doesn’t need me,” the Dao King chuckled. “She has never needed me. My final resting place has always been here. With my flesh and blood as sacrifice and soul as catalyst, I will summon the spirits of heaven and earth.”","Boooom.","The Dao King fully dissolved and faded away in the void. The power of heaven and earth streamed to them from all sides and barrelled into Lu Yun and Qing Yu’s body.","“You two are the hope of all living beings, so... don’t disappoint yourselves.”"]},{"number":2167,"title":"Chapter 2167: Chapter 2122: Immortal Dao Blossoms Again","paragraphs":["Chapter 2122: Immortal Dao Blossoms Again","“Ai...” In the primordial world of immortals, Mo Yi sighed as she watched the Dao King fade away. She knew that he’d safeguarded her all this time, but she hadn’t been at liberty to return his affections. Therefore, she’d never expressed anything to him.","He’d died countless times for her in the countless iterations of reincarnation, but this time, he was truly dead. He would never appear in front of her again.","A tiny ripple disturbed her long frozen heart, but it quickly vanished without a trace.","She felt no emotion, so although a person who’d protected her for life upon life had just died in front of her, only a tiny ripple marred her mindset.","......","Space and time recovered as a white flower blossomed gracefully over Lu Yun and Qing Yu’s head.","Everyone within the palace stared, tongue-tied, at the scene. They didn’t know what’d happened, why these two people had suddenly appeared, and why something similar to the presence of the heavenly dao had abruptly appeared over their head.","But emotion stirred in their hearts all the same. They seemed to see... hope.","Within Jingzhou City, Yuan Yi lifted her head and looked in the direction of the heavenly palace.","An enormous white flower blossomed there and illuminated the bleak landscape. What had been a dim and feeble sun also flared with dazzling radiance.","Greenery crept over the world at a pace visible to the naked eye.","“Lady Yuan Yi, I can feel the heavenly dao!” murmured a plainly dressed girl who stood next to Yuan Yi. She was the only disciple that Lu Yun had taken in this world—Wang Shu.","Wang Shu was a girl to begin with, but she’d been so thin and frail before that it was impossible to tell her gender. Not that Lu Yun had ever cared about that.","“Mmhmm.” Yuan Yi nodded, a smile gracing her face for the first time. She pointed at the greenery budding outside of the city. “Look, that is hope.”","......","Craaaaaack.","Cracks snaked through the world that was about to be made into a brick. It abruptly split open and the external shell like a sarcophagus dispersed.","Life flooded into the dead young man’s empty gaze and vitality infused his body. It reached through the void as he threw his head back with laughter and vanished where he stood.","“This is my world and she has come back to life. I will protect her with my own heart!” His voice echoed in the void while he himself fully disappeared into the nothing.","This was a refinery to craft bricks. There would be someone who came along to investigate why something had gone awry with this particular brick. The dead young man’s goal was to kill whoever came to investigate.","......","Everyone in the heavenly palace was on their knees and worshiping the two people in front of them. They could sense the ripples of heaven and earth, that the world was coming back to life. No matter who these two were, they were this world’s saviors.","“You...” Qingfeng flushed as she looked at Lu Yun and Qing Yu.","Lu Yun came back to his senses with a mournful sigh. The Dao King’s last words were correct. They should not disappoint themselves. They weren’t doing this for the Dao King, mistress, or all of life, but for themselves.","The world connected with Lu Yun the moment the Dao Flower bloomed. He knew that it was only a matter of time before the world of immortals broke through the void and his friends and family followed it to arrive in this world.","His task at the moment was to fashion this world into a true world of immortals so it could welcome his loved ones.","“We...” Qing Yu paused and looked at Lu Yun since she wasn’t familiar with this world.","“Much of this world has declined and requires revitalization. We need to shower immortal dao into every corner of this world and turn all of its inhabitants into cultivators!” Lu Yun held her hand and smiled at her. “From henceforth, immortal dao is the great dao of this world and all shall walk the path of immortality!","“This world is henceforth renamed to the world of immortals!”","The world of immortals! Lu Yun’s homeland!","“I am the Immortal Emperor and you are the Immortal Empress.” He smiled faintly.","Qing Yu nodded silently. Being the emperor and empress of this world wasn’t a matter of wielding power or basking in glory. It was a responsibility. Since her dao partner was willing to shoulder this burden, she would naturally keep him company.","“So it turns out that Saint Lu is a saint no matter where he goes,” she teased.","Lu Yun coughed awkwardly.","“Greetings to the Immortal Emperor! Greetings to the Immortal Empress!” Hundreds of powerhouses in the place called out.","They’d become part of immortal dao the moment the Dao Flower blossomed and their cultivation levels from blood and qi were spontaneously transmuted to levels of immortal dao. Since they were closest to the flower, the great dao’s rhythm melded into their bodies when the flower bloomed and transformed them from the very core of their essence.","Some immortal dao cultivation methods, combat arts, and dao methods even filtered into their minds via the great dao. This wasn’t the strength of the Dao Flower, but the Dao King.","He’d used his life essence to compel the flower before he died, directing it to force knowledge and power into these powerhouses and planting the seeds of immortal dao into their bodies.","Those in the palace could quickly assimilate into immortal dao, but the beings of the world beneath them could not. They had to walk the path of cultivation and find their way into immortal dao.","Lu Yun smiled at those in the hall. “You may now enter the world below and sow the seeds of immortal dao through the world of immortals!”","“Understood!” There were three hundred and sixty-five powerhouses in total, including Qingfeng. It was a special number that hearkened to the worlds. They were all immortals now, and the strongest of them were Supreme Immortals of Original Order.","Due to the Dao King’s efforts, the levels of immortal dao here were far stronger than those in the nothing. A Supreme Immortal of Original Order was many times stronger than the strongest in the nothing. They’d reached the true end of immortal dao!","The next stage after it would be Lu Yun’s cultivation level. While he’d yet to reach the realm of the subjective affecting the objective, he ranked among the strongest of the realm below it. He rivaled the dead young man he’d met before.","He was immortal dao now, and he was defined by the immortal dao’s cultivation levels. His level was that of immortal emperor."]},{"number":2168,"title":"Chapter 2168: Chapter 2123: Bad Love Interest","paragraphs":["Chapter 2123: Bad Love Interest","Darkness shrouded the world when night arrived. Ghost zombies roamed the land, searching for any living thing that they could devour.","Many of the heavenly palace’s powerhouses were down in the world below clearing out ghost zombies. They hadn’t cared about the living on the ground before because those insignificant life forms were all guilty. They were the reason why this world had fallen.","The lofty residents of the palace wouldn’t pay any attention to the guilty, if not for the occasional appearance of preeminently strong cultivators.","With the reappearance of great dao and all living things beginning to revitalize, those of the palace naturally set aside their past hatreds. All three hundred and sixty-five of them had reached immortality.","The lowliest of the zombie kings—such as the one that Lu Yun killed first—was the equivalent of a true immortal. The one stronger than it and those on Qingfeng’s level were empyrean immortal.","The fire demon they’d encountered on their way to the palace was a peak ghost zombie king—those were august immortal.","Of the powerhouses in the heavenly palace, most of them were greater than empyrean immortal.","However, this collection of strength was far from enough to fully resurrect the world. More immortals born of the immortal dao needed to roam the land. Thus, the three hundred and sixty-five descended to the ground below to recruit and teach its inhabitants. They established sects and factions in the brand new world of immortals so that the great dao could fully flower and bear fruit.","They’d been confined to the heavenly palace before, fated to become stone sculptures when their life forces ran out. That power restricting them dissipated with the germination of immortal dao.","Lu Yun and Qing Yu strolled hand-in-hand through the awakening land, hunting down ghost zombies. These were the most direct enemy in the current world. They eliminated only the strongest ghost zombies, leaving the rest for other cultivators as a form of trial and tempering.","“Your Majesties, there seems to be a city up ahead!” Qingfeng remained by their side as a guide. This world was still too foreign to Lu Yun, but Qingfeng was rather familiar with it since she’d often visited to search for powerhouses who’d reached a zombie king’s cultivation level.","They were headed to a place called the Bewildered Domain. It was already one of the most mysterious places in this world before heaven and earth died. Now, a strange power surrounded it, keeping immortal dao at bay.","Immortal dao would be incomplete if it couldn’t saturate the world. It wouldn’t be able to replace this world’s heaven and earth to become its sovereign.","Three Supreme Immortals of Original Order had visited it days beforehand, but failed to enter the domain. Thus, Lu Yun and Qing Yu were here in person.","Lu Yun paused and looked ahead of him. There was a faint city skyline barely perceptible through the gray fog.","“It’s a ghost zombie emperor.” Lu Yun frowned at the city. Ghost zombie emperors were stronger than zombie kings and had reached the golden immortal level. He’d slaughtered his fair share of them over the past few days, but the city in front of him... gave him an incredibly dangerous feeling.","That city was the primary body of a zombie emperor.","Lu Yun could see numerous people come and go from it, but none of those were real. They were just illusions manifested by the zombie emperor.","“Let’s go around it,” Lu Yun decided.","“Is it stronger than us?” Qing Yu raised her brow. Although she was the Immortal Empress given the favor of immortal dao, she’d yet to reach that level with her personal strength. Instead, she was a peak peerless immortal.","The peerless immortals of this world were infinite times stronger than the strongest powerhouse in the nothing.","Ghost zombie emperors were just an overall category, their strength varied according to the zombie. The weakest of that level was on par with a golden immortal and the strongest—the city in front of them—rivaled a Supreme Immortal of Original Order.","Although they possessed differing levels of strength, their core nature was the same. They were superior to ghost zombie kings, yet hadn’t reached the next level. Thus, they were all defined as ghost zombie emperors.","“Supreme Immortal of Original Order,” Lu Yun nodded. “It would be a remarkable battle if I fight it and the fallout might affect the entire world. I will not provoke it before full preparations are made.”","This zombie emperor was so terrifying that Lu Yun would need to pay too great of a price if he wished to kill it. Additionally, this world could not endure a fight of such caliber.","At least, not yet.","It should be able to after they visited the Bewildered Domain and brought immortal dao into it.","Lu Yun discovered more than one harrowing ghost zombie emperor along the way, but he avoided all of them and refrained from crossing their path. As boundless as reality seemed to be, it was also extraordinarily weak and susceptible to collapse at any time.","Hellfire had been refining it into a brick all this time. The fire was extinguished when immortal dao traversed it, leaving Lu Yun to collect the rest of it. Free of this external pressure, the world slowly revitalized.","However, it was becoming more fragile at the same time.","“Why take the long way around if you’ve already come?” A clear voice rang out just as Lu Yun’s group set another route. A young man wearing pale blue robes and holding himself with a stately air abruptly appeared, his eyes fixed on Qing Yu.","“To think that such a stunning beauty would be present in this barren fragment!” He smiled gently at Qing Yu.","Lu Yun frowned slightly, seeing that the zombie emperor in the distance had shrank into a miniature city and was casually held in the young man’s hand. He hoisted it like he was flaunting his possession, sweeping Lu Feng and Qingfeng like he were a sophisticate considering country bumpkins.","When his gaze turned to Qing Yu, however, it grew ardent with desire.","Qing Yu rubbed her nose and quietly hid behind Lu Yun. It was her first time attracting attention like this in her many years of life. She’d always appeared as a man and was already Lu Yun’s woman when she recovered her true gender. Who’d dare treat her like this then?","It was such an interesting feeling to hide behind her man and wait for him to chase off unwanted courting!","Lu Yun immediately sensed Qing Yu’s nervous, but also excited state. He couldn’t help but break out in a grin. The young man in front of them was an oaf that didn’t bear regard. The tiny city he held in his hand though, was a ghost zombie emperor on the level of a Supreme Immortal of Original Order.","Why would such a powerful being be willingly enslaved by a living being? Can it be...","Perhaps the death of this world and the source of all ghost zombies lay with this young man?","“Give this woman to me, kid, and I will leave you with an intact corpse. Otherwise, everything that is you will be eradicated from existence.” The young man sneered at Lu Yun, deigning only to flick a glance at the country bumpkin. The ghost zombie emperor in his hand emanated powerful ripples as he spoke.","“Do you know where you’ve gone wrong?” Lu Yun grinned.","“Wrong?” The young man started, then roared with laughter. “That’s right, how would a lowly being like you understand my might—”","“You went wrong when you decided to hold that city with your hand.” Lu Yun raised his hand and grabbed at the young man."]},{"number":2169,"title":"Chapter 2169: Chapter 2124: Kill","paragraphs":["Chapter 2124: Kill","Booooom.","Lu Yun’s hand missed the young man, instead landing on the void beside him and shattering it. A massive black hole appeared and sucked the young man through. Lu Yun grabbed Qing Yu’s hand and stepped through the black hole.","The unbounded nothing was found outside the black hole. Compared to the nihil of their home, this was true nihil. It wasn’t an empty void—it was truly empty.","There was no space, time, or any other concepts. Nothing existed.","The nothing wasn’t simply black—there was no concept of color. It really was the absence of everything.","Lu Yun was briefly disoriented when he arrived in the nothing, like he’d been thrown into an unknown circumstance. Everything here should be part of him, but also not part of him. It was a very paradoxical feeling that made him feel infinitely big, so big that the entire nothing and world was him. But he was also interminably small, so small that he shouldn’t exist.","The feeling lasted for a fleeting moment before he returned to normal—the external circulation of heaven and earth rumbled into motion. Monumental power burst from his body, forcefully creating “something” within the “nothing”.","A lost Qing Yu was jarred back to her senses. She clung tightly to her dao partner, fear and shock warring over her face.","“This is the true nothing!” she exclaimed. “Ordinary beings are immediately assimilated when they enter this area and turn into nothing.”","That was what Lu Yun had felt moments ago. He’d been infinitely big, yet also undefinably small. The whole world had been him and also not him. That was the feeling of being assimilated by the nothing.","If he hadn’t been protecting Qing Yu, she would’ve already become one with the nothing.","“Don’t worry, you’ve got me.” He squeezed her hand with a smile before turning his sights to the young man in front of them.","Their enemy was overlaid with the shadow of a city. He grew larger than life and postured like a tyrant of the nothing. Imposing and untouchable, he looked down at the couple from on high.","“You’re a smart one. You sent me out here because you know that brick can’t withstand my strength, didn’t you?” The young man was one with the city and the full strength of a zombie emperor erupted from him. A terrifying aura roiled in all directions.","Of course, there was no such thing as “all directions” in the true nothing. But there was “something” in this nothing now—Lu Yun, Qing Yu, and the young man created the definitions of “something” and “existence” in this nothing.","Thus was space and time also born at the same time, but that was all there was to these concepts. They would vanish if the trio disappeared; they would not linger afterward unless a mighty subjective existence that affected the objective appeared. That existence would need to use their subjective will to redefine this nothing before “something” could eternally “exist” in the true nihil.","Whether it was Lu Yun or the young man who’d become one with the zombie emperor, neither of them had reached the level of creating an eternal “something” within “nothing.” Even though Lu Yun was but a step away from that level, that one step was an insurmountable distance.","The young man made his move. Standing tall over the city, he balled up his fists and brought a punch down on Lu Yun’s head. There was nothing he could make use of in the nothing since it was the absence of everything. He could only rely on his own strength, but his own strength had become one with the zombie emperor.","A zombie emperor at Supreme Immortal of Original Order possessed unbounded power and could inflict indelible injuries on the new world of immortals with a single blow!","Lu Yun watched the punch approach him and floated away, still holding Qing Yu’s hand. They backed an unknown distance away before he returned the blow.","BOOM!","The void shook and the young man’s attack instantly shattered. The momentum of wind and thunder crashed into the young man like they were tangible forces. He opened his mouth and spewed out fresh blood.","“The power of wind and thunder! How is this possible?!” His eyes went wide open.","These two powers came from the strength of heaven and earth, but that didn’t exist in the nothing! Even he and the ghost zombie emperor could only use their innate strength—pure force.","“Nothing is impossible.” Lu Yun shook off his right hand. His left still held Qing Yu’s, the ripples from the collision hadn’t affected her. He walked forward with her and calmly pushed his palm out.","The power of metal, wood, water, fire, and earth flowed into each other and formed a multi-colored handprint. It crashed into the young man and elicited a large mouthful of blood from him. The zombie emperor that’d become one with him nearly disintegrated from the blow.","Both of them howled with pain and indignity, their combined states nearly falling apart.","“Thank goodness we’re in the nothing.” Lu Yun’s heart palpitated with fear. That palm strike had been so strong that even its ripples would overwhelm the new world. His strength was beyond the limits of what it could endure.","He hadn’t been willing to fight the hidden ghost zombie emperors not because he was worried they would hurt the world throughout the course of their fight, but that he was too strong. If he erupted at full strength, it wouldn’t take too much before he destroyed everything that was the new world of immortals.","“How can you be so strong?!” the young man shrieked and tried to retreat.","Lu Yun bounded in front of him with one step and grabbed his head, sending power of the soul into the depths of the young man’s soul and reading his memories. Lu Yun’s external circulation of heaven and earth fully flared at the same time, isolating the young man from everything around him. Even a powerhouse standing behind the young man wouldn’t be able to peek into Lu Yun’s domain.","The young man quickly quieted down and died. The zombie emperor city shattered at the same time. Their lives were tied together. Both fell if one perished.","......","In a massive city floating in the husk of a desolate world.","The world outside was dead without any signs of life, but vitality brimmed in the enormous city. An elder in black robes suddenly opened his eyes, the look in them so cold that those around him shuddered without choice.","“Luo’er just died,” he rasped. “Investigate!”","“Understood.” A man dressed in black armor bowed to the old man."]},{"number":2170,"title":"Chapter 2170: Chapter 2125: Cities of The Nothing","paragraphs":["Chapter 2125: Cities of The Nothing","Bam!","A massive hand descended from the sky and smashed the black armored man flat when he turned around. A ring of hazy light flashed through the air before a man and two women appeared in front of the elder.","“Don’t bother, here I am.” Lu Yun stood in front of the elder with Qing Yu’s hand in his. Qingfeng stood behind Lu Yun and Qing Yu; the elder sat on a throne. He glanced sharply at the newcomers and shot to his feet.","“So you murdered Luo’er?” The look in the old man’s eyes was vicious and cruel. He only had one son—Luo’er was the apple of his eye. He’d subdued a ghost zombie emperor who could walk through the nothing to protect his son, but Luo’er had still died to foul play!","“Yeah.” Lu Yun waved him off with a half smile. “But I didn’t kill him, just refined him. I read everything about his soul, memories, and life.” His smile deepened diabolically. “It looks like this Luo’er was your only son, Snowmountain City Lord. What a pity that he’s gone, just like that.”","City lord of Snowmountain!","Cities of the nothing!","When the world collapsed, it dissolved into endless minute worlds in the void, like stars in the night sky. Those worlds were so small that once living beings grew to a certain cultivation level, such as Supreme Immortals of Original Order, those small worlds could no longer contain their existences.","The same applied for the three Supreme Immortals of Original Order in the heavenly palace and the stronger ghost zombie emperors that Lu Yun had seen. They would never be able to verify their dao in a small world like that and become subjective existences that could affect objectivity.","And so, a crazy plan was hatched.","One, two, three... increasing numbers of powerful beings walked into the nothing and used their immense strength to turn other worlds into bricks, building cities in the nothing.","Each of these tiny worlds carrying the seeds of life was mercilessly refined into bricks to build city upon city in the nothing. The powerful beings could use these cities as a foundation to continue cultivation.","There were plenty of cities like Snowmountain within nihil, Snowmountain was just one of the smaller cities. Its city lord was the strongest of this region and the now world of immortals had been under his jurisdiction. He was responsible for killing heaven and earth and for turning the world into a brick.","Snowmountain would naturally send someone to investigate when one of their bricks went awry. Thus, the city lord’s son set off in pursuit of answers. He ran into Lu Yun as soon as he arrived and was refined in turn.","Lu Yun gained a general overview of the situation in the nothing after refining Xue Luo and brought the fight to Snowmountain. This city was a scourge of evil and the world of immortals would be constantly harassed if it wasn’t eliminated. Annihilation would only be a matter of time.","Based on the cultivation levels of immortal dao, the Snowmountain city lord was a half step immortal emperor. Since he was a hair weaker than the young man, Lu Yun decided to come knocking on his doorstep.","These bastards had the ability and strength to reshape heaven and earth, to consolidate the tiny worlds into one big world. However, doing so would consume their own energy. They didn’t need to expend any of their own resources when building cities of the nothing. Heaven and earth died in these tiny worlds because their core essence was ripped away!","One city within the nothing provided sufficient resources for these powerhouses to continue cultivating and be kings of the nothing. They felt no obligation to protect the people, everything they did was in pursuit of self interest.","If they acted on behalf of the greater good, it would be an action that neither benefited others nor helped themselves.","Lu Yun wasn’t going to ape them or permit the world of immortals to be exposed. The world of immortals could absolutely grow into a big world, one with a complete existence. If it was exposed or discovered, all of the city lords in the nothing would race for it and fight to claim it.","The young man had no interest in allowing his hard work to benefit others. So just to be safe, he had to kill the Snowmountain city lord. Not only did this city lord have to die, but all of the cities around the world of immortals had to be eliminated as well.","He would consolidate the cities for his own use and fashion them in a moat around the world of immortals. Whoever dared approach the growing world would die!","Not only did this new world of immortals carry the hopes of all life, it also nurtured his home, family, friends, and child. He’d also found a way to bring the little fox to him and would commence that shortly. As for Lu Qing, well, his son had his own fortunes. He’d grown bigger than his father, so there was no need to bring him over to be a third wheel.","Thus, Lu Yun grinned happily at the Snowmountain city lord.","“How do you want to die?” His aura built until the energy of heaven and earth burst forth. The external circulation rumbled into motion and turned all fifty thousand kilometers within him into his heaven and earth.","The city lord went slack jawed with dismay.","“The subjective affecting the objective—so you’ve already reached these heights!” He was as pale as a sheet and backed up as quickly as he could, not desiring to fight at all.","“Not yet, I’m still a tiny ways off.” Lu Yun smiled and snapped his fingers. Hellfire appeared and slowly ignited the city lord’s body. Everything within his domain fell under his purview. Whoever he wanted to die would die.","At the same time, the city lord wouldn’t take his demise lying down. He sent out his strength in a desperate final strike, fashioning it into a tidal wave that crashed down over Lu Yun. The wave undulated in all directions and crashed into his own city as well.","There was nothing alive in his city, just endless ghost zombies. Everything within the bricks was transformed into ghost zombies during the refinement process and turned into his personal troops.","Living beings? There were none in a city of the nothing apart from the city lord and their descendants. The man in a black armor from earlier was simply a puppet.","Cities of the nothing were built for the city lord’s own purposes and one at the city lord’s level was long used to loneliness. The notion of service for the greater good was an utterly foreign notion.","Lu Yun remained steadfast in the face of such domineering strength, but he was unable to fully curtail it. The strength spreading in all directions could destroy everything it touched.","This was why he’d been unwilling to fight the zombie emperors in the world of immortals. His external circulation of heaven and earth had yet to reach an omnipotent level as he wasn’t truly at the pinnacle.","But no such reservations applied in a city of the nothing. After ensuring that Qing Yu and Qingfeng were safe, he balled up his hands and smashed them into the city lord’s face."]},{"number":2171,"title":"Chapter 2171: Chapter 2126: Fading Away","paragraphs":["Chapter 2126: Fading Away","Lu Yun’s fists came fast and furious, beating the Snowmountain city lord until he saw stars and begged for mercy.","It wasn’t until now that terror set in for the old man. All of his combat arts, immense strength, and everything that he was was impotent in front of this genteel young man. Had the enemy reached such heights??","No, not yet.","If he’d reached the pinnacle, he could change the entire layout of the nothing from where he stood. He wouldn’t need to take any action to reduce Snowmountain to rubble.","“Who, who are you??” the city lord shrieked.","Instead of answering, Lu Yun continued slamming his fists into the man’s face and rendered his features indecipherable.","“Surrender, I surrender! I yield!” the city lord begged. “All of Snowmountain is yours. Everything here and the billions of ghost zombies!”","“Do I need your surrender?” A cold lilt upturned Lu Yun’s lips.","Ghost zombies?","That was an existence that could not be reversed. He wasn’t able to return them to the state of the living even if he used the power of reincarnation. Since they couldn’t be salvaged, what did he want those disgusting and idiotic things for?","Their corpse qi assimilated other living beings when they touched others, so the only thing Lu Yun wanted to do with the ghost zombies was to stamp them out of existence forever.","As for the lords of the cities of nothing who’d created them... he held only one thought about them as well—kill!","Thus, Lu Yun grabbed the Snowmountain city lord’s head while black sparks danced in his eyes. The city lord wailed with anguish as he burned to ashes amid a sea of flames. His soul was also refined by the young man.","After perusing his new wealth of knowledge, Lu Yun frowned when he discovered more about the nothing.","“What is it?” Qing Yu walked up to him and grasped his hand tightly.","“I see...” Lu Yun caressed her head with a smile. “Nothing, I’ve just learned why the first patch of existence was destroyed. It’s a thorny issue and if it’s not taken care of, the world of immortals will still be destroyed by it even when it’s complete.","“But that isn’t why these bastards build cities in the nothing and plague all of life.” He clenched his fists tight.","“The framework of the world of immortals is not stable.” A dream-like voice drifted in from a distant space and time.","Lu Yun started.","“Mo Yi?” he asked subconsciously.","“Yes,” the mistress nodded. “From dao came one, and one begat two, two gave birth to three, and from three... three results in all living things. No matter what kind of world it is, whether it is reality in the nothing or not, nothing escapes this theorem. Only with the three worlds as support can all things be derived.”","Lu Yun nodded without a word.","“I have come to bid you farewell.” Mo Yi’s voice was ethereal and airy; the relief of release could be heard within it.","Lu Yun froze.","“My old friend has passed and I am needed to complete the final step. Farewell.”","......","Her voice wasn’t heard from again after that final greeting. Lu Yun’s heart clenched tight—a very important person was leaving him forever.","While he’d never viewed her with any semblance of love or even anything that could strictly be defined as friendship, she’d been of vital importance throughout the course of his development. Without her, there would be no Lu Yun of today.","But now, she was forever departed from him.","A faint shadow slowly filled in next to Lu Yun. Tushan Miao—the little fox.","She flung herself into his arms the moment she materialized and bawled for all she was worth. Her dense grief and yearning filled the burning city, setting all of it on fire. Ghost zombies, including the immensely powerful zombie emperors, were reduced to ash in a sea of boundless black flames.","Faces that smiled with the relief of eased suffering vanished in the void.","......","The little fox’s arrival filled in the last hole in Lu Yun’s heart.","“Lu Yun Lu Yun, the mistress gave me something before she sent me here.” The little fox paused her nuzzling of the young man’s chest when she suddenly thought of something. She took out a tiny seed from her robes.","“A seed of nothing?!” Lu Yun’s eyebrows rose into his hairline. In his current state, he fully understood what a seed of nothing was. It was a divine item that could grow into a real world in the nihil.","That only major world of the nothing that’d once existed had developed from such a seed. The world of immortals had possessed one too; it’d become one with the world and given it the potential to reach the nothing.","There was another one in the little fox’s hand now, one perfect without flaw.","“The three worlds as one!” Lu Yun understood Mo Yi’s plans when he saw the seed.","She meant for this seed to grow into a patch of reality and become one with the new world of immortals. When Lu Yun’s home broke through the void, it would become one with the new world of immortals and form the momentum of two worlds.","The seed of nothing would be another world and form the momentum of three worlds with the other two.","“This seed of nothing nurtures the kingdom of hell...” Lu Yun’s eyes widened when he sensed the Tome of Life and Death upon holding the seed in his own hand.","The treasure that’d been hidden within his body all along finally revealed itself and reoccupied Lu Yun’s sea of consciousness. It didn’t alter his strength, but he could fully wield reincarnation now and use its power to refine the seed of nothing in front of him.","This seed was formed out of the kingdom of hell!","“So this means that our home has become one of the three worlds and awaits the moment to break out of the void.” Qing Yu also understood the significance of the seed.","Lu Yun nodded.","“I... I am the master of our world now.” The little fox bit her lip. “Big sis Mo Yi helped me. She...”","She sighed when she mentioned the mistress and couldn’t say anything. The dead had departed.","“Mm,” Lu Yun agreed. “The other cities of the nothing will likely receive word that Snowmountain has fallen. They’ll send someone to investigate. Our current task is to think of how to send immortal dao through the new world of immortals and help it to grow.”","These city lords would stop at nothing to claim an existence that could become a major world. Or at the very least, they would destroy it in its infancy.","Once the world of immortals grew into its own, that would be the doomsday of these cities in the nihil."]},{"number":2172,"title":"Chapter 2172: Chapter 2127: Blazemountain City Lord","paragraphs":["Chapter 2127: Blazemountain City Lord","Lu Yun didn’t hesitate at all when destroying Snowmountain City. He burnt it to the ground in a blaze of flames and extracted its core essence of the world, infusing it into the new world of immortals.","At the same time, a hint of green developed in the new seed of nothing that he’d just obtained.","“It looks like the core essence of the world is needed for this seed to germinate and grow into a kingdom of hell...” Lu Yun’s external circulation of heaven and earth was fully operating and ensconced Qing Yu and the little fox with protection. Their cultivation level wasn’t very high—they’d barely set foot into the dao immortal realm, and that was through borrowing Lu Yun’s external circulation.","“If I’d known about this before, I would’ve given the core essence to the seed of nothing instead,” Lu Yun mumbled dejectedly.","“Don’t worry, there are so many cities in the nothing and none of them are anything good. We’ll just eliminate them one by one!” The little fox was eager to flex her muscles after gaining an understanding of the situation in reality. She never seemed to know the meaning of fear.","“The other cities should be on guard after Snowmountain was destroyed,” Lu Yun sighed. “But something else is also a high priority for us. If we ignore it, the ghost zombies will continue to endlessly pour forth and wreck the core essence of the world of immortals, even if we raze all of the cities.”","“What is it?” Qing Yu and the little fox asked in unison after looking at each other.","“A tomb,” Lu Yun murmured with a frown. “The last great personage who could affect the objective with the subjective was buried in a tomb after he died. However, his resentment lingers and his tomb has become one of inauspicious evil.","“His tomb destroyed the last patch of existence and is the source of all ghost zombies. It must be destroyed, or there will be no end to all of this.”","Lu Yun finally understood why these powerhouses would rather create cities in the nothing and establish farms of ghost zombies than rebuild the world. Someone had tried to rebuild the world before him—they’d even succeeded. But in a pivotal moment that would herald success, the tomb appeared and shattered the new reality.","That was why these heavyweights despaired and gave up to build cities in the nothing. No one was born a villain and no one wanted to remain in a city of lifelong solitude. They just couldn’t see any other way out.","No matter what, these people were all corrupted and the notion that the world could not be remade was deeply rooted in their minds. They refined worlds in the nothing and used them as bricks for cities, so that a real world would not be born.","Lu Yun gave a long exhale—these people had to be eliminated.","“Fuxi... invented feng shui and raided tombs probably because he was practicing for this final tomb, wasn’t he?” Lu Yun mused with understanding.","......","The destruction of a city of nothing naturally raised a great commotion through the nihil.","Snowmountain was one of the weaker cities and its city lord the bottom of the totem pole compared to other city lords. Thus, no one paid it any attention other than his wife, the city lord of Blazemountain. The Xue Luo that Lu Yun had killed earlier was her son with the Snowmountain city lord.","As weak as the latter was, the Blazemountain city lord was inordinately strong. She was one of the peak existences in the nihil and Snowmountain had been established only with her help. The two were dao partners before the great devastation, but their child was born after reality was destroyed.","They’d lived in Blazemountain at first, yet as their strength grew stronger, one city alone wasn’t sufficient for their cultivation. Thus, the Blazemountain city lord helped her husband build another city.","The Snowmountain city lord settled into his new home with their son. The couple would build a new city in the nothing for their son when he grew strong enough. The Blazemountain city lord had set out for Snowmountain as soon as she sensed her son die. But when she arrived, she saw only the ruins of Snowmountain.","She was a beautiful woman with flaming red hair, clad in a scarlet silk dress. She stood with fury burning in her eyes outside of Snowmountain and looked around the nothing.","“Something” came into being when the city lord arrived, creating the four cardinal directions, up, and down.","“Someone who could kill my husband without making a sound, and do so so quickly that not even a cry for help could be emitted, is no ordinary person.” The Blazemountain city lord calmed herself down with effort. Nothing met the eye as she looked everywhere.","“Whoever killed him did so to seize Snowmountain’s core essence.” A frosty glint leapt in her eyes. “Whoever you are, now that you’ve dared touch one of mine...”","Her body shook as she vanished in the void, taking “something” with her and returning nihil to a state of nothing.","Lu Yun slowly materialized after the city lord left. His appearance didn’t disturb the nothing or create the concept of “something” within it. It was like he was part of the nothing.","“That person was nearly the same level as me, she was also an immortal emperor!” Lu Yun took a deep breath, thanking the Tome of Life and Death for finally appearing. He’d used the treasure just now to conceal the world of immortals.","“No, this won’t do, I need to make more plans.” He furrowed his brows.","The Blazemountain city lord hadn’t closely inspected the perimeter because she suspected that other city lords were behind this. If she had, she would’ve discovered traces of the world of immortals.","He had to distract her before she had a chance to.","“Snowmountain, Blazemountain... There’s also Shaman Mountain, Miu Mountain, Bluemountain... They were part of the same faction before reality perished and are still allied with each other in the nothing.”","Having refined the city lord of Snowmountain, Lu Yun could work out a few situations in the nothing given the late city lord’s memories.","Blazemountain was the leader of their faction and she possessed twelve cities under her banner. All was not a picture of peace in the nothing because their cities were not really worlds. Their core essence of the world was continuously depleted and even detonated when emptied.","Thus, the city lords needed to constantly forge bricks. Some even attacked each other to seize another city’s core essence.","As weak as Snowmountain had been, no one dared march on it since the city lord was the dao partner of the Blazemountain. Everyone knew that the Blazemountain city lord would pursue things to the end if someone harmed her dao partner.","“Apart from Snowmountain, Bluemountain looks to be the weakest under her banner. Let’s take out Bluemountain first!” Lu Yun vanished in a streak of light when he made up his mind."]},{"number":2173,"title":"Chapter 2173: Chapter 2128: Dregs","paragraphs":["Chapter 2128: Dregs","There were no concepts of anything in the nothing.","But once a powerful existence appeared within it and was defined as “something”, then the nothing was affected by the “something” and generated the concepts of up, down, the four cardinal directions, and time.","In other words, direction and space came to be when there was a frame of reference to refer to. At the same time, this reference object needed to be strong enough so that its “something” wasn’t assimilated by the nothing.","That reference object could be a Supreme Immortal of Original Order of the new immortal dao, for example.","Lu Yun had exceeded that level and reached the higher immortal emperor realm. His external circulation of heaven and earth could craft a complete system of heaven and earth in the nothing. When he entered the nothing, he could create a world that was very similar to reality.","The immortal emperor realm did not possess such an ability. This ability came from the external circulation of heaven and earth that Lu Yun invented. This new cultivation technique was yet to fully meld with immortal dao.","Currently, they stood right in front of Bluemountain. His external circulation hummed around him as he halted beside it and silently assessed the city.","“So you have indeed come.” The city lords of Blazemountain, Bluemountain, Shaman Mountain, and Miu Mountain appeared in unison. Apart from the Blazemountain city lord who’d barely reached the immortal emperor level, the rest were the equivalent of Supreme Immortals of Original Order.","“Did you kill my husband?” The Blazemountain city lord looked at Lu Yun with haunting killing intent.","Lu Yun nodded without a word.","“Who are you?? There is no such character as you in the nothing!” The Bluemountain city lord also regarded Lu Yun frostily. He wasn’t much stronger than the late Snowmountain city lord, so survival wasn’t likely if the powerhouse came for him.","There were plenty of cities in the nothing, but the person in front of them was absolutely not a city lord. He lacked the decrepit air of decay that all city lords possessed. City lords spent their days with ghost zombies, so while they weren’t a zombie themselves, they were tainted with the presence of one.","There were a dozen ghost zombie emperors hiding in the surroundings apart from the four city lords. They would charge forward with a single word from the Blazemountain city lord and rip Lu Yun to pieces.","“Me?” Lu Yun quirked his lips. “I’m the one who’s going to eliminate all of you. I’d planned to come for you one by one, but all of you are gathered here. How lovely, you’re saving me a lot of trouble.”","An arctic glare shone out of his eyes as he promptly struck, bringing a fist down on the Miu Mountain city lord closest to him.","His target was well aware of Lu Yun’s might and was well guarded. The city lord rapidly backed away the moment the young man made his move and zombie emperors winked into place, blocking Lu Yun’s path.","BOOM!","A loud explosion in the nothing created the concept of sound. Lu Yun obliterated three zombie emperors with one punch. These were much stronger than the ones of Snowmountain—they’d reached peak Supreme Immortal of Original Order and were only a hair weaker than immortal emperor. They could be called half-step immortal emperor.","“So strong!” the four city lords gasped in unison.","“This guy’s not a city lord, so he must be one of the dregs trying to restore the worlds,” Blazemountain huffed. “We’ll keep him here. Go find the other city lords, Bluemountain. Have them come here to eliminate him together!”","“Alright!” Bluemountain was the weakest among them and wouldn’t be of any help if he stayed here. He immediately shifted away and vanished in the nothing.","“The dregs trying to restore the worlds?” Lu Yun’s expression shifted at hearing their conversation. So he wasn’t alone in the nothing? There were other powerhouses like him, trying to resurrect the worlds? Were the Dao King, mistress, and God part of them?","Sadly, they were dead now. One had sent Lu Yun here, another sent Qing Yu here, and the last sent the little fox here.","Sorrow filled his mind when his thoughts traveled here. The descriptor of “dregs” stung too much, so his blows grew more cutting and merciless as a result.","Increasing numbers of ghost zombie emperors crowded around him. There were now several hundred, compared to the dozen at first. The four cities of the nothing were on full display and took up positions in the four cardinal directions, surrounding Lu Yun in their center.","The Blazemountain, Miu Mountain, and Shaman Mountain city lords were not to be underestimated either. The Blazemountain city lord was on par with Lu Yun. If it wasn’t for the young man possessing an external circulation of heaven and earth, shifting everything within his domain according to his will, he would’ve already been torn apart by the three.","It was also because of this external circulation that he firmly held the upper hand. The endless zombie emperors were just cannon fodder, here to simply prevent him from advancing.","“You are indeed one of the dregs seeking to revive the worlds!” came a furious yell as a scorching presence rapidly approached them.","An enormous fireball exploded next to Lu Yun, forcing the young man to hastily back up and evade the fireball’s range of effect.","An elder in red robes manifested in the nothing. He emanated the presence of fire origin energy that dyed the surroundings into a sea of flames.","“An external circulation of heaven and earth?” Lu Yun’s pupils contracted violently, but he quickly realized that it was something different, despite being very similar. He circulated the true power of heaven and earth, the core essence of a world. The elder in red circulated pure fire origin energy. His domain was a world of fire origin.","The elder had deviated into another path. Although he obtained tremendous power doing so, he would never reach the pinnacle of the subjective affecting the objective. The power of heaven and earth was the legitimate force that encompassed everything. A world of fire origin was just a world of fire energy. It could never form the power of a real world and was thus a rootless creation.","However, the elder in red was incredibly terrifying. Lu Yun had to back up an unknown distance before he evaded the explosion of fire origin energy.","“Inferno City Lord!” The others breathed out more easily to see the newcomer.","Lu Yun was so ferocious that they wanted to run. Thank goodness that the Inferno city lord was here! He was an absolute heavyweight in the nothing who was stronger than Blazemountain.","There were once dregs who tried to recover the worlds in the nothing, but Inferno had executed them all. He’d been the reinforcement that Bluemountain set off to locate.","“What an endless pool of dregs,” Inferno snarled at Lu Yun. “Are you still trying to recover the worlds? Do you really want the nothing to become a true nothing and obliterate all signs of life that ever existed?”"]},{"number":2174,"title":"Chapter 2174: Chapter 2129: Why Don’t You Run Already?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2129: Why Don’t You Run Already?","“Obliterate all signs of life that ever existed?” Lu Yun snorted when he heard the Inferno city lord’s words and couldn’t be bothered to answer. He splayed out his hand and summoned a massive bolt of lightning from it, flinging it at the city lord.","Death art, Thunder Palmstrike.","RUMBLE!!","A bolt of thunder and lightning ripped through the void and smashed down on Inferno. He paled with dismay and rapidly backed up, flaring his world of fire origin at the same time to block Lu Yun’s Thunder Palmstrike.","RUUUUUMBLE!","Lu Yun rotated his external circulation at the same time, suffusing it with bolts of aureate lightning. The purest power of heaven and earth manifested into the force of thunder and lightning.","“A world of thunder and lightning?” Inferno jumped with shock and backed up even further, watching his world of fire origin be ripped apart by bolts of lightning.","“Wrong,” Lu Yun sneered. “A world of thunder virtue.”","A world of thunder and lightning was the collection of natural force, whereas thunder virtue was the force grasped by the living, for the living!","Lu Yun swiftly pressed his advantage upon seeing the Inferno city lord fly backward. He ignored everyone around him—all of the other city lords and the ghost zombie emperors. His only target was Inferno!","Killing one Inferno city lord was a thousand times stronger than slaughtering ten thousand Bluemountain or Snowmountain city lords.","Blazemountain was startled by Lu Yun’s actions. She was far weaker than someone who’d cultivated a world of his own like Inferno. She would’ve been heavily injured, if not already dead, had Lu Yun brought out this level of strength earlier.","“He’s using himself as bait!” she gasped. “We are the fish. What does he want to do with the city lords?! Everyone, use your greatest strength to kill him!”","This person was too dangerous. He couldn’t be permitted to leave the premises alive. Blazemountain, Miu Mountain, Bluemountain, and Shaman Mountain flung themselves forward, joining efforts with Inferno to attack Lu Yun. There were one thousand ghost zombie emperors on the scene.","The violent ripples of their combat imparted a momentum of civilization to the void. Countless “something” and existences formed, on the verge of becoming a world before they were destroyed and reborn again while the powerhouses fought.","The nothing was so immense that these “something” twinkled momentarily, like a firefly in the night, before they were assimilated. All the same, the constant stream of budding existences sparkled in the dark, giving one the illusion of continued light in the gloom.","It was as if an eternal existence that could never be extinguished had come into being in the nothing.","Lu Yun fully deployed his world of thunder virtue. He ignored the other four city lords and the zombie emperors, instead focusing firmly on the Inferno city lord. He was going to take this guy out even if it resulted in grave injuries to himself!","He’d only refined a Snowmountain city lord before this, and that city lord had come into his strength only after he entered the nothing. He knew too little and most of his knowledge was vague, or even from snippets of conversation with the Blazemountain city lord.","There were many secrets that not even Blazemountain were aware of.","Lu Yun needed to refine someone of sufficient standing to gain adequate understanding of the nothing—particularly if he wished to probe the tomb of that unparalleled powerhouse and why it continued to destroy the world.","He wasn’t confident in his chances against the tomb. All he could do was to collect as much information about it as possible. A minor character like Snowmountain only knew about the tomb’s existence, but nothing else apart from that.","Inferno was one of the peak heavyweights of the nothing, he would certainly know much more. He might’ve even paid it a visit before!","Lu Yun didn’t think it likely that the city lords had never thought of defying their fate, that they’d never thought of trying to raze the tomb. Surely they hadn’t just defaulted to building cities in the nothing from day one!","He fully deployed his world of thunder virtue and stabbed through Inferno’s world of fire origin with bolts of lightning.","Inferno shrieked and wailed with horror. He read resolute killing intent in Lu Yun’s eyes. Despite being riddled with injuries from the other four city lords and a thousand ghost zombie emperors, the young man’s expression remained unchanged and he continued to furiously attack the city lord.","Inferno was nearly losing his mind.","“Madman, madman!” Inferno howled and he summoned his city. He flew into its relative safety and directed the city to ram Lu Yun.","BOOM!","A massive explosion rang out as parts of the nothing shattered, transforming into bits of “something”. Lu Yun vomited blood, but the look in his eyes remained resolute. He called upon his full strength and released it with equal intensity.","“Break!!” he screamed. The force of thunder virtue surged as he punched outward, condensing his entire world into a massive fist that collided with Inferno.","At the same time, the cities of Blazemountain, Miu Mountain, Bluemountain, and Shaman Mountain also rammed the young man. All five cities crashed into him at the same time!","A sneer curved Lu Yun’s lips as his body and the world of thunder virtue vanished without a trace.","Death art, Boundless Step.","The next moment...","Kaboom!","Five cities of nothing slammed into each other. The weakest of Bluemountain immediately vaporized while Miu Mountain and Shaman Mountain shattered into pieces. Blazemountain was heavily injured and fractured into eight sections, but remained hovering in the void. Inferno was likewise devastated, but it remained in one piece despite the ugly gashes fissuring through it.","The collision of five cities of nothing obliterated countless ghost zombies.","“Heh heh heh.” A cackling Lu Yun walked out of the void.","The Bluemountain, Miu Mountain, and Shaman Mountain city lords had died from the impact. Blazemountain heaved for air and Inferno stirred weakly.","Lu Yun strode into Inferno without hesitation and gripped the city lord’s throat, funneling hellfire into his body.","“Hellfire... reincarnation!” Inferno shrieked, but his voice couldn’t travel beyond his mouth.","Black flames burst from his body and began devouring everything that was the city lord. It refined his memories at a leisurely pace. Lu Yun flicked a glance at the fragmented Blazemountain as the process took place—her city lord lived and her body reflected the same damage that her city had suffered. She gaped with horror at the young man refining the Inferno city lord.","“Why isn’t this idiot running yet? How will the other city lords learn of my existence if you don’t escape? How will the so-called dregs know that another one of their own is out here?” Lu Yun grumbled. “I’ve already slowed down my rate of refinement by several times, so why don’t you run already?","“You’re next after I refine this old guy,” he couldn’t help but remind the Blazemountain city lord. She seemed petrified with shock."]},{"number":2175,"title":"Chapter 2175: Chapter 2130: Darkness","paragraphs":["Chapter 2130: Darkness","The Inferno city lord was still alive while hellfire ignited every inch of his body. Wails of agony pierced through the void, sending shudders of horror down Blazemountain’s back.","“Ahh!!” She reacted after an indeterminate period of time and fled, leaving her fragmented city behind.","Lu Yun sagged with relief to see the city lord run in the opposite direction and vomited another mouthful of blood. He sat down cross-legged in the void and meditated to recover from his injuries.","“Heh heh heh, little fellow. Here I thought you really were invincible.” Inferno leered to see Lu Yun suddenly stop his refinement and retract hellfire. Not only did he still live, but his wounds began to close as well. “I thought you let her go on purpose. So it turns out that you’re at the end of your rope!”","Lu Yun looked noncommittally at Inferno and didn’t say anything. He concentrated on recovering from the harm that he’d suffered from the fight. The last blow had gravely injured him as he’d yet to reach the pinnacle. But after that fight, he was beginning to better understand the strength of the city lords in the nothing.","Civilization had decayed in the nothing; the cultivation systems and levels were hazy and ambiguous. Lu Yun was dividing thepeoplem according to the definitions of immortal dao, but it was an imprecise categorization.","Take the Inferno and Blazemountain city lords, for example. They were both immortal emperor to Lu Yun’s senses, but one Inferno could easily destroy ten Blazemountains because he controlled something similar to an external circulation of heaven and earth.","Unfortunately for him, his strength had deviated from the proper path and lost the support of a real world. He would never touch the level of true heaven and earth; his way forward was dead.","However, Lu Yun didn’t think that Inferno was the strongest kind of existence in the nothing, there had to be others stronger than him!","While the city lords could just barely be categorized using immortal dao, they didn’t cultivate immortal dao. So who knew what other aces they had up their sleeves?","There had to be others stronger than who he’d encountered thus far, there had to be!","“Aren’t you afraid of Blazemountain suddenly coming back at this time and giving you a fatal blow?” Inferno continued when Lu Yun remained silent. “Or do you think Blazemountain is a coward and she won’t dare seek revenge on you after you’ve slaughtered her dao partner, son, and troops?”","“There’s one thing I’m curious about,” Lu Yun finally raised. “Even a bumpkin like Blazemountain had others under her banner. You’re a heavyweight many times more powerful than her, so why are you alone?”","Inferno’s heart skipped a beat. Lu Yun spat out another mouthful of blood and closed his eyes in quiet meditation.","Stillness reigned in the void for a moment.","Inferno continued to recover and he continued to leer unblinkingly at Lu Yun. However, unease was beginning to creep into his heart. Although he steadily recuperated, he couldn’t contact his city no matter what.","The void was rootless and devoid of everything—it was the pure concept of nothing. The city lords could walk through it and wield such strength because they had their cities.","Crafting “something” in the nothing and providing a basis for them to stand all came from the cities. They were the roots and sources of their strength. A city lord was as good as crippled once they lost their city.","Lu Yun had let Blazemountain go because her city was destroyed. She was no longer a city lord. She could only latch onto a stronger existence and survive from their largess.","If she was lucky, her new patron might craft a new city for her—just as she had once done for Snowmountain. But regardless, she was crippled. Without a city, her strength would gradually recede until she was assimilated by the nothing, even if she was as strong as an immortal emperor.","......","“Dregs trying to resurrect the world?” A massive collection of cities in the nothing forced something into existence in this part of the nihil. They were like a world, but not really a world. They were just a gathering of countless cities of nothing into something that resembled a world.","Each city possessed power of the world, but their power was tattered beyond belief. They were forcefully stuck together, like a broken mirror glued back into a whole. They looked complete on the surface, but were actually a handful of pieces.","A broken mirror could never be what it once was.","The Blazemountain city lord did not have the right to come here. She would be chased off if she even tried to draw near it. But this time, she ran into no obstacles because her wounds were too severe and contained a hint of a complete world.","The power of a complete world, a complete heaven and earth... was the most frightening existence in the nothing. A complete heaven and earth would attract that terrible structure and destroy everyone.","A man in long black robes knitted his sharply angled brows together. He stared intently at Blazemountain. “Did he leave that power on you?”","“Yes.” Extremely wan, she took a deep breath. “My troops have been decimated and my city razed. That person is refining the Inferno city lord as we speak.”","“Just him alone?” the black-clad man considered gravely. His eagle eyes stared intently at Blazemountain—or rather, the hint of a complete world on her.","It was a full demonstration of force, just a hint, but it was enough to make his heart palpitate.","“Yes, just one person.” Blazemountain hung her head and didn’t dare keep anything from the man.","He suddenly extended his hand and manifested a black city.","Rumble—","An incredible rumbling echoed in the void as another city floated out of the nothing. It was the fragmented Blazemountain that’d split into eight sections.","It recovered in the next second.","“My thanks to the Darkness city lord!” A sharp light flashed through Blazemountain’s eyes when she saw the change. Although she thanked the man, her heart filled with despair.","The Darkness city lord was one of the tyrants of this collection of cities and an absolute powerhouse in the nothing. He was far stronger than the Inferno city lord. To Darkness, Inferno was just a hunting dog and Blazemountain an ant.","The Darkness city lord had been closest to the pinnacle before the world collapsed. He once championed people against the horrific tomb, wanting to kill its owner.","Sadly, he failed and had to bow his head to destiny, constructing the Darkness city in the nothing. Despite his efforts, he was no benevolent soul nor some magnanimous saint who cared about life. Everything he did was for his own benefit—such as helping Blazemountain restore her city.","“Go spread the word of that person and say that he has a complete world on him.” Darkness’ thin lips moved. “This time, I’m going to erase all of the dregs.”"]},{"number":2176,"title":"Chapter 2176: Chapter 2131: Saviors","paragraphs":["Chapter 2131: Saviors","“Darkness, those dregs who refuse to see the limits of their strength are still probing for where the tomb is.” A frowning person appeared next to the city lord with a turn of their body. “Inferno is trash, so it’s not hard to defeat him. Those dregs have always been cautious and don’t seem like they’d mobilize en masse for this.”","Blue hair cascaded down over blue robes while water ripples circulated around the person. She was a very pretty woman.","“Weilan,” Darkness greeted her with a smile. “Those dregs are living beings too, so they’ll have their own personal desires. They may not be as united internally as they appear to be.”","The Darkness city lord stretched out his hand, looking at the small ball of power from heaven and earth that bobbed above it. He’d collected it from Blazemountain when repairing her city.","“This is power from a complete heaven and earth... It is anathema to us city lords, but to that scum...” His lips curved upward and he smiled deeply. “We won’t even have to act ourselves after you spread the word.”","The Weilan city lord brightened. City lords known for ulterior motives such as them weren’t the best candidate to disseminate the rumors. Blazemountain was the optimal choice as she was a victim and bore traces of a complete heaven and earth on her. Those would attract quite a lot of attention to the city lord by themselves.","“The dregs have always styled themselves as saviors of all, but the worlds they’ve created a few times have always met their end at the tomb’s hands. They’ve depleted the nothing of life again and again—they are the true sinners of life!” Weilan’s lips curved with contempt as she looked at Blazemountain’s departing figure. “Our ideals are different from them, but it is all the same in the end. We both seek to act on behalf of all life,” she sighed.","“I’m not that grand.” Darkness smiled at Weilan. “I just want to live.”","“I want to live too,” Weilan snorted with laughter and leaned her head against Darkness’ embrace, murmuring, “I just don’t want to live such a lonely existence.”","I want to see blue skies, white clouds, green mountains, and blue water again.","If one had a choice, would one choose to live in the empty nothing that lacked everything? If one had a choice, would one be willing to spend their days with odious ghost zombies?","Darkness sighed and caressed Weilan’s head, a deep look appearing in his eyes.","Everything was done for the sake of survival.","......","Lu Yun began refining the Inferno city lord again. The latter’s shrieks echoed in the void, creating the concept of sound in the vast emptiness and then traveling elsewhere.","A figure suddenly walked out of the void. Tall, slender, it was a woman dressed in black. She held a head in her hands—Blazemountain’s.","“Who would’ve thought that the city lord who killed Pantian would die to a newbie like you!” Excitement and hope flashed through her eyes when she saw Lu Yun.","Although Inferno was still screaming, he was dead. The anguished wails were just the concept of “screaming” that’d been born in the nothing.","Pantian had been a powerhouse of the faction known as the Saviors. He’d set a personal goal of reshaping the world and saving all of life. He once gathered countless small worlds and crafted them into a mid-sized world, then helped the world blossom with light in the nothing.","Sadly, he’d fallen for one of Inferno’s traps and died to the city lord.","Having refined this part of Inferno’s memories, Lu Yun knew of Pantian and how important he’d been to the Saviors. He was far stronger than Inferno, but had been refined to death through one of the city lord’s schemes. The mid-sized world that he’d created was turned into a brick and added to Inferno’s city.","“Motong.” Lu Yun raised his head and called out the woman’s name.","“You know me?” Motong paused. She’d never seen Lu Yun before and had found the young man through Blazemountain’s tracks. When she received word that a city lord was requesting help in the nothing, she’d intercepted Blazemountain and learned of Lu Yun’s existence when she killed the city lord.","To think that the unknown Savior would recognize her with a single glance!","“I refined the Inferno city lord’s memories,” Lu Yun nodded.","“That’s still not right!” Motong’s brows drew together. “My identity is special, so the Inferno city lord can’t possibly know me... There’s a traitor among us!” She immediately realized.","“Not a traitor,” Lu Yun shook his head. “This person was on the city lords’ side from the very beginning. They’re a sleeper agent.”","Motong sat down next to Lu Yun and frowned ferociously.","“Do you trust me that much?” Lu Yun snorted with laughter to see the newcomer completely relaxed around him. “Aren’t you afraid that this is a trap? You won’t stand a chance if I attack you when you’re sitting so close to me.”","Motong was stronger than Blazemountain, but far weaker than Inferno. The Saviors weren’t limited by the cities of nothing since they lacked such cities. They could travel at will through the nothing, but that also meant their strength was limited. In the nothing, a city lord was much stronger than a Savior of the same level.","The Saviors gained their strength from the small worlds.","“Trading an Inferno city lord for me is an incredible loss for the city lords.” Motong wasn’t the least bit concerned. “It’s precisely because we’re afraid this is a trap that I’m here.”","She was very frank—they suspected Lu Yun, so they sent an expendable Motong.","The Saviors didn’t plan on bringing Lu Yun back to their headquarters. They’d fallen for this trick too many times and had been heavily set back by Pantian’s death. These days, they repeatedly tested any Savior they met, even if the other was the genuine article.","The great world shattered into infinite pieces when it broke and created numerous planes in the empty nothing, depositing the concept of something in many parts of the nihil. Who knew what might arise from that?","The Saviors had come from these tiny worlds. There were so many of the worlds that despite the city lords crafting them into bricks, there was still an infinite sum.","Of course, just as these small worlds could give rise to Saviors, so could they give rise to more city lords. No one knew who they faced, so they had to be careful.","If it wasn’t for Motong’s side sensing the presence of a complete heaven and earth on Blazemountain, it might’ve been an even more insignificant person who came."]},{"number":2177,"title":"Chapter 2177: Chapter 2132: Zero Times and Infinite Times","paragraphs":["Chapter 2132: Zero Times and Infinite Times","Based on the division of immortal dao cultivation levels, Motong’s strength was also denoted as immortal emperor. She also grasped a complete circulation of the world.","Instead of an external circulation of heaven and earth similar to Lu Yun’s, hers was one similar to the Inferno city lord. It was a world of darkness composed of dark origin force.","Motong was weaker than Inferno because the late city lord possessed a city. If he didn’t, he would be on par with Motong. But even with the degree of strength she possessed, she still wasn’t a core member of the Saviors. Of course, neither was Inferno important to the city lords either. He also didn’t have the right to enter the grouping of cities.","It was thus apparent just how terrifyingly strong the nothing was, and how prosperous the great world must’ve been when it still existed. In the same vein, it illustrated how horrific the ancient tomb that’d destroyed the world was.","“It looks like the newly born immortal dao isn’t detailed enough. Its cultivation levels are neither thorough nor comprehensive enough for the nothing.” Lu Yun ignored Motong and thought over his great dao.","Immortal emperor was the final cultivation level of the new immortal dao, but the variations within this cultivation level were a bit too large. Someone like the Blazemountain city lord was an immortal emperor, but so was someone like Motong, one who could twist the city lord’s head off with a single hand.","The difference between the two was more than heaven and earth.","Of course, another reason for the gap between them was that Motong commanded a world of darkness. However, Lu Yun could tell that she hadn’t called upon it when she yanked Blazemountain’s head off. The city lord had fully recovered from her injuries then; her city had also been fully repaired.","He could see through the past and future in his current state. There was no sense of time in the nothing, so his level of cultivation fully imparted what’d happened to the Blazemountain city lord before her death.","A living being could defend itself against such scrutiny, but a dead corpse absolutely couldn’t.","Lu Yun could also see what the Inferno city lord had experienced throughout his life, but the young man couldn’t be bothered. He’d refined the city lord’s memories, so anything he wanted to know was accessible with a single thought.","It consumed considerable energy to peer into a corpse’s past and future, but something such as refining memory could be done through the power of reincarnation.","“Why aren’t you saying anything?” Motong closely assessed the mysterious young man. He looked to be eighteen years old and clean-shaven. There wasn’t any hint of dejection or dispiritedness on him. Rather, there was a vibrant force of energy.","It was so similar to how she’d been back in the day. She’d risen from a small world and defended against an attack from a city of nothing. She’d led the beings of her tiny world onto a path called hope.","But in the end, reality smacked her firmly across the face. Her home was destroyed, her friends and family dead in the disaster. They were turned to ghost zombies and her world surrounded by countless cities of nothing. In the end, it was refined into a brick.","She was the only one left, so she joined the Saviors.","However, she also knew full well that the homeless Saviors scurrying for shelter in the nothing were a bunch of unfortunate souls who’d lost everything. They swore to recover the worlds and save all of life, but they couldn’t save even themselves.","As opposed to saying they were the Saviors, it would be more accurate to call them the Avengers.","Recover the worlds? That was the wish of the first batch of heavyweights who’d survived the destruction of the original world. Those of them from the small worlds just wanted revenge against the cities of nothing, so Motong had twisted Blazemountain’s head off her head as soon as she saw the city lord.","She’d ripped off the heads of countless city lords in her time, and now she saw in Lu Yun who she’d originally been. The same vigorous zest for life and full of hope, while Motong saw only darkness at the end of her life.","“What do you want me to say?” Lu Yun cocked his head. “Who the undercover spy among the Saviors is?” He thought for a bit and said with resignation, “Inferno’s level was too low. He only knew that there was at least one undercover spy or traitor among the Saviors. He didn’t know who.”","Inferno may be ashes, but Lu Yun possessed all of his memories. The young man stood up and manifested the world of purple thunder and lightning. He was going to use its power to destroy Inferno.","“What are you doing?” Motong asked.","“I’m going to destroy the city, of course.” Lu Yun flicked a sidelong glance at her.","“But it possesses the core essence of a world!” she quickly said. “It can be infused into a small world and help it grow into a medium sized one!”","“But...” Lu Yun drew the word out. “The bricks of this city are ashes of the dead.”","Motong blinked.","“I also wanted to use these cities to strengthen the worlds at first, I didn’t want to waste a single iota of energy.” Lu Yun quirked his lips in a smile. “But I’d be polluted too if I do that.”","“Polluted?” Motong gaped at Lu Yun.","“Yes,” he nodded. “I don’t mind reusing things, but this trash contains more than just the remains of the dead—it also contains the strength of the ghost zombies. If the power of heaven and earth from a city of nothing is incorporated into a world, then the world will be truly ruined.","“Not just the world, but the hearts and souls of the people as well.”","The difference between some things was zero times and infinite times.","Cities of nothing were built from refined bricks of small worlds. If Lu Yun refined a city, his heart and soul would be affected. When he could no longer use the cities to strengthen the worlds, he would cast his eyes on other small worlds.","He would then slowly become another city lord.","Motong looked at him with sudden enlightenment. If it wasn’t for countless cities of nothing mobbing her home when it existed, then she might have eventually walked down that path.","“Did you see all of this from the Inferno city lord’s memories?” she asked with a dry voice.","“The Inferno city lord’s level is too low, I need to refine more powerhouses to know more.” Lu Yun stomped the city to pieces with one foot and churned the fragments into shards with thunder and lightning.","“Isn’t there only zero times and infinite times when it comes to refining living beings?” Motong looked at Lu Yun with a trace of horror.","“Indeed,” he nodded with a smile. “That’s how I’ve made my way here. Although many people call me a saint, I’m really not a good guy. If need be, I’ll refine even you Saviors.”","He smiled an utterly innocent smile and spoke in a very gentle tone, but the hair rose on the back of Motong’s neck."]},{"number":2178,"title":"Chapter 2178: Chapter 2133: Controlling the Nothing","paragraphs":["Chapter 2133: Controlling the Nothing","A deep-seated fear rose in Motong’s mind as she studied the look in Lu Yun’s eyes. This simple, harmless young man might be thinking of how to refine her!","She was weaker than the late Inferno city lord, but she knew far more than him. Inferno had been small fry on the fringes of the cities of nothing. Meanwhile, she was a part of the core of her faction. Given that the Saviors were weaker than the cities, someone as weak as her was still a vital part of its backbone. In contrast, Inferno had been nothing but an insignificant part of the cities despite his strength.","“You...” She looked at the young man with alarm.","“Don’t worry, I won’t do anything to you guys as long as you don’t run afoul of me.” Lu Yun’s smile was as gentle as his tone, but his words were a clear warning. Motong had come with ill intent. He’d easily picked up a trace of enmity and greed underpinning her thoughts.","“While I have the power of a complete heaven and earth on me, I don’t intend to hoard everything for myself.” A ball of light appeared in the young man’s hand with a flip of his wrist.","Power from a complete heaven and earth?","Immortal dao cultivators used the power of a complete heaven and earth from the void realm. Hence, this wasn’t a particularly valuable resource. Even immortals of the new world of immortals grasped a complete heaven and earth.","Lu Yun stood to lose nothing if he shared the cultivation method of heaven and earth with the Saviors. Only when one set foot in immortal dao could one cultivate a complete heaven and earth. Not only would immortal dao be strengthened with the addition of a large group of powerhouses, he could also propagate immortal dao through the nothing and create numerous “somethings” that belonged to immortal dao.","It would save him a great deal of effort.","Beyond that, it didn’t matter what the Saviors actually thought and if they were kindly disposed toward him or not. They were just tools to provide free sermons.","Nothing would be left to their own devices after they joined immortal dao.","The power of heaven and earth within immortal dao wasn’t the external circulation of heaven and earth that Lu Yun cultivated. His method was one that led to the pinnacle of subjectivity affecting objectivity. He wasn’t fool enough to teach this method to a group of heavyweights with mixed motives.","He’d only taught that method to Yuan Yi and Wang Shu for now.","“This is the cultivation method of heaven and earth. Take it.” He tossed the ball of light to Motong.","She caught it with a half-stunned expression. “Are you not coming back to our headquarters with me?”","“Go back with you?” Lu Yun snorted with laughter. “If I did, either you guys or I would die. This is good enough, go on.”","He created a tiny patch of heaven and earth in the nothing and sat down cross-legged to meditate.","Motong took another deep look at Lu Yun before leaving with the ball of light. Her mission was complete—she was here for the complete power of heaven and earth. As for Lu Yun... it didn’t matter who he was or whether he lived or died.","They just needed to lay hands on what they wanted.","In the same vein, Lu Yun would never give the method for an external circulation of heaven and earth to the Saviors. He’d given them a comprehensive method from the void realm. It was completely different from the external world that they cultivated; the two conflicted with each other on a fundamental level.","Their cultivation method had deviated from the proper path starting from the very beginning. It wasn’t something that could be corrected just by showing them scenery from the correct road. If they wished to walk the right way, they needed to withdraw from the erroneous path and re-walk their progress.","Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered with them. His bait resulted only in a Motong bearing enmity toward him. It’d taken a great deal of effort to not refine the woman.","With her departure, he settled into a cross-legged position in the nothing and continued his cultivation.","“Is the nothing really the nothing?” Lu Yun suddenly opened his eyes and looked around him. He stood up, gazing upon the world outside of his patch of heaven and earth.","Instead of a profound darkness that entered his line of sight, it was a sense of being sightless. Just as the blind might see the world, it wasn’t darkness, but an unexplainable sense of failing to see anything.","Where did the nothing come from?","Lu Yun snorted at himself when his thoughts traveled here. He was thinking too much. Life was an accident and matter a fortuitous circumstance. This was what the core origin of the world should be—completely devoid of everything.","Yet accidents abounded everywhere, just as a meteor occasionally streaked across the tranquil night sky and delivered a moment of eternity.","Unbeknownst to him, Lu Yun’s mentality underwent world-shaking changes as he mused. Why was he fixated on creating existence in the nothing? Why did he need to use his subjectivity to affect the vast objective nothing?","The nothing was enormous and unbounded without end. It was also incredibly small and a single base point. It was because life existed here that there was meaning to the nothing. Then, was the pinnacle of subjectivity affecting objectivity really a proper path? Did an accident in the nothing have the right to affect this eternal tranquility?","Lu Yun couldn’t help but think of the ancient tomb somewhere out there. An unparalleled being was buried inside, one who could affect the objective with the subjective. However, he’d perished all the same.","He’d left a deep impression in the minds of others, but was gone without a trace after a fleeting moment—just like the meteor shooting across the sky. It briefly illuminated the entire night sky, but beyond that?","Lu Yun’s eyes turned pure black as the immortal force and strength of heaven and earth within his body receded like the tides. It was replaced by a power that didn’t possess any attributes. His body also began to fade and disperse.","The nothing barrelled into his body, seeking to assimilate it.","But in that moment, he jerked to his senses. The power of heaven and earth grew within his body and immortal force returned, expelling the nothing.","The nothing was without attribute or violent energy. One could easily repel it if one was strong enough. If one’s cultivation wasn’t sufficient to enter the nothing, one would be instantly assimilated by it.","“I was a bit too hasty, I haven’t reached that level yet. I may not be able to come back if I become the nothing.” His lips curved upward as he extended a finger. A tiny dot of nothing hovered over it, the size of a grain of rice.","This pinprick of nothing was under his full control.","Subjectivity affecting objectivity was just a certain type of influence. It was using his own will to change the nothing, forcing rules to sprout within it. That was all.","The tiny dot of nothing in his hand was wholly under his sway. He could transform it into anything he wanted with a single thought.","Such was meant from something being born from nothing.","From nothing came dao, from dao came one, and one begat two, two gave birth to three, and from three resulted all living things.","Lu Yun had tread the path that led to subjectivity affecting objectivity, but now he seemed to have created another fork in the path.","This fork was be larger, broader, and stretched further than the original path. He changed direction without hesitation and took the fork."]},{"number":2179,"title":"Chapter 2179: Chapter 2134: Hand","paragraphs":["Chapter 2134: Hand","There were so many roads out there; it was hard to say which was correct and which was incorrect. But there was a saying on Earth that the southern shafts of a cart run counter to northern tracks.","Some chose the path that would lead to the pinnacle of subjectivity affecting objectivity, but somehow, their selected path ended up leading in another direction. The worlds that the powerhouses of the nihil cultivated were a prime example of this.","Rather than pure power of heaven and earth, their worlds contained various attributes. This power could travel to the end of a great path, but it could not truly affect the objectivity of the nothing.","For the nothing, all great daos and all powers were meaningless. The only things that could exist among the nihil were heaven and earth and a complete world.","Only a complete heaven and earth could survive in the nothing. Only a complete world would find its footing and put down roots to truly affect the nihil.","But now, Lu Yun felt that this path wouldn’t reach the end he wanted either. Therefore, he decided to take on another path and refine the nothing!","It was still the path of cultivating a complete heaven and earth, but the complete heaven and earth was its focus. The path didn’t revolve around affecting the nothing. Instead, the cultivator became part of the nothing, then extracted themselves from it to slowly refine and control the nothing.","The nothing was objective and lacked consciousness. That meant it was wholly without meaning and contained the power to protect itself. Taking this path to the end would eventually enable Lu Yun to take control of the entire nothing.","He’d already glimpsed the doorway and refined a tiny hint of nothing to show for his efforts.","......","Lu Yun’s lips curved upward as he stood up and looked above him.","An immense hand had appeared over his head at some point in time and created a tiny patch of something. A pair of faded black eyes above the hand regarded him silently.","“You’ve been watching me for a while, do you have something to say?” Lu Yun tilted his head back and addressed the eyes.","“The heaven and earth you shared with Motong is different from what you used to kill the Inferno city lord,” came an aloof voice from above the eyes.","They were indeed different. Lu Yun had shared a cultivation method from the void realm of immortal dao with Motong. It was one that resulted in pure power of heaven and earth and collected it into one’s body.","What Lu Yun had used to kill Inferno was an external circulation of heaven and earth. It was a way of using heaven and earth that could impact the objectivity of the nothing.","“Hand it over and I will permit you to live,” the eyes said coldly.","“Heh,” Lu Yun snorted with laughter. “Your greed indeed knows no bounds.”","He could tell that the hand and eyes of faded black were part of the same body—they were the remnants of some powerhouse that’d died. Their life force was so strong that even their remaining limbs had become sentient and set foot on the path of cultivation again.","Bam!","Instead of answering, the giant hand struck downward.","Beings of the nothing were very decisive. They attacked at the slightest hint of disagreement. No mercy was possible if one wanted to survive in this environment.","Lu Yun’s tiny patch of something was immediately eroded through by the corrosive force emanating from the palm. He narrowed his eyes and vanished on the spot, reappearing over the hand.","BOOM.","He stretched out his hand and slapped the hand with his own corrosive strength, catching it off guard and breaking it to pieces.","However, the broken sections immediately transformed into thousands of small hands that swirled toward Lu Yun from all directions. Each of them bore terrifying corrosive force and the void shook from their fight, turning into a massive battlefield.","Both the city lords of nothing and Saviors closely observed the proceedings. The archenemies somehow reached a tacit agreement to just watch and refrain from interfering.","“How is this possible?!” the voice exclaimed when Lu Yun easily blocked all of the hands.","“What isn’t possible?” he sneered as a tremendous power of heaven and earth circulated around him—the external circulation of heaven and earth.","Since he’d caught a glimpse of the true path, the power of heaven and earth or the external circulation didn’t matter to him anymore. Anyone who wanted to see it was free to observe it, he’d never intended to keep his knowledge to himself.","He had even stronger aces up his sleeve; whoever dared run afoul of him would die.","The power of heaven and earth exploded like tidal waves, sweeping through the nothing and turning whatever it touched into existence, forming worlds. These worlds appeared and died in the blink of an eye, their longevity mere flashes in the nihil.","Lu Yun was letting loose with everything he commanded.","The hand was as weak as paper in the face of battle strength that’d almost reached the pinnacle. It didn’t even have time to beg for mercy before Lu Yun destroyed it on the spot.","“It’s not a Savior or a city lord, who was that clown?” Lu Yun stood with his hands behind his back and surveyed the surroundings. His clear voice carried through the void, but everyone shivered and no one dared answer.","He’d thought the hand was part of the Saviors at first, but the Saviors in the surroundings had also been startled by the hand. Plainly, it wasn’t one of them.","“Affecting objectivity with subjectivity?” the Darkness city lord broke the silence with a conflicted voice. “Have you reached that step already??”","“Affecting objectivity with subjectivity?” Lu Yun snorted. “It would be my doomsday if I set foot in the pinnacle.”","Using subjectivity to affect the objective meant to use one’s own strength to influence the nothing. The nothing was objective and didn’t have any strength to resist. But to affect objectivity was like an ant trying to shake a tree. The only outcome would be a merciless crushing by objectivity and then assimilation.","Just like that unparalleled existence back in the day.","A meteor streaking through the firmament thought it lit up the night sky, but it ultimately returned to the nothing and burned away to ashes.","Stars shone brightly in the night sky because they were part of the cosmos. Their fate was also to fall silent in nirvana.","Darkness furrowed his brows, not entirely understanding Lu Yun. But since the young man could easily destroy the hand, that meant his strength was on par with it.","“Do you want to become a Savior, or do you want to join us cities of nothing?” he asked after a moment of silence.","“Darkness, he is a Savior.” Someone walked out from the other faction’s side as soon as he finished speaking. He bore a small world on him and strode through the void.","“Did Motong make it back?” Lu Yun raised a brow.","“She’s dead,” the newcomer replied after a brief hesitation. “The hand killed her on her way back to us.”","“I see.” Lu Yun nodded, not affected by the news. If she was dead, then the cultivation method he’d shared hadn’t been delivered to the Saviors.","No wonder they looked at him with complicated expressions."]},{"number":2180,"title":"Chapter 2180: Chapter 2135: The Will of the Nothing","paragraphs":["Chapter 2135: The Will of the Nothing","“Since the whole gang’s here, I will disseminate dao from this location.” Lu Yun suddenly sat down cross-legged and raised a portion of heaven and earth, playing the notes of great dao from it.","He spoke of his cultivation method, the external circulation of heaven and earth, and even the Dragonquake Scripture. Loud and resonant, his voice formed waves of dao notes that traveled through the void.","The void shook as existence upon existence was born. The notes of heaven and earth also rose from them, resonating with Lu Yun’s methods.","The city lords were shocked senseless and the Saviors likewise at a loss. What did this person want by so easily sharing his knowledge?? Didn’t he know that the nothing was a savage and brutal place? Did he have a death wish?","Selfless?","This word didn’t exist in the nothing.","Whether it was the Saviors or city lords, everything everyone did was for themselves—their survival. That was all.","But in this moment, the beings of the nothing luxuriated in the melody of heaven and earth. Unbidden, they began circulating the great dao etched in the notes.","Immortal dao!","Immortal dao was the foundation and basis of all. It was superseded by the external circulation of heavens and earth and the Dragonquake Scripture. If one wanted to cultivate the methods that Lu Yun was sharing, one needed to switch to immortal dao.","The city lords and Saviors resisted the call, but what Lu Yun taught was too compelling. That was a complete dao of heaven and earth! It would enable them to find their footing in the nothing. They would be free of having to run hither and thither or spend their days with the odious ghost zombies!","There was a trace of beguilement in the notes of heaven and earth, compelling those with a weaker mind to relinquish their great dao and join the banner of immortal dao. The Saviors did so the fastest, assimilating into the new dao and exchanging their cultivation level for one under immortal dao.","A seed seemed to appear in the nothing and called the shadow of a massive tree to hover over the new world of immortals, enveloping the world. Countless immortal dao surged from the world and became one with the new immortal dao in the nihil. Thus fortified, immortal dao swiftly developed and grew stronger.","“Stop, stop already!” the Darkness city lord roared with dismay. The city lords around him were changing their personal dao into immortal dao. When they did so, the ghost zombies in their cities of nothing began recovering, reverting back into the living under the nourishment of immortal dao!","He was truly panicking. He was the strongest in the nothing and far stronger than his brethren. No one among the Saviors could compare.","At the moment, he could clearly sense a massive darkening slowly descending upon the nothing. Horrific tomb aura spread through the surroundings, a power that induced despair and was all too familiar.","“The ancient tomb is here... none of us will survive it.” Darkness gnashed his teeth at the still lecturing Lu Yun. “Do you seek to destroy all of creation and consign nothing back to nirvana?”","Lu Yun raised his eyes to the city lord and sighed, “Running from the problem won’t solve anything. As opposed to struggling for gasps of breath, we might as well take a stand and fight to the death.","“The Dao King, mistress, and God have found the way to break the ancient tomb.” He rose and looked squarely at the city lord. “We have a chance if you meld your great dao into immortal dao too and come under the sway of heaven and earth.","“If you insist on going against me, I will kill you first and then...” The young man stopped speaking, instead shifting his gaze to a black, ball-shaped object in his hand.","Nothing.","A concept of nothing at all hovered quietly in Lu Yun’s palm.","“There is no such thing as the Saviors. That faction are but pawns of the ancient tomb,” Lu Yun murmured. “The same goes for you city lords of nothing. You are just knives used to cleanse the nothing.","“Look at what all of you have done. The ancient tomb doesn’t need to act when a new world is born. You refine it into a brick for your cities. This results in decreasing existences in the nothing and fewer living beings. One day, all will be silenced and we exist in a state of nirvana.”","The Darkness city lord started, shock blossoming in his eyes.","“What, what do you mean by that?” His eyes went wide.","“The core of the nothing is objective for no reason at all,” Lu Yun sighed. “It is an absolute stillness, an absolute nihil. Our appearances are but accidents, but the moment we came to be, the nothing was no longer as pure as it once was. It contained space, time, and the concept of all things.","“In that vein, a will was naturally born within it.”","Lu Yun looked at the spreading darkness. The nothing had failed to be the nothing long ago. There was a will here that sought to destroy everything and relegate it to the pure nothing that it’d once been.","The will attacked the strongest of all first—Mo Yi’s father—the first to affect objectivity with subjectivity. He’d been trying to modify the objective nothing to make it a place appropriate for living beings to live in.","The will of the nothing arrived before he could finish the task and killed him. What was buried in the tomb wasn’t his will, but that of the nothing. It occupied his body because he could affect objectivity, which meant he could be devoured in turn.","This kind of influence ran both ways.","In actuality, the great devastation wouldn’t have occurred if the only patch of existence in the past hadn’t seen the birth of a being who sought to affect objectivity. Such was the instinctive nature of life—always seeking a higher heavenly dao.","“You have two choices. One, I will kill you and then wipe out that will. Two, you will transfer to immortal dao and incorporate everything you are into immortal dao to strengthen it. You will help me that way.” Lu Yun’s tone was noncommittal, as if he was so superior to life that he looked down over all.","He stopped continuously refining nothing the moment he set foot on another path, instead practicing absolute control over it. It wasn’t the shape of the other path, but that he used an extremely domineering way to occupy the nothing for his own use.","“Choose.” His face darkened as he released a ponderous aura from his body. It was more pressure than the city lord had ever seen from anything—it almost rivaled what the ancient tomb brought to bear.","“I...” Darkness set his jaw and sat down cross-legged, choosing to practice immortal dao.","He just wanted to live."]},{"number":2181,"title":"Chapter 2181: Chapter 2136: Revenge","paragraphs":["Chapter 2136: Revenge","“That’s a good boy.” Lu Yun’s lips curved upward as he looked at the city lord.","Do you want to live?","Then be a good boy or I’ll have you die right now.","It was futile to speak of logic and reason with beings in the nothing. No reason or logic was more compelling than life and death for them. They listened only when their survival was threatened.","Immortal dao continued to grow stronger, sending out branches and firmly taking root in the nothing like a towering tree.","A strange existence took shape in the nihil, one that was completely removed from its surroundings. The smile playing at the corners of Lu Yun’s lips turned into a sneer as he looked at the massive shadow.","The clearer the will of the nothing became, the more it wanted to destroy all existence within the nothing. After it cleansed it of all life, it would self destruct and return the nothing to its core essence.","The cities of nothing also underwent transformations when nourished by immortal dao. Living beings that’d turned into ghostly zombies gradually returned to their core essence, becoming living beings again when irradiated with the power of heaven and earth contained in immortal dao. The bricks of the cities also began reverting back to real worlds!","The Darkness city lord was stunned. He had no idea what was going on, why life that had passed on would flourish again! He saw dead kin, friends that’d died, and everything he’d ever lost!","“What... what is this??” He stared at Lu Yun with incredulity.","“Reincarnation,” the young man responded calmly. “Everything reawakens under reincarnation.”","Reincarnation was a strength that should not exist, but the mistress, Dao King, and God had forcefully shaped it into being in the past, present, and future. It wasn’t until Mo Yi and the Dao King sent the little fox and Qing Yu to him through their deaths that Lu Yun understood the cause and effect of everything.","Reincarnation had never been under the control of one single person. Past, present, and future were all vital for it.","The little fox of the past built a karmic relationship with the mistress of the future—this was also a karmic tie of reincarnation. It enabled reincarnation to traverse past, present, and future, becoming a true whole.","Reincarnation was never about the birth, life, and death of living beings. It was the beginning and end of all things and the interchange of nothing and existence. That was the magnificent blueprint that the trio had conceived. It was also the power that could truly end the will of the nothing.","Thanks to it, Lu Yun set foot on a brand new path and controlled the nothing. It was precisely through reincarnation that he exercised control over it. Without reincarnation, he wouldn’t have been able to take that step forward even if he’d discovered the path.","Reincarnation was the conversion between nihil and existence; it granted him the ability to truly command the nothing.","......","“My city of nothing has returned to its origin and become a world again.” The Weilan city lord looked at the Darkness city lord next to her. “My cultivation has also returned to its peak, but I am still unable to withstand the tomb.”","Darkness sighed, “This Lu Yun has forced us into dire straits. This path will either lead to our final triumph or death. We will not be able to prolong our last gasps like we did before. Let’s hope it leads to life!”","Everything had drawn to a temporary close. The two returned to their cluster of former cities alongside the rest of their fellow city lords. They gathered together, in full combat readiness, to await their ancient enemy.","The cluster of cities had become a patch of real worlds. The worlds called to each other and showed signs of becoming an even greater world. Instead of joy, the new world lords felt deep fear and incredible uneasiness.","The ancient tomb wouldn’t permit a world like this to exist... Once the world formed, it would descend and kill everything.","“Don’t worry, everyone. Perhaps that Immortal Emperor really has a grand plan for the tomb,” Darkness sighed. “All we can do now is increase our strength so we can ensure our own safety!”","“Bad news, Darkness!” someone shouted with alarm.","“What is it?” His expression shifted and he hastily asked, “Is the tomb here already?”","“Not the ancient tomb, the Saviors!” came the urgent, fearful reply. “They’re mounting an attack!”","“What?!” Darkness frowned. “Why are the Saviors here?”","The strongest of the world lords were gathered in the heart of the cluster to discuss strategy for the impending encounter with the tomb. The weaker ones who’d always drifted around the perimeter were standing in as guards.","The world lords and Saviors had always been enemies. Other than the ancient tomb, their feud was the only conflict in the unbounded nothing. The former had been solidly stronger than the rootless Saviors in the past, but now they were all part of immortal dao and cultivated heaven and earth. With the power of heaven and earth taking root in the nothing, the Saviors had their foundations as well.","Therefore, they chose this timing to attack en masse.","“Let’s go!” Darkness and Weilan charged at the front, leading a group of their peers to meet the enemy.","......","“What do you mean by this, Panmeng?!” Darkness roared at the Saviors leader.","“What do I mean?” The sharp-eyed Panmeng wore long robes made from animal hide. His hair flowed down his shoulders in an unkempt mess and he wielded a greataxe in his hand. He sneered, “I mean to make you demons with blood on your hands to pay the price, of course!”","The city lords had killed countless beings in their quest to refine cities of nothing. They’d ground endless bodies into mud and melded them into bricks, refining them alive. Only a select few had the right to become ghost zombies in the tiny worlds. While they’d come back to life, plenty more were obliterated forever...","Hence, the Saviors were here for revenge.","Or really, they were here to seize the cluster of worlds that the cities of nothing had become. The cities could no longer fight for the former city lords now that they’d become worlds again. Hence, they were resources free for the taking.","“Is this really the appropriate time?” Darkness forced out through clenched teeth. “The ancient tomb is about to go on a rampage. We should unite together to withstand it! Setting ourselves at each other’s throats and depleting our strength is the last thing we should do!","“We can settle any grudges or scores we have after we take care of the ancient tomb!” Darkness looked frostily at Panmeng.","The latter wouldn’t dare show himself in front of the Darkness city lord in the past. But now, Panmeng was likely to be on par with Darkness.","“I’m afraid... that a group of demons like you will stab us in the back when we fight the ancient tomb,” Panmeng sneered. “So it’s better to annihilate you first and avoid later troubles!”","“Kill!!” Numerous Saviors charged with overwhelming fury."]},{"number":2182,"title":"Chapter 2182: Chapter 2137: Await My Return","paragraphs":["Chapter 2137: Await My Return","A great battle commenced with startling abruptness. Blood and gore rained through the nothing in a split second, dying the entire cluster of worlds red.","......","“Do we... just watch them fight?”","The world of immortals.","Qing Yu and the little fox were curled up in Lu Yun’s arms. The little fox raised her head and planted a kiss on the young man’s cheek.","“They changed from what they should be a long time ago,” Lu Yun nodded. “Like a virus, they broke away from order and grew in a barbaric way according to whatever they wished and wanted. They have gone to all extremes in order to live, so it is only a matter of time before they become a source of trouble if they’re kept around.","“The true seeds of life were never things like them.” A cold light glinted in his eyes as he spoke.","The Saviors were the same as the city lords they abhorred. Many of them had also been overtaken by the will of the nothing. They sought not to revitalize the worlds, but to cleanse the nothing of all existence.","The current battle was inevitable, and no one was wrong.","The city lords were not in the wrong as they simply wished to survive. That was a basic instinct of life.","The Saviors were not in the wrong as they’d been pursuing their ideals and safeguarding their worlds all this time. They’d just been overcome by the will of nothing later on.","Even the will of nothing was not in the wrong as it was just respecting the core essence of nothing and maintaining true nihil.","What was wrong was their perspective. In their eyes, Lu Yun was also wrong.","He’d thrown caution to the wind and created heaven and earth—the worlds—within the nothing. His actions summoned the ancient tomb and would be the doom of them all. He’d extinguished the hope of the nothing and was the greatest evil of all.","And now he sat on a hill, watching tigers fight in the form of the world lords and Saviors. Not only did he not put a stop to the hostilities, but he actually added fuel to the flames from the shadows...","Those actions weren’t very aboveboard.","However, the seeds of immortal dao had been sown. The great dao would be strengthened by their power even if all of them died, so it didn’t matter. Since Lu Yun controlled reincarnation, the Saviors and world lords would enter the cycle of reincarnation upon their deaths. They would reincarnate into new beings and be much more honest and upright for it.","Otherwise, they would stab Lu Yun in the back sooner or later.","Additionally, immortal dao required sacrifices and blood. It needed to be forged in blood.","When human dao manifested immortal dao in the end days of the great wilderness, it’d done so through Daoist Ingress’ never-ending series of slaughters. He’d used the countless daos of great emperors to forge immortal dao.","Immortal dao was drenched in blood.","......","Immortal dao grew rapidly through the course of stunning battle in the nothing. While Lu Yun enjoyed the show, he remained on high alert.","A vast majority of Saviors were under the sway of the will of nothing. With it in control, their goal was more than the cluster of worlds. They were actually targeting the world of immortals. They just hadn’t been able to locate it before because Lu Yun had hid the world of immortals within the nothing.","But with the establishment of immortal dao and Saviors also cultivating it, it was simply a matter of time before they found it.","While powerhouses abounded within the world of immortals, they were weaker than the Saviors. The world would perish once the faction found it. Thus, Lu Yun, Qing Yu, and the little fox remained standing outside of the world, waiting for the enemy to arrive.","The shadow of the ancient tomb was still growing stronger. Once it manifested, the ancient zombie within would step forward to destroy everything within the nothing. The world lords were correct, it was their final stand. Either they wrested victory and survival from the jaws of doom, or they died.","Immortal dao had taken shape and filled the nothing. The ancient zombie would be destroying everything that was immortal dao and erasing everything. Therefore, Lu Yun needed to enter the tomb before the zombie awoke and destroy it—he needed to take control of the will of the nothing.","Only when he controlled the will and used reincarnation to transform it into a living being would he solve the problem at the root.","But right now, he didn’t dare move. If he did, the Saviors would come and destroy the world of immortals. There were far more of them in the nothing than imagined. The group attacking the cluster of worlds was only a small part.","“I thought you’d go help those former city lords,” came a familiar and aloof voice. Motong—someone who should be dead—reappeared in front of Lu Yun.","“As I thought, it’s you.” Lu Yun glanced at her right hand. The hand possessed by the will of the nothing that he’d destroyed was her hand. She hadn’t died, she was the one hidden the deepest within the Saviors.","She seemed weak, but her identity had changed innumerable times. The will of the nothing had initially come from her.","“So you guessed it.” Motong drew her lips up in a blithe, radiant smile. “You seem to be almost at the realm of the subjective affecting the objective.”","Lu Yun nodded. “Yes, but so are you. Are you the second person to reach the pinnacle in the nothing?”","“The subjective affecting the objective? That’s just a dead end,” Motong sighed. “The vast objectivity and unending nothing is the true path. Living beings should resign themselves to the embrace of nothing and everything should return to the core origin of nihil.”","She abruptly attacked while sighing and brought her palm down on Lu Yun. He met her strike head-on.","When they met, the void shook and great daos sounded in unison. Immortal dao dao collided with another great dao in the nihil. They gave rise to endless possibilities and all existences were born and died over and over again.","Qing Yu and the little fox naturally retreated behind their husband. They were impassive as this scene was well within expectations. Although they didn’t participate in the fight, they fully sent their power of reincarnation to Lu Yun.","“I will show you today what subjectivity affecting objectivity looks like!” Motong suddenly shouted and opened her arms, releasing waves of immense energy that swirled with uncanniness.","This part of the nothing was suddenly isolated and everything within it expelled. Only pure nihil remained. Motong was affecting the objective nothing and returning everything within it to its core essence, becoming the purest of nothing.","She sent the blackest of nothing down on Lu Yun with a sudden punch.","“The power of the nothing?” Lu Yun snorted and pushed out with both hands. He used the external circulation of heaven and earth instead of his method to control the nothing.","The external circulation of heaven and earth deployed the power of heaven and earth to affect objectivity. It was markedly different from Motong’s subjective affecting objectivity. Hers used personal will to affect objectivity, whereas Lu Yun’s external circulation used personal will to communicate with heaven and earth and borrow its power to affect objectivity.","In other words, Motong used brute force while Lu Yun borrowed a tool, a lever to influence objectivity.","The two kinds of force collided in the nothing and created a terrifying deep passageway in front of Lu Yun. His eyes widened with dismay, caught off guard by the development. He was uncontrollably pulled into the passage before he could react.","“Lu Yun!!” Qing Yu and the little fox gasped.","“I’m fine!” His voice traveled back to them, followed by a magnificent burst of power that barreled into their bodies. “Protect the world of immortals and protect our future. Await my return!”"]},{"number":2183,"title":"Chapter 2183: Chapter 2138: Rebirth Through Possession","paragraphs":["Chapter 2138: Rebirth Through Possession","Qing Yu and the little fox stood dumbly on the spot, at a loss for what to do. Lu Yun and Motong had both fallen into the deep passage and it closed the second they entered.","In the crucial split second he had, Lu Yun sent all of his strength into his dao partners. They now grasped all of the great daos he’d ever cultivated, including the method to control the nothing.","“He’s not dead, he must be alive!” Qing Yu rasped out in a voice so charged with emotion it was like she was crying.","“Mmhmm!” The little fox shook as she spread out her hands. A black book appeared in them.","The Tome of Life and Death.","......","Incredible pain coursed through every inch of Lu Yun’s flesh and bone. It was like his body was disassembling. It was fading away and his will slowly deteriorating.","He’d sent away the Tome of Life and Death at the last possible second, gifting everything he owned to the little fox and Qing Yu through the ties of karma.","Finally...","Boom!","When his body fully faded away, so did his consciousness turn hazy. In this moment, he seemed to see another body that’d also just died. His struggling soul barrelled into it.","Whoosh!","A tiny memory part suffused his soul, occupying everything that was him.","“Yushi Moli... Is that your name?” Lu Yun exhaled gently. He was reborn through taking possession of another.","In these unknown straits, he latched onto a newly dead young man for the sake of his own survival. Unexpectedly, a sword shadow that towered to the sky floated out of the boy’s mind and stabbed into the memories of Lu Yun’s soul.","Lu Yun trembled and found that his memories were being sealed off by the sword! The shrewd look in the boy’s eyes immediately cleared up to utter purity.","Everything of the past began to drift away from him.","“This is just as well... Only with losing the past can I grow anew and fight my way back to the nothing. Only then will I... not miss everyone. Little Yu, little fox, wait for me.”","......","The unending Origin Continent.","The Qiulan Empire.","The northern expanse of the Nebula Prefecture to the north, Aurora City.","The backyard of the city lord’s residence.","A young man roughly thirteen years old gripped a qingfeng sword, raining sweat through the air as he stabbed forward again and again. White robes clad his tall and slender frame, red lips and white teeth were set in a handsome face. Determination suffused his black eyes.","The sword in his head moved steadily, swiftly piercing the air in front of him again and again.","“Nine hundred sixty-seven!","“Nine hundred sixty-eight!”","......","“Nine hundred seventy-two...","“I can’t do it anymore... I’m so tired, I can’t go on!” Pain flashed through the young man’s eyes. “No, I have to go on! I, Yushi Moli, am the son of the Aurora city lord. I have to keep going!","“I can’t cultivate true qi because I have no sense of qi, but I still can’t give up! Not being able to cultivate true qi means I can’t become a martial cultivator, so I’ll be a top notch swordsman instead! I won’t let father lose face!","“One thousand strokes a day, not even one less will do!”","The boy persevered! Despite being tired beyond his limits, the sword in his hand remained as steady as Mount Tai. It didn’t lean in any direction, droop, or tremble.","“Legends say that the great sword master Long Qianjue of one thousand years ago possessed an qi absentia constitution, but his sword skills were marvelous and he reached the celestial rank with them. He dominated his era!","“So while I cannot become a martial cultivator, I will become a swordsman like Long Qianjue! I will bring honor to the family name!","“Nine hundred and eight-nine!”","......","“Moli continues to persist.”","Two men stood side by side in a tower of the city lord’s complex and looked at Yushi Moli in the backyard. One of them sighed heavily.","“His furious training will destroy him. Are you not going to stop him?” Ouyang Du looked at the massive man in front of him. This was the lord of Aurora City, the strongest of its citizens!","Yushi Jianchou.","“He has herbal baths and fare nourishing him. He won’t die,” Yushi Jianchou replied expressionlessly.","“Are you that heartless? He is your son, my nephew!” Ouyang Du’s lips twitched. “His cultivation method is completely incorrect.”","“Correct or not, it is his choice.” Yushi Jianchou stared at the boy below. “Since he has chosen, that is his business. I will not interfere, and the Aurora city lord residence has never kept trash around.”","“You...” Ouyang Du brandished his sleeves with a sharp crack and left in a huff.","An expressionless Yushi Jianchou continued looking down at the boy below.","......","“One thousand!” Yushi Moli finally finished one thousand pierces. He was drained of energy and his right arm flopped weakly. He could barely lift it and wanted to lie down on the ground. “No, no, I can’t lie down or I’ll have wasted my earlier efforts!”","He held fast against the weariness of his heart and stood ramrod straight like a spear, shifting to practice a sword method.","“The eldest young master is relentless when he cultivates!” Two maids gossiped off to the side.","“The eldest young master is the city lord’s son. Although he can’t cultivate true qi, he’ll still be a wealthy scion who lacks for nothing for the rest of his life. Why does he work so hard?” The younger maid didn’t understand Yushi Moli’s actions.","“You dummy! It’s because he’s the city lord’s son that he works so hard. The city lord is the strongest powerhouse of Aurora City and the eldest young master in the only stain on his glory.”","“I feel bad for the young master then...” Sympathy welled up in the younger maid’s eyes.","“What are you feeling bad for?” The older maid next to her curled her lip with disdain. “He’s the city lord’s son and lives a life that ordinary people can’t dream of! Apparently, the herbal food and baths he takes costs one hundred gold coins every month. Ordinary people won’t even earn that many gold coins in their entire life!","“Anyone else would already be a high level martial cultivator after two years of these resources! But him? Heh. I suspect the city lord would rather this young master not work so hard.”","“Huh? Why?” The younger maid failed to understand.","“It’s a waste of resources. Even a pig can advance to the human rank with so much valuable food and baths. But what’s the difference between throwing them into the gutter and using them on the young master? Throwing them into the gutter would at least raise some ripples, but on this one...? Heh,” the older maid snorted. “C’mon, back to work. Us servants shouldn’t talk about stuff having to do with the masters.”","The younger maid shrank in on herself and stuck out her tongue before leaving.","......","Although Yushi Moli wasn’t a martial cultivator, he’d been born with keener senses than others and thus heard every word of the maids’ conversation. He clenched his fists so tight that the veins popped on them.","He’d heard this kind of jeering ever since he was a child. Whether it was within the city lord’s residence or Aurora City, most sighed when they heard the name Yushi Moli. A tiger father had beget a dog son!","His heart spasmed with pain every time he heard talk like this, like a dagger had been plunged through it. But the more this was so, the more he wouldn’t give up.","He exhaled noisily and regained his usual determination.","“Waste of resources?” Yushi Moli reached into his robes and ran his hand over the silk handkerchief on him. “I’ll let you know that nothing I’ve done is a waste!”","He gave another long sigh and retracted his sword aura, accepting a bowl of medicinal soup from a servant and draining it with one gulp.","“Moli!” Ouyang Du walked over.","“Uncle?” Yushi Moli smiled happily when he saw the buff young man. Ouyang Du was the younger brother of Yushi Moli’s mother. The two had a strong relationship.","“That’s enough training today, Moli.” Ouyang Du couldn’t bear to dash Moli’s hopes when he saw the young man dripping with sweat.","“No, I’ve got three more techniques to practice before I’m done for the day.” Yushi Moli shook his head with great reluctance.","“Wait a minute, uncle’s brought you a piece of great news today!” Ouyang Du grinned. “Alchemist Grandmaster Yuqing Yang of the celestial rank will be visiting Aurora City soon.”","“Huh?” Yushi Moli looked curiously at his uncle. “What’s Grandmaster Yuqing Yang have to do with me?”","“Grandmaster Yang is a celestial rank alchemist. They say he can refine a celestial rank pill called the Qi Elevation Pill that can enhance a martial cultivator’s sense of qi! Anyone will gain a sense of qi upon taking the pill, so long as they don’t possess a qi absentia constitution!”","Yushi Moli’s eyes lit up. Obtaining a sense of qi meant that he’d be able to cultivate true qi and become a martial cultivator. This was what he dreamed of!","“Being a celestial rank pill... the Qi Elevation Pill... isn’t cheap, isn’t it?” Yushi Moli frowned.","“Well, the price is apparently one million gold coins.” Ouyang Du started, then answered with a wry smile. As young as his nephew was, he was sharp witted and very few things flew under his register.","“Then forget it, I’ll just stick to practicing sword techniques.” Dejection flashed through Yushi Moli’s eyes.","One million gold coins?","Yushi Jianchou was the city lord, true enough, but he didn’t have one million gold coins to spare. The entire city lord residence was likely worth one hundred thousand. Just one gold coin alone was sufficient for an ordinary family to live in the lap of luxury for an entire year!","Spending one hundred coins on herbal baths and food every month was already undue pressure on Yushi Moli’s young heart.","One million gold coins?","He didn’t dare think about it.","Instead, he raised his swollen arms and returned to his training."]},{"number":2184,"title":"Chapter 2184: Chapter 2139: The Shadow of the Sword of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2139: The Shadow of the Sword of Heaven and Earth","“Eh? Moli...” Ouyang Du chuckled ruefully when he saw the boy return to sword training. “I actually have another idea in mind. You can become Grandmaster Yang’s disciple and become an alchemist. Alchemists enjoy the same status as martial cultivators. It would bring honor and glory to Aurora City if you became an alchemist!”","“An alchemist?” Yushi Moli retracted his sword aura and turned back to Ouyang Du.","“That’s right, become an alchemist,” the young man nodded. “Of the four cities in Nebula Prefecture—Qingqiu City, Tianyi City, Cloudscape City, and Aurora City—only Aurora City lacks an alchemist. If you can become one, the help you can offer your father will be far greater than you being a martial cultivator.”","“But Grandmaster Yang is a celestial rank alchemist. The line of people who wish to take him for their master probably runs from Aurora City to the Nebula capital. It’ll never be my turn,” Yushi Moli laughed self-deprecatingly. Although he was young, he didn’t crave for things high and out of reach.","Gain Yuqing Yang as his master? It was more practical to practice his sword techniques!","But when Yushi Moli heard the name “Qingqiu”, a hint of light flared through the depths of his eyes and an air of sorrow wafted from his heart, like something was about to break out of its shell.","At the same time, a sword shadow flickered into view and suppressed the memory about to break free.","Ouyang Du didn’t notice the undercurrent of reactions, he fell silent as he also knew that becoming Yuqing Yang’s disciple was far more difficult than obtaining a Qi Elevation Pill.","“But no matter what you do, you need to give it a try. It’s an opportunity, after all,” he said.","“Thank you uncle, I hear you!” Yushi Moli turned around and grinned radiantly at Ouyang Du.","......","Yushi Moli was loath to waste a single second of his days. He spent the mornings stabbing his sword forward a thousand times, then practicing three sword techniques. The afternoons were spent on strengthening his body.","But even when he trained his body, the young man kept his sword firmly in hand, gripping it at every second.","Any ordinary person would’ve fallen to the ground halfway through the one thousand pierces, paralyzed from the effort of such rigorous and intense training. It was beyond the limits of what a human being could endure. However, Yushi Moli had the aid of herbal baths and food. He always recovered in the shortest amount of time possible even when his body was gravely injured.","Night fell and ushered in the brisk breezes of autumn.","Yushi Moli wore a thin shirt and sat cross-legged on his bed. A slightly open collar revealed taut muscles that were at odds with his years.","“I hope it really does work, that I haven’t persevered all this time for nothing!” A gossamer-thin piece of silk slowly unfurled in front of Yushi Moli. There was a sword drawn on it, one with sword aura rushing to the heavens.","The Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth!","It was why Yushi Moli insisted on training everyday. The sword chart was not defined by the requirements of true qi. True qi was the strength formed by collecting the energy of heaven and earth in a cultivator’s body. In contrast, the sword chart used heaven and earth as the teacher and all living things as the sword, breaking the shackles imposed by the heavens.","Once a cultivator set foot into the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth, the energy of heaven and earth would be summoned to them and become true qi, even if they didn’t themselves possess a sense of qi.","But to set foot into the sword chart... one must reach the level of holding a sword in one’s heart. Only with the heart in the sword and the sword in the heart could one reach the peak of all things as the sword.","At Yushi Moli’s current level of mastery, all he possessed was a sword in his hand. That was the prerequisite for bearing a sword in the heart. The latter was simply too difficult to reach!","According to the records of the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth, not even the great sword master Long Qianjue had reached such august heights. It was an unfathomable goal far out of reach for Yushi Moli.","He practiced with the sword everyday, conducting one thousand pierces to familiarize himself with the sword and developing a firm grip with it. With that, he could imprint the sword onto his heart.","Yushi Moli was well practiced with sword techniques now. Even one hundred moves had been beyond him at first, but now he achieved one thousand pierces everyday and then practiced three sword techniques.","Given that he was only thirteen years old, his achievements were profoundly stunning. While he was yet to reach great perfection in the realm of sword in the hand, the boy was absolutely a sword expert!","Yushi Moli sat cross-legged on the bed and closed his eyes, sketching out in his mind the sword etched in the sword chart. This kind of mental observation method was one of the cultivation methods recorded in the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth.","He’d managed to outline the shadow of a sword in his mind three months ago. The shadow of unknown purpose happened to suppress his memories from another world. But thanks to its creation, he was more proficient in his training during the day.","And now, resolution and desire alike flared vigorously in the depths of his heart.","Not only because he wished to amount to something and shake off his past, but also because there seemed to be an extremely important calling waiting for him!","He didn’t want to wait for a single second—he needed to grow stronger as quickly as possible!","Yushi Moli continued to observe his inner mind. He focused his entire concentration on the white shadow in his consciousness, becoming one with it. The more he observed it, the clearer the shadow became.","As time went on, he felt that he might be approaching the second level of the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth—sword in the heart. There was a tendril of a connection between him and the shadow in his mind.","......","Early next morning, Yushi Moli practiced in the yard after eating breakfast.","“Hmm? One thousand pierces is easier today than yesterday! It must be because of the sword shadow in my mind!” He brightened. “Do I want to increase the difficulty? Fifteen hundred pierces, maybe?”","His heart sped up with excitement.","“Wait, no! One thousand a day is the limit of my current capabilities. Fifteen hundred would end me and not even herbal baths can save me then!”","He forced down the impulse dancing in his heart and stopped training for the day after practicing the three sword techniques. Yushi Moli was well aware that though he could easily complete one thousand pierces, his body would collapse if he did any more. He was only thirteen years old, after all, a time when his body was developing. He absolutely had to refrain from doing anything that pushed his body beyond capacity.","“Big brother!” A four year old child accompanied by a slender and tall middle-aged man bounded into Yushi Moli’s yard. He was Yushi Moli’s younger brother—Yushi Mowang.","Prior to Yushi Moli’s mother disappearing four years ago, she’d given birth to Mowang. After the boy was born, she vanished without a trace. Yushi Moli had found the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth in a book that she’d left him.","“What are you doing here, Mowang?” Yushi Moli grinned at the boy.","“Hug, big bro!” Yushi Mowang didn’t care that Yushi Moli was soaked with sweat and threw himself into the older boy’s arms.","“Okay!” Yushi Moli swung his brother upward.","The man behind Yushi Mowang furrowed his brow, plainly displeased with the action, but he couldn’t say anything, seeing as Yushi Moli was also the city lord’s son.","“Here you go, big brother. Father gave me this pill this morning.” Yushi Mowang snuck a pill into Yushi Moli’s robes, warming the older boy’s heart.","Although Little Mo was only four years old, he was very mature and had a close relationship with Yushi Moli. Most important of all was that he possessed prodigious talent. He was only four, but all of his meridians were open and he could cultivate as soon as he turned six.","Yushi Jianchou had given him this pill to nurture his foundations, but here Yushi Mowang was, giving it to his older brother instead.","“You keep this, Mowang! Big bro doesn’t have a use for this pill and it’s too sweet. Big bro doesn’t like sweet stuff, remember?” Yushi Moli tucked the pill back into his brother’s robes. It would actually be very beneficial for him too, but it was too expensive!","He naturally recognized it since he’d studied many ancient records. This was an Origin Doubling Pill and it cost ten thousand gold coins! It was one tenth of his father’s entire fortune!","Aurora City lacked an alchemist, so Yushi Jianchou must have paid too costly a price to obtain the pill. Yushi Moli would never take it.","“Huh?” Yushi Mowang rubbed his head with a small hand and smiled foolishly. He was easy to fool since he was only four years old.","“Eldest young master, milord requests your presence in the living room,” said the middle-aged man behind Yushi Mowang."]},{"number":2185,"title":"Chapter 2185: Chapter 2140: Sanguine Dusk Tavern","paragraphs":["Chapter 2140: Sanguine Dusk Tavern","Zong Yan was guard captain of the Aurora city lord residence and one of its three celestial rank cultivators. He was also Yushi Mowang’s future martial instructor. With his skills, he’d easily picked out Yushi Mowang giving the Origin Doubling Pill to Yushi Moli, but thankfully, the latter had returned it.","Otherwise, Zong Yan would’ve forcefully taken it back.","“Ah, Uncle Zong!” Yushi Moli realized who the man was and greeted Zong Yan.","“Go now, don’t keep milord waiting,” Zong Yan rushed the boy along with a frown. He didn’t like Yushi Moli.","Just as the maids had gossiped about, Yushi Moli was trash and a waste of resources in the city lord’s manor. One hundred gold coins worth of herbal baths and fare could support an incredible number of powerhouses anywhere else.","Zong Yan wasn’t at liberty to say anything, however, because Yushi Moli was the city lord’s son.","“Alright.” That didn’t leave Yushi Moli time to change his clothes. He headed for the main hall with Mowang still in his arms.","“Father!”","Yushi Jianchou sipped from a cup of tea in the main hall. He raised his head when he saw his two sons arrive.","“Sit!”","“Understood.” Yushi Moli put down his younger brother and sat on a nearby stool.","“Zong Yan, take Mowang with you,” Yushi Jianchou dismissed the guard captain.","“Understood.” Zong Yan walked away with Mowang.","Although Yushi Mowang was very reluctant to leave, he didn’t dare disobey his father.","“Moli, you are already thirteen years old,” Yushi Jianchou intoned when he turned around.","Yushi Moli’s heart quailed.","“I set out for trials and journeyed alone when I was your age,” he continued.","“Mm.” Yushi Moli pursed his lips; he knew what his father was about to do.","“We own a manor fifteen kilometers to the east of Aurora City. Go look after it for me,” Yushi Jianchou sighed.","“Thank you, father!” Yushi Moli stood up with reddened eyes and bowed to the man. Had this day finally come?","He walked out of the hall in a daze. Although he’d long anticipated that his father would want him to leave the city, he hadn’t thought this day would come so early. Subconsciously, Yushi Moli felt that he shouldn’t be this sad. He wasn’t from this world and neither was he the real Yushi Moli.","However, the sword shadow sealed away his original memories. He’d assimilated the memories of this body like he was a blank soul.","In this moment, he was Yushi Moli. He felt the same emotions as the boy would. They shared the same experiences; everything that was the two of them melded together perfectly.","Lu Yun’s sleeping memories stopped trying to force their way through the seal imposed by the sword. He would return to the nothing when he was strong enough and naturally awaken his true self then.","......","“Don’t you think you’re being too heartless?” Ouyang Du appeared in front of Yushi Jianchou with a frosty look in his eyes.","“How much more can Moli endure if I don’t do this?” The man’s expression remained unchanged.","“How much more? You mean his training? Do you begrudge him that little bit of resources? He is your son!” Ouyang Du’s face darkened.","“You would understand if you lived in the city lord’s residence,” Yushi Jianchou sighed.","“Do you mean... the idle chatter?” Ouyang Du blinked.","“Moli is just a child. He can ignore it for now, but it will ultimately affect his personality,” Yushi Jianchou said expressionlessly.","“Who would dare say anything if you gave the order?” Ouyang Du didn’t understand.","“Didn’t you see Zong Yan’s attitude toward him and how the servants look at him? I can expel everyone from the complex and even chase Zong Yan away, but it won’t change a thing.” Yushi Jianchou shook his head. “He is my son, after all.”","“Excuses!” Ouyang Du snorted and left the hall.","......","Yushi Moli left the city lord’s residence and Aurora City. He didn’t bring much with his departure—just an old servant and the Qingfeng Sword.","The old servant had served his mother and was now in charge of brewing his daily medicines. The Qingfeng Sword was the sword that he normally practiced with.","Apart from that, he didn’t take anything else. Not a single article of clothing.","Yushi Mowang didn’t know that his older brother was leaving, so only Ouyang Du came to send him off. His uncle shoved a package of herbs into his hands.","In everyone’s eyes, the trash young master that was Yushi Moli had been expelled from Aurora City because he didn’t find favor in his father’s eyes.","“Father’s doing this to protect me, so I won’t suffer from all the gossip and hateful comments!” Yushi Moli heaved a long breath after he left the complex he’d grown up in.","He’d lived a very stifling life in the city lord’s residence. Although it appeared that he didn’t care about the sidelong glances and muttered judgments, he’d found it very hard to bear the looks that the servants regarded him with. That was why he trained with crazed fervor, seeking to relieve the depression lurking in his heart.","He didn’t dare go out on the streets or even wander through the complex. Yushi Moli was deathly afraid of seeing more looks of contempt cast his way.","In his current condition, he was just a child. He’d long since lost Lu Yun’s memories and experiences. Yet, all the same, he understood that Yushi Jianchou sending him out was his father’s way of protecting him.","“I won’t let father down!” Yushi Moli looked back at Aurora City in the distance and balled his hands up into fists. A voice in his subconscious also told him that he couldn’t let down those waiting for him to return.","......","Fifteen kilometers to the east of Aurora City was a manor at the foot of Qingqiu Mountain. It was named Clearsnow Estate and occupied roughly fifty acres. Sitting at the foot of a mountain and next to running water, it enjoyed beautiful sights.","With the year being in early autumn, multicolored tree leaves drifted through the air and fish swam vigorously through the river’s clean waters. Yushi Moli immediately liked what he saw when he arrived at his new home.","Fifty acres made Clearsnow Estate a modest size. Roughly one hundred farmers operated the property and were overseen by a steward from the city lord’s residence.","The steward was called Xun You and treated Yushi Moli with all due respect, despite the young master having been reassigned to the estate. Granted, he took his orders from Yushi Jianchou, but he still would not have treated Yushi Moli with disdain. The boy was the city lord’s son, after all.","“You’re here, young master.” Xun You greeted the charming young man with a congenial smile. “Clearsnow Estate has prepared a welcoming banquet for you.”","“No need to go to all that trouble, Uncle Xun. Life should proceed as normal,” Yushi Moli responded with resignation. “I’m just another mouth at the table.”","......","Clearsnow Estate housed roughly one hundred families who ran various industries on property grounds. The estate was self-sufficient and sent its monthly surplus back to the city lord’s residence in Aurora City.","Most of the residence’s profits came from these kinds of properties. Clearsnow specialized in agriculture and regularly supplied the city lord with grains, fruits, and vegetables. Their monthly profit wasn’t much—a few dozen gold coins a month at best.","That wasn’t enough for even one month of medicine for Yushi Moli. Thus, Clearsnow Estate wasn’t a very important property to the city lord.","Ouyang Du had given his nephew three months worth of medicinal ingredients when the boy left, but Yushi Moli was on his own after that. He had to find a way to earn money himself as he needed the medicines for his training. Without them, his body would collapse and his progress would halt.","That night, he perused the books in the estate’s library instead of mentally observing the sword chart. Reading was one of his greatest hobbies.","Martial cultivators started training at six years old, but since he lacked a sense of qi at that age, Yushi Moli couldn’t. He could only increase his knowledge through perusing books and ancient records.","He’d read everything in the city lord’s residence by the time he turned nine. It wasn’t until he discovered the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth in the book that his mother had left him that he officially began training.","Most of the books in Clearsnow Estate’s library were new to him, so he decided to spend some of his meditation time tonight reading.","“Money, money! How am I supposed to get some?” he sighed as he flipped through “Memoirs of the Continent’s Experts”. “Ask uncle? No! Uncle’s helped me a lot these years. I need to rely on myself now since I’m here!”","Yushi Moli shook his head. “I still have one hope, and that’s to become a disciple of Grandmaster Yuqing Yang. I can be an alchemist! But... I wonder if I have the potential for becoming one.","“Oh? Is this a memoir of Senior Long Qianjue? Eh? He was a star assassin of the Sanguine Dusk Tavern before he made a name for himself?” Yushi Moli blinked.","“Sanguine Dusk Tavern? Assassin? I think there’s one in Aurora City!”"]},{"number":2186,"title":"Chapter 2186: Chapter 2141: Sword in Hand","paragraphs":["Chapter 2141: Sword in Hand","Long Qianjue was the late Yushi Moli’s hero. That didn’t change when Lu Yun inherited everything from the boy.","Yushi Moli had idolized the legendary swordsman ever since reading about Long Qianjue’s feats when he was eight. He often daydreamed about being a powerhouse like Long Qianjue—able to vault into the top ranks of the continent’s heavyweights through sword skills alone!","Four years of cultivation!","The young Yushi Moli had wanted to give up more than once, but the presence of his idol stoked his fighting spirit again and again. Sadly, his previous training methods had been wrong and overtaxed his body. Even the medicinal baths hadn’t been enough and he’d died from fatigue.","Another soul took up residence in his body, becoming the new Yushi Moli. The new version of him now read about Long Qianjue’s other feats in another book.","A gold medal assassin of the Sanguine Dusk Tavern!","“So the Sanguine Dusk Tavern is an assassin organization? Just like that, out in the open?” Yushi Moli blinked dazedly. He put his current book down and walked over to the bookshelves. “Ah, found it, this one.”","He pulled out “Winds of Change in the Continent” from the shelves. Not only did it detail the rise and fall of dynasties in the continent, but it also recorded the makeup of numerous factions.","He’d paged through it earlier, but hadn’t been very interested.","“Found it, Sanguine Dusk Tavern!” Yushi Moli lit up. “The Sanguine Dusk Tavern is one of the seven unfading factions of the continent. It reigns over the empire!”","Shock bloomed in his eyes. In his understanding, Qiulan Empire was the strongest, most mysterious, and loftiest entity out there. His father, Yushi Jianchou, was the strongest of Aurora City and a peak celestial rank expert. But even he had to bow and scrape before the empire.","To Yushi Moli, celestial rank cultivators were the strongest existence there was. There were too many to be counted in the empire, but Sanguine Dusk Tavern outstripped it!","How strong must it be!","Yushi Moli’s hands shook as he continued to read about the tavern. Though its status as being one of the seven unfading factions on the continent made it incredible beyond belief in the eyes of ordinary people, it was nothing special to veteran cultivators. Neither was its existence some sort of secret.","“Sanguine Dusk Tavern is the foremost assassin organization on the continent! Its assassins are divided into bronze, silver, gold, and aureate assassins. Its origins are unknown and it has sent out only six aureate assassins throughout the course of its history. Whenever they did so, an emperor fell!","“Someone as strong as Senior Long Qianjue was only a gold medal assassin, so how strong does that make their aureate ones?” Yushi Moli grew excited the more he read. “If the senior can do it, so can I!","“Senior Long Qianjue was a qi absentia constitution, but I’m not! I cultivate the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth and observe the sword of heaven and earth. I’ll do better than the senior!”","A fire ignited in Yushi Moli’s chest after he learned about these movers and shakers of the continent. More importantly was that he somehow felt he would surely grow stronger, and that something unexpected would happen after he broke through celestial rank.","......","The days passed, one by one, in simple monotony. Yushi Moli ate, slept, practiced, tempered his body, and studied. He occasionally took a walk around Clearsnow Estate or the nearby paths of Qingqiu Mountain.","A month passed by in the blink of an eye.","Though he’d left his childhood home, life was very enjoyable for him. His heart and mind cleared up once he was removed from the idle gossip and unwarranted eye rolls of the city lord’s residence.","His mind was strong to begin with and many things came easily to him, like they were his natural instincts. Training with his sword was easier than before. Most important of all was that the shadow in his mind continued to grow clearer.","He stopped his daily practice of one thousand pierces—it was superfluous in his current state and completely ineffective for his cultivation.","What he did everyday was practice the basic sword techniques with his weapon. They were the only sword methods that he knew.","Mornings were spent with the sword. Afternoons for tempering the body. Evenings were reserved for reading and meditation.","He slept very little as the observation method recorded in the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth was more effective than sleeping. All an exhausted Yushi Moli needed to do was to meditate for a few hours to be revitalized again.","In the middle of autumn.","The forests of Qingqiu Mountain.","Yushi Moli practiced the basic sword methods again and again. They were flawless and seemed like they were a natural part of him when he deployed them.","Yet, he was still dissatisfied—sword in hand was a basic maneuver. He repeated the techniques time and time again.","The grass and trees had yellowed in the mountain’s forests and the autumn wind fluttered gently past them. Leaves drifted from the balding trees; Yushi Moli’s mood was suddenly affected by the atmosphere of this part of the land. He seemed to sense the aura of the seasons—the desolate bleakness of autumn.","An ambience of all life quieting, all creation declining wove through his heart. The sword in his hand began to slow down and a tenor of something different seemed to outline them. His sword shifted from fast, to slow, and fast again until it smoothed out into a gentle transition.","It was as if the sword was the autumn wind drifting through the mountain, carrying a hint of desolation and bleakness. The sword and aura of autumn seemed to blend together.","Whoosh!","Yushi Moli’s sword trembled and an intangible gust of qi burst forth.","Crack!","Five meters in front of him, a branch the width of a thigh broke upon impact, jarring Yushi Moli out of his peculiar mental state.","“That was... what was that?” He stared dumbly at the weapon in his hand. “The mid stage of sword in hand?” He breathed out incredulously.","He’d been initial stage of sword in hand before, but now he’d suddenly set foot into mid stage. That stroke had been the power commanded by an upper human rank cultivator! Incredible!","One had to know that since he lacked true qi, his body was weaker than even a lower human rank cultivator, but his sword could deploy the might of upper human rank!","“That was...” Yushi Moli frowned slightly at the Qingfeng Sword, musing over the feeling he’d just felt.","He suddenly slashed forward, delivering a move that was like the autumn wind. Bleak! Desolate!","Whoosh!","Intangible sword qi burst forth again and another small tree in front of him was severed!","This time, his breathing was rapid—a testament to how draining the move was.","“Since this move comes from the autumn wind... Let’s call it Autumn Wind!” Joy shone out of his face. He’d finally gained something after four years of cultivation!","But at the same time, he also felt that his sudden accomplishment seemed to have nothing to do with his past training.","“I must succeed, I will become a peak swordsman like Senior Long Qianjue! Father, I won’t let you down! I won’t... let any of you down,” he promised heroically, not realizing who he meant by “any of you”."]},{"number":2187,"title":"Chapter 2187: Chapter 2142: Alchemy","paragraphs":["Chapter 2142: Alchemy","“Uncle! What are you doing here?” Yushi Moli was surprised to see Ouyang Du at Clearsnow Estate when he returned to the property.","“What, not happy to see me?” A fond look appeared in Ouyang Du’s eyes when he saw the boy.","“No no, not at all.” Yushi Moli hastily shook his head. “It’s cold out, uncle, come inside!”","“Okay, I’ll stop teasing you. I won’t be going in,” Ouyang du chuckled. “I came to tell you that Grandmaster Yuqing Yang is visiting.”","“Huh?” Yushi Moli blinked.","“Your uncle commands just enough face to gain an audience with the grandmaster for you. But it’s up to you to take advantage of the opportunity,” Ouyang Du said solemnly.","“I have a chance to meet the grandmaster?” Yushi Moli lit up.","“Yes!” Ouyang Du smiled. “Give it a try. Even if you don’t have the potential to be an alchemist, leaving a good impression might help you get an Origin Elevation Pill.”","“Okay!” Yushi Moli agreed decisively.","“Alright, we’re heading back to Aurora City! Do you know how to ride a horse, kid?” Ouyang Du roared with laughter.","“Of course I do!”","......","Two fine white horses darted out of Clearsnow Estate and galloped for Aurora City fifteen kilometers away. Their hooves sped over the land and sturdy city walls came into view fifteen minutes later.","It was Yushi Moli’s first visit since leaving a month ago, but it felt like he’d been gone an entire lifetime.","Compared to the hustle and bustle of a city, he far preferred the serene tranquility of Clearsnow Estate. It seemed to suit his mentality more.","“Grandmaster Yuqing Yang is staying at the Nineheavens Inn. We’re going that way!”","“Okay!”","Ouyang Du took Yushi Moli to the largest inn after they entered the city. There were plenty of people crowded around it. News of a celestial rank alchemist’s arrival had spread like wildfire and many wished to catch a glimpse of Yuqing Yang. They either wanted to beg a pill off him or ask to become his disciple.","But Yuqing Yang was so illustrious that he wasn’t easily accessible in the prefecture’s capital, much less a mere Aurora City. These people were just here to try their luck.","“So many people!” A taken-aback Yushi Moli clucked his tongue when they arrived at the inn.","Nineheavens Inn was the largest inn in Aurora City and the most expensive. It would never entertain so many guests during regular times.","“Ignore them, we’re going upstairs.” Ouyang Du headed upstairs with his nephew.","“Halt!” someone called out to them. “Who are you, don’t you know that Grandmaster Yuqing Yang is staying on the second floor? You will disturb the notable grandmaster if you go upstairs. Can you afford the consequences of doing so??” A middle-aged man wearing green robes made them stop.","“We’re going to see the grandmaster,” Yushi Moli responded.","“Hahaha! What a joke!” snorted the man. “Who is the grandmaster, huh? He’s not for two buffoons to see whenever they wish!”","Since the man wasn’t from Aurora City, he naturally didn’t recognize Yushi Moli or Ouyang Du.","“That’s right, the two of you can stay down here with us and wait for Yuqing Yang to summon you! But I don’t think the likes of you will ever see him,” someone else sniffed.","Ouyang Du looked less than thirty years old and Yushi Moli was only thirteen. Dressed as commonplace as they were, no one thought much of the two.","“It’s not up to you if the grandmaster sees us or not,” Ouyang Du dismissed and moved to go upstairs with his nephew.","“What’s with the ruckus here? I already told all of you that my master will not be receiving visitors today. Please make your way elsewhere, everyone,” hectored a tall and slender young man at the top of the stairs.","“Sir, it’s not us who are raising a fuss, but these two muddleheaded fools. They’re trying to force their way to the second floor, but we stopped them,” the man in green robes hastily explained.","“Oh?” The young man looked at Ouyang Du.","“Please notify the grandmaster that Ouyang Du of Aurora City and Yushi Moli, son of the city lord, is here to pay our respects,” Ouyang Du responded amiably.","“You’re Ouyang Du?” the young man blinked.","“I am,” he nodded.","“My master has said that Sir Ouyang Du can proceed straight in if he visits.” A slight smile floated onto the young man’s face.","“My thanks!” Ouyang Du raised cupped fists at the young man and walked upstairs with Yushi Moli, stunning those on the first floor.","The middle-aged man’s cheeks burned with mortification. So these were guests that the grandmaster had identified by name! He’d thought himself clever when he stopped them!","“So it’s them!” A short and stout man looked on with understanding.","“Who are they?” someone else asked curiously.","“The city lord’s brother-in-law and his trash of a son who can’t disciple,” the stout man sneered. “The city lord’s brother-in-law is from the Ouyang family in the capital. They are one of the greatest families in the empire, but something happened four years ago and Ouyang Du had to seek shelter in Aurora City.","“It would seem that he has some connections and perhaps left a previous impression on the grandmaster. That’s why they were able to arrange a meeting. Being granted an audience with the grandmaster is all a disgraced Ouyang down on his luck can manage.","“As for Yushi Moli... he’s just trash that can’t cultivate. The city lord threw him out of the city a month ago, so I think that needs no clarification,” the stout man chortled.","“So it’s them!” jeered the man in green robes. “I bet Ouyang Du is trying to beg for an Origin Elevation Pill for Yushi Moli. Trash is still trash, even with the pill.”","“But the pill is worth one million gold coins. The Ouyangs might have been able to afford it in the past, but the current Ouyang Du absolutely doesn’t have that much money to his name!” A general air of schadenfreude permeated the atmosphere.","“What a pity that they’re the ones who can meet the grandmaster. If it was me, I might soar to the heavens with this single step.”","......","Yuqing Yang had reserved the entire second floor at ten times the usual rate. All he wanted was peace and quiet.","Yushi Moli was surprised when he finally saw the elder. Yuqing Yang’s aura projected comfort and set people at ease.","“You are Yushi Moli?” Yuqing Yang wore loose white robes and his hair and beard were white. However, his face was flushed with good health. As a result, he didn’t seem that old.","“Yushi Moli greets the grandmaster!” Yushi Moli promptly swept a circumspect bow.","“No need to stand on ceremony as you are Ouyang’s nephew.” Yuqing Yang smiled involuntarily as he studied Yushi Moli’s features.","“We meet again, grandmaster,” Ouyang Du grinned.","“You’re still the same after so many years, kid!” Yuqing Yang chuckled.","“Indeed I am. I have a request to make today, sir,” Ouyang Du cut straight to the chase. “Will you take a look at this child’s potential? If he passes muster, will you take him for a disciple?”","HIs words made a frown cross the forehead of the slender young man next to Yuqing Yang.","“Place your hand on the crystal ball.” Yuqing Yang nodded and manifested a crystal ball the size of a head with the flip of his hand. “Let’s see if you possess the potential to become an alchemist.”"]},{"number":2188,"title":"Chapter 2188: Chapter 2143: Won’t Give Up","paragraphs":["Chapter 2143: Won’t Give Up","Yushi Moli’s inner state was completely calm; not a single ripple marred it. He remained entirely steady, but a tiny bit of agitation bubbled in the depths of his heart.","An alchemist?","That didn’t seem that hard. What he wanted to be was a pill master—that was a profession even stronger than alchemist!","Yushi Moli felt that he could create a pill that was superior to the Origin Elevation Pill. In fact, he felt that he could do a lot of things, but he couldn’t remember what he could do. His mind was blank.","He gently rested his hand on the translucent crystal ball.","“Focus all of your concentration on the crystal ball.” Yuqing Yang smiled when he looked at the boy. “You don’t seem nervous at all.”","“Mmhmm.” Yushi Moli nodded and sent his vast soul force out as mental power. But perhaps due to certain internal caution, he instinctively withdrew most of it before it reached the crystal ball. In the end, less than a hundredth of his soul force transformed into mental power.","Even the boy himself didn’t know how he managed the feat.","Humm!","Dazzling white light erupted from the crystal ball.","“This is... incredibly strong mental power! It’s stronger than even some earth rank alchemists!” Yuqing Yang jumped with shock. “How is his mind so strong??”","Ouyang Du’s eyes widened. “Grandmaster, do you mean that Moli has the requisite potential to become an alchemist?”","Yushi Moli was also enormously excited.","“The requisite potential to become an alchemist? Of course!! Who does if he doesn’t?” Yuqing Yang grew more agitated the more he looked at the crystal ball. Power and mental strength that’d already reached the earth rank? The boy was a natural-born alchemist!","“Mmhmm.” Yushi Moli nodded, as if this had been within his expectations.","“But...” the elder frowned. “As strong and pure as his mental strength is, the edge in his mind is too sharp.”","“What does that mean?” Ouyang Du blinked.","“Child, you practice sword dao, don’t you? And you have achieved moderate proficiency with it.” Yuqing Yang looked at Yushi Moli.","The young man started, then nodded. “Yes, I practice the sword everyday.”","“Ai, what a pity!” Yuqing Yang shook his head. “Mental strength is most important for an alchemist, but yours is filled with the keenness of a sword. If this kind of mental strength is used to refine pills and medicines, their effects would be sliced through before they could form!”","“What?” Ouyang Du gaped.","Yushi Moli furrowed his brow, feeling that the elder was somehow wrong. He remained silent, however, because he didn’t know how to refute those words.","“Therefore, you must give up sword dao if you’d like to become an alchemist. You must tend to your mind at all times starting from now and blunt the edge of sword dao in your thoughts. You can never hold a sword in your hands again.” Yuqing Yan looked at Yushi Moli with a deep gaze. “Are you willing to give up sword dao? If you are, I will take you as my disciple.”","Ouyang Du blinked. He knew how devoted Yushi Moli was to the sword and that his idol was Long Qianjue. But the chance to become a noteworthy alchemist was right in front of him!","Alchemists enjoyed higher status than martial cultivators!","“Hurry and say yes, Moli!” Ouyang Du urged. In his eyes, Yushi Moli’s cultivation methods were incorrect. Doggedly tempering the body and practicing the sword were not the correct ways. How strong could one become without cultivating true qi and focusing only on the body?","Lower human rank, at most! He’d be less than human rank cultivators who possessed true qi. But a human rank alchemist was more noble than earth rank cultivators!","Ouyang Du had left his nephew to his own devices all this time because he didn’t wish to shatter the boy’s cherished dreams and hope..","“I...” Yushi Moli’s brows creased.","Should I say yes to Yuqing Yang and give up sword dao? Or do I turn him down and insist on following my path?","“Can I... choose both?” he asked after momentary thought.","“...that would be my wish as well, but the edge of your sword dao is so keen that it affects your mind. Pursuing it will prevent you from being an alchemist. If you wish to become an alchemist, you must give up sword dao.” Yuqing Yang’s words brooked no questioning.","Yushi Moli fell silent once more. The subconsciousness in his mind also quieted down, leaving this decision to the memories and experiences of the original Yushi Moli.","It was a difficult decision.","One would catapult him to the heavens and place him over everyone. He would bask in the admiration of all and win glory for his father. The other was a bottomless abyss, a path that he himself wasn’t certain was viable. What was certain was that it would be a road filled with contempt and derision.","Scenes from his past flashed in front of his eyes.","The shock and awe he’d felt when he first read about Senior Long Qianjue in a book.","The delight he’d felt when he discovered the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth in a book that his mother had left him.","His sweat and tears through four years of one thousand pierces a day.","The monotonous and dull internal observation every night for the past four years.","And the stroke of Autumn Wind he’d somehow created at the foot of Qingqiu Mountain this morning.","“No, I can’t give up sword dao!” Resolution flashed through his eyes. “This is my dao, the path I will take in the future! No matter how arduous and dangerous it is, it is still my decision!”","Yushi Moli knew that the reason for his prodigious mental strength was because of his nightly meditations. Forsaking sword dao and giving up internal observation would dissipate his mental strength!","Most importantly was that he needed to cultivate sword dao. Only sword dao could control the sword shadow and release what it suppressed.","The memories that he’d forgotten.","“My deepest apologies, Grandmaster Yang. I cannot give up sword dao,” Yushi Moli said softly.","Ouyang Du paused, dazed. The thin young man next to Yuqing Yang also stared. A thirteen year old boy had turned down Yuqing Yang! He’d turned down a celestial rank alchemist!","Yuqing Yang remained merry, as if this decision was within his expectations.","“You have not let yourself down,” he smiled easily. “Ouyang says you have no sense of qi and thus cannot cultivate true qi?”","He leisurely changed the topic.","“Yes, so I came to ask about the Qi Elevation Pill.” Yushi Moli was as noncommittal as ever.","“Do you know how much it costs?” Yuqing Yang remained as genial as before.","“One million gold coins!” Yushi Moli paused, somehow feeling that one million gold coins weren’t that much.","“Yes, one million gold coins. I will refine one for you for free if you are willing to forsake sword dao and become my disciple,” Yuqing Yang coaxed. “Even without sword dao, you’ll be able to train in martial dao after you gain a sense of qi.”","“I... um... thank the grandmaster for your generosity...” Yushi Moli smiled, more unwavering than the grandmaster anticipated he would be. The boy was thinking that he could become an alchemist without taking Yuqing Yang as his master.","“Hahahaha!” Yuqing Yang threw his head back with laughter. “I will remain in Aurora City for three years. If you can collect five hundred thousand gold coins within three years, I will sell you one of the pills for that price.”","Five hundred thousand gold coins in three years!","Yushi Moli brightened, then regained his composure.","Three years?","He felt that he wouldn’t need three years to master how to refine the pill. He would even create a pill stronger than it!","“Yushi Moli, you walk the path of sword dao and give up the chance to become an alchemist for it. This demonstrates how adamant you are,” Yuqing Yan seemed to have a good impression of the boy. “Stick to your resolve and five hundred thousand will not be hard.”","“Thank you for your compliments, grandmaster,” Yushi Moli took a deep breath.","“I have a little bauble for you as a greeting gift.” Yuqing Yang tossed out a porcelain bottle. “There are ten Boneforge Pills inside. Taking one a day will benefit your cultivation.","“These are a welcome gift and you may purchase more from me for one thousand gold coins per pill.”","Ouyang Du shuddered when he heard the pill’s name."]},{"number":2189,"title":"Chapter 2189: Chapter 2144: Favor","paragraphs":["Chapter 2144: Favor","Yushi Moli didn’t notice his uncle’s expression. He was fixated on the bottle of pills in his hand and the pills that were worth one thousand gold coins each!","These are really expensive too!","Yushi Moli swept a surreptitious gaze around the room, instinctively thinking that these Boneforge Pills were worth far more than one thousand gold coins. He looked at Yuqing Yang with surprise—this old man isn’t not half bad!","“Of course, you can have as many as you wish whenever you think things through and are willing to learn from me,” Yuqing Yang chuckled.","“My deepest thanks to the grandmaster, I will definitely think it over,” Yushi Moli responded politely. His conviction, however, grew stronger.","“Alright then, we will not disturb the grandmaster further. Sir, we take our leave,” Ouyang Du said.","“Go on,” Yuqing Yang waved them off.","When the visitors left, the grandmaster’s disciple couldn’t help but protest, “Teacher, although Ouyang Du comes from the Ouyang Clan, that family is a far cry from their former heights. Surely the favor he once did isn’t worth that much? The Boneforge Pill is an upper human rank pill. One of them goes for ten thousand gold coins!”","Ten thousand gold coins!","The true price of the Boneforge Pill was ten thousand gold coins, not one thousand!","Yuqing Yang had just casually handed out pills worth one hundred thousand gold coins! It was the equivalent of the Aurora city lord’s entire personal wealth!","“Although I have some relationship with the Ouyangs, that bit of relationship is indeed not worth this much.” Yuqing Yang shook his head and picked up the crystal ball that was used to test Yushi Moli.","Craaaack!","Deep fissures snaked through the crystal ball. Having tested an unknown number of candidates for alchemist potential, the crystal ball fell to the ground in pieces.","“Do you understand now?” Yuqing Yang looked at the tall and skinny young man.","“Such incredible mental strength, he’s going to be much more than an earth rank alchemist!” the disciple sucked in a sharp breath.","“We can take it slow. He’ll make the correct decision once he realizes he’s on the wrong path. What I need to focus on is helping him come to that realization faster. I will have this genius disciple!” A smile bloomed across Yuqing Yang’s face. The child was young, but his mentality was remarkably mature. He’d even kept part of his abilities back!","“Then why didn’t teacher speak of this openly? Why go to all of this effort in such a roundabout way?” The young man didn’t understand.","“While the boy is young, the look in his eyes is very determined. His personality also leans extreme. Ten oxen will not pull him back if he doesn’t realize his own mistakes,” Yuqing Yang chuckled. “He is very much like you in this regard, Guan Chong. You were a martial dao genius, but now you follow by my side and learn from me.”","......","“Uncle...” An unexpected look appeared in the bottom of Yushi Moli’s eyes. Rather than excitement, it was more like he owed someone a favor. “This Bone...”","“Don’t say anything. Wait until we’re outside!” Ouyang Du swept a look around the first floor and stopped his nephew from speaking further. He pulled the boy outside.","He knew the real value of a Boneforge Pill. Ten of them were worth one hundred thousand gold coins! Such massive wealth would invite fatal attention.","“Oh? Those two?” Someone on the first floor of the inn had fully taken their demeanors in. “The boy seems steady and dependable, he’s not someone to wear his heart on a sleeve. But he looks like he owes someone a favor, so he must’ve gotten something from the grandmaster!","“Bone...? Can it be a Boneforge Pill?? The pill worth ten thousand gold coins??” The middle-aged man dressed in green brightened and surreptitiously followed after the duo.","“Moli! The human heart can be malicious. You need to learn to hide yourself and not display everything on your face, got it?” Ouyang Du said solemnly when they left the inn.","“Goooooot it, uncle!” Yushi Moli drawled, his expression showing that he didn’t care.","He really didn’t, he at most felt that he owed the elder a favor. He’d thought that his uncle didn’t know, but it seemed that he did know the pill’s true value.","“Uncle, what good is this thing?” Yushi Moli asked with bafflement. It should be a wondrous pill, but he’d seen a look of true fear cross his uncle’s face. Regardless of what the pill’s actual price was, just the grandmaster’s words placed it at ten times Yushi Moli’s usual monthly expenditure.","One hundred gold coins worth of herbal baths and food was one entire month’s supplies. But here, one thousand gold coins was just for a single pill!","“It’s used to hone and temper your body,” Ouyang Due whispered. “One pill is the equivalent of one year of your training.”","“One year?” Yushi Moli blinked. This was turning into a massive favor that he’d been granted!","“Your usual way of tempering the body is incorrect. Although it strengthens you, it will not help you reach the level of a martial cultivator. What you have in your hand is what cultivators use to forge their bodies.” His uncle didn’t call the pill by its name.","“This... will help me become a cultivator?” Yushi Moli brightened.","“Just in terms of physical prowess,” Ouyang Du smiled.","There was one more thing he didn’t speak of—Boneforge Pills were meant for martial cultivators. They needed to be refined with true qi before they could be fully absorbed. For an ordinary person like Yushi Moli, he would struggle to absorb even one hundredth of its properties.","These ten pills were worth one hundred thousand gold coins, but they would be wasted by his nephew.","However, Ouyang Du could tell what the grandmaster was planning, so he didn’t say anything. Yuqing Yang was unwilling to give up on such a disciple. That was why he’d gifted this caliber of the pill.","“Alright, let’s go eat and I’ll take you back later,” Ouyang Du changed the topic.","“Okay,” Yushi Moli sighed as he caressed the pills in his arms. Even he didn’t know why he was so unmoved by them. If it was before, he’d already be jumping for joy. He would be very satisfied if his physical body could reach the level of a martial cultivator.","The two led their horses to a moderately sized tavern and ordered a few dishes.","“I’ve finally found you, boss!” A man in a combat uniform rushed into the tavern halfway through the meal. He whispered a few words into Ouyang Du’s ears, causing the man’s face to darken.","“Bastard!” he spat and took a deep breath. “Moli, go back to the city lord’s residence after you finish your meal. Remember, don’t go back to the estate alone! I need to take care of something first.”","“I understand, uncle. Go on,” Yushi Moli nodded. He wouldn’t add to his uncle’s plate of troubles.","Ouyang Du left with his man after he paid for lunch.","“Those damned Black Winds robbers! How dare they covet even my goods!” Ouyang Du snapped.","“I wonder what’s happened? It’s my first time seeing that kind of expression on uncle’s face.” Yushi Moli frowned as he watched Ouyang Du leave. “I’m going to finish eating, buy some presents for Little Ying and the others, then go back to the estate.”","Go to the city lord’s residence? He... didn’t really want to. Although part of the reason why he trained so hard was because of his father, he seemed to have subconsciously rejected his father at some point in time.","It was like his father wasn’t his father.","Thus, he shopped through the city after he finished eating. After buying some baubles and snacks, he rode out of Aurora City alone.","“He’s alone? Perfect! The pill that’s worth ten thousand gold coins is mine!” The man in green robes rubbed his hands together."]},{"number":2190,"title":"Chapter 2190: Chapter 2145: Oh Dear, I’ve Killed Someone","paragraphs":["Chapter 2145: Oh Dear, I’ve Killed Someone","“The Boneforge Pill can temper my body and grant me the physical prowess of a martial cultivator...” Yushi Moli was in fine fettle on his way home. “Long Qianjue must have taken similar pills like this back in his day!”","The boy’s lips turned upward and he smiled easily. His uncle had said that the pill was the equivalent of a year’s hard work. Then the pills in his hand were ten years’ worth!","As mature and steady as he might be, he couldn’t help but grow excited at the implications. He’d always craved to rapidly grow and develop his strength so he could complete something he was very anxious about. It was a goal he highly desired to achieve, so he inwardly thanked Yuqing Yang for the favor.","“But there’s only ten of the pills. I’ll have to buy them for one thousand gold coins each after ten days. One thousand gold coins...” Yushi Moli sent his horse into a moderate trot as he rapidly considered various plans. “And five hundred thousand more in three years!”","His sights were also set on the Origin Elevation Pill.","“I’m a poor soul right now, so I’ve got to figure out a way to make money... My options are to either hunt monsters in Qingqiu Mountain or become an assassin at the Sanguine Dusk Tavern.","“Well, I can forget about becoming an assassin. It’s not like they’ll accept me with my level of strength. Therefore, my only way to earn money is to kill low ranked monsters in the mountain!","“My Qingfeng Sword can deploy the might of upper human rank. I shouldn’t have a problem killing human rank monsters.” Yushi Moli thus decided on his next course of action.","For some reason, thinking of Qingqiu Mountain nearly made his heart burst with yearning. But since his memories were sealed away, he couldn’t remember who it was he missed.","Two faint figures steadily revolved around his heart.","“Ten days! I’m going to use these pills over the next ten days to temper my body and grow stronger! After that, I’ll head into the depths of the mountain to hunt beasts! That’s what I’m going to do!”","Yushi Moli beamed with excitement. “I’ll hunt monsters for a while and also temper myself, raising my strength. Then I’ll go apply for missions at the Sanguine Dusk Tavern and become an assassin! Low ranked monsters aren’t worth much—a couple dozen or hundred gold coins at best. If I want to earn five hundred thousand in three years, taking on missions is the fastest way!”","He’d read everything he could about the assassin organization, learning that the bounties posted for their missions were enormously high. They were a few hundred gold coins at the least, with some reaching a million!","“I need to get back to Clearsnow Estate as soon as possible. I need to train and see how well these pills work for me! Giddy up!” Yushi Moli cracked his whip out of excitement, sending the horse beneath him into a gallop of lighter gait.","He quickly left the city’s vicinity and neared Qingqiu Mountain. The trees began to forest the side of the road more thickly.","“Oh?” The boy abruptly yanked on the reins with a smirk. Someone’s trying to ambush me? “Woahhhhh.”","The white horse kicked up its front hooves and came to a standstill.","“What’s that??” He saw a rope tied parallel to the ground. A tripwire? Well read in assorted subjects, Yushi Moli quickly recognized what he saw.","Whoosh!","He narrowed his eyes as an impulse of violence rose from his heart. If it wasn’t for the twinge of a sudden internal warning, he would’ve fallen into the trap without question. His horse had been traveling at high speed and once it threw him after tripping, he’d break at least a few ribs in the fall.","“Why is there a horse trap here?” Yushi Moli jumped down from his steed, immediately grasping what was at hand. “Hmph! I spend my days in quiet cultivation and never provoke trouble. To think I’d attract this kind of attention today because of a few pills!”","He sneered inwardly to himself, knowing that one did not reveal the silver in one’s pocket when traveling. It was just that he hadn’t thought much of this level of wealth in the first place; his only thoughts were that he owed the grandmaster a favor.","“Oh? So you were lucky enough to discover the trap?” came a voice from the trees by the side of the road. A middle-aged man in green robes and a ruthless expression on his face walked out.","“It’s you!” Yushi Moli was surprised, but the reveal made sense. He tightened his grip on his sword, recognizing the man. This was the first person to stop him and his uncle at the Nineheavens Inn.","Here he was again—did he mean to kill Yushi Moli for his goods? His outfit didn’t indicate that he lacked money, but his character...","“Hahaha! You’re a lucky kid to get a Boneforge Pill from Grandmaster Yuqing Yang! It’s worth ten thousand gold coins! Hand it over and I’ll leave you an intact corpse!” The man—Luo Qing—threw his head back with laughter.","“You’ll still want to kill me after taking my pill?” Yushi Moli responded with flippant amusement, like he was watching a clown. Being threatened by death seemed like such a familiar, yet removed sensation. He viewed it almost with... nostalgia.","Yushi Moli shook his head, halting his strange thoughts.","“You’re the son of the Aurora city lord. If I rob you, but don’t kill you, that would just be letting you go tattle to your father. Do I look like I want the city lord to come for me? I, Luo Qing, am not fool enough to think I can withstand the fury of a celestial rank powerhouse!” Luo Qing leered. “Killing and looting! How can I loot if I don’t kill?”","He darted forward and grabbed Yushi Moli by the neck; he couldn’t be bothered to waste more time in idle talk. “Die!”","Luo Qing was a mid human rank cultivator. Yushi Moli was an ordinary child who couldn’t cultivate, so he didn’t think much of the boy. His strength was sufficient to crush an ordinary boy’s neck!","Whoosh!","Sword light appeared in front of Luo Qing. Yushi Moli had unsheathed his sword and brought it down on his attacker’s right hand.","“Hmph, of course. Trash that can’t cultivate wields the most ordinary qingfeng Sword. You dare attack me? You can die now!” Luo Qing sneered. In his eyes, this was just the dying struggles of a child.","“AHHHHH!” he screamed in the next second. His right hand had been cut clean through with that stroke!","A horrifying killing intent approached him before he had a chance to react. At the same time, a bleak and desolate air rose in his heart. Was that the autumn wind blowing over him? Why did the gust of wind come with such an awe-inspiring, cutting edge?","“Upper... human rank!” Luo Qing abruptly realized. This wasn’t wind, but Yushi Moli’s sword qi! It was the equivalent of an upper human rank cultivator!","Pfft!","Intangible sword qi cut through his throat. Luo Qing gurgled and bubbled out sounds, his wide eyes full of incredulity. He couldn’t get any words out before he toppled over, dead, on the ground.","Yushi Moli stood with his head cocked to the side, sizing up his dirty sword. A faint smile curved his lips.","“Oh dear, I’ve killed someone!” he shrieked performatively. He didn’t feel anything, much less the disgust the books said he should feel. It was... an interesting feeling, like he’d opened the door to a new world. Like it wasn’t wrong to kill.","Without a doubt, Luo Qing had been a martial cultivator and Yushi Moli an ordinary person. He’d executed a cultivator? Although it made perfect sense, he couldn’t help but ponder—am I really this strong? It looks like my previous training was good for something after all!","“I got lucky just now!” Yushi Moli murmured as he looked at the dead man. “A cultivator like him has plenty of fighting experience. I was able to catch him off guard because he didn’t think anything of me.","“If he’d known of my strength beforehand and my trump card, I would be the one dead!” Though Yushi Moli came to a rational conclusion, he found the explanation a bit odd.","It was almost as if... he would’ve still easily killed Luo Qing had the man been combat ready and brought his full strength to bear.","“When did he start following me? Oh... he left the inn when we left too. He probably noticed my expression then. I only said the word ‘bone’ at the inn, but that was enough for him to guess it was the Boneforge Pill. He set up an ambush and waited for me here after that.","“This is what uncle means by the human heart can be malicious. I need to learn to conceal my thoughts!” He reflected over the lessons taught by his first ambush. “Would I never understand this if I hadn’t undergone this experience? But why do I feel like I’ve gone through this plenty of times? What’s happening to me?”","Confusion swirled in Yushi Moli’s mind, but he couldn’t think things through.","Forget it, he wouldn’t bother trying to get to the bottom of it then."]},{"number":2191,"title":"Chapter 2191: Chapter 2146: Boneforge","paragraphs":["Chapter 2146: Boneforge","Yushi Moli decided not to think further about these matters after spending some time in a daze. His lips curved upward when he looked at Luo Qing’s body on the ground.","“Killing and looting?” he chuckled. “I know how to do that too.”","Luo Qing had failed to kill him and was killed in return. Didn’t that make Luo Qing’s possessions his spoils of battle? Just look at his clothes, he must come from money!","Yushi Moli walked up to his would-be robber and felt up the corpse that was still pliable.","“There really is something here...” He found a cloth bag on the man. It held a couple hard objects that seemed to be a book and a few gold coins. “Lower human rank body method—Galewind Step?”","Yushi Moli raised an eyebrow when he took the book out of the bag. Other than a cultivator’s own training in determining their strength, the methods, techniques, and weapons they wielded were equally important.","Take Yushi Moli, for instance. He only knew one martial technique—basic sword techniques. Since cultivation methods were useless to him, he couldn’t practice them at all. Regardless, the procurement of a lower human rank body method brought a smile to the boy’s face.","“I’ll hunt through Qingqiu Mountain with greater confidence if I can master this method...” Yushi Moli smiled in great spirits. “Let’s see what else he’s got... Hmm, five gold notes valid for one hundred gold coins each and a dozen gold coins as well. Not bad, martial cultivators are definitely rich!”","Five hundred gold coins was no small sum for Yushi Moli—they were half of a Boneforge Pill!","Other than his monthly medicinal supplements, his allowance at the city lord’s residence had only been one or two silver coins a month. One gold coin was worth one hundred silver coins in this world.","Luo Qing carried nothing else on him, so Yushi Moli carefully tucked the gold notes away. They were issued by the ten biggest trading companies on the continent and could be exchanged at any of their branches.","The gold notes were made of special material that were impervious to fire and water. They were difficult to destroy and printed with anti-counterfeit symbols jointly created by the trading companies.","Yushi Moli ignored Luo Qing’s corpse, instead choosing to undo the tripwire. He didn’t want it to hurt someone else. Hmm... I feel like people called me a saint before? So doing all this is what I should be doing?","But... Yushi Moli scratched his head. What have I ever done? This is the first good deed I’ve ever done in my life! Well, I killed a bad guy who wanted to rob and kill me, so father would praise me if he found out, but he won’t call me a saint...?","He hopped back onto his horse and headed for Clearsnow Estate.","“Little Ying, Little Hua!” He called out when he reached a village close to the estate.","“Big brother Moli is here!”","“C’mon, big brother is here!” A group of kids ran out from the village.","“I just got back from the city and have presents for everyone!” Yushi Moli handed out candies, cakes, and trinkets that he’d picked up in Aurora City. He was very popular in the village and it put him in a good mood to see smiles on the children’s faces.","It always felt like he gazed at a certain kind of hope when he looked at these children—as if a tiny dot of illumination had flitted into view in a bottomless abyss. It represented hope and light.","Yushi Moli liked spending time with these kids. In the city lord’s residence, his younger brother was kept under heavy guard and there was usually no trace of his father to be found. Other than his uncle Ouyang Du, he didn’t have a single person to talk to.","Meanwhile, there were a few small villages close to Clearsnow Estate; many boys and girls his age lived in them. Whenever he tired of cultivating, he came here to play with the children and while away the hours.","After he passed out his souvenirs, Yushi Moli leisurely led his horse through the village and greeted everyone he saw. Though the village residents knew that the boy lived at Clearsnow Estate, they didn’t know who he was. Regardless, they very much liked the boy who always had an easy smile on his face.","“You’re here, Moli! I’ve just baked some bread, come share it with us!” a sixty year old woman called out to Yushi Moli.","“I can’t, I’ve got to get back because I have some business to take care of later,” Yushi Moli declined with a smile.","“This is for you, big brother!” A girl two years younger than him and a bow on her head ran up to him. She shoved a simple cloth doll into his hands. “I made it myself!”","The bow on her head was a present from Yushi Moli.","“Thank you Little Ying!” He accepted the doll and stored it in his robes. The girl called Little Ying beamed with contentment and waved goodbye.","Yushi Moli returned to Clearsnow Estate after a short while, his emotions no longer as calm as they appeared.","The Boneforge Pill and Galewind Step!","He couldn’t wait to try them—they would enhance his cultivation incredibly in a very short period of time!","“Let’s try the pill first!” Cloistered in a meditation chamber, Yushi Moli took a deep breath before placing the fragrant medicinal pill in his mouth. It melted into a pool of refreshingly sweet liquid that traveled straight to his stomach.","Boom!","Something exploded in his stomach before he had the time to react. Currents of air rushed out of his stomach and shot into his limbs.","“Are these the effects of the Boneforge Pill?” Yushi Moli tilted his head to the side and carefully took in the sensation. As expected of a pill meant for martial cultivators!","However, he quickly frowned and raised his eyebrows.","Pain!","Bone-piercing pain!","It felt like countless ants were nibbling at his bones. Pain and numbness!","It was worse than death, but at the same time, he felt that he should be able to endure it.","“Ugh, it hurts so much...” he exclaimed because it seemed to be the expected reaction, then continued to carefully assess the pill’s effects.","While his mind could endure the agony, his body was too weak. Sweat poured out of his body and soaked his clothes. He’d never encountered this kind of pain in his entire life. Although he could put up with it, his body still reacted instinctively.","“How is this a Boneforge Pill? It’s a Killing Pill!” Yushi Moli heaved a sigh of resignation, but his tone remained untroubled.","As time went on, the torment felt like someone was hammering all of his bones to pieces. An ordinary person would’ve fainted dead away a long time ago or even died from the anguish. Thin lines of blood seeped out of his pores.","“The old me probably would’ve undergone a mental collapse by this point... When did I start changing? Am I still me?” As much as it hurt, Yushi Moli still had the capacity to entertain certain wild thoughts.","He was using less than one hundredth of his mental capacity to manipulate the pill’s effects into honing his body. When Ouyang Du took his first pill, he was wrung inside and out and ultimately fainted from the torture. Even now, he didn’t have the courage to try a second Boneforge Pill.","“I think I’m reaching my limit... Why is my body so weak?” Yushi Moli grumbled. His mind was mind, but his body was startling to buckle from the strain.","His eyes suddenly lit up.","“That’s right! I can meditate on the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth and use the sword shadow to suppress the pain!” A stroke of inspiration struck Yushi Moli and he sat down cross-legged, meditating on the sword shadow in his mind.","Humm!","A note reverberated in his mind as a snowy sword shape floated to the fore. His concentration was squarely focused on it. While his body and bones continued to ache, his mind was completely preoccupied by the sword shadow. It suddenly shifted and suppressed the pain coursing through his body. Though the pain continued, it no longer damaged his nerves.","What Yushi Moli didn’t know was that if he hadn’t turned to meditation, the pain would’ve lasted a few dozen more breaths at most. He didn’t possess true qi and thus couldn’t fully digest the pill’s effects. It would’ve dispersed from his body after making a full circuit.","But now that he’d started mentally observing the sword chart, the sword shadow in his mind flared with light and helped him digest the effects of the Boneforge Pill.","Yuqing Yang had counted on the pill helping Yushi Moli realize that his path was wrong. After he endured pain that regular people couldn’t, yet didn’t obtain the effects that he anticipated... The immense disappointment would cause him to change his mind.","However, he didn’t know that the boy possessed the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth, or that Yushi Moli’s soul was so strong that the pill’s searing pain was just a commonplace event for him."]},{"number":2192,"title":"Chapter 2192: Chapter 2147: Autumn Wind","paragraphs":["Chapter 2147: Autumn Wind","Yushi Moli slipped into a mental state that blurred the boundaries between him and the world. As the sword form in his mind grew clearer, it exuded strange ripples.","Autumn Wind?","He suddenly felt a familiar presence from the sword. Did it come from the technique that he’d created by accident?","Guided by the thought, his mind immersed itself in the meaning behind Autumn Wind. He simulated the move again and again, throwing his efforts into perceiving the technique.","Trickles of blood gathered outside his body, gradually forming a thick layer of bloody scabs that enveloped him. When he came back to his senses after an indeterminate period of time, blackish-red scabs flaked off his body whenever he moved. The skin underneath was pristine and glistened like jade.","“This...” Yushi Moli stared at his hands and marveled at the vigorous strength coming from him. A knowing smile spread across his face. “This is the effect of the Boneforge Pill, I really owe the elder a big, big favor!","“Luo Qing said that this pill is worth ten thousand gold coins. The effects are great, it’s worth way more than that! I’ve doubled my strength compared to before, which is so much more than what I can achieve in a year. I would never reach this level if I continued to train according to my old methods!”","Being different from the Yushi Moli of before, he understood that his previous training methods were incorrect. Not even the medicinal baths would keep him alive for much longer.","“Weird, I should’ve died a few days ago based on my old ways. How am I still alive?” His mind wandered down strange paths again.","When he stood up and stretched, Yushi Moli further discovered some changes in certain key joints and bones. His previous training had forced them into very awkward angles and positions, causing a sliver of deviation from what should’ve been smooth sword techniques.","It was these incorrect practices that damaged his body. Seeing as he was only thirteen years old, a period in which his body was developing, his old training regimen was more accurately described as a self-devastation regimen.","“It’s incredible that I’ve survived till now,” he laughed at himself.","Thanks to a pill worth ten thousand gold coins, the misaligned bones and damaged membranes of his body had somewhat recovered. He moved much more easily than before.","“I can’t continue in the same way. Although it appeared to make me stronger, it was a slow form of suicide!” Yushi Moli shook his head rapidly. The training of martial cultivators should not be thus. He’d been too influenced by his idol worship of Long Qianjue.","“I need to stop this training that weighs my body down. I need to stop. I’m going to stop!”","Important things bore repeating thrice. Four years of diligent training had only made his body slightly stronger than his peers. If it wasn’t for the spontaneous comprehension of autumn wind and an inexplicable calmness from the bottom of his soul, he would’ve died when Luo Qing ambushed him.","The Autumn Wind technique also had nothing to do with his previous training. It was facilitated purely by talent from the depth of his soul.","His previous regimen could strengthen a mortal’s body, but it was useless compared to what cultivators underwent! If he wished to grow stronger, he needed to use the proper way. For the moment, the most direct process he could utilize was the Boneforge Pill.","“Although it hurts a lot, I can manage it. The sword of heaven and earth helps suppress the pain and fully digests the pill’s effects.” Yushi Moli was mortified when he thought of how he’d been earlier.","Just some aches and pains had nearly caused his body to fall apart? How humiliating! Certain people would laugh their heads off at him if they knew!","Eh? Certain people? Who people?","“I’ll practice the Galewind Step next! Today is the first day. I’ll head into Qingqiu Mountain after nine days and start hunting beasts!” An urgent desire rose from his heart—he needed to grow stronger!","“The Boneforge Pill is a good supplemental option if I can’t buy the Qi Elevation Pill!” Yushi Moli walked out of the meditation chamber, showered, changed his clothes, and entered the mountain.","The sun was already setting to the west. He took a seat between the trees, warmed by the golden rays of late autumn. As he paged through the book, he memorized the key points of the lower human rank body method and its movements.","“Okay.” With how strong Yushi Moli’s mental force was, he possessed a nearly photographic memory. He moved in uncoordinated fashion, twisting his body to follow the instructions in the book. “This is really hard!”","He quickly found out that it was much more difficult than what he’d imagined. A lower human rank body method was vastly different from a basic sword technique. The basic sword techniques weren’t ranked, and thus even mortals could try them.","But a method that was ranked—even lower human rank—was out of reach for ordinary people. They required the facilitation of true qi! Only with the circulation of true qi could the full force of body methods and martial techniques be deployed.","Since Yushi Moli lacked true qi, he seemed clumsy and off balance when he practiced Galewind Step, despite the strength of his soul.","After a while, he plopped to the ground and wiped off the sweat on his face.","“The Galewind Step is really hard. The steps need to be bolstered by true qi before they can be completed...” Yushi Moli found himself in a quandary. “But... it was the same case when I first started practicing the sword! If I don’t succeed the first time, I’ll try a second time, then a third. I’ll succeed one day!”","He stood up with determination and started practicing again. Although martial techniques required the usage of true qi, he still felt that he would be able to master them.","......","Another three days passed by in the blink of an eye. Yushi Moli took three more Boneforge Pills during this time and his body and strength improved noticeably once more. He was now on par with an adult man in their prime.","Thanks to the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth, the effects of the three pills were nearly fully absorbed and almost none went to waste. His misaligned bones and latent injuries were mostly recovered.","For the past three days, he spent mornings practicing the sword and afternoons on the Galewind Step. But no matter how hard he tried, he didn’t even set foot into understanding the technique.","“Weird, it’s been three days already. With uncle’s temper, he would’ve come and lectured me in person once he found out that I didn’t listen to him.” Yushi Moli found his uncle’s absence increasingly odd as time went on. Ouyang Du was the person he was closest to in this world and it was highly unusual that they hadn’t seen each other in three days.","Not only was he not used to this situation, but he was also starting to worry.","“Uncle didn’t look too good when he left. Did something happen?” Yushi Moli could barely sit still when his thoughts traveled here. He might’ve once had more people he cared about—his younger brother and father, but their images were dimming in his heart. The only person left was the uncle who treated him well.","Unfortunately, it was already afternoon. If he visited Aurora City now, he wouldn’t make it back before tomorrow.","Yushi Moli was beginning to reject the city lord’s residence entirely—not because his father had ignored him during this month, but because as time went on, he felt more and more that it wasn’t his home. That that person wasn’t his father, and it’d be slightly awkward if the two of them met.","“I won’t make it back tonight if I go now... so let’s go tomorrow morning.” Yushi Moli shook his head and practiced the Galewind Step again. “I’m making no progress despite matching my movements and gestures to what the book describes. It really does need true qi.”","The boy frowned.","“The basic sword techniques can also be combined with true qi, but why are mine as powerful as an upper human rank cultivator?” Yushi Moli still recalled Luo Qing misidentifying him as an upper human rank cultivator before he died.","A tendril of brisk autumn wind fluttered by, refreshing his thoughts when it breezed through his hair.","“That’s right, autumn wind!” He chased after the tendril, stepping forward and reappearing three meters in a different spot."]},{"number":2193,"title":"Chapter 2193: Chapter 2148: The Mental State of Wind","paragraphs":["Chapter 2148: The Mental State of Wind","Yushi Moli came back to his senses and stared dumbly at where he’d just been. What... what’d just happened? Blinking, he stood frozen on the spot for a dozen more breaths before jerking back into motion.","“Did I do it? Is this the Galewind Step?” He still recalled how he’d followed the gust of autumn wind like it was second nature, stepping out with the wind. “The feeling of autumn wind... to follow the wind...”","Yushi Moli took another step forward.","Whoosh!","His body moved sideways by a meter and reappeared to the left to his previous position.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","He closed his eyes and looked inward, feeling the autumn breeze with his heart. He felt that he was turning into the wind himself. Following that, his body flashed through the woods of the mountain, chasing after the breezes. His motions were undeniably smooth, just as the book said they should be.","When he stopped fifteen minutes later, he was sweating profusely and his breathing rapid. Plainly, he’d consumed too much energy.","“So this is... mental state...” Yushi Moli realized. Martial techniques didn’t necessarily require true qi—mental state was the most important!","If he could grasp a technique’s associated mental state and use it to deploy the technique, the resulting effect was far stronger than employing true qi!","Wind!","Yushi Moli had comprehended the mental state of wind and used it as the starting point of the Galewind Step, elevating it beyond the rank it should have. It was now an upper human rank body method.","......","Yushi Moli was in a wonderful mood the next morning. He’d practiced into the wee hours of the night and returned to Clearsnow Estate only after he exhausted the last bit of stamina in his body. He felt that he’d fully mastered Galewind Step and even modified it, keeping only the essence and discarding the dross.","Not only had his Galewind Step reached great perfection, but it’d broken through to upper earth rank! He remained in the dark about this change, however, since he was unfamiliar with the ranks of this world’s martial techniques.","After one night of meditation, he was back to his usual energetic self. Upon eating breakfast and taking another Boneforge Pill, he cleaned up his room and left the estate.","Yushi Moli wouldn’t be at ease if he didn’t check on his uncle.","......","Aurora City.","The welcoming hall in the city lord’s residence.","“Stop trying my patience, Yushi Jianchou!” roared a thin elder.","“You need to know your place as well, Luo Hanye. This is Aurora City, not your Coldnight Estate,” Yushi Jianchou replied expressionlessly.","“So? You still need to give me an explanation since you are the city lord and my nephew has died in your jurisdiction!” glowered the elder named Luo Hanye.","“How preposterous!” snorted Yushi Jianchou. “So many die all the time in Aurora territory, am I to give each of them a personal explanation?”","The world of martial cultivators was filled with death and slaughter. Someone died at almost every second.","An explanation? How?","Ordinary people were curtailed by law, but martial cultivators made decisions according to their moods.","“My nephew followed your son out of town! His death must have something to do with Yushi Moli,” Luo Hanye bit off. “Have your son come out and we’ll sort things out!”","“Luo Hanye, my son is a mortal who cannot cultivate. If your nephew followed my son with malicious intentions, I should be the one who takes you to task first—”","“But the one dead is my nephew!” Luo Hanye shouted Yushi Jianchou down.","......","Yushi Moli wandered into Aurora City close to noon. Arctic wintriness was beginning to thread its way through autumn, but the city remained a hub of activity.","The boy went straight to Ouyang Du’s home when he arrived.","“Uncle Liu!” Yushi Moli greeted the steward standing at the door.","“Aiya, it’s young master Moli! Come in, come on in!” the steward responded enthusiastically.","Ouyang Du treated Yushi Moli like the boy was his own son. The Ouyang servants were also completely different from the ones at the city lord’s residence—they truly treated Yushi Moli as their young master.","“Where’s my uncle?” Yushi Moli walked in with a smile.","“The lord is, is not at home,” Steward Liu answered stiffly.","“Not home?” Yushi Moli blinked. “Where’s he gone then?”","His mental strength was so strong that he could now meditate over the sword shadow of heaven and earth whenever he wanted to; his perception of the surroundings was also growing keener. In fact, Yushi Moli was finding that he could observe the emotions of others.","Hence, he’d caught a split second of awkwardness from the steward.","“Some complications have come up with the business and so milord needs to leave Aurora City for a while.” Steward Liu managed to squeeze out a smile on his face.","“Uncle Liu!” Yushi Moli looked solemnly at the steward and asked solemnly, “Where has my uncle gone?!”","“Well...” Steward Liu hesitated when he looked into the young man’s eyes.","“How about this, tell me what happened to the Sliverlight Trading Company three days ago,” Yushi Moli demanded as a sharp light shot out of his eyes.","Steward Liu felt enormous pressure descend over him, as if it wasn’t a young man in front of him, but a mighty powerhouse that towered to the heavens.","Sliverlight Trading Company was a trading company that Ouyang Du had started from scratch. Headquartered in Aurora City, it was one of the largest companies around thanks to Yushi Jianchou’s support. At the same time, the city lord’s residence saved a great deal on their daily necessities and supplies due to their relationship with Silverlight.","“Ah...” Steward Liu paled, but quickly found the pressure dissipating. It was still a thirteen year old boy in front of him, so he sighed. “Robbers have made off with a shipment of trading goods and the lord was heavily injured three days ago. He is resting at the city lord’s residence.”","Yushi Moli spun on his heel without another word and left for his old home. Ouyang Du was the only person he cared about in this world. He had to pay a visit when his uncle was injured!","The boy bumped into an aloof Zong Yan when he reached the front doors.","“What are you doing here?” Zong Yan frowned when he saw the boy.","Yushi Moli frowned as well and a keen light flashed through the depths of his eyes. “Uncle is hurt, so I’m here to see him.”","“It has nothing to do with you, go back.” Zong Yan swept a gaze over Yushi Moli.","“My uncle is hurt!” Urgency shot out of his eyes. The old Yushi Moli would never talk back to Zong Yan, but now...","“You have departed from home and look after milord’s businesses. You are not allowed to return home without his summons, this is the rule,” Zong Yan replied coldly. “These are the rules and they cannot be broken. Do not force me into taking action against you.”","He snorted while killing intent narrowed Yushi Moli’s eyes. Somehow, it raised shock and fear in Zong Yan’s heart. He said to the two guards beside them, “You two, escort the young master back to Clearsnow Estate.”"]},{"number":2194,"title":"Chapter 2194: Chapter 2149: Just Bring Back a Head","paragraphs":["Chapter 2149: Just Bring Back a Head","Zong Yan felt suffocating pressure drape around him as he faced Yushi Moli. He’d always been one to hold fast to his words; the same applied even as he faced the boy’s current state. He didn’t budge an inch—he’d said that Yushi Moli wouldn’t enter the residence, and so the boy wouldn’t.","No one could make him change his mind, not even Yushi Jianchou!","Yushi Moli stared coldly at him while Zong Yan grit his teeth, the fear in his heart too much to put into words. He didn’t understand it—how was the cowardly and stubborn young master exuding such a terrifying aura?","He’d never felt this kind of feeling before, not even from the city lord!","“I don’t need your men to escort me out, I’ll go myself.” Yushi Moli looked deeply at Zong Yan before turning on his heel. He felt that he should be furious, but oddly enough, he was quite calm inside.","It seemed that the guard captain only wanted to annoy Yushi Moli, not truly infuriate him. Why was that?","The boy didn’t understand it, not this or any of the changes that’d taken place in his body lately. They surprised even himself, but it also seemed like this was who he truly was.","Yushi Moli walked off with an unperturbed expression.","......","“Sir... isn’t this... a bit out of line?” The two guards at the door heaved sighs of relief. The pressure exerted by Yushi Moli moments ago had been too frightening.","Although the young master was trash that could not cultivate and had been assigned to Clearsnow Estate as a result, he was still the city lord’s son. Additionally, Yushi Moli seemed to have... changed. It was over the top to block him at the door.","“Hmph.” Zong Yan was slightly ashen and his back slick with sweat. “He could’ve come back earlier or later, but he just had to come back now. Luo Hanye from Coldnight Estate is still visiting. Who knows what will happen if he catches sight of Yushi Moli?”","Luo Hanye was also a celestial rank martial cultivator. Although he was weaker than Yushi Jianchou, he was not someone to provoke if one could help it. His nephew had died on account of the young master, he would never easily let this go!","If Yushi Moli had remained at Clearsnow Estate like he was supposed to, Luo Hanye wouldn’t dare seek him out even if he knew where the boy was. That was Aurora City property—it would be the equivalent of declaring war if he dared attack someone on the estate.","Coldnight Estate was very strong, but it paled far in comparison to Aurora City.","So while Luo Hanye blustered with extreme hostility, it was all talk. On the other hand, if Yushi Moli returned to the city lord’s residence at this time, matters would progress and worsen. Neither side would come off better in the end.","Although Yushi Moli’s current aura was quite strong, Zong Yan still thought of him as the boy of old. Perhaps the brief hint of pressure earlier had been a misconception?","“Should we go protect the elder young master?” the guard asked.","“No.” Zong Yan swept a glance over him. “Let him go.”","The boy seemed to be keeping certain secrets.","......","“I thought it was me unwilling to return home, but now I see that it is they who don’t welcome me at all—“ Yushi Moli mumbled to himself, yet otherwise not too affected by the encounter. He didn’t know what’d taken place behind the scenes. “Forget it, I’ll stay away if that’s what they want. It’s enough to know that uncle’s fine.”","He didn’t have too many lasting memories of the aloof city lord’s residence. Much of what he recalled about it was starting to get blurry. He seemed to have lost most of his attachment to this place a long time ago, including... his father and younger brother?","“I lived there for thirteen years and it’s only been one month since I moved out. Have I become so heartless so quickly?” Yushi Moli walked toward Aurora City’s eastern gate, eschewing riding his horse. His emotions were peaceful and his thoughts part of nature as he sensed the rhythm of the wind.","“Isn’t that boy Yushi Moli?” Two cultivators paused when they saw his departing form.","“Which Yushi Moli? ...the son of the Aurora city lord?” A tall and skinny cultivator next to him blinked.","“That’s him. Our young master chased him out of the city three days ago. Since he met his end in Aurora territory, it has everything to do with their city lord!” A dangerous light sparkled in his short and fat companion’s eyes.","“People should realize that it’s not that safe around the city. If our own young master died here, that means it’s entirely reasonable for the Aurora city lord’s son to die too!” A faint smile appeared on the tall and skinny cultivator’s face.","They belonged to Coldnight Estate. Their lord had brought numerous men with him on his trip to demand an explanation from Aurora City. These two were in charge of monitoring the city and preventing the city lord from ambushing their people. It was why they hadn’t followed their lord into the city lord’s residence. The duo remained outside to collect information.","They were drinking at a small tavern close to the city gates while they awaited Luo Hanye’s return.","“C’mon, the lord will be very happy if we kill him!” The two grinned savagely at each other.","“And where are you two off to?” A young man dressed in scholarly robes appeared in front of them.","“Mister Zhou!” The two started and subconsciously glanced at Yushi Moli. The boy had already passed through the city gates. “Mister Zhou, that’s Yushi Moli—Yushi Jianchou’s son!”","“Oh? That boy is Yushi Moli?” Mister Zhou brightened.","“Yes!” replied the tall and skinny cultivator.","“Make sure you clean up after yourself. Don’t leave anything behind. Just bring back a head.” Mister Zhou waved them off.","“Understood!” The two beamed after receiving approval for their actions.","......","Five kilometers out from Aurora City found small paths winding through sparsely populated areas. Yushi Moli sighed.","“Why am I always ambushed on my way back from the city?”","Did his face say “ambush me” or something like that? First it was Luo Qing, now two weird strangers. Though they hadn’t revealed themselves, he’d been sensing sharp killing intent that’d locked onto him.","An internal alarm was ringing in his mind again, but no ambush was forthcoming. Instead, someone stood in the road ahead. Tall and skinny, their face was concealed.","“So it’s you... guys.” Another short and fat man appeared behind Yushi Moli, blocking his avenue of retreat.","Although both had their faces covered, Yushi Moli had seen them on his way out of town. With his memory, he recalled a trace of their presence, despite not specifically paying attention to them. His senses had been growing stronger in recent times, not only because he meditated over the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth, but because something seemed to be awakening in the depths of his soul.","“Who are you?” Preoccupied with sensing the rhythm and profound meaning behind the autumn wind, his tone carried a hint of the autumn wind’s cutting edge.","“Someone who wants your life, of course!” snarled the fat man behind the boy. He didn’t want to waste too much effort talking.","“Kill him, we just need the head.”","The shorty rushed behind Yushi Moli and smashed a fist down on the boy’s back. His skinny companion stood with his arms crossed over his chest, not intending to make a move. Yushi Moli was just trash that could not cultivate. Although he grasped a sword, that was just for show.","“I’ll be dead without a doubt if this punch connects with my back!” Yushi Moli’s eyes narrowed. “You just need the head? Aren’t you... confident.”","The boy sighed. Who have I angered this time??","He stepped to the side in an almost instinctive reaction.","Bam!","The short and fat man was an upper rank cultivator. When his punch missed, it raised an explosive sound in the air.","“Where is he?” he blinked.","“Careful!” the tall man cried out with horror. And then... the fat man saw a very familiar body rise in front of his eyes while his thoughts sank forever into darkness."]},{"number":2195,"title":"Chapter 2195: Chapter 2150: Earth Rank","paragraphs":["Chapter 2150: Earth Rank","Decapitation with a single stroke. Clean, smooth, and neat.","“What?!” shrieked the tall man. His comrade had been upper human rank and a hair stronger than him!","How could a young man, one who couldn’t train in martial dao, execute a cultivator with one stroke?!","This was a conspiracy!","Yushi Moli was plainly a formidable swordsman, but the rumors circulating in Aurora City made him out to be useless trash. Stories of his ineptitude were everywhere within one hundred kilometers of the city and many jeered that he was the dog son of a tiger father.","Was all of this a conspiracy planted by Yushi Jianchou?","A myriad of emotions assailed the tall man, but he felt incredible fear more than anything. Whether it was the angle or speed of Yushi Moli’s blow, it rivaled, if not surpassed what an experienced swordsman could deploy.","The strength behind it was on par with upper human rank! Yet the man didn’t sense the ripples of true qi from Yushi Moli!","“This won’t do, Yushi Moli plainly has the strength of upper human rank and is an old hand at killing people. I’m no match for him if we go toe-to-toe!” The tall man frowned. “This must get back to the rest, the lord must know!”","Yushi Jianchou had concealed a major killing weapon in his family. He certainly wasn’t harboring any resemblance of good intentions in doing so!","Run!","A frosty glint in his eyes, Yushi Moli tensed, ready to test his skills and fight the other man. Who would’ve thought that his opponent’s next reaction would be to run away instead?","“He’s gone?” Yushi Moli blinked. “Is he that cowardly?”","The boy shook his head, but didn’t mind the development. There would be others who came along for revenge, but he really didn’t care. The man was very fast and vanished amongst the trees with a few rises and falls. Yushi Moli wouldn’t be able to catch up to him even if he wanted to.","“I need to get out of here as soon as possible. I’ll be dead without a doubt if he comes back with helpers!” Although caution ran through Yushi Moli’s mind, he moved at a leisurely pace that belied what he said he should do. He searched through the headless body and found a cloth bag.","“Three gold coins and a dozen silver coins? He’s so poor and he doesn’t have any secret methods on him.” Yushi Moli blinked at what he found on the fat man’s body. “It looks like who I killed last time is no ordinary person. Are these guys here to take revenge for Luo Qing?”","He realized what was going on when he connected the dots. Yushi Moli quickly hopped onto his horse and urged it back to Clearsnow Estate.","The two martial cultivators who’d ambushed him today most likely had something to do with Luo Qing. Those two wouldn’t have a reason to kill him otherwise.","Killing two more people today didn’t raise any uncomfortable feelings in Yushi Moli’s heart. He was neither excited nor dejected by his deeds. It was like he’d done something so insignificant that it didn’t bear consideration.","He also wasn’t worried about the one who’d gotten away. Clearsnow Estate was Aurora territory. Even with how small it was, there were martial cultivators standing guard over it. No one would dare make trouble here.","Yushi Jianchou was the city lord of Aurora City and its strongest cultivator. He still possessed a certain amount of authority.","Granted, Yushi Moli felt that he would have nothing to fear even if his father didn’t possess his reputation and there were no cultivators in residence at the estate.","......","The boy put recent affairs out of his mind when he returned to Clearsnow Estate. It was like a tiny wave had risen in the boundless sea, gone after it died down. The only thing he felt was that he and Aurora City weren’t meant to be.","Life had been far from ideal when he lived in the city and now that he’d moved out, he always ran into bizarre ambushes after he visited.","He wouldn’t be visiting in the future then!","Yushi Moli raised his sword in the forests of Qingqiu Mountain and continued practicing his sword techniques and body method.","......","“You’re back.” Mister Zhou raised his brows when he saw the tall man return to Aurora City.","“Mister Zhou, we’ve all been fooled!” The man knew to conceal his emotions, so there was no particular expression on his face at the moment. He placed his lips close to the young man’s ears and whispered a few sentences.","Mister Zhou frowned. “Take me to it!”","In the middle of a small path five kilometers out from Aurora City.","The fat man’s headless body was sprawled over it. His robes were slightly open, a sign that someone had searched through them.","“What a forceful blow!” Mister Zhou sucked in a sharp breath when he saw the wound on the corpse. “Even certain earth rank sword experts will find it difficult to deliver such a stroke. Was it really Yushi Moli who killed him?”","“Yes!” the tall man confirmed emphatically. “Yushi Moli’s body method is odd. It’s a bit like the Galewind Step, but it’s many times more sophisticated! He only struck once, but I didn’t even get a clear look before fatty died!”","The tall man inwardly rejoiced when he heard Mister Zhou’s assessment of the blow. Earth rank! Thank goodness he’d immediately run away instead of fighting Yushi Moli. He’d also be dead if he tried to take down the boy.","Mister Zhou took in a deep breath and crouched down, carefully examining the fat man’s wound.","“This wound is very similar to the one on the young master’s throat. It’s obviously from the same person, but this one is much more sophisticated.” It was a very unwelcome discovery. “If he wasn’t hiding his strength three days ago, then he’s continuously improved during this time. This person is very frightening!”","“We...” the tall man began.","“Dispose of his body and don’t let word of this spread. I’m going to find the lord and see what he decides,” Mister Zhou ordered.","......","“What?? How is this possible?!” Luo Hanye had received nothing but a stomach full of anger for his time in Aurora City. He ran into Mister Zhou when he left the metropolis.","Mister Zhou was the grand steward of Coldnight Estate. Although he was young, he was very experienced and possessed a high cultivation level. Luo Hanye trusted him immensely.","Although Mister Zhou had followed his master to Aurora City, he didn’t accompany Luo Hanye in visiting Yushi Jianchou. Instead, he’d brought a gift to pay his respects to Yuqing Yang.","Not only did Mister Zhou fail to see the grandmaster, but his gift was also returned.","Luo Hanye’s expression shifted when he heard Mister Zhou’s report upon leaving Aurora City.","“If Yushi Moli really is behind it, then the boy has fooled everyone,” Mister Zhou nodded.","“Hmph, so that runt killed Qing’er. How will I ever face my brother if I don’t take revenge for Qing’er!” Luo Hanye ground his teeth.","Luo Qing was the son of Luo Hanye’s elder brother—Luo Lengye. The two brothers had founded Coldnight Estate near Aurora City thirty years ago. Upon its establishment, they were attacked by the biggest band of robbers in the vicinity—the Blackwind Robbers.","The fight lasted three days and three nights. Although the Blackwind Robbers were eventually repelled and never dared set foot into the estate again, its lord—Luo Lengye—died from his injuries. He left behind only his son, Luo Qing.","The two brothers were very tight knit and Luo Hanye treated Luo Qing as his own son after the death of his elder brother. Sadly, Luo Qing’s martial potential was incredibly poor. Even with the aid of countless cultivation resources, he only managed to ascend to mid human rank despite being nearly forty years old.","When Luo Qing heard of Yuqing Yang visiting Aurora City three days ago, he secretly slipped away to meet the grandmaster. But Yushi Moli killed him when greed overtook him.","“Yushi Jianchou can’t possibly be in the dark that Yushi Moli killed my nephew. Since he insists on playing dumb, then let him keep up the act.” Killing intent flashed through Luo Hanye’s eyes. “We can’t do anything in Clearsnow Estate. Set a watch on it and kill Yushi Moli when he sets foot out of it!”","As livid as he was, Luo Hanye didn’t lose his reason. The consequences would be disastrous if he sent people into the estate, even if they were assassins. Coldnight Estate could not endure Yushi Jianchou’s wrath. The city lord was the strongest in the surrounding area."]},{"number":2196,"title":"Chapter 2196: Chapter 2151: A Quick Sword","paragraphs":["Chapter 2151: A Quick Sword","There wasn’t only Yushi Jianchou around, but also another stunning powerhouse at Clearsnow Estate—Xun You!","It appeared to others that Yushi Jianchou didn’t value the estate situated at the foot of Qingqiu Mountain. However, he’d assigned Xun You to the property.","Plainly, it was a very important estate to Aurora City.","Luo Hanye was yet to fully assess Xun You, so he had to wait for Yushi Moli to leave the estate before taking any action.","If the lands around Aurora City were so dangerous that even his nephew died in them, it wouldn’t be surprising that Yushi Jianchou’s son would meet his end when traveling through them. It would be the boy’s doomsday if he dared leave Clearsnow Estate again, even if he possessed an earth rank cultivation.","With Coldnight Estate’s strength, it was able to kill a celestial rank cultivator. If not, they would hire an assassin from the Sanguine Dusk Tavern!","......","Six days passed as Yushi Moli digested the remaining Boneforge Pills. His physical body was now so strong that it was unfathomable; it’d truly reached the level of a martial cultivator. Each of his strokes carried a force of more than five hundred kilograms—the limits of human rank.","Although his body reached the robustness of a martial cultivator, he wasn’t a true cultivator because he lacked true qi. Regardless, he was very confident in his capabilities. His current weakness was his best disguise. Having the enemy underestimate him was also a kind of strategy!","Yushi Moli lacked true qi and looked like he would blow away with the wind, but anyone who dared think lightly of him because of that would do so to their detriment.","However, there were all kinds of people in this world. Not everyone who met him would underestimate him, so he always had to be on guard. Some might pretend to take him lightly, but actually ise their full strength and reflexes against him.","......","Yushi Moli chose to focus on speed for his battle style. His blows needed to be so fast that they were unpredictable. If his moves were faster than what his enemy could react to, he would defeat them before they could bring their full strength to bear!","Thus, in addition to his usual daily practice, he concentrated on studying swift movements over the six days. He incorporated the meaning of wind into his methods, a starting point that already defined quickness.","Combined with the Galewind Step, it also enabled his body to move with alacrity.","At the same time, he researched how to meld his sword techniques with his body method. He wanted to deploy both at the same time so that he could attack while evading.","......","Yushi Moli flitted through the forests of Qingqiu Mountain like he was wind incarnate. He was one with the wintry gusts breezing around him as he sensed the rhythm of the wind and breathed its freedom.","Sword light flashed through the air in an interplay of sword and light. It shot out unerringly when some leaves drifted off of bare branches.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Seven sword strokes stabbed forward within the span of a breath. Yushi Moli reappeared in the public eye when leaves fluttered to the ground.","“I did it!” He smiled when his eyes fixed on the seven leaves on the ground. There was a tiny sword mark in each of their centers.","Seven strokes in one breath! Each of them had pierced through an exceedingly fragile and withered leaf, yet the leaves suffered no other damage apart from the tiniest of marks in their center. They hadn’t fragmented from the impact or stuck to the sword.","Not only did this require unfathomable speed, but it also demanded intricate sword skills and superb observation skills.","“I’ve finally succeeded after six days of hard work.” Yushi Moli wiped off the sweat on his forehead. “There’s no more Boneforge Pills to use, so I have to head into the mountain tomorrow to hunt beasts.”","He’d decided on hunting beasts both to earn money for more pills and to hone his sword skills. For some reason, sword dao felt very unfamiliar to him. He had the nagging sensation that progress would be much swifter if he switched to another discipline, that he might even attain much higher accomplishments.","But he had to pursue sword dao because the Sword Chart of Heaven and Earth had manifested a sword form that suppressed something very important to him. Only when he reached great perfection in practicing sword dao could he break through that seal and retrieve whatever it was.","Yushi Moli didn’t know what the sword kept away, but it must be something very important to him. It was something more important than his own life!","Perhaps the past him had shouldered a mission that caused one to despair. As he grew and developed, his motivation for cultivating had changed. He no longer did so for Yushi Jianchou or to find favor in the eyes of others. He was searching for his past self, he wanted to help his past self break free of the sword shadow.","“My sword style comes from the autumn wind, but autumn is about to pass. It does not blow in the winter...” Yushi Moli blinked, then suddenly laughed. “How am I worrying about something so stupid? Wind in autumn and winter is both wind, just in a different form.”","He finally realized that he’d been so silly all along. The meaning of wind encompassed a myriad of things.","......","Yushi Moli didn’t head to the depths of Qingqiu Mountain the next day because Ouyang Du arrived instead. His uncle lectured him ferociously and brought him an allowance of one hundred gold coins.","The boy heaved a sigh of relief to see that his uncle was fine. However, Ouyang Du didn’t mention the matter of his trading company being robbed. Regardless, Yushi Moli committed the culprits to memory—the Blackwind Robbers. They’d stolen his uncle’s goods and injured him!","These robbers were the strongest group within one hundred and fifty kilometers. They were also Aurora City’s number one enemy.","Yushi Moli packed his belongings on the third day and left Clearsnow Estate before the sun rose. He took only a cloth bag with him. It held some rations, a fire starter, and a piece of clothing to withstand the cold. He gripped the Qingfeng Sword in his hand.","This was very light equipment for someone hunting beasts in Qingqiu Mountain.","“Oh? He’s out!” A human rank cultivator standing guard jerked awake.","Those of Coldnight Estate had set up shifts to keep an eye on the area in recent days. Their standing orders were to send the fastest horse possible back to the estate as soon as Yushi Moli walked out.","Although Yushi Moli practiced his sword in the forests on the outskirts of Qingqiu Mountain, that was essentially Clearsnow’s backyard. It was the equivalent of him staying in the estate.","“Notify the lord, I’ll keep an eye on him and make marks along the way!” a human rank cultivator called out to one of his peers.","“So the kid’s finally come out?” The other brightened. “I haven’t taken a shower or slept a good night’s sleep in six days in order to keep an eye on him. I’ll notify the lord, stay close to him.” He glared at Yushi Moli’s departing back with a hint of fury.","“Don’t worry, he won’t get away.” A sinister smile played on the lips of the cultivator who’d seen Yushi Moli walk out. “Much of the credit goes to us if we can kill him. We’ll have some fun in Aurora City then!”","......","Autumn was a short season in the northern expanses of the Qiulan Empire. It’d only been a short while, but leaves were all on the ground and a biting chill wafted through the air when the sun was down. A little flurry of snow occasionally swirled around.","Yushi Moli slowly entered Qingqiu Mountain, but something felt off to him, like something was following him. Yet when he took a look around, he discovered nothing out of the ordinary.","“I need to be careful. Although Qingqiu Mountain isn’t big, who knows if there are any incredibly strong beasts inside?” Yushi Moli appeared relaxed, but he was actually keeping a close eye on everything.","“It may not be beasts!” He suddenly recalled that he’d killed two cultivators. One of them was the noble Luo Qing, the other sought revenge for him.","Yushi Moli had also let one of them go... which meant that the person surveilling him now was most probably one of Luo Qing’s. The boy didn’t think much of Luo Qing because it’d been an insignificant matter. Since more of his men had come to avenge him, Yushi Moli didn’t mind helping himself to some more wealth that’d fallen into his lap.","“Ah, I’m not a saint. I’m a sophisticated subscriber to the ideals of self gain. So I’m going to... kill and loot others now?” Yushi Moli chuckled to himself."]},{"number":2197,"title":"Chapter 2197: Chapter 2152: Within Qingqiu Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 2152: Within Qingqiu Mountain","Yushi Moli proceeded with caution after entering Qingqiu Mountain. Beasts and monsters roamed the land, even celestial rank cultivators had to be on their guard when traveling inside.","Although a strange confidence flourished in his heart, it was his first trip inside Qingqiu Mountain proper and he was indeed a bit weaker than ideal for this undertaking. There were many things that he didn’t understand—although he instinctively felt that none of it was a challenge to him, he still didn’t take things lightly.","It was his first time venturing into Qingqiu Mountain, but he didn’t seem like a boy fresh behind the ears.","“Is there really no one following me?” Yushi Moli remained in place for a while before speaking in overly loud tones, then headed into the depths of the mountain.","......","“He almost discovered me!” Hidden behind a tree, Kang Cheng breathed out more easily when the boy moved on. “The kid’s too alert, I need to be even more careful or I’ll end up dead before the lord sends more backup.”","Kang Cheng excelled in tracking, but he wasn’t that strong. He was only lower human rank, whereas Yushi Moli had already killed an upper human rank cultivator from Coldnight Estate. He knew that he was no match for the boy.","Thus, he didn’t dare expose himself at this time.","But next thing he knew, a dense layer of goosebumps popped up on the back of his neck. A piercingly cold sensation laid horizontal to the back of his neck.","“Out with it, who are you?”","The voice was very young, like it belonged to a boy who’d yet to grow up. However, a frosty edge peeked through its playful lilt.","Yushi Moli!","Kang Cheng shuddered with dread.","“I’m, I’m a hunter who lives in the mountains. I’m out here to hunt!” He had indeed disguised himself as a hunter to prevent Yushi Moli from discovering him. Kang Cheng even carried numerous hunting tools on him—but, of course, they were all for show.","“A hunter? A hunter who dawdled around Clearsnow Estate for six days straight?” Yushi Moli’s smile didn’t reach his eyes. In fact, there was a dangerous curve to it.","Color drained out of Kang Cheng’s face. Yushi Moli’s mental strength was too powerful! Even if he didn’t specifically pay attention to someone, he retained an impression of a person’s movements if he so much as glanced at them.","Apart from his usual training, Yushi Moli spent time relaxing every day to alleviate his nerves. A careful balance of tension and ease was the most ideal way to cultivate. His previous dogged pursuit of training at the expense of his own health had indeed ended in his death.","Thus, he’d seen this person a fair number of times. Although the man was dressed differently each time, Yushi Moli still recognized him with a single glimpse.","He hadn’t thought much of it at first, or rather, he couldn’t be bothered with such trivial details. But who would’ve thought that this person would follow him into the mountain, staying so close that he could sense the steady circulation of true qi within Kang Cheng’s body?","“I...” Kang Cheng was flabbergasted. He’d thought that he’d disguised himself well, but the boy had seen through him on sight!","Snick!","Kang Cheng’s right ear fell off when Yushi Moli waved his hand.","“AHHH!!” The man screamed, but didn’t dare move. It was like the boy’s sword hadn’t moved—it was still resting on the back of his neck!","“So out with it. Who are you, or you guys?” Yushi Moli instinctively felt that this man was with Luo Qing. Who was Luo Qing? A continuous string of people had come to take revenge for him, so he was no ordinary person.","Yushi Moli had already killed two people, so it didn’t matter if he killed a few more. They all wanted to kill him, anyway. Would a swordsman be afraid of killing people?","“I’m, I’m from Coldnight Estate!” Kang Cheng revealed under the brunt of enormous fear.","“Coldnight Estate?” Yushi Moli raised an eyebrow. He’d heard of the estate before—it was one of the very few who could talk back to Aurora City within one hundred and fifty kilometers. Although it was also called an estate, its scale of operations was numerous times larger than the diminutive Clearsnow Estate.","“You, you killed our lord’s nephew, so our lord wants to kill you!”","Yushi Moli blinked. Their lord’s nephew? The one who wanted to kill him and take his Boneforge Pill?","He was speechless at the revelation. Coldnight Estate was much richer than the city lord of Aurora City. The city lord had to support an entire city, but the estate was all family. To think that its young master had wanted to kill and loot someone! Did he really need that little bit of wealth?","Kang Cheng was just an ordinary cultivator, so he revealed everything he knew in his overwhelming desire to live.","“So this Mister Zhou you speak of could tell from the fatty’s injury that I’m the one who killed Luo Qing?” Yushi Moli found it fascinating that this Mister Zhou could read so much from a wound. He was far more than met the eye, and it looked like Yushi Moli needed to clean up the corpses next time he killed someone. After all, he wanted to work for the Sanguine Dusk Tavern.","It wouldn’t do to have someone easily tell where he came from.","Yushi Moli had actually known all this beforehand, but he’d subconsciously dismissed it as a minor matter and thus overlooked its importance at this stage of his life.","“That’s right, that’s right. Mister Zhou said that.” Kang Cheng rapidly bobbed his head up and down. “Can you... let me go now?”","“You made quite a few marks along the way, didn’t you?” Yushi Moli abruptly asked.","“Huh?” Kang Cheng started, he hadn’t talked about this. He was actually thinking of how to stall for time until reinforcements arrived.","Whoosh!","As he paused with confusion, Yushi Moli’s sword cut his head off. Kang Cheng’s eyes were wide with disbelief. Who would’ve imagined that the young man would be so decisive and kill without another word??","“There’s a hint of killing intent between your brows, so you’re obviously bringing people to kill me. I’d really be a saint if I let you go, but I want to be an unwavering swordsman!” Yushi Moli said in all seriousness, then used his sword to carve a few words into the tree next to him.","Yushi Moli is the killer!","The words were floated gracefully and brimmed with killing intent!","I, Yushi Moli, never offend anyone. I kill only because people want to kill me! Since Coldnight Estate has come knocking, I’ll make you wish you never bothered me!","These words were purposefully arrogant because he wanted to taunt Coldnight Estate. They knew it was his sword, anyway, so why not leave a prominent calling card? Maybe it’d come across as the impulsive hotheadedness of youth and cause them to underestimate him.","Hmm, not a bad idea at all.","Yushi Moli turned around and vanished in the mountain.","......","Arf arf arf!","The sound of dogs barking came from the road leading to Qingqiu Mountain, followed closely by thunderous horse hooves.","“Milord, you could’ve just left this matter to me.”","Three dozen fine horses sped over the paths heading into the mountain. Black hunting dogs the size of young cows ran in front of them. The contingent’s leader was Luo Hanye, lord of Coldnight Estate. Mister Zhou traveled next to him. They rode in front of a group of upper human rank cultivators and three earth rank experts.","Coldnight Estate commanded more strength than this, but if they sent a small army, that would raise attention from Aurora City. Luo Hanye didn’t wish to see an investigation develop into his matters. Additionally, this show of force was more than sufficient to deal with a mere Yushi Moli.","Luo Hanye had come only because he wished to personally execute the boy to assuage his fury.","“These are Kang Cheng’s marks.” Mister Zhou looked at the unobtrusive marks left on the road, trees, or weeds. “Follow them!”","The group entered Qingqiu Mountain with the marks guiding them.","“Hold!” Mister Zhou suddenly stopped and dismounted. “We can’t ride horses inside the mountain. It’ll raise the attention of the monsters.”","“Mm,” Luo Hanye nodded as well.","Everyone dismounted and the hunting dog quieted down. They proceeded on foot, but a pungent scent of gore wafted into their noses not long after they entered the mountain.","“Is that... Kang Cheng?!”” Everyone stopped with shock.","Kang Cheng’s headless body sprawled beneath a tree while his head had rolled off to the side. A couple fierce characters were carved into the tree behind him.","Yushi Moli is the killer!"]},{"number":2198,"title":"Chapter 2198: Chapter 2153: Complete Annihilation","paragraphs":["Chapter 2153: Complete Annihilation","The characters brimmed with the edge and passion of youth.","Luo Hanye and the others glowered.","“Bastard!” Luo Hanye shrieked with infuriation, ready to vomit blood. His shriek echoed through the surroundings and startled countless animals in the vicinity. “Kill him! We must kill that cretin!”","......","“They’re here, alright.” Yushi Moli paused when he heard a furious roar and looked behind him, derision playing on his lips. He jumped upward and darted into the trees, vanishing into the depths of Qingqiu Mountain.","The mountain was enormous and Coldnight Estate would never find him without Kang Cheng’s marks. Yushi Moli wasn’t foolhardy enough to think that he could take on their entire group by himself. He was at most an earth rank cultivator in his current condition.","Since Coldnight Estate knew that he’d already killed an upper human rank cultivator, there would certainly be those he couldn’t defeat in the party this time. And judging from that howl, Luo Hanye seemed to have come in person.","It was his nephew who’d died, after all.","A nephew he viewed as his own son.","Thus, Yushi Moli could only run from his pursuers; he couldn’t attempt to meet them head-on. His actions earlier were just to enrage them and to inspire contempt for their quarry. Someone shrewd or calculating would never do what he’d done. They would conceal themselves after entering the mountain and observe from the shadows. They would never leave such provocative words.","Yushi Moli decided to go against convention, but he didn’t know that Coldnight Estate had brought hunting dogs.","After the dogs identified the boy’s scent at the scene, they led the estate’s experts straight to him.","......","Yushi Moli wandered aimlessly through Qingqiu Mountain. Though he’d come to hunt beasts, reality was cruel compared to daydreams. There were plenty of beasts in the mountains, but they weren’t lining up to meet the boy.","Besides, he was on the outskirts of the mountain. It was winter and most beasts were hibernating. Who would be lingering outside for no reason? Any who did usually became food for others.","The boy finally stumbled upon his target when the sun hovered in the south.","“Oh? Is that a monster beast?” Yushi Moli paused when he saw a white bear napping on the ground. Regular beasts were long in hibernation at this time of the year. Only monster beasts could move about normally.","Dappled sunlight warmed the ground since it was noon. Although it was still very cold, it was a rare day of good weather for monster beasts. Thus, the blizzard bear lazily took advantage of the opportunity for some sun.","Yushi Moli had read about these monster beasts in books. A first rank blizzard bear was the equivalent of a lower human rank cultivator.","“This guy’s more than five meters long, he’s pretty big. Even if I kill him, I won’t be able to bring him back...” Yushi Moli pondered. “Well, I don’t need the whole bear. Its paws and pelt are the most valuable.”","He’d conducted some research of various Qingqiu monsters before commencing his hunting trip. A blizzard bear’s paws and pelt sold for the most money—roughly five hundred gold coins.","Arf arf arf!","Earthshaking barks echoed behind him just as he considered how to take down the bear.","“Found him! The kid’s ahead!” Shouts rose and fell through the air.","“They found me that quickly?” Yushi Moli blinked, then sagged with resignation when he saw the massive hunting dogs. “Oh, of course, they’re not idiots. Eh, time to run!”","He shot out like an arrow and grazed past the blizzard bear before vanishing into the woods.","“After him!” Coldnight cultivators had caught sight of him and immediately gave chase.","“ROAR!!”","They were interrupted by a tremendous roar and an enormous white body pouncing on them.","“What is that?!” The cultivators only had Yushi Moli in their sights, so they were caught off guard by the massive being.","It smacked one of them down before they had a chance to react. It bit its target on the neck and killed an upper human rank cultivator before he could defend himself.","And then...","The blizzard bear ran off with its prey, leaving a shell-shocked party from Coldnight Estate.","A monster beast?","A first rank blizzard bear!","“Bastard!!” Luo Hanye shrieked again. A first rank monster beast was an ant! An ant had dared make off with one of his men right in front of him! “AFTER HIM!!”","“After... which one?” His men blinked. The bear or Yushi Moli? Those were two different directions!","“The boy, of course!!” Luo Hanye was nearly apoplectic with fury.","His men jerked awake and frantically shot off in Yushi Moli’s direction. There was no need to conceal themselves anymore, so true qi exploded out of their bodies and raised a ruckus along with their hunting dogs.","“ROAR!!” came another furious howl from deep within the mountain. Ominous aura spread in all directions as a massive bear the size of a mountain stared coldly at the trespassers. It seemed to have just awoken and a cruelly violent air raged over it.","“An upper fourth rank monster beast?? This is a terra bear!” Luo Hanye gasped.","Third rank monster beasts were the equivalent of celestial rank cultivators. Fourth rank... and upper fourth rank... could smack a celestial rank to death with one blow.","He turned and ran without further consideration. Being a celestial rank cultivator, he was strong enough to escape from the encounter. His men, however, were not so lucky. They were swiftly smashed into piles of meat. Even the highly valued Mister Zhou was torn to pieces.","Coldnight Estate suffered enormous losses on this incursion.","......","Up in a tree, Yushi Moli curled his lip when he observed what was taking place below.","“Although I didn’t know you’d bring hunting dogs with you, you’d have your ways of finding me since you came for me,” Yushi Moli chuckled gently. “Here you go, have a big present.”","He’d discovered the terra bear early on and stayed close by, waiting for those from Coldnight Estate to find him. The boy kept up a constant string of harassment in the absence, thoroughly irritating the bear. When his pursuers arrived, he smacked it and sent it into a towering rage.","But since the bear couldn’t find the boy, it vented its spleen on the hapless Coldnight contingent. After it rampaged through the humans and killed them all, it ran off in chase of Luo Hanye.","As a celestial rank cultivator, Luo Hanye’s ripples of true qi were extremely noticeable, like a bright lamp in the darkness. A terra bear enraged beyond reason didn’t hesitate to hunt him down as well.","Chuckling, Yushi Moli headed in another direction. The blizzard bear that’d run off earlier was very valuable, he didn’t want to give it up. He was also hungry and wanted a taste of bear."]},{"number":2199,"title":"Chapter 2199: Chapter 2154: My Name Is Lu Yun","paragraphs":["Chapter 2154: My Name Is Lu Yun","“Found it!” Yushi Moli ran a few kilometers before he found the blizzard bear. It’d already munched through the hapless Coldnight Estate cultivator and hugged a leg to itself as it napped in a clearing.","“It looks like it’s living a good life.” Yushi Moli’s lips curled upward and he jumped down lightly from the tree, landing in front of the bear.","The blizzard bear was uncommonly vigilant and scrambled up from the ground when it discovered the boy’s presence. Wide-eyed, it glared watchfully at him. It could sense a terrifying presence from the minuscule human in front of it.","“Be careful!” A shout rang out just as Yushi Moli was about to attack.","Three people had appeared behind him at some point in time—a young boy and two older companions. The blizzard bear had been too petrified to move when it sensed Yushi Moli’s aura, but the shout snapped its last strand of reason. It roared and charged the trio.","“Ahhh!” the young boy shrieked with abject fear as the bear thundered down on them.","Yushi Moli: ......","You’re a freaking upper human rank cultivator, okay?! You can beat this bear to death with a single hand, what are you yelling for?!","“Yunge!” One of the boy’s older companions yelled and smacked the bear back.","“Are you alright?!” The young boy’s hair was standing on end and he looked at Yushi Moli with trepidation. “What are you doing here alone? This is Qingqiu Mountain, it’s very dangerous!”","His voice carried a hint of softness. Though he was dressed as a young boy, one could tell that he was actually a young girl.","Yushi Moli rubbed his nose and didn’t respond. What was he supposed to say, that the blizzard bear was his prey? That if the three weren’t present, he would’ve already attacked the bear?","Even if Yushi Moli couldn’t take the bear with him, its paws were a rare delicacy. Ouyang Du had brought one to him once. Not only was it delicious, but it was also extremely nutritious and very beneficial for cultivation.","One paw fetched one hundred gold pieces at market, with the pelt going for more than that. The qingfeng sword couldn’t slice through it, but Yushi Moli’s sword could.","“Oi, are you also out on a secret training trip that your parents don’t know about?” exclaimed the disguised girl when she saw the sword in Yushi Moli’s hand. Staring at him with bright black eyes, she wasn’t the type to feel awkward even when Yushi Moli ignored her.","The other two with her were a man called Duan Lin and a woman called Qiu Yu—they were both earth rank cultivators.","“Hmm?” Duan Lin and Qiu Yu reassessed Yushi Moli when they heard their companion’s words.","He looked frail and a pampered air marked some of his gestures; he seemed to be the young master of a rich family. But their foreheads knit together when they noticed his hands.","They were pale and slender, the flesh so tender that they were more precious than a girl’s hands. It was the hands of one accustomed to living in ease and comfort. More importantly was that there were no ripples of true qi on him. He was very much an ordinary person, and it was a miracle that he’d gotten so far.","Thus, the three were convinced that the young man in front of them was the scion of a rich family. He’d entered the mountain with a sword to test himself and had made it this far because he was lucky.","Yushi Moli noticed the looks in their eyes and how they’d scanned his hands, quite resigned with the conclusions they’d drawn. A thick layer of calluses previously covered his hands due to prolonged practice with the sword. They were also criss-crossed with scars, and so looked incredibly coarse and rough.","But after taking ten Boneforge Pills, it was like his body had been reborn. His calluses and scars were gone.","“Child, who are you? It’s very dangerous to enter the mountain on a day like this.” Duan Lin relaxed. The boy in front of them posed no threat to them.","“My name is Lu Yun and I’m from Aurora City. I entered the mountain to train,” Yushi Moli offered with a sudden stroke of inspiration.","Lu Yun... was a name both removed and familiar. It seemed that this should be his name instead? But right now, it also seemed right that he was Yushi Moli and not Lu Yun.","He didn’t know who these people were and if they were connected to Coldnight Estate. It was better not to invite trouble, so he offered a name different from his.","“Lu Yun... I’m Xiangliu Yunge from Cloudscape City!” the girl smiled.","Duan Lin and Qiu Yu had wanted to stop her from replying, but she offered her real name without further ado.","“Big sis Qiu, Uncle Duan, let Lu Yun join us! He’ll be in danger if he's here alone,” Xiangliu Yunge said to her two companions.","“It’s big bro Duan! I’m only twenty-eight this year, not yet thirty!” Duan Lin responded solemnly.","“We can let him join us, but he has to listen to us in everything.” Qiu Yu was more softhearted and nodded with a look at Yushi Moli.","“Um, ah... you guys don’t have to...” he protested weakly.","These three were extreme burdens in his eyes, particularly Xiangliu Yunge. She was an upper human rank cultivator, but she’d been so frightened by a lower rank monster beast that she hadn’t been able to move!","How was he supposed to train following these three? How was he supposed to hunt beasts? The sparkling mounds of gold coins were getting further and further away from him!","“Kid,” Duan Lin grinned at Yushi Moli. “You must’ve read quite a few tales of young heroes and seen how they trained in the mountains when they were young. You probably idolize how these peerless characters dominated the land?”","Yushi Moli lowered his head without a word. He had indeed read quite a few of those biographies and been inspired, which was why he’d entered Qingqiu Mountain to train.","“I can tell you now that those are all lies,” Duan Lin snorted. “Judging from your actions, it’s your first trip into the mountain. If you don’t have a powerhouse accompanying you on your first time, there won’t even be bone shards left of you when you die!","“You want to temper yourself in Qingqiu Mountain with just a qingfeng sword? That’s nothing more than a daydream!”","Yushi Moli didn’t want to respond. With his mental strength, the monster beasts wouldn’t even find him if he wanted that to be.","“Our young master is benevolent and kind enough to allow you to follow us. This is your good fortune and you’ll learn quite a few things that you normally won’t read about in books, such as how to survive in a mountain.” Duan Lin looked at Yushi Moli. “I won’t stop you if you want to leave, but I guarantee that you won’t survive the night.”","“Young master? More like young miss,” Yushi Moli mumbled.","Xiangliu Yunge: ......","Duan Lin and Qiu Yu were likewise at a loss for words. It’s enough that you know the truth, is there a need to speak it out loud?","“You’re called Xiangliu Yunge? Compound surname Xiangliu?” Yushi Moli blinked before finally agreeing, “Alright, I’ll go with you three. Thanks for looking after me.”","The surname Xiangliu gave him a remarkably familiar feeling... like he had a friend in the past with a similar name.","And so, he changed his mind despite himself. If he didn’t go with them, they would likely die a very grisly death tonight.","The nights were terrifying within the mountain. Two earth rank cultivators and an upper human rank who didn’t know how to fight... that spoke of a doomed ending.","“Come along then, little guy.” Xiangliu Yunge smiled warmly to see Yushi Moli agree to their proposal. “We’re going to spend ten days in the mountain. You can stay with us during this time and learn how to survive in the wild. It's up to you whether you leave with us or stay after our outing is over.”","Qiu Yu and Duan Lin couldn’t care less. They were already chaperoning one person, so adding another didn’t make a difference. Being earth rank cultivators, they felt very secure wandering around the outskirts of the mountain.","Although Xiangliu Yinge was an upper human rank cultivator, her battle strength was similar to the boy called Lu Yun. They wouldn’t have a chance to exert even five percent of their strength if they ran into trouble.","Yushi Moli nodded without a word. He’d decided to join this group because of Xiangliu Yinge’s name. Perhaps it would awaken some of his memories or help him recall something. He was certain that the sword of heaven and earth was suppressing a part of his memories. Qingqiu and Xiangliu were names that seemed very familiar to him, so it must have something to do with his sealed memories. He even thought that he’d long ceased to be Yushi Moli, but was someone else with Yushi Moli’s memories—someone who was trying to find his way back to himself.","Xiangliu Yunge was quite happy to see Yushi Moli stay. The shadow lingering over her heart from the blizzard bear thoroughly dissipated. She was a cheerful girl of sunny disposition.","“Alright, we’re relatively safe since this is the blizzard bear’s territory. We can prepare dinner now.” The group didn’t carry rations, so the bear was their lunch. Although the sun had just begun to tilt toward the west, the days were short in the shady parts of Qingqiu Mountain and it would be dark soon.","“Don’t look!” Yushi Moli said to the girl as Duan Lin began to dress and handle the bear.","“Why not? You two will never improve if you don’t spill blood and this trip will have been made in vain.” Duan Lin curled his lip as he fished out the bear’s internal organs. He seemed to be purposefully rough with his motions and splashed the pungent scent of gore everywhere.","Although it would attract other monster beasts or wild beasts, the two powerhouses weren't concerned.","“I’m worried she won’t be able to keep anything down for the next couple of days if she does.” Yushi Moli swept an impassive look over the bloody scene. “If she doesn’t eat, she won’t have the energy to confront danger and endure the cold. That will be very dangerous in the frozen landscape of Qingqiu Mountain. You two can deal with monster beasts, but what about the cold and tiredness?”","Xiangliu Yunge had wanted to take a look, but turned her head away when she heard Yushi Moli and stood far away.","“If just looking at blood is a form of training, then we can just take a walk through a butcher house. But I think seeing this kind of blood just grosses ourselves out.” Yushi Moli smiled at his older traveling companions.","Duan Lin and Qiu Yu blinked. They hadn’t thought that the boy would hold these kinds of views and abruptly revised their opinion of him. It hadn’t been pure luck that brought him this far."]},{"number":2200,"title":"Chapter 2200: Chapter 2155: Three Thousand Reincarnations, The Final Way Out","paragraphs":["Chapter 2155: Three Thousand Reincarnations, The Final Way Out","“It’s simple enough if you want to spill blood,” Yushi Moli grinned suddenly. He abruptly unsheathed his sword and sent cutting sword qi at the young girl in front of him.","“What are you doing?!” Duan Lin and Qiu Yu sprang up with alarm. They wanted to stop him, but found that everything was changing around them.","Their lively, biddable, and gentle ward turned ugly and repulsive.","“Tsk tsk tsk, that was too easy for you,” Xiangliu Yunge chuckled and slowly reached out a hand to catch Yushi Moli—Lu Yun’s blow. “I thought you would stay immersed in this world and your identity until you broke through the seal imposed by the sword of heaven and earth in your mind.”","“Motong,” Lu Yun intoned. “I would have that if you hadn’t appeared. I’d fully forget myself in this identity and would’ve seen it through to the end.”","He shook his head with a sigh, “But you are. And here I am. Are you here to kill me?”","His physical body was gone and he lacked immortal dao. The Tome of Life and Death had taken the power of reincarnation to Qing Yu and the little fox. However, Motong remained at her peak. She could crush Lu Yun with a single hand.","“No,” Motong shook her head with a chuckle. “It was your doing that helped me break away from the control of the will of nothing. You helped me regain my freedom.”","Lu Yun frowned. “Where are we?”","“The Origin Continent.” Nostalgia appeared in Motong’s eyes. “The little fellow that you’re borrowing is Yushi Moli. If you hadn’t happened upon the scene, he would grow up to be one of the legendary characters of this era and ultimately help that person comprehend subjectivity affecting objectivity. That would cause the disaster to happen.”","“That person?” Lu Yun blinked.","“The person lying in the ancient tomb,” Motong sighed. “My dao partner.”","Lu Yun pursed his lips without a word.","“He was the first one to be affected by the will of nothing, I am the second. When he died, he became responsible for destroying everything that shouldn’t appear in the nothing with the power of death.","“I am the second to be infected by the will of nothing. I became its spokesperson in the nothing. When you took control of a small part of it, you created a hole in its perfection. Thus, I was freed.”","“Is this Origin Continent the sole existence in the past?” Lu Yun asked. “Wasn’t it destroyed? How did I end up here?”","There was no concept of time in the nothing. Living beings existed in only the present and could not reverse time, much less change the past or future.","“It’s because you made the nothing imperfect that I was able to bring you here,” Motong answered. “We didn’t travel through space and time, but used the power of reincarnation to create a world of reincarnation. The Origin Continent was recreated within reincarnation so that you could truly become one of the living beings here—Yushi Moli. You became Yushi Mowang’s brother.”","“Mowang?!” Lu Yun’s eyes narrowed at the sudden mention of another name. “You don’t mean... that Mowang was the first being to affect objectivity, the one who was killed by the will of the nothing and his body summarily possessed?”","Motong nodded. “I... am Xiangliu Yunge. I met Yushi Mowang through Yushi Moli and ultimately became dao partners with him. Yushi Moli helped us reach the peak and become the strongest of the continent.” She sighed, “I’d wanted to have you become Yushi Moli so you could retrace his life, but have Lu Yun’s instincts stop everything from happening.","“But I underestimated you. Even though you were lost in this world and forgot yourself, your instincts constantly reminded you of what you should be doing. You... awoke the moment you saw me, didn’t you?”","Lu Yun nodded mutely. He’d started awakening the second he offered Lu Yun as a name to Xiangliu Yunge.","“And now? I ruined your plans, so what do you plan to do now?”","Motong sighed again after some thought. “The Origin Continent isn’t the first existence within the nothing. That belongs to an even vaster and more magnificent world in the past!","“That is where immortal dao truly arose and is where the mistress, Dao King, and God call home. It is the true world of immortal dao.”","Lu Yun shook and he looked at Motong with sudden comprehension.","“The mistress, Dao King, and God once spoke of a world of immortal dao in which civilization had reached its peak,” Motong said. “Where even the great daos and heavenly dao had materialized and possessed their own wills as they ruled over all. They were even able to destroy the will of nothing when it was born.”","In the current world, the heavenly dao was an objective rhythm without emotions, desires, or thoughts. But in that world of immortal dao, they’d taken human form and ruled the world as daos with thought.","How terrifying were those implications? All of life would be enslaved the second they possessed their own desires.","“In that case, how did that world end?” Lu Yun frowned.","“The mistress said that they self-destructed,” Motong laughed at herself. “A willingness to do battle is forever the instincts of the living... One of their powerhouses once said that, ‘Since we are invincible among the world, who do we fight if not heavenly dao?’","“And so, he led all beings to conquer the heavens. Heavenly dao and the great daos were torn asunder after that battle and life was made miserable.","“Thus was the will of nothing born again and the world destroyed. The nothing became an objective nothing.”","Lu Yun remained silent.","“You have the karmic repercussions of Yushi Moli on you now, and a tie with the will of nothing.”","Although Lu Yun had awoken ahead of time, her plans extended beyond Origin Continent. She was ready with another plan.","“What do you intend to do?” he asked, easily sensing her emotions. She’d opened her soul up to him. If he wished, he could read the memories of her soul and even eat it if he wanted to.","“I plan to send you to that world and use the power of reincarnation to have you experience three thousand cycles. Those cycles will wash away everything having to do with your current identity. You will go to that world with your karmic ties and take the heavenly dao for your master!","“You can control the nothing and the immortal dao here. You might be able to destroy the will of nothing on Mowang—but so long as the nothing exists and objectivity exists, the will of nothing will never end.","“Only a heavenly dao with its own thoughts can combat it. I hope that you will become the heavenly dao in that world and then return to safeguard ours.” Motong bit her lip. “If we don’t use the power of reincarnation to wash away the various marks of identity on you, that world’s heavenly dao will see you as a heretic and kill you. Since you carry the karmic ties of the future, the heavenly dao will immediately understand and accept you when it sees you...”","Lu Yun nodded. “This is the final way out that the mistress and others left, isn’t it?”","“...yes,” Motong nodded. “The method of nothing you grasp is tattered and incomplete. It is an opening to the previous path of reincarnation and the path of all hope.”","The cause was in the future and the effect was in the past."]}]);
